window.AKK_DIRECTED_INNER_VOICE_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_DIRECTED_INNER_VOICE_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":201,"title":"Chapter 201: Selection of Candidates for the Guest Travel Academy","paragraphs":["A look of curiosity immediately appeared on Yue Fuguang's face. \"Has Your Majesty found out who is responsible?\"","The crowd watched the forced look of curiosity on her small face. They couldn't tell if it was just their imagination, but they suddenly felt that the Junior Preceptor's expression at this moment was even faker than when she used to spin tales to trick them.","Could it be that she was so disappointed in them that she didn't even want to bother acting anymore?","Yue Fuguang: Is it possible that this is just my real acting? Eye roll JPG","Emperor Mingxi let out a long sigh and nodded, saying, \"Wei Ping and the others have indeed found some clues. All signs indicate that Prince Qi did it.\"","\"Didn't Prince Qi commit suicide? Was this a dying order he left behind?\"","Emperor Mingxi: What kind of sane person leaves their last words to an assassin before dying!","Wei Ping smiled and added, \"Junior Preceptor, according to the confession of the captured assassin, their master's name is Qi Xie. But based on his description of the man's appearance, I drew a portrait, and unexpectedly, it turned out to be the deceased Prince Qi. Later, Lord Cai and I found some evidence in Prince Qi's manor, all of which indicates that the one who took poison to commit suicide was his body double, not Prince Qi himself.\"","Yue Fuguang nodded. \"I see! Then has Lord Wei found Prince Qi's hiding place?\"","Wei Ping shook his head apologetically. \"Not yet! But please rest assured, Junior Preceptor, I will definitely bring Prince Qi to justice.","During this time, we will also increase your protection. What happened last night will certainly not happen again.\"","Emperor Mingxi also chimed in, \"Apart from telling you who the mastermind behind yesterday's assassination is, the other reason I called you here is to let you go to the Kexing Institute to select a group of personal bodyguards.","There is no limit to the number; you can take away anyone you fancy.\"","With a grand wave of his hand, Emperor Mingxi was generously assigning people to Yue Fuguang to put her mind at ease.","\"The Kexing Institute, what is that place? A place where Your Majesty trains guards?\"","This was truly the first time Yue Fuguang had heard that the imperial court had such a government office.","Xie Zhiyan explained, \"Didn't the Junior Preceptor once ask me about the people of the martial arts world, and even mentioned wanting to hire some martial artists?\"","Yue Fuguang nodded. She did have such a plan; after all, this involved a few of her missions.","Xie Zhiyan continued, \"This Kexing Institute is a government office that recruits martial artists who wish to serve the imperial court. The people inside are all martial artists with excellent skills.","This office has a long history. For example, General Wei Shouyi's father originated from the martial arts world and came out of the Kexing Institute. He later went to the battlefield and established illustrious military merits, which led to the Wei family of today.\"","Wei Shouyi immediately chimed in, \"Rest assured, Junior Preceptor, the martial artists who can enter the Kexing Institute are not lacking in either character or martial arts skills.","The families of these people also live in residences arranged by the government offices in the capital, so you can be completely at ease.\"","What he didn't say was that those who were qualified to be brought before the Junior Preceptor for her to choose from had been screened over and over again. They had already started preparing these candidates when the Junior Preceptor was assassinated for the first time.","Emperor Mingxi also said, \"These people receive salaries from the imperial court, so there is still a difference between them and true wandering martial artists.\"","Learning civil and martial arts to sell to the imperial family was not just an empty saying. Truly far-sighted martial artists still hoped to integrate into the imperial court, obtain an official position, and in the future, bring honors to their wives and children and glory to their ancestors.","Otherwise, wouldn't the life and death of even the most prestigious great hero still depend on a single word from the imperial court?","The martial arts world was not just about fighting and killing; it was also about the ways of the world and human relationships.","Yue Fuguang revealed a smile and said, \"Since that's the case, then shouldn't I carefully select a few more useful people?\"","Since they were giving her manpower, she wouldn't hold back!","As for whether there were any hidden spies of the Emperor or others among them, she wasn't worried at all. In fact, she was more afraid that the Emperor wouldn't know what she was doing.","Having someone help pass on messages would actually save her the trouble of dropping bombshells and watching the drama unfold in the imperial court.","Suddenly thinking of something, Yue Fuguang asked, \"Your Majesty, do these people all have proper official titles?\"","Since they were able to enter the Kexing Institute, it meant they wanted to be civil servants. They were all ambitious people with aspirations.","If they followed her and remained commoners, wouldn't that go against their wishes? It would make them somewhat less willing to be commanded.","Emperor Mingxi smiled and nodded. \"The lowest official rank is an upper seventh rank, and there is no limit to this number. I will also give you five lower sixth ranks, three upper sixth ranks, and one lower fifth rank.","As for who to give these official ranks to, you can decide for yourself. Once you have finalized the list, just submit it to the Ministry of Personnel.\"","Yue Fuguang nodded inwardly. The Emperor wasn't bad. It seemed he was wealthy and generous, even letting her choose the person for a lower fifth rank position herself. He was quite considerate.","Emperor Mingxi: One cannot catch the little immortal lord without sparing some official ranks. If it weren't for the fact that he hadn't elevated her status yet, giving an upper fifth rank or a lower fourth rank wouldn't be impossible, as long as this person didn't always think about running away!","As soon as the Emperor offered the lower fifth rank position, many people present also had faces full of envy. Although military officials were naturally considered a rank lower than civil officials, given the current development of the Great Yan Dynasty, there would sooner or later be a war with their neighboring countries. The Great Yan Dynasty, blessed with the descent of an immortal lord, would certainly no longer be satisfied with the current state of division among several countries.","The current Great Yan was slowly undergoing changes. Not only would it not perish as it did in the original history, but it would even embark on the path of hegemony to unify the five countries.","With the imperial court, or rather, the Little Immortal Lord acting as their backer on the battlefield, military merits were much easier to earn than before.","Didn't you see that those with foresight had all sent their descendants to serve under Wei Shouyi, keeping Yu Boming of the Yu family company?","They called it gaining experience, but wasn't it just an indirect way of clinging to the Little Immortal Lord's coattails?","They looked at the current monarch, Emperor Mingxi, and the future heir, Xie Zhiyan. These two would certainly not let slip this once-in-a-lifetime opportunity to unify the world.","Even if those two wanted to give up, the bloodthirsty warmongers in the Ministry of War would definitely push them down this path.","Yue Fuguang: And me. If they don't take this path and it affects my ability to earn points, I wouldn't mind swapping them out for someone more obedient to sit on the throne.","Emperor Mingxi and Xie Zhiyan suddenly felt a chill down their spines, a fleeting sensation of being targeted by some ferocious beast flashing across their minds.","Ji Hongming ignored the myriad of thoughts swirling in his colleagues' heads. Seeing His Majesty mention the Ministry of Personnel, he tactfully took a step forward and said, \"If Lord Junior Preceptor needs it, this humble official can send a secretary to accompany you to select the personnel.\"","The Crown Prince also said, \"I shall accompany Lord Junior Preceptor as well.\"","Wei Shouyi added, \"This general will also go.\"","With a simple, honest smile, he said to Yue Fuguang, \"Lord Junior Preceptor, I, Old Wei, am familiar with that place. I know exactly who has real skills.\"","Yue Fuguang replied with a polite smile, \"That would be wonderful. I'll have to rely on General Wei to help me pick out some good men later.\"","The group took their leave of Emperor Mingxi and excitedly headed toward the Guest Courtyard.","Passing by several government offices along the way and seeing the busy figures inside, Yue Fuguang could actually smell the distinct, heavy scent of overworked corporate slaves wafting off them.","Thinking about having to attend court and go to school at the tender age of nine, it was indeed a bit tougher compared to peers of the same age!","But for the sake of points, it seemed it wasn't unbearable.","With this kind of mindset, Yue Fuguang didn't even need anyone's coaxing; a simple shift in thought, and the prospect of points was enough for self-comfort!","After all, a penniless person had no right to slack off and lie flat!","The laziness of the past few days was instantly cured after taking a look at the points balance!"]},{"number":202,"title":"Chapter 202: Selecting People Based on Favorability","paragraphs":["Yue Fuguang shook her head silently. She was indeed still a mortal at heart. Living as an 'Immortal Lord' for the past half a year hadn't bestowed much 'immortal aura' upon her!","At the end of the day, she was just a special kind of corporate slave working under the Main System!","Before Yue Fuguang could sigh any further, the group arrived at the entrance of the Guest Courtyard.","From afar, Song Xingzhou, the director of the Guest Courtyard, came out to welcome them. He bowed to the Crown Prince, Yue Fuguang, and the rest, saying, \"Your Highness, Junior Preceptor, please come in. This humble official has already ordered everyone to wait in the courtyard.\"","Yue Fuguang nodded. \"Thank you for your trouble, Lord Song.\"","This man also held a position in the Ministry of Works, which was why Yue Fuguang remembered him. More importantly, his favorability towards her was over sixty.","Seeing that the Junior Preceptor recognized him, Song Xingzhou was naturally overjoyed. He smiled and said, \"It is all within this humble official's duty.\"","He guided them inside with great attentiveness, introducing the situation of the Guest Courtyard as they walked.","Seeing his job being snatched away and that surnamed Song ignoring him completely, Wei Shouyi was immediately displeased.","Following behind the group, he clamored, \"Old Song, you see your Old Wei here, and you don't even greet me?\"","Song Xingzhou said impatiently, \"You come here every few days and are more familiar with this place than your own home. Do you still need me to introduce it to you?\"","At a glance, it was clear the two were old acquaintances, the kind of bantering friends who spoke without any reservations.","\"I already agreed with the Junior Preceptor to help her select people, so don't you try to steal my thunder!\"","Song Xingzhou scoffed. \"Speaking of which, who knows the backgrounds and martial skills of the people in the Guest Courtyard better than I do?\"","With a look of disdain, he added, \"Just stand aside and watch. Don't delay the Junior Preceptor's selection.\"","Wei Shouyi was very dissatisfied with his attitude and words. \"I've sparred with all the good fighters here, I...\"","Without waiting for him to finish, Song Xingzhou immediately interjected, \"I know, just a couple of days ago you were pinned to the ground by Wang Qingxiao and...\"","Before he could say the word 'rubbed', he was immediately interrupted by Wei Shouyi. \"Old Song, look, we're here. Enough with the idle chatter, hurry up and get down to business.\"","Seeing Wei Shouyi's stifled expression, the System burst out laughing and couldn't help but tease, 'Master, was the word Lord Song didn't finish rubbed?'","Hearing the Divine Artifact's words, a suspicious blush immediately appeared on Wei Shouyi's bronzed face.","Yue Fuguang communicated, 'General Wei might be slightly inferior to the people here in one-on-one combat, but when it comes to battlefield formations, these people definitely cannot compare to him.'","Wei Shouyi nodded vigorously in his heart. Yes, yes, yes, the Junior Preceptor is right. When it comes to fighting a war, they can't compare to me.","Yue Fuguang and the Crown Prince stood side by side on the high platform, looking at the hundred or so people standing neatly below.","There were both men and women, ranging in age from their teens to their thirties. She nodded secretly in her heart.","Setting everything else aside, the mental outlook of these people was quite good.","The men looked robust and vigorous, and the women were all radiant and stood tall, possessing the free-spiritedness of women from the martial world.","Song Xingzhou must have briefed them before they arrived, so the gazes these people directed at her were very fervent.","If they knew that Emperor Mingxi had given her a quota for official ranks, these 'martial artists', most of whom were still commoners, would likely look at her with even more fervor.","She originally wanted to say that anyone unwilling to follow her could step down now, and she promised not to blame them. But seeing their eager expressions, she realized those words were unnecessary.","Yue Fuguang suddenly felt a bit curious about what Song Xingzhou had told them to elicit such expressions.","Song Xingzhou thought to himself: The Junior Preceptor is completely oblivious to her own status in the officialdom of Great Yan. These people who harbored ambitions of securing an official position had long heard of this newly risen noble.","Some of them had even tried to accidentally encounter her on her way to and from the imperial court, though unfortunately, none had succeeded.","During the Junior Preceptor's two assassination attempts, a few people from their Guest Courtyard happened to be present and had personally stepped in to help the guards fend off the enemies.","A few days ago, he had merely leaked a little news that the Junior Preceptor might come here to select guards, and that very day, quite a few people had sought him out, expressing their desire to participate in the selection.","To fight for these one hundred spots, these people had engaged in quite a few private brawls.","After sweeping her gaze over the crowd, Yue Fuguang spoke in a voice that was youthful yet carried authority. \"I presume your Lord Song has already told you the purpose of my visit.","I have many rules here. Those who are born loving freedom and cannot bear to be restricted may withdraw now.\"","After waiting for half a minute and seeing no one move, Yue Fuguang nodded like a little adult. \"Very well. Since no one is withdrawing, those who are selected must strictly abide by my rules.\"","Saying this, Yue Fuguang first cast her gaze upon the twenty or thirty women standing at the very front. Some were pretty, some were delicate, and there were even a few young girls with ordinary faces that were not easily remembered.","'System, help me sort the favorability of these hundred people from highest to lowest.'","'Is the host going to select people based on favorability?'","'Naturally. Martial arts skills are secondary; the most important thing for the people by my side is loyalty. Although favorability doesn't equate to loyalty right now,","we won't be able to fully understand these people anytime soon. Favorability is the best basis. No matter how strong someone is, what use do I have for them if they have no favorability towards me?'","Yue Fuguang then looked at the sixty or seventy sturdy men in the back. Judging by their facial features alone, they all looked like decent people. Huh, Yue Fuguang even spotted a familiar face in the crowd.","Seeing that Yue Fuguang was merely looking and taking no action, Wei Shouyi couldn't help but lean in and ask, \"Junior Preceptor, do you need this humble official to explain the backgrounds of these people in detail?\"","Seeing his job being snatched by this guy, Song Xingzhou was secretly annoyed.","Yue Fuguang said, \"I'll take a look at the roster first.\"","She took the roster handed over by the Crown Prince and flipped through it one by one. The backgrounds, special skills, and other details recorded on it were quite comprehensive.","\"How does the Junior Preceptor plan to select people? Do you need them to have a sparring match?\" Wei Shouyi suggested. He advocated for seeing real skills through combat.","Yue Fuguang shook her head. \"There's no need for such trouble. I'll just look at the roster and call out their names directly.\"","As she spoke, she nodded at Song Xingzhou, who was a step behind them, and said, \"I trust Lord Song's eye for people. Now, I am simply picking those who are pleasing to the eye.\"","Song Xingzhou cupped his hands, showing unhideable excitement amidst his trepidation. \"This humble official thanks the Junior Preceptor for your trust!\"","The commotion on the platform naturally did not escape the eyes and ears of the people below. They already knew that this Junior Preceptor held a transcendent status in the officialdom of Great Yan.","They didn't expect that seeing was believing. Lord Song, who was a top-tier figure to them, not only had to act cautiously around her, but even the Crown Prince vaguely showed a respectful demeanor towards her.","Realizing that this was an even more powerful patron than they had previously imagined, everyone felt an inexplicable surge of excitement in their hearts. Their mental outlook became even better than when Yue Fuguang had first arrived.","Yue Fuguang looked at the flushed faces of the crowd below and silently nodded in her heart. Looking at the roster, but actually looking at the system panel, she began to call out names.","\"Shen Chunying, Shen Dongxue, Zhang Fang, Liu Wei, Xu Chunshan, Xu Xiaoman, Gao Zhifan...\" Yue Fuguang called out the names of twenty-six people in one breath, all of whom had a favorability of over forty."]},{"number":203,"title":"Chapter 203: Official Positions","paragraphs":["Originally, she wanted to gather exactly thirty people, but she didn't think much of those with a favorability score below forty. After thinking it over, she decided it was better to be short of the quota than to settle for mediocrity.","Among the twenty-six people, fourteen were women, and out of the twelve men, that familiar face was surprisingly present.","\"System, take a look at that burly man named Zhang Fang. Is he the one we saw at the auction who bought the Cloud-Cleaving Sword?\"","[It's him. He trimmed his beard.] It was obvious that he had properly washed and dressed up for today's selection.","Yue Fuguang nodded and called forward another seven people whose favorability scores were above fifty. Looking at the seven, she said, \"I have a position for a Secondary Fifth Rank official here.","Do you want to spar to decide who is the strongest among you?","The winner will not only receive this position but will also be your future leader.\"","Hearing about a Secondary Fifth Rank official position, never mind the three men, even the four women's eyes lit up.","The seven of them exchanged glances, their faces flushed. Yue Fuguang thought they were about to fight, but unexpectedly, the others silently took a step back, leaving only Zhang Fang standing at the front.","Shen Chunying spoke on behalf of the group, \"We wouldn't dare deceive you, Junior Preceptor. In terms of martial arts alone, we are far inferior to Zhang Fang.\"","At this, their faces grew even redder. It wasn't that they didn't want to fight for the Secondary Fifth Rank position; it was simply that against Zhang Fang, they couldn't win!","Yue Fuguang nodded. She hadn't expected this man to be the undisputed strongest among them by such a wide margin. She just wondered if he was the strongest out of all the others.","\"Zhang Fang, can you read?\"","This was quite important. It would be a joke if a leader and an official was illiterate.","Zhang Fang cupped his hands and replied, \"To answer you, Junior Preceptor, your subordinate has studied for a few years, and there are also teachers who give regular lessons at the Guest Courtyard.\"","Yue Fuguang nodded and cast an appreciative glance at Song Xingzhou. Song Xingzhou smiled and said, \"Rest assured, Junior Preceptor. Those who came for the selection were carefully handpicked by this humble official. Not only are their martial arts superb, but they also have a basic grasp of reading and writing.\"","\"Lord Song is very thoughtful.\"","She then turned back to Zhang Fang. \"From today onwards, you will take up the position of Secondary Fifth Rank Protectorate. Shen Chunying and Shen Dongxue will take up the positions of Primary Sixth Rank Deputy Protectorate.\"","Thinking that these were all strangers and that she needed her own people in the team, she immediately swallowed the Primary Sixth Rank position she had originally intended to give Xu Chunshan and changed her words, \"Liu Wei, Xu Chunshan, Xu Xiaoman, and Gao Zhifan will take up Secondary Sixth Rank positions.\"","As Yue Fuguang's words fell, the few of them were stunned on the spot. It wasn't just them; the others who were selected and those who weren't all looked at them with excitement or envy.","The courtyard was dead silent, save for the thumping heartbeats and heavy breathing of the seven people.","The few who had just been hit by this massive stroke of luck only blanked out for a few breaths before immediately dropping to one knee to express their loyalty and submission.","In loud, unison voices, they declared, \"Your subordinates thank you for the promotion, My Lady!\"","Yue Fuguang said indifferently, \"Rise. Doing your duties diligently in the future will be thanks enough!\"","\"Yes! Your subordinates will definitely do our utmost to protect your safety, My Lady!\"","Yue Fuguang swept her gaze across the courtyard, very satisfied with everyone's reactions. It had basically achieved the effect she wanted from conferring official titles on the spot.","Looking at the remaining nineteen people, she said, \"The rest of you will all hold Secondary Seventh Rank positions.\"","Gasp!","Someone in the crowd couldn't help but draw a sharp breath. They looked at Yue Fuguang as if she were a god. This... this lady was way too favored by His Majesty!","Regardless of what the people below thought, the nineteen who were similarly struck by this immense surprise followed the example of the previous seven, dropping to one knee to pledge their loyalty and submission.","Secondary Seventh Rank! From now on, they were officials too!","Even as the twenty-six of them walked out the gates of the Guest Courtyard, their feet still felt like they were floating on clouds. Casting a final backward glance at the familiar gates, they realized that the longest any of them had lived here was over three years, and the shortest over a year. Today, they were finally walking out of these gates as officials.","Looking ahead at the Junior Preceptor walking shoulder-to-shoulder with the Crown Prince, their previously drifting hearts suddenly found a sense of belonging.","This was especially true for the fourteen women. In the Great Yan Dynasty, apart from the female officials in the palace and the female generals from generations of military families, they were currently the only group of female officials in the imperial court with proper official ranks!","Originally, coming to the Guest Courtyard, the best outcome they could hope for was to become bodyguards for royal noblewomen. That was completely different from following the Junior Preceptor, a court official.","They had to work even harder and do their utmost to protect Her Ladyship well. They needed to prove to the officials in the imperial court that the Junior Preceptor hadn't chosen the wrong people, and that they were worthy of these official titles!","After bidding farewell to the Crown Prince and Wei Shouyi and returning to the Yu Manor, Yue Fuguang tossed the group over to the butler for him to arrange.","The Yu Manor also had guards, so the head butler naturally knew how to handle these matters better than she did. She wouldn't bother worrying about it; overthinking would stunt her growth!","Starting the next day, besides Cuizhu, she had eight more guards by her side, five women and three men. After returning to the Yu Manor yesterday, Yue Fuguang had directly given the remaining Secondary Sixth Rank position to Cuizhu.","As for the last Primary Sixth Rank position, Yue Fuguang tossed the problem directly to Yu Chongshan, asking him to help find one of their own people.","She also saved a Secondary Seventh Rank spot for the Yu family. Counting the hidden guard who protected her during her daily commutes to and from court and had survived two assassinations, her thirty-person guard squad was finally complete.","Yu Chongshan immediately understood that his granddaughter was seeking benefits for their family!","They all knew that, excluding his younger brother Yu Chongyan's family, the most suitable candidate in their household was Fourth YU, who was currently still a commoner.","That very night, Yu Chongshan summoned Yu Mochun to the outer study and gave him a good talking-to. The main point was to help his niece keep an eye on these people, not to put on the airs of an elder, and not to act privileged in the guard squad just because he was a member of the Yu family.","The guard squad belonged to Yue Fuguang, not the Yu family. Those people were colleagues, not servants.","Upon hearing that he was being given a Primary Sixth Rank position, which was higher than the rank of a magistrate in some remote little counties, Yu Mochun was thrilled for quite a while.","He was finally no longer a commoner!","As for whether it would be a loss of face for him, an uncle, to work under his niece, Yu Mochun felt it was the exact opposite!","He was now his own niece's subordinate, which instantly brought them much closer. At the very least, from now on, he would be closer to Fuguang than his third brother was!","Finally, hearing his father tell him not to put on the airs of an elder in front of Fuguang, Yu Mochun was rendered speechless. Let alone him, neither his brother nor his father had ever dared to put on the airs of an elder in front of that little ancestor.","You all dote on her and coax her in every possible way, so what makes you think I have the guts to act like an elder?","Is it because I'm a concubine-born son of the Yu Manor, or because I'm the only commoner? Who says the barefooted can't be afraid of the one wearing shoes?","Yu Mochun swore and took an oath on the spot, expressing his true feelings, \"Father, your son knows that Fuguang is looking out for me with this position. Is your son someone who doesn't know what's good for him?\"","He knew his father had long planned to get him a vacancy, but finding a suitable one was not easy.","The capital was full of people with backgrounds like his, and countless eyes were fixed on every good position!","His father had planned for so long but still hadn't waited for a suitable vacancy.","Later, when Fuguang emerged in their family, he knew he would get an opportunity sooner or later, and here it was."]},{"number":204,"title":"Chapter 204: Has Trouble Erupted in the Second Household Too","paragraphs":["Thinking of this, he ingratiatingly poured a cup of tea for his elderly father, chuckled twice, and continued, \"Anyone with a discerning eye can see that following my niece has a bright future. Even if your son were a fool, I'd still know this is a rare opportunity. I will only help my niece look after her affairs properly and won't bring shame to you or her.\"","Yu Chongshan felt very comfortable being waited on by his son, and the words were pleasing to hear. He knew his son didn't take this for granted, understood that his niece was looking out for him, and was grateful for her patronage.","He was quite satisfied with his youngest son's tactfulness.","Having finished lecturing his son, he was eager to shoo him away, waving his hand as if swatting a fly to tell him to leave quickly.","Yu Mochun tactfully refilled his father's tea and turned to leave. Before he even reached the door, Yu Chongshan called him back.","\"Fourth Son, make a trip to your Second Uncle's house. Tell him there is still a vacancy for a secondary seventh-rank official in Fuguang's guard escort. You can also generously share your own good news with them.\"","Yu Chongshan didn't feel like he was showing off at all.","Therefore, the next day, when Yue Fuguang finished her studies and stepped into the manor with her two older sisters, the butler ran over to report that the Second Master had come to visit and that dinner would be served in the main hall.","Yue Fuguang said, \"Uncle Butler, please inform Grandmother that my sisters and I will return to our rooms to change our clothes before heading over.\"","She directly made the decision for her two sisters; otherwise, they would definitely be too embarrassed to return to their own courtyards first.","Second Grandfather was a close relative, and as the younger generation, they were expected to go and pay their respects immediately.","Waiting until the butler had walked away, Yu Ningxuan smiled and said, \"Fuguang, we sisters thank you!\"","She tugged at a small ink stain on her sleeve and said, \"Otherwise, I would have had to meet our guests in dirty clothes.\"","Yu Ningxin also chimed in, \"Exactly. Second Sister's ink stain is on her sleeve, and mine is on the front of my dress. It really would be inappropriate to go over looking like this!\"","Yue Fuguang said nonchalantly, \"It's a small matter. Hurry and go, sisters.\"","She could roughly guess why Second Grandfather's family had come over at this time.","However, she hadn't expected that a minor secondary seventh-rank position would actually prompt the whole family to come over.","How could Yue Fuguang have known that in the eyes of others, she was now a highly promising prospect? Let alone the fact that she had a secondary seventh-rank official position to offer.","Even if a commoner could stay by her side and tie their fortunes to hers, there would be droves of people fighting for the chance to come.","When she was selecting people, she intentionally praised Song Xingzhou a bit more. Her original intention was to build a good relationship first, so that when she came to select people in the future, Song Xingzhou would save some capable hands for her.","Who knew that after yesterday, she wouldn't even need to go looking herself; there were plenty of people lining up, waiting for her to choose.","By the time she arrived at the main hall, Yu Chongshan and his sons were already there. Well, she was the last to arrive again.","Did this count as acting like a diva?","This was also Yue Fuguang's first time seeing Second Grandfather's family since the New Year, and they exchanged a good round of pleasantries upon meeting.","Of course, the ones exchanging pleasantries were the others; she only needed to maintain an appropriate smile.","Yu Chongshan and Yu Chongyan's couple went from mutually flattering each other's children and grandchildren at the beginning, to eventually showering all their praises on Yue Fuguang alone.","Hearing the adults throwing all kinds of free-flowing compliments at her, anyone with thinner skin wouldn't have been able to stand listening.","Yue Fuguang thought: After visiting relatives and friends during the New Year, my skin has already grown thick. This is just a few people, a piece of cake! Doge JPG","Their family was also a bit different. Usually, when others praised one's own child, the family members would offer a few words of modesty.","But her grandfather and grandmother did the exact opposite. While Yu Chongyan and his wife praised her from the front, Yu Chongshan and Old Madam Yu would add more compliments from behind.","It was as if they were afraid that the younger brother and sister-in-law's praises for their granddaughter weren't comprehensive enough!","Yue Fuguang thought: I haven't even eaten dinner yet, but I'm already full from all the praise!","Even though she had thick skin and could handle it, there was absolutely no need to endure such torment!","So she racked her brains and quickly came up with a way to divert everyone's attention. She asked inwardly, \"Little Zhu, after the Great Yan fell, what happened to my Second Grandfather's family?\"","Yu Chongyan thought: Here it comes, here it comes. I've finally waited for you, my time of death!","With the appearance of Yue Fuguang's question, the sound of praise in the room noticeably weakened by a third.","In order to better hear what followed, Yu Chongshan directly invited everyone to take their seats for the banquet.","Although a family of flesh and blood wouldn't strictly adhere to the rule of no talking while eating at the table, speaking a little less wouldn't make people feel it was too abrupt.","[Master, the ending of your Second Grandfather's family wasn't very good either. Although they didn't completely die out like your family, only the youngest daughter-in-law survived, taking along a pair of children.","In such chaotic times, it's easy to imagine how long a weak mother with young children could survive.]","Hearing the word die out again, Yu Chongshan's endurance was much better than before. With his granddaughter giving him confidence, he was now afraid of nothing.","Yu Chongyan's originally pale face and the hand that trembled too much to hold his chopsticks steady instantly calmed down upon meeting his older brother's firm, reassuring gaze.","Especially when he saw Yue Fuguang taking small sips of her soup, an infinite strength suddenly welled up in his heart.","Regardless of the past, now that their two families had her holding down the fort, no matter what happened to other families, theirs would be perfectly fine!","To say something highly disrespectful, even if the Great Yan fell, their Yu family wouldn't fall with it anymore!","\"Oh, tell me what happened. Did a troublemaker also appear in Second Grandfather's family?\"","[Master, you really hit the nail on the head. Their family also produced a menace, causing your Second Grandpa's entire family to lose their protection after your Grandpa and the others passed away, which quickly led to the ruin of their family.]","\"Didn't the Yu Manor perish together with the Great Yan Dynasty? At that time, foreign invaders came in, burning, killing, and looting. As long as they didn't run away, wasn't it normal for a family to be destroyed?\"","[When the foreign tribe invaded, even though they had an inside man to open the gates for them, they didn't break in all at once. It was only after a few days of defending the capital that they found an opportunity to secretly open the city gates. At that time, five days had already passed since the Yu family was murdered by Yu Ningrou. That is to say, on the night the foreign tribe entered the city, the menace from Yu Chongyan's family took the opportunity to lead people to ransack their Second Branch.]","\"I see. Who exactly is the menace of the Second Branch?\"","This question also lingered in the minds of the entire Yu family.","The Second Old Madam, Madam Wu, hid her hand under the table, tightly gripping her husband's broad, sweaty palm.","Yu Chongyan's hand ached from the grip of his usually frail wife, but even though her nails were about to dig into his flesh, he didn't utter a single sound.","He only patted the back of her hand reassuringly, managing his facial expressions well so that the little ancestor at the table wouldn't notice anything amiss.","[It is Yu Huaijian, the third concubine-born son of Yu Boyuan from the eldest branch.]","Yu Huaijian? Yu Chongyan thought about it for a long time but couldn't recall having such a grandson in his family, let alone from his eldest son's branch.","His eyes silently glanced at Yu Boyuan. When Yu Boyuan heard the name Yu Huaijian, he immediately felt a wave of guilt and panic.","His face paled from fright. Being stared at by his own father at this moment, he swallowed hard, his face turning from pale to red. He pretended to eat and drink, simply not daring to look at his father and eldest uncle.","As soon as Yu Chongshan and Yu Chongyan saw Yu Boyuan's reaction, they knew that he definitely had such a son.","Since they didn't know about it, then...","[Master, are you unable to recall ever meeting this Yu Huaijian?]","\"Indeed, I've met all the children from Second Grandpa's family, and I really don't remember such a person. Is he Uncle Yuan's son from an outside mistress?\""]},{"number":205,"title":"Chapter 205: How Did He Bring Disaster to the Second Branch of the Family","paragraphs":["Yue Fuguang was considered half an ancient person anyway. Since the child wasn't raised in the estate, he must have been born to a mistress kept outside. This wasn't hard to guess.","[He is indeed an illegitimate child. His biological mother comes from a poor background as the descendant of a convicted official. Yu Boyuan didn't dare to bring them back to the Yu family. Therefore, even though Yu Huaijian is already fifteen years old, he has never stepped through the doors of the Yu family.","He feels both yearning and resentment towards the Yu family. On one hand, he longs to be officially recognized and return to his ancestors; on the other hand, he harbors extreme resentment towards his brothers who can openly and legitimately live as sons of the Yu family.]","Yu Boyuan's face went blank for a moment. In front of him, Jian'er had always maintained the image of a well-behaved and sensible son. Whenever the Yu family was mentioned, his face would be filled with pride.","He also showed great affection towards his brothers at home. Even though they had never met, Yu Boyuan felt that the child would definitely get along well with his brothers.","How could he harbor resentment towards his family members?","\"How did he ruin the second branch?\"","[This Yu Huaijian has a rather special hobby. He likes to open brothels. Calculating the time, this year he will take the money he asked from Yu Boyuan to open his very first brothel.]","\"It's not strange to like doing business, but how could someone like opening brothels? Uncle Yuan is quite wealthy! The money he gave to an illegitimate child is enough to open a brothel!\"","Yue Fuguang couldn't help but make a snide remark to stir up trouble for Yu Boyuan, her gaze towards him carrying a hint of disgust.","In this era, having three wives and four concubines was the norm. Although Yue Fuguang couldn't stand it, she respected it, as she couldn't change it anyway.","But it was too much to sneak out for a fling when there were already several women at home, and then to keep that mistress hidden away in a golden house to raise a child.","Yu Boyuan's wife, Madam Cheng, was twisting the handkerchief in her hands so hard it was almost torn to shreds.","The atmosphere at the adults' table was a bit off, and the children at the other two tables also sensed it. Although some didn't know what had happened, relying on their keen animal-like instincts, they knew they had to restrain themselves.","Yue Fuguang also pretended to be curious and looked up at her grandfather and grandmother. Seeing that they still had gentle expressions, she continued to lower her head and focus on eating.","[Because his biological mother, Huang Dongmei, was a pure entertainer born in a brothel, who was redeemed and kept by Yu Boyuan.","This Huang Dongmei didn't have many acquaintances in the capital; everyone she knew was in the brothel.","So after she had no worries about food and clothing, she didn't cut off contact with her sisters in the brothel. Yu Huaijian naturally became familiar with these aunties.","Therefore, his liking for opening brothels was somewhat influenced by the professions of his mother and aunties.]","\"So far, I don't see how bad Yu Huaijian is. As for his resentment towards the Yu family, it's human nature.","This Huang Dongmei is still willing to contact her past sisters, so she's not the kind of person who forgets her friends after becoming prosperous.","Although I can't bring myself to like this mother and son, I really can't figure out why Yu Huaijian would harm the Yu family later.\"","[Later, Yu Huaijian's opening of the brothel was discovered by Yu Boyuan. He beat his son up and forced him to close it.","As the saying goes, where there is a policy from above, there is a countermeasure from below. Since he couldn't open it openly, he secretly set up a few hidden brothels.]","\"Is he that persistent? Isn't his career ambition placed in the wrong spot?\"","[Master, you forgot his age. He is right in his rebellious phase, and since he likes doing it, the more his father forbids him, the more he wants to do it.","It was also at this time that he met some people and embarked on another path.]","\"What people?\"","[Does Master still remember Drunken Rakshasa? She's the woman who set a trap for Cai Bing and Huo Shui.]","\"I remember. Yu Huaijian met this woman?\"","[Yes, before opening his first brothel, Yu Huaijian had seen her at the Cangchun Brothel. At that time, Drunken Rakshasa was still in the guise of a fallen young woman.","She was a free person, just temporarily registered under the name of Cangchun Brothel. Because Cai Bing and Huo Shui, two men fighting over one woman, she gained a great reputation.","Also, due to the instructions of the Huo and Cai families, she had fame, but her days on the surface were not easy.","Yu Huaijian even tried to poach her to his own brothel, but unfortunately, she refused him.]","Yu Chongshan's eyes flashed. This Drunken Rakshasa had been hunted down by Cai Xian and Huo Ying before the new year, but unfortunately, she managed to escape in the end.","Hearing the two say that the two people who came to rescue her were both dressed in black, masked, and highly skilled in martial arts. Judging from their moves, they didn't entirely look like people from the martial world.","It must be known that this Drunken Rakshasa, Black Widow, and Poison Young Master were known as the three weirdos of the martial world. As for what was weird about them, it was unknown, but all three were alike in that they were not people to be trifled with.","\"This Drunken Rakshasa hiding in a place like a brothel must have a mission, right? Oh right, Cai Xian listened to my advice and locked Cai Bing at home, forbidding him from going out.","Huo Ying's Huo Shui had no opponent. Did we indirectly ruin her mission?\"","[Absolutely. I didn't explain it to Master in detail last time. Their plan against the two was actually a series of interlocking traps. As long as both went, at least one of them would definitely have an accident.","As for who would have the accident, it all depended on fate. Anyway, the goal was to ensure the Cai and Huo families would clash.","In the original timeline, Drunken Rakshasa's mission succeeded, and she was targeted by the two families. Her life was difficult, yet she didn't leave.","Even when Yu Huaijian offered a high price to poach her, she wouldn't go.]","\"Does that mean she still had a mission at that time and had to stay there?\"","[Probably. But later, for some unknown reason, she took the initiative to contact Yu Huaijian, who was running the hidden brothels, and introduced a few young male escorts and girls to him.]","\"Is there something wrong with these people?\"","[Yes, besides people from Great Yan, these people also included people from Nanzhao, Nanyue, Beili, Xiqiang, and Dongyi.]","Yue Fuguang almost laughed out loud. \"He's running this like the United Nations. With such a mixed composition, does he himself know?\"","Brothers Yu Chongshan and Yu Chongyan both frowned. As officials, they naturally did not lack political sensitivity.","They couldn't help but feel that these people were not simple, and the master behind Drunken Rakshasa was even less simple.","Originally, Cai Xian and Huo Ying guessed that the person behind this should be a certain faction of Great Yan causing trouble behind the scenes.","Now it seemed that it was really hard to say whether that person was from Great Yan.","Was he only targeting Great Yan or all six countries?","Yu Chongshan was startled by his own guess. Even their Emperor wouldn't dare to simultaneously play tricks and set stumbling blocks for the high-level officials of the other five countries, attacking on multiple fronts.","At most, they would send out spies to gather information and take the opportunity to sow discord, but they would not purposefully target certain factions.","[At first, he definitely didn't know. Those people all had proper household registrations of Great Yan. However, these people all belonged to the lowly class, so it wasn't hard to get those registrations.","Later, he discovered the difference in these people, and Drunken Rakshasa took the opportunity to pull him into their group, and he helped them do a lot of things.","When the city of Great Yan was breached, Yu Huaijian led a portion of these people into the Yu estate, killing anyone they saw and robbing any valuables they found.","In the end, only Yu Jinan's wife and two children, a son and a daughter, escaped from the Yu family.]","Yu Chongshan paused. His third son, Jinan, only got married last year, and his third daughter-in-law hadn't gotten pregnant yet. Calculating the time, his future grandson and granddaughter would be at most seven or eight years old when Great Yan was destroyed.","Orphans and widows in troubled times... Yu Chongyan closed his eyes. Actually, his family's situation wouldn't be much better than his eldest brother's!"]},{"number":206,"title":"Chapter 206: Yu Chongyan Did Not Die a Natural Death Either","paragraphs":["Yu Jinan also thought of this, and his feelings toward his wife and children who had managed to escape went from initial joy to his current worry.","Yue Fuguang thought for a moment and raised her own doubts, \"That's not right. According to your previous description of Drunken Rakshasa, the person behind her must have a grand scheme.","Pulling someone like Yu Huaijian into their group shouldn't be just for a small Yu family, right?\"","[Indeed, destroying the Yu family and snatching their wealth was merely the personal action of Yu Huaijian and a few of his close friends.","Drunken Rakshasa and the organization behind her wouldn't even bat an eye at the Yu family's meager assets.]","\"So in the end, it was an inside job! This Yu Huaijian seems to harbor an excessively deep hatred for the Yu family. The grudge of destroying the entire family—could it just be because he wasn't allowed to officially acknowledge his ancestors and return to the clan?\"","[No. A year later, Yu Boyuan will find a way to bring the mother and son into the Yu residence, and Yu Huaijian's name will also be added to the Yu family genealogy.","However, the rules of the Yu residence are strict. The mother and son didn't live the life they imagined; instead, they were bound by rules everywhere.","Although Yu Boyuan still doted on this son and even had the legal wife, Madam Cheng, find him a good match, Yu Boyuan later took in new concubines.","He stopped visiting Concubine Huang's courtyard as often. Back in the brothel, this Concubine Huang had played the role of a 'talented woman', usually favoring the romantic sentiments of gifted scholars and beautiful ladies.","Having been redeemed and freed from her suffering by Yu Boyuan, she naturally invested more of her feelings in him. Now, seeing him smile at the newcomers, her sentimental, artsy side emerged, weeping over the passing of spring and mourning the autumn.","Watching Yu Boyuan take in one new concubine after another, she was heartbroken over her fading beauty and his waning love. Within two years, she died of depression.","Yu Huaijian's wife also died in childbirth that same year, and he blamed the Yu family for the deaths of both his birth mother and his wife.]","\"This... did the Yu family really have a hand in it?\"","[No, Madam Huang's health was inherently weak, and being neglected by Yu Boyuan led to her depression.","His wife's difficult labor was also due to physical reasons; no one was scheming behind the scenes.","Yu Huaijian was eighteen that year, and his wife had just turned fifteen when she gave birth. Being so young, her body was already frail, and she nourished the baby in her womb to be too large. Was it any wonder it ended in the tragic loss of two lives?","Why is it said that childbirth for mortal women is like walking through the gates of hell? Besides poor medical technology offering no guarantees, it's mostly because the women giving birth are too young.","Their own bodies haven't even fully developed before they are nurturing a new life. How could it not be like walking through the gates of hell!]","\"Help me make a note of this. When I have time, I must talk to the Empress Dowager and the Empress. Even if it can't be written into the laws of Dayan, we should have the higher-ups push back the age of marriage for men and women.","What those above favor, those below will follow even more. I imagine the common folk might slowly be influenced by the upper class, forming a customary trend.\"","[Alright, Little Zhu will definitely remember to remind Master. This Yu Boyuan is an old scoundrel. His son lost his mother and wife in succession, but apart from shoving a few bed-attendants his way, he didn't care about anything else.","Instead, he holed up in the rooms of his young and beautiful concubines, living a life of debauchery. Seeing this, Yu Huaijian naturally harbored resentment again.","His birth mother's bones were not yet cold, but his father was taking in concubine after concubine, while his other brothers' children were born safely one by one. His mind gradually became unbalanced.","His resentment was naturally noticed by those 'friends' in the shady brothels, which ultimately led to the tragedy of the Yu family's second branch when Dayan City fell.]","\"He's so old and yet taking concubine after concubine. Isn't he afraid of ruining his health and dying early? Doesn't my Second Grandfather do anything about it?\"","[Your Second Grandfather is already lying in the ancestral tomb. If he wants to do anything about it, he can only visit him in his dreams at night!]","Listening to the two of them, Yu Boyuan's face flushed red all the way to the base of his neck. At the thought of his father coming to find him as a ghost, his face instantly turned from red to pale white!","\"So that's how it is. He let it go to his head the moment he became the master of the house!\"","Yue Fuguang glanced at Yu Boyuan again, the disgust in her eyes practically overflowing.","[Master, your gaze is too obvious. Don't let the Yu family notice. After all, officially, this Yu Boyuan is still your elder.]","Yu Chongshan and Yu Chongyan: What kind of elder is this bastard! Since their granddaughter/grandniece doesn't like him, they really ought to think of a good excuse to give this bastard a beating!","Thus, when everyone headed to the study to discuss matters after the meal, a trembling Yu Boyuan followed behind his brothers, wondering how he was going to explain himself to his uncle and father in a moment.","Suddenly, a loud shout interrupted his thoughts. He heard his father say, \"Zhongqing, Jinan, tie your eldest brother up for me.\"","Tie him up? Now? At his uncle's house, in front of everyone!","He was, at the very least, the eldest son of the second branch. Was his father so angry that he wouldn't leave him any face at all?","Looking at the rope the two brothers brought over, Yu Qinchun suddenly found it very familiar. Wasn't... wasn't this the very rope his father had used to tie him up before beating him, after finding out what he had done to Fuguang?","The mottled bloodstains on it must still be his own!","However, only the brother who had acted on their father's behalf, their father who supervised, and the younger brother who watched the spectacle knew about him being beaten.","Not even his mother, Old Madam Yu, was aware that her third son had been taught a lesson by his old man.","At this moment, Yu Qinchun looked at the surrounding crowd, especially the younger generation. He suddenly felt that although his father and brother had been a bit ruthless when they double-teamed him back then, they still loved him. At least they had saved him some face!","Right now, Yu Boyuan really wanted to bury his face in his hands. Before doing so, he made one last desperate struggle. Knowing full well what the answer would be, he asked, \"Father, it seems your son hasn't done anything wrong tonight. Why do you want to beat me? My Huaiming and Huaixian are both watching. I beg you, Father, please leave me some dignity.\"","Yu Chongyan sneered, \"Dignity? Do you even need such a thing? As for the reason, I saw you step out the door with your left foot first just now. It rubbed me the wrong way, so I felt like beating my son!\"","His reasoning was as dominant as it was completely unreasonable. The younger generation, unaware of the underlying context, looked utterly baffled. However, those who could hear the inner voices knew that their father or Uncle Yuan wouldn't be able to escape this thrashing!","The system even chimed in, [He deserves it! Master, you must not plead for him!]","\"Don't worry. For the sake of our family ties, the fact that I'm not doing it myself is already giving him enough face.\"","Soon, Yu Boyuan's ghostly wails and wolfish howls echoed from outside. To save him some embarrassment, none of the younger generation went out to watch, except for Yue Fuguang.","[Master, stand a bit further back. Don't let the blood splatter on you!]","Yue Fuguang, knowing it was always wise to heed good advice, obediently stepped back two paces.","Seeing Yue Fuguang there, Yu Chongyan beat his son with even more vigor.","\"Little Zhu, look at Second Grandpa. He seems quite robust right now. He doesn't even need to catch his breath while beating his son. How could he pass away in less than two years?\"","Yu Chongshan glanced at his younger brother. Chongyan was three years his junior; logically, he shouldn't have passed away so early.","[Master, Yu Chongyan didn't die a natural death. To be precise, he was afflicted with a chronic poison. The poisoning dragged on for over a year before it finally killed him.","The physical symptoms were general weakness and frequent illnesses. Because of this, right up until his death, the Yu family, including your grandfather, all believed he had died of an illness.","Does Master want to know who was behind it?]","Yue Fuguang rolled her eyes. Wasn't that a stupid question? There was clearly some juicy gossip to be had; how could she refuse a treat that was offered right to her lips?","Yu Chongyan's life had to be saved. With him holding down the fort, the Second Branch would become an asset to her rather than a hindrance."]},{"number":207,"title":"Chapter 207: He will never go down the same old path again in this lifetime","paragraphs":["Although she wouldn't engage in nepotism, in this patriarchal society, as long as she could keep her clansmen in line, they would be one of the best cards in her hand.","The male family members were the sharpest knives, and the sisters were her great helpers.","[The ones who took action were Concubine Huang's brother and eldest nephew. In fact, the matter was quite simple. Yu Chongyan initially opposed Yu Huaijian and his mother entering the mansion.","Yu Boyuan's wife was the daughter of his good friend, whom he had gone to great lengths to ask for in marriage for his son.","He never expected that Yu Boyuan was actually raising a son on the outside, and this son was the same age as his second grandson, Yu Huaixian! Naturally, he would not agree.","Later, when the mother and son finally managed to enter the mansion, he refused to let Concubine Huang's niece marry Yu Huaijian. This naturally caused the Yu family to hold a grudge against him.","Speaking of the Huang family, they fled their home because of a snow disaster. The whole family escaped and only arrived in the capital city of Shangjing this spring, where they unexpectedly ran into Concubine Huang.","So the whole family just clung to them like leeches to suck their blood!]","\"Are the Huang family members really that bold? My second grandfather is an official, after all. How could a commoner dare to do such a thing, and how did he manage to pull it off?\"","Only after coming here did she see with her own eyes and hear with her own ears how much the common people feared officials. They would hide far away just seeing an official's sedan chair. Those who dared to kill an official must be desperadoes.","[The Huang family had taken more than one or two lives on their escape route. Their human ferocity had been stimulated, completing their transformation from commoners to a violent mob along the way.","Compared to those desperadoes, they merely had the status of law-abiding citizens and the appearance of honest and simple farmers.","Through Concubine Huang's connections, Eldest Son Huang entered the Yu mansion to serve as a follower for his cousin Yu Huaijian. Moving around the outer courtyard, he seized an opportunity when Yu Chongyan was sick to poison his medicine pot. He then repeated the same trick a few more times, and that was how he sent the old man to his grave!]","Hearing the news of his own death, Yu Chongyan was surprisingly calm. He knew very well in his heart that since he knew who had harmed him, he just needed to find them and kill them!","He definitely wouldn't repeat the same mistakes in this life!","In the end, the reunion dinner of the two branches of the Yu family concluded happily, with everyone else beaming with smiles, while only Yu Boyuan was carried out the door.","Oh, right, Yue Fuguang also gained her thirtieth subordinate—Yu Huaixian.","Yu Huaixian was Yu Boyuan's second son. It seemed Yu Chongyan was going to put great effort into cultivating his eldest and second grandsons.","In the future, he would directly let his eldest grandson, Yu Huaiming, bypass his father to take charge of the family business of the Yu family's second branch.","Otherwise, it would be hard to explain to his other two sons.","Yu Zhongqing and Yu Jinan naturally saw through their father's plan and felt that it wouldn't be unacceptable for their nephew to take charge of the family in the future.","As for splitting the family right now? They had never even entertained such a thought.","The reason their eldest uncle's family was willing to lend them a helping hand was out of respect for their father. If they separated from the family, their relationship with their eldest uncle's family would become even more distant.","Seeing that the Yu family was about to prosper, they couldn't possibly do something so foolish.","[Host, in the original historical timeline, this Huang family also colluded with the Zhou family. That daughter of the Huang family who didn't marry Yu Huaijian later married Second Son Zhou.]","\"Don't worry, the Zhou family is finished, and the Huang family won't live past this month. The things they did later will never happen again.\"","The next day, Yue Fuguang took her top enforcer, Yu Huaixian, to attend the morning court session. Why call him her top enforcer?","Because among her many new subordinates, aside from Yu Mochun, the one with the highest favorability was Yu Huaixian, followed by Shen Chunying, Shen Dongxue, and a few others.","This guy Yu Huaixian's favorability score skyrocketed overnight from the original seventy to eighty, second only to the sisters Yu Ningxuan and Yu Ningxin.","[Master, you at least have a few kittens under your command now. Do you want Little Zhu to give you that book on training intelligence agents and special forces?]","\"Wait a bit. We'll talk about it after these people are completely loyal!\"","The hands of the sisters Shen Chunying and Shen Dongxue visibly trembled as they helped Yue Fuguang into the carriage.","Yue Fuguang nodded in satisfaction. The two of them were actually able to resist looking up at her and were trying their best to hide their panic, which was excellent!","As for the Shen sisters, the older sister Chunying was steady and meticulous, while the younger sister Dongxue was lively and cheerful. Although the younger sister was adopted by their parents, the bond between the sisters was truly very good.","Among the people she had selected from the guest courtyard, currently only half had reached the threshold to hear her inner thoughts. Among them, the Shen sisters, Liu Wei, Xu Xiaoman, and Zhang Fang had the highest favorability.","This was also the first time these few people heard her inner voice. Shen Wei and Xu Xiaoman, who were a few steps behind, only paused for a moment before quickly catching up.","As for Zhang Fang, who was seeing them off at the door, his hand rested on the Cloud-Cleaving Sword at his waist. He only forcefully held back from drawing it when he heard the familiar 'Wait a bit'.","So this was the miraculous aspect of their Junior Preceptor that Senior Mr. Yu had hinted at?","She clearly hadn't opened her mouth, yet she could speak. What kind of divine martial art was this? Could it be the long-lost art of ventriloquism?","And where was that little fellow who called her Master hiding?","Zhang Fang, who had the highest martial arts skills, searched for a long time but still couldn't find the owner of that voice.","[Alright then. Once they completely acknowledge you as their Master, I'll bestow some medicine upon them. The martial arts of these mortals are just too poor. Having such weak people protect you makes Little Zhu uneasy.]","\"With Little Zhu around, this Immortal Lord's safety is guaranteed. The people in my hands are merely to put the Emperor and the others at ease.","As you said, the power of mortals is indeed a bit lacking, but if there are good seedlings in the future, perhaps I can cultivate one or two for my own use.\"","Mortals? Immortal Lord? What did that mean?","Shen Chunying, Liu Wei, and the others looked at each other in dismay. Why did the Junior Preceptor call herself an Immortal Lord? And that Little Zhu not only looked down on them but also called them mortals!","The few of them carefully checked their surroundings a few more times and found nothing unusual... Actually, they did notice something. Out of their team of twelve, only eight of them had strange expressions on their faces.","Wang Qingxiao and three others acted as if they hadn't heard anything, their expressions natural. Seeing the expressions of the other eight constantly changing, they even revealed looks of confusion.","With faces full of questions, they were just short of asking out loud: What's wrong with you guys? Your faces look so terrible, are you sick?","Along the way, the eight of them got an earful of that entity calling itself Little Zhu scolding everyone from the Emperor to the civil and military officials in front of the Junior Preceptor.","The reason was that transporting some kind of seeds for them had consumed a lot of its 'divine power'!","All of them had decent martial arts skills, and even through the carriage walls, they could hear that only the Junior Preceptor's heartbeat was inside. Where on earth was that Little Zhu hiding?","It dared to brazenly insult the Emperor and the officials. It might dare to curse, but they didn't dare to listen!","The few of them felt like they were waiting for death, but they just didn't associate it with inner voices or deities. They only thought they had encountered a supreme martial arts expert.","After all, they had seen people calling themselves Immortal Lords in the martial arts world before. Which of those charlatans tricking people into drinking talisman water didn't claim to be the reincarnation of a deity, coming to the mortal realm to impart teachings?","The few who felt like they were waiting for death didn't yet know that this was just the beginning. This wasn't even the thing that would shatter their worldview the most.","With anxious hearts, the few of them, who had already started thinking about their last words, watched as the Junior Preceptor's carriage drove straight into the imperial palace."]},{"number":208,"title":"Chapter 208: It is, of course, a scandal involving the royal family.","paragraphs":["It took less than half an hour for her to come out, and she was not the only one.","Following the Emperor and the Crown Prince at the front were over twenty high-ranking officials.","Shen Dongxue whispered, \"Sister, this is my first time seeing the Emperor and so many lords!\"","Shen Chunying thought to herself: Who isn't!","Thinking this, she did not forget to instruct her younger sister, \"Keep your voice down. Don't embarrass the Lord Junior Preceptor.\"","The Lord Junior Preceptor had promoted several of them, all women, to official positions. This had offended the eyes of quite a few people. To prove themselves, they could only do better than the men.","What followed was even more shocking. With the Emperor's carriage leading the way, the Lord Junior Preceptor's carriage followed closely behind, traveling side by side with the Crown Prince's.","That was not all. Along the way, that Little Zhu called out the Emperor and the lords one by one...","Seeing the expressions on some of the lords' faces, which looked as if they had eaten shit, and the increasingly obvious smile on the Crown Prince's face, one would know that they had all heard it. Yet, no one spoke up to stop it, and they even deliberately pretended not to hear anything.","Upon hearing that the Crown Prince would die an early death, they could not help but quickly glance at His Highness's expression.","Uh... why was he still smiling and talking to the Lord Junior Preceptor? The smile on his face did not look like a fake smile either!","The Lord Junior Preceptor's status in the royal court seemed to be even more awesome than they had known!","Even Wang Qingxiao and the other few who could not hear the inner voices looked at the Lord Junior Preceptor, who was following closely behind the imperial procession, riding neck and neck with the Crown Prince's carriage, talking and laughing.","They were filled with profound respect. As people who admired the strong, they instantly developed a sense of reverence for the nine-year-old Yue Fuguang.","Just as their favorability broke through the sixty mark, an abrupt voice suddenly echoed in their ears, [Master, Gao Ming was secretly executed by the Emperor.]","Wang Qingxiao and the other three were almost scared out of their wits by this sentence. Gao Ming's name had been causing a massive uproar lately, known by everyone and anyone.","Executed by the Emperor, and secretly at that—was this something they were allowed to hear?","The few of them were so frightened that they wanted to drop to their knees, but they were stopped in time by the Shen sisters.","Although they still did not know what was going on, since everyone from the Emperor to the Crown Prince and the lords were pretending not to hear,","they must also 'not hear' it!","Shen Chunying's beautiful eyes darted around. She felt that this matter was not simple. From Elder Lord Yu's hint, it could be seen that they had known about this early on, but no one had spoken of it!","Among all this... she quickly glanced at the leading carriage. Did the Lord Junior Preceptor know about this?","\"Gao Ming? Whether it's the crimes he committed or the public uproar he caused, he deserves to die. It's normal for the Emperor to behead him, but why execute him secretly?\"","Shen Chunying sighed inwardly; it seemed the Lord Junior Preceptor did not know.","Shen Dongxue grabbed her sister's hand. The two sisters exchanged a glance, both understanding the meaning in each other's eyes.","Shen Dongxue gently drew a stroke on her sister's palm, then silently pointed at herself.","Shen Chunying shook her head firmly and pushed her back a little.","[Of course, it involves a royal scandal.]","Hearing the words 'royal scandal', not only the twelve guards following Yue Fuguang, but even the Crown Prince and the lords behind them closed their eyes!","Here it comes again. They shouldn't have tagged along to join the fun!","Although they thought they shouldn't have come to join the fun, their ears perked up very honestly.","With that eagerness, if they weren't sitting in their carriages, they would have loved to scoot closer to the Lord Junior Preceptor.","As for Emperor Mingxi, whose face had already turned dark, he quickly consoled himself. His only comfort was that this was not the royal court, and there were only about twenty important ministers following behind him.","They naturally wouldn't spread royal 'rumors'!","System: It had really given the Emperor a lot of face by not exposing this matter in the royal court! Tsundere JPG.","\"A juicy piece of gossip? Let's hear it.\"","Yue Fuguang had just taken out some sunflower seeds when she saw her cousin Yu Huaixian slipping up to the front of her carriage. His face was pale, looking as if he wanted to say something.","But the words were stuck in his mouth, and he couldn't make a sound. Seeing that he couldn't speak, he began to look warily at the Emperor, the Crown Prince, and their guards.","As long as these people made a move, he would immediately take his younger cousin and flee for their lives!","Yu Huaixian had only partaken in listening to gossip at his granduncle's house a few times before. This was his first time consuming such a life-threatening 'poisonous gossip'!","Even if his cousin's status was special, it was hard to guarantee that the Emperor wouldn't fly into a rage out of humiliation!","Emperor Mingxi: Are you underestimating me? Am I the kind of emperor who lacks a view of the big picture?","Even if he wanted to make a move, today would only become his, Xie Fei's, death anniversary, and his Crown Prince would ascend the throne right on the spot!","Besides, regarding this gossip, he glanced at some of the people behind him—letting them hear it wouldn't be a bad idea. There is no harm without comparison, after all!","[This is also related to the death of Emperor Mingxi's father. Master, do you still remember Qu Zheng, the schoolmate who was killed by Gao Ming?]","\"Of course I remember. Didn't you say before that he was evading an assassination before Gao Ming killed him? He was just a scholar, why would anyone want to harm him?\"","[This Qu Zheng's real name was Zheng Qu. He was originally from the Zheng family of Yuzhou, and his father was the illegitimate younger brother of the Zheng family head.]","\"The Zheng family with over five hundred years of heritage? Then how could he bear to change his first and last name? Taking his mother's surname?\"","Usually, the descendants of prominent aristocratic families would only have children who changed their surnames if the mother's family was powerful and lacked an heir, which was also done to inherit the mother's family wealth and connections.","But since she married a concubine-born son as his legal wife, his mother's family couldn't possibly be more powerful than the Zheng family.","[Not necessarily. Qu Zheng's biological mother, surnamed Wu, came from a humble background. However, she had a cousin of her father's generation named Wu Shouxian, who was the second most favored figure before the late emperor—the illustrious Grand Companion Wu.","Because Wu Shouxian was highly favored by the emperor, the entire Wu family rode his coattails to prominence.]","\"Little Zhu, I recall that while these great aristocratic families might commit all sorts of filthy deeds in the dark, they still fiercely guard their reputations in public.","A good name is the very foundation of their standing. Naturally, they wouldn't want to be associated with eunuchs. How could they allow their son to marry a eunuch's niece?\"","[That's because Qu Zheng's biological grandmother, Concubine Wu, also came from the Wu family. With her sweet talk, she persuaded the head of the Zheng family at the time to let his son marry her own niece from her maiden family.","By using the next generation, she managed to keep her family tied to the Zheng family.","Before Concubine Wu was taken into the Zheng family, Wu Shouxian had not yet risen to power.","It was only after he made a name for himself and rose to prominence that the Zheng family realized they had a slight familial connection with the emperor's favorite eunuch.","During those years, the younger generation of the Zheng family happened to be struggling academically, with a lack of promising scholars. After weighing the pros and cons, the master of the Zheng family agreed to the marriage.","After all, he had plenty of concubine-born sons. Sparing one to form a marriage alliance with such a highly favored figure was hardly a loss.]","\"So their mouths said no, but their actions honestly facilitated the marriage alliance. Hypocrites!\"","[Exactly! It may have looked like Concubine Wu begged for the arrangement, but the old master never truly intended to oppose it. Otherwise, he wouldn't have later used Wu Shouxian's connections to send Concubine Wu's daughter—Qu Zheng's aunt—into the imperial palace.","This aunt, named Zheng Huaying, inherited her mother's looks and was as beautiful as a flower. As soon as she entered the palace, the lecherous emperor bestowed upon her the title of Beauty Hua, and she enjoyed his immense favor for quite some time.","One day, the old emperor took some aphrodisiacs and went too far, suffering a sudden stroke during his escapades. He died within a few days. Because his death was so sudden, it left Prince Rong with no time to move the treasures out of the vault.","Otherwise, with that kind of wealth backing him, Emperor Mingxi would have had a much harder time trying to get rid of his younger brother.]"]},{"number":209,"title":"Chapter 209: Is This a Vine with One Melon After Another","paragraphs":["Emperor Mingxi nodded to himself. Wasn't that the truth? If his old man hadn't died early, his succession wouldn't have been so smooth.","Therefore, he had been quite lenient when dealing with Beauty Hua. He only had her buried with the late emperor in the imperial mausoleum and did not implicate her maiden family.","Even regarding the eunuchs and maids responsible for the late emperor's bedchamber affairs, he only executed the chief culprit, Wu Shouxian.","\"Actually, the emperor's death can't be entirely blamed on Beauty Hua, but since he died in her bed, she and the Zheng family shouldn't have been able to get off easily, right?\"","[Exactly. The old emperor didn't know how to restrain himself, and even dragged a few people down to the grave with him as scapegoats on his way out!]","The monarch and officials of Great Yan: Lord Artifact, is that how the term scapegoats is used? If the late emperor knew, wouldn't he crawl out of the imperial mausoleum to speak up for himself!","Some people's eyes flickered. They had long heard rumors about the cause of the late emperor's death. Now that it was confirmed today, the historian Ma Yuanqian's eyes, in particular, lit up by two degrees.","He showed absolutely no panic at hearing a royal scandal. If Yue Fuguang saw his current expression, she would definitely find it very familiar, as it gave off the exact same vibe as a paparazzi digging up a massive celebrity scoop.","Of course, Lord Ma's work was far more respectable. Anyone who dared to record true history, especially royal scandals like this, was an admirable badass!","Looking again at Yue Fuguang's escort guards, every single one of them had a wooden expression, giving off the aura of the living waiting for death.","They couldn't help but look up at the azure sky. This might just be the last time they ever saw the sun in their lives!","Naturally, Yue Fuguang had no idea her escort guards were all waiting to die. She continued talking to the system, \"Isn't the Zheng family still doing fine even now? Although they have declined a bit, I haven't heard of the royal family punishing them. If I remember correctly, doesn't Lord Zheng Ziling come from a branch of the Zheng family?\"","Zheng Ziling's eyelids twitched. He and the Yuzhou Zheng family were already past five generations of separation; they couldn't be considered the same family anymore.","[Yes, but the two families don't seem to interact much. After Emperor Mingxi ascended the throne, he only dealt with Wu Shouxian and a few other main culprits. He merely reprimanded the Zheng family. However, the old family head at the time was afraid of subsequent royal retaliation, so he expelled Qu Zheng's branch from the clan and drove them out of the Zheng family lands.","The reason Qu Zheng changed his name and surname was that within two years, first his father, and then his two older brothers and one older sister successively died, either from illness or in accidents.","Qu Zheng's mother, Lady Wu, seemed to know something. After finishing her second son's funeral, she took Qu Zheng and left Yuzhou overnight, traveling all the way to Yizhou.","Zheng Qu also changed his name to Qu Zheng. The mother and son didn't enjoy many years of peace before his mother contracted an illness and passed away.","Qu Zheng moved again, and a few years later, he encountered that assassination attempt.","Qu Zheng died. Now, Emperor Mingxi has secretly executed Gao Ming because Gao Ming knew the cause of the late emperor's death. But what the emperor doesn't know is that Gao Ming knew another secret he hadn't told.]","Emperor Mingxi: Did I kill him too early again?","The crowd was also speechless upon hearing this. Their Majesty's hands were truly too fast. Prince Rong had died too quickly, making them miss out on knowing about the Great Yan treasure and the late emperor's treasury.","Now that they encountered Gao Ming, they already had the man in their grasp. Couldn't he have waited? Why was he in such a rush to kill him?","His Majesty could keep that Chonghua and Zhou Yunxin alive, but he didn't let Gao Ming live for even a single extra day!","\"What secret? Is this a case of one melon tied to another on the same vine?\"","[Master, take a guess. Who do you think hunted down Qu Zheng, or rather, at whose hands did his entire family die?]","This actually stumped Yue Fuguang. Although Qu Zheng was the last to die, the first to pass away was his old man, so this grudge must have started from the previous generation.","However, the main branch of the Zheng family seemed fine. This was targeting their specific family branch alone.","\"Does it have to do with the palace? Didn't Wu Shouxian and Beauty Hua both get dragged down to the grave with the old emperor? It couldn't be His Majesty who did the dirty work, right?\"","Emperor Mingxi: He was perfectly fine enjoying the gossip about his own father, when bam! A massive pot of blame flew out of nowhere and smashed right onto his crown!","Emperor Mingxi was utterly speechless. When would these two ancestors ever change their habit of constantly pinning the blame on him!","The officials following closely behind hid in their carriages, their mouths twitching uncontrollably. They had to try their hardest to hold back from laughing out loud.","Yu Huaixian was guarding his female cousin's carriage closely. Upon hearing this, his body swayed, and he nearly tumbled off his horse!","He couldn't help but feel like his head was wobbling on his neck, ready to run away from home at any moment.","Looking back at the carriages of his granduncle and two uncles, how were they acting like nothing was wrong! Were the elders really this thick-nerved?","[Master, this matter is indeed inextricably linked to the palace, but this time it really wasn't the emperor's doing. He is still completely in the dark!]","Emperor Mingxi: Hehe? Not hehe! Hearing the first half, before he could even be happy, he was hammered into a pit by the second half.","Emperor Mingxi simply gave up. He was lying flat; whatever happens, happens!","[The person who made a move against Qu Zheng's family is named Wu Chengye. This person is Wu Shouxian's son. Not the kind of godson you can grab by the handful in the palace, but his actual biological son. Wu Shouxian was castrated and entered the palace at sixteen. At that time, his lover was already pregnant with Wu Chengye.","Before Gao Ming killed Qu Zheng, the jade pendant he took from him originally belonged to Wu Shouxian. It was accidentally obtained by Beauty Hua, who secretly sent it out of the palace.","This was also a piece of blackmail material she left for her family. She didn't expect the old emperor to die of a sudden stroke during intercourse in his own palace, resulting in Wu Shouxian and herself following closely behind as burial sacrifices.","The jade pendant that was originally kept for blackmail now became a death warrant for the entire family.]","\"What is that jade pendant?\"","[The jade pendant is a keepsake and also a token of authority. Once, Beauty Hua stumbled upon Wu Shouxian's secret and stole the jade pendant.","If the late emperor hadn't died so suddenly, Wu Shouxian wouldn't have lacked the time to make a move against Beauty Hua. Because of this matter, Beauty Hua wouldn't have lived long anyway.","It was also because Emperor Mingxi acted fast. Wu Shouxian only had time to notify his son before he was arrested by Emperor Mingxi, who killed him without even letting him survive the night.]","Yue Fuguang sighed in admiration, \"I would like to call the emperor Great Yan's number one quick shoot... quick executioner!\"","Emperor Mingxi: He couldn't shake the feeling that this wasn't a compliment, but he couldn't even voice his proof! Aggrieved.JPG","[Master, do you still remember the time Cai Bing and Huo Shui were schemed against?]","Cai Xian and Huo Ying: We remember, we remember! What's going on, it's connected to this too?","\"Little Zhu, is the mastermind behind the scenes about to surface?\"","The system immediately fired off a flattering remark, [Master has definitely guessed it. The person who plotted this was Wu Chengye. He essentially inherited Wu Shouxian's mantle after his death. It can be considered a son inheriting his father's business. This Wu father and son duo are in the same gang as Drunken Rakshasa. Their organization is even more mysterious than Youtan.]","\"So this Wu father and son are just minor pawns as well?\"","[Correct. The jade pendant in Qu Zheng's hands was their proof of identity. With it, one could even mobilize a hidden hundred-man squad in the capital city of Shangjing.","After Qu Zheng died, Wu Chengye traced it to Gao Ming. By this time, Gao Ming had already passed the imperial examination as a Jinshi and become a capital official, so Wu Chengye changed his plan from silencing him with death to roping him in.","If it weren't for Gao Ming's murder of his wife being exposed, he would have joined them this year, becoming yet another protective umbrella for Wu Chengye.]","Emperor Mingxi recalled the items Ping Yi had submitted after searching that residence; there did indeed seem to be a uniquely shaped jade pendant among them."]},{"number":210,"title":"Chapter 210: Wu Shouxian Also Has a Son","paragraphs":["\"Did the late Emperor not know that the number two eunuch by his side had another identity?\"","[That old fool definitely didn't know! Emperor Mingxi takes after his father. When he killed Wu Shouxian back then, he only confiscated lands, houses, and shops. He didn't find much liquid wealth, yet he never even suspected where the rest of the stuff went.]","Emperor Mingxi: Calling me out again! Calling me out again! How could I not suspect anything? At the time, I just thought it was embezzled by the subordinates who carried out the confiscation!","He had just ascended the throne and his footing wasn't steady yet, so he didn't pursue the matter. How was he supposed to know there was more to it?","Furthermore, as a son, he took after his mother, not that father of his!","The Crown Prince lowered his head to drink tea. As for Lord Divine Artifact calling his imperial grandfather an old fool or whatever, he heard nothing. Because his father had not been favored, the grandfather and grandson only saw each other a few times a year, so his affection for his imperial grandfather was very weak anyway.","Shen Chunying and the others now wore the same bitter expressions as Yu Huaixian. They constantly felt as though their little lives were drifting uncertainly, liable to vanish at any moment.","The few of them stared intently at the Emperor's carriage ahead, wondering when this person would erupt in fury.","Emperor Mingxi: I don't dare to erupt even a little bit! Besides, I'm actually happy she's scolding my old man. It would just be better if she didn't drag me into it too!","[Most of the wealth Wu Shouxian embezzled was given to his son. Relying on this sum of money, the father and son managed to recruit quite a few people.]","\"And no one knew Wu Shouxian had such a son?\"","[Little Zhu doesn't know about others, but the previous and current emperors definitely didn't know. Otherwise, how could Wu Chengye still be messing around in the capital city?","Later on, nearly ten civil and military officials in the imperial court were directly or indirectly schemed to death by him. The chaos in the court during the later period was the result of manipulation by several factions.","Among them was the shadow of the organization run by Wu Chengye and his people.]","It was unknown how the others felt, but in the very last carriage, Wu Yuanjing was already sweating buckets despite the cold weather.","Seeing that his father's expression had been poor ever since Lord Divine Artifact mentioned the Wu family, and that he was now deathly pale, Wu Yong hurriedly poured him a cup of hot tea. \"Dad, what's wrong? Quickly, drink some tea to calm your nerves.\"","Seeing his old man's somewhat vacant gaze, he couldn't help but lower his voice to gently advise, \"Don't take it to heart, old man. Now that we have the Junior Preceptor, no one will be in danger.","If you're still uneasy, you can offer a few more sticks of incense to those two once we get back.\"","Yue Fuguang and the system still didn't know that they had already begun passively receiving incense offerings.","Hearing the mention of offering incense, Wu Yuanjing's vacant face finally showed a reaction. He tremblingly took the tea his son handed him. \"Right, offer incense, offer a few more sticks of incense!\"","He didn't tell his son that ever since he met Wu Chengye two years ago, the man had frequently interacted with him in private. Before the new year, he had even hinted at wanting to unite their clans.","Uniting clans with that kind of person was tantamount to asking a tiger for its skin. Their family's lineage was thin; who knew when they would be chewed up until not even bones remained.","\"This organization is trying to uproot the Xie family!\"","[Under the influence of various factors, they actually managed to pull it off in the end. Over a hundred years later, they even established a short-lived dynasty, just like the Sima family's Great Wei.","They all gorged themselves on the blood of the previous dynasty to achieve their own success!]","The system thought for a moment and added, [Oh right, Master, that chubby little guy Wu Yong who's always planting vegetables for you will be schemed to death by Wu Chengye in three years.","In the end, all of the Wu family's assets fell into his hands.","I see that this person is quite respectful to you, Master. You can save his life when the time comes!]","Clang!","The teacup slipped from Wu Yuanjing's hands. His hand was scalded, but he didn't even react.","He knew it! Why would Lord Divine Artifact judge his twilight years to be bleak? Even though he only had one son, his son was obedient and filial; there was no way his old age could be miserable!","So the root cause was here: his son was murdered by that evil thief!","Then what about his little grandson?","Hearing his own date of death so abruptly, Wu Yong still felt a sense of unreality. Seeing his father's scalded red hand, he quickly grabbed a handkerchief to wipe it for him.","Looking at his father's face, which was as gloomy as still water, and his clenched jaw, he hurriedly and softly advised, \"Dad, I know you're furious, but don't be angry just yet.","Hasn't this not happened yet? Besides, now that we all know, not to mention our family, even His Majesty won't let that Wu Chengye off.\"","Seeing that his father remained unmoved, he leaned his chubby face close to his father's ear and continued to coax softly, \"Didn't you hear Lord Divine Artifact say that she wants to save your son's life?","This is Lord Divine Artifact's acknowledgment of your son!\"","Hearing his words, Wu Yuanjing performed an immediate face-change on the spot, turning from a stormy downpour to clear skies. He nodded repeatedly, saying in a flurry, \"Right, right, right!\"","He slapped his large hand onto his son's shoulder and suppressed his voice, \"My son is right. With that golden thigh around, no one can... hurt you!\"","Before he could finish speaking, tears began streaming down his face. Wu Yong quickly pulled out a handkerchief to wipe them for him. \"You can't cry. The Junior Preceptor might see you when we get off the carriage later.\"","Wu Yuanjing nodded. His son was right; he couldn't cry. He couldn't let the Junior Preceptor notice anything unusual. Today was a day of great rejoicing for the Great Yan Dynasty. He could only laugh, not cry!","However, at the thought of the white-haired sending off the black-haired, Wu Yuanjing's heart throbbed with spasms of pain.","In the middle of the Si hour, the group arrived at Yue Fuguang's estate once more. After not seeing it for about ten days, a faint touch of green could actually be seen on the mountain from afar.","Even the wind blowing against them wasn't as cold as last time.","In early March, spring returned to the earth and all living things revived. It was also the time for her to fully display her skills.","The crowd followed Yue Fuguang all the way to the granary on the estate.","As soon as the estate manager opened the door, he automatically retreated far away. Over thirty cartloads of items had been delivered inside yesterday evening, all packed in large bags. He had no idea what was stored inside.","At night, when the others urged him to go take a look, the estate manager recalled the words left by that person upon departure, and his newly aroused interest was instantly extinguished.","He firmly shook his head and refused. He wasn't stupid; how could he get his entire family killed just for a little curiosity?","As for secretly skimming a little off the top like before, he felt that his courage had completely vanished after seeing His Majesty and the various officials last time.","Emperor Mingxi was the first to step into the warehouse. Anyone could tell that his footsteps seemed somewhat impatient.","What met his eyes were hundreds of large white bags stacked up in the massive storehouse. It was completely different from the scene he had imagined of things piled haphazardly on the ground; it was far too clean and tidy.","When the others followed him inside, they first saw the same sight. Before they even had time to be surprised, they saw their Emperor pull a beautiful small sword from his waist and gently slice at a bag.","Huh? Emperor Mingxi froze for a moment. It didn't cut open!","Was his strike too light? He added thirty percent more force to his hand before finally tearing a slit in the bag.","After taking a glance at the contents inside, Emperor Mingxi finally had the mind to examine this bag used for holding grain.","It was white and slightly transparent, with obvious warp and weft threads, yet the material at the tear was unrecognizable.","[Look, Master, the Emperor is dumbfounded seeing the bag, isn't he? He's never seen such a sturdy bag before.","Hmph, Little Zhu picked bags that are moisture-proof, insect-proof, sturdy, and durable. They are not something those garbage gunny sacks of Great Yan can compare to.]"]},{"number":211,"title":"Chapter 211: You even need to pick a date just to dig up a few barrels of potatoes","paragraphs":["\"Little Zhu, won't they be suspicious if you use bags that don't exist in this world!\"","[What's there to be afraid of? If the emperor asks, you can just push it onto your maritime merchant friends, Master. They won't be able to find me anyway.] The system's voice was filled with smugness.","Yue Fuguang imagined herself shaking her head and claiming complete ignorance; the thought was quite amusing.","Sure enough, Emperor Mingxi wasn't in a hurry to see the contents of the bags. Well, he had just taken a peek—it was golden inside, which should be corn.","Instead, he asked about the bags. \"Fuguang, I have never seen this kind of bag before, nor can I tell what material it's made of. Have you heard your friend mention it?\"","Yue Fuguang shook her head, playing dumb while knowing perfectly well, and asked in return, \"Your Majesty, aren't all bags the same? Does our Great Yan not have this kind?\"","Lu Qi and Yu Chongshan also leaned in. Lu Qi examined it for a long time and said, \"It's neither hemp nor silk. It feels even sturdier than the clothes I am wearing.\"","Yu Chongshan touched his own soft and breathable clothes, which were made from several bolts of fine cotton cloth his granddaughter had gifted the family during the New Year.","It was said to be woven from the kind of cotton she was going to plant. Because of this cotton cloth, the adults in the family were now even more attentive to that cotton field than Fuguang herself.","Before the Lantern Festival was even over, the family steward had already taken a group of people over to clear the wasteland.","Yu Chongshan touched the bag; it wasn't the kind of cotton cloth he was wearing either. None of the materials these men had ever seen matched the bags in front of them.","Emperor Mingxi instructed Wang Shouchen, who was standing behind him, \"My dear Minister Wang, instruct the farmers of the Court of Agriculture to be careful when opening the bags. Do not ruin them.\"","They could absolutely use these bags to store some delicate seeds. He still remembered Lord Divine Artifact saying that this material was pest-resistant and moisture-proof.","Only after inspecting the bags did the group of people turn their attention back to the grain seeds inside.","They each grabbed a handful, carefully examining the golden corn kernels in their hands under the sunlight streaming through the window.","\"Why do these seed kernels look bigger than the ones we ate last time?\"","\"Elder Minister Wang has good eyes. The ones we roasted and ate last time were tender corn, which is best eaten fresh by roasting or boiling.","These ones in the bag have a high starch content and a high yield, making them the most suitable as a staple grain.\"","Hearing another new word, Wang Shouchen quickly asked out of curiosity, \"What is this 'starch' that the Junior Preceptor mentions?\"","Yue Fuguang paused, realizing she had just slipped up and blurted out a modern term. She braced herself and explained, \"It's a substance contained in corn. The rice and wheat we usually eat also have it.","The higher the content of this substance, the stronger the feeling of fullness in a person's stomach after eating.\"","[Good thing you didn't say that starch is a natural high-molecular carbohydrate synthesized by plants, Master, otherwise these people would ask you what a carbohydrate is again.]","Hearing this, everyone silently memorized the new term 'carbohydrate' in their hearts. Some of the sharper ones even wondered if this was the knowledge of biology, chemistry, and physics that the Little Immortal Lord had mentioned.","After looking at the corn, next was the sweet potato. Yue Fuguang had chosen two varieties for Emperor Mingxi this time. As for herself, she was going to test plant all seven or eight varieties. Mainly because they were all delicious and hard to choose between.","Looking at the list the system gave her, Yue Fuguang said to Emperor Mingxi, \"Your Majesty, my friend selected two varieties this time.\"","She picked up a sweet potato weighing nearly half a pound and said, \"This kind has red skin and white flesh. It also has a high starch content and a high yield, but the texture is a bit dry.\"","Then she picked up another sweet potato that was significantly smaller and said, \"This kind has red skin and yellow flesh. Its yield isn't as high as the white-fleshed one, but it tastes sweeter and has a softer, more glutinous texture.","If used to make sweet potato sugar, the sugar yield is higher.\"","[The sweet potato is a treasure from top to bottom. It can be grown from cuttings, and the vines can be used to feed livestock. If made into sweet potato sugar and glass noodles, the waste material can also be used to feed livestock.]","\"Sweet potato leaves and stems can also be made into a dish, and the waste material you mentioned can serve as rations for people during famine years.\"","Everyone smiled as they listened to her detailed explanation, learning that sweet potatoes could also be made into glass noodles, although they didn't know what that was.","But since Lord Divine Artifact mentioned it alongside sugar-making, it must be something good.","They gazed at Yue Fuguang earnestly. The Little Immortal Lord would surely tell them, right?","After the sweet potatoes, they looked at the potatoes. Upon seeing the potatoes, Wang Shouchen suddenly said, \"Junior Preceptor, is it time to harvest the potatoes in the greenhouse? I noticed the leaves have turned a bit yellow.\"","Uh... Hearing Elder Minister Wang's question, Yue Fuguang finally remembered that she still had several large vats of potatoes planted in her glasshouse!","Ever since he found out that the vats contained high-yield potatoes, Yue Fuguang hadn't needed to worry about them at all. Elder Minister Wang had been serving those vats of potatoes as if they were the emperor.","Speaking of which, she hadn't been to the greenhouse for nearly a month and had almost forgotten about it.","Concealing her inner embarrassment, Yue Fuguang put on a confident, all-knowing expression and said, \"It is indeed time to harvest them.\"","Wang Shouchen glanced at his emperor and probed, \"Then shall I have the Imperial Astronomy Bureau choose an auspicious day?\"","What did that mean? Choosing an auspicious day just to dig up a few vats of potatoes? Choosing a day was one thing, but getting the Imperial Astronomy Bureau involved!","Wasn't that making a mountain out of a molehill?","What was the Imperial Astronomy Bureau for? They were only consulted for picking dates for sacrifices, the emperor's birthday, and the crown prince's wedding.","Getting the Imperial Astronomy Bureau to dig up potatoes—wasn't he afraid the emperor would take offense and the imperial censors would impeach him?","Yue Fuguang openly glanced at Emperor Mingxi, then shot a look at Feng Tang, who wasn't far away. Unexpectedly, both of them were nodding in agreement.","Seeing Yue Fuguang's expression, everyone knew what she was thinking. To the Little Immortal Lord, it might just be digging up a few potatoes, but to their Great Yan, it held extraordinary significance.","Emperor Mingxi swept his gaze over everyone present. They were all his trusted pillars of the state, so there was nothing to hide. In fact, if it weren't for saving face, he would have wanted to play the pity card with Yue Fuguang.","\"Fuguang, although the snow disaster from last winter has passed, there are still many rumors circulating among the people. The common folk are ignorant, and many live in fear because they believe these rumors.\"","Yue Fuguang thought: Isn't the ignorance of the common folk the result of your generation after generation of obscurantist policies? And as for the rumors, aren't they just saying that the snow disaster is a punishment sent by heaven because the emperor lacks virtue?","God in Heaven: Sleeping, do not disturb!","Seeing Yue Fuguang's calm expression and that Lord Divine Artifact didn't jump out to scold him, Emperor Mingxi let go of his anxiety a little and continued, \"Therefore, we need a tremendously good piece of news to boost the morale of the common folk.\"","As long as they could see hope and the promise of better days ahead, the populace wouldn't fall into chaos. Once potatoes with a yield of thousands of pounds per acre were revealed, those with ulterior motives could forget about slandering him anymore.","The Crown Prince also chimed in, \"Sweet potatoes and corn won't be ready to harvest until autumn, so the living potatoes growing in the pots are the best choice.","When the seeds currently in the warehouse are harvested, Great Yan will hold a grand sacrificial ceremony to inform Heaven and Earth.\"","Yue Fuguang nodded. \"Your Majesty and all the lords can arrange it as you see fit.\" It didn't matter to her; she wasn't the one doing the work. She would just act as a mascot when the time came.","Speaking of which, lately, she had been feeling a bit strange, from her soul down to her physical body. When she asked the system, it couldn't figure it out either, and there had been no response after contacting the main system.","Therefore, she was anxious to complete this natural disaster quest, which was worth one hundred and eighty thousand points."]},{"number":212,"title":"Chapter 212: I Want to Build Houses and Roads","paragraphs":["Thinking carefully about Emperor Mingxi's words, she felt that boosting the morale of the common people was a good point. As long as there was no chaos, fewer people would die.","Of course, she wasn't someone who just made empty promises. \"Your Majesty, my lords, please come this way.\"","Yue Fuguang led the crowd to another warehouse, which contained about a hundred bags. She opened one and said, \"This warehouse stores the seeds of grain crops like sorghum, soybeans, rice, and wheat.\"","\"Are... are these really all...\" Emperor Mingxi and the officials were a bit dizzy from this massive, unexpected windfall that had suddenly dropped into their laps.","\"They are all seeds. I wouldn't dare say how excellent they are, but their yield will definitely be higher than what the people of Great Yan are currently growing.\"","The seeds sold in the System Shop were all original strains, so there was no fear of them failing to acclimatize. Out of modesty and caution, she spoke very conservatively.","Everyone's mouths fell open into wide O shapes. It was no wonder they were so surprised. They truly hadn't dared to imagine that, besides the three high-yield crops they had been dreaming of day and night, they would unexpectedly stumble upon such a good thing today!","This was especially true for Emperor Mingxi. He hadn't even started to play the pity card yet, and the Little Immortal Lord had already bestowed so many blessings upon Great Yan!","With a voice that was both authoritative and trembling, Emperor Mingxi called out, \"Crown Prince!\"","The excited crowd, including the Crown Prince, was jolted awake by Emperor Mingxi's voice. Xie Zhiyan bowed and replied, \"Imperial Father.\"","Emperor Mingxi didn't look at him. Instead, he gazed at Yue Fuguang with deep gratitude and said, \"Thank the Junior Preceptor on my behalf for her life-saving grace toward Great Yan and its people.\"","Everyone silently nodded in agreement. His Majesty was right. Was it not a life-saving grace? If it weren't for her, the lifespan of Great Yan would have already started its countdown.","The Crown Prince accepted the order. After his personal eunuch helped him straighten his robes and crown, Xie Zhiyan bowed deeply and solemnly to Yue Fuguang, declaring loudly, \"Xie Zhiyan thanks the Junior Preceptor on behalf of my father. I thank the Junior Preceptor on behalf of the people of Great Yan.\"","Following the Crown Prince's bow, the officials behind him also bowed down, and even the members of the Yu family were remarkably among them.","Of everyone present, the only ones still standing straight were Emperor Mingxi and Yue Fuguang.","She accepted the gestures openly and naturally, without dodging or evading. As she watched him solemnly bow three times, her mind was quite active: With this posture, if the Crown Prince were holding three sticks of incense, it would look even more...","Before she could finish her thought, the System's voice rang in her ears. [Master, mind your persona, your persona! You are currently a subject. Being thanked and bowed to by a future monarch, shouldn't you act a bit more terrified and overwhelmed? Look at your expression, isn't it a bit too calm? It looks exactly like how you act when a group of minor immortals greets you.]","\"Uh... I suppose it is a bit, but I don't know how to make a terrified and overwhelmed expression! Little Zhu, even though I've lost my memories, how many people in heaven or on earth could make me act like that?\"","[What Master says is right. As long as you are happy. But if these people suspect your identity...]","\"Junior Preceptor, may this humble official take a look at the seeds inside?\"","Wang Shouchen hurriedly spoke up. He was a little afraid to hear what the Divine Artifact would say next, feeling that it wouldn't be anything good.","The crowd cooperatively looked toward the bags of seeds, their eyes full of eagerness, completely failing to notice anything wrong with Yue Fuguang accepting the full formal bows from the Crown Prince and themselves.","\"Of course you may. Please, feel free to look,\" she said, handing Wang Shouchen a small booklet. \"Lord Wang, this is a seed manual. If there's anything you don't understand, you can follow the steps written inside.\"","But they shouldn't ask her, because she wouldn't know even if they did.","\"Little Zhu, look, they don't think there's anything inappropriate about me accepting their bows.\"","[Master, that's only because we are in the mortal realm. If we were back on our Lingxu Mountain, ordinary minor immortals wouldn't even be able to catch a glimpse of you, even if they wanted to.]","\"You said it yourself, this is the mortal realm. We can't set our expectations too high. There isn't even an Earth Immortal here.\"","Wang Shouchen took the planting manual with both hands, carefully tucked it into his robes, and then gave Yue Fuguang another solemn bow. \"This humble official thanks the Junior Preceptor!\"","Although he had a thousand words of gratitude in his heart, when they reached his lips, they only formed a simple thank you.","\"Little Zhu, do you think I should dodge now to fit my persona?\"","[There's no need. Your official rank and grade are already higher than his. As for your age, the sum of the ages of everyone present wouldn't even match your immortal age...]","\"Little Zhu, that's enough. You may take your leave!\"","After looking at the plump, large grains of the various seeds, everyone's face was filled with smiles. Wang Shouchen's old face wrinkled into a smile so wide it resembled a blooming chrysanthemum.","Even with the bumpy carriage ride on the way back, Yue Fuguang was the only one who felt the journey was arduous.","Therefore, when it was time to part ways, Emperor Mingxi, his smile undiminished, asked Yue Fuguang if there was anything she wanted.","She told Emperor Mingxi quite bluntly, \"Your Majesty, please have the Ministry of Works repair the road leading to my estate. The round trip is far too bumpy.\"","\"These are trivial matters. Is there anything else?\" Lu Qi had told him earlier that the Ministry of Works had produced quite a lot of cement and stone slabs. They had originally intended to pave the road to the royal villa, and all the other materials were ready. But now, it seemed they would have to prioritize the Junior Preceptor.","\"Also, renovate the houses on the estate.\" As she spoke, Yue Fuguang took out a blueprint from her sleeve, though it was actually from her storage ring.","\"Renovate it according to this layout plan. As for the cost, just deduct it from the payment for the seeds.\"","Lu Qi took a look and his eyes lit up. He said loudly, \"Junior Preceptor, the Ministry of Works will definitely get this job done well for you.\"","Then, looking a bit embarrassed, he added, \"It's just that... could our Ministry of Works use some of the fixtures shown in this drawing?\"","He pointed to the flush toilets and showerheads in the various rooms on the blueprint and asked, adding, \"Our Ministry of Works will definitely use the best materials to make them for you.\"","Yue Fuguang understood. The blueprints produced by the System included not only the overall layout plan but also some detailed drawings.","Especially for items that did not exist in this world, the drawings were incredibly detailed. By following the blueprints, there was no fear that they wouldn't be able to produce something similar.","After receiving his repeated assurances, Yue Fuguang smiled and said, \"Lord Minister, you may take them and use them. If His Majesty likes them, the Imperial Palace can also be fully equipped with them.\"","Hearing their conversation, Emperor Mingxi also became curious and took the blueprint. After only a few glances, he immediately took a liking to the matching fixtures inside.","\"My beloved minister Lu, make a few first to test the results. If it works, the palace will be refitted alongside the Junior Preceptor's estate.\"","Yue Fuguang suddenly thought of the Bright Moon Pavilion where she lived and added, \"Also the Yu Manor, Lord Minister, please don't forget.\"","\"This humble official naturally would not dare to forget.\" Despite suddenly receiving so much more work, Lu Qi didn't find it troublesome at all; instead, he smiled very cheerfully.","It was a good thing that the nobles had needs! This meant that their Ministry of Works was valued by His Majesty and the Junior Preceptor, which would elevate the Ministry's status among the Six Ministries.","Speaking of connections, who among the Six Ministries was closer to the Junior Preceptor than they were? Her grandfather was right here in their department!","Seeing his granddaughter fighting for their family's benefits, Yu Chongshan naturally felt very warm in his heart. He had already begun calculating that he should find a few of his trusted aides to handle the construction of Yue Fuguang's estate and the road.","Their craftsmanship was excellent, and they were respectful to him as their superior. These people would definitely put more effort into his granddaughter's affairs.","...","\"Your Majesty! This subject risks death to remonstrate! This matter is absolutely unacceptable, Your Majesty!\""]},{"number":213,"title":"Chapter 213: Hope You All Read More Books","paragraphs":["Yue Fuguang, who had been sleeping groggily, was suddenly jolted awake by this tragic cry, shivering as she instantly snapped to full consciousness.","She couldn't help but rub her ears and ask the system, 'Little Zhu, what's the situation? What is that old man doing?'","[Master, listen closely. This matter actually concerns you.]","The system kept her in suspense. Mainly, it was its first time seeing an official willing to risk death to admonish the emperor in court, and over such a trivial matter at that. It was currently busy checking this person's background.","Yue Fuguang looked down and saw a white-haired old official kneeling at the very front of the civil officials' ranks. The cry that had startled her awake just now came from his mouth.","At this moment, the air in the grand hall instantly froze following his admonishment. Emperor Mingxi frowned slightly, a hint of anger on his face, showing not a trace of the amiability he had when facing Yue Fuguang.","He said, \"Minister Zhang, why is it inappropriate?\"","\"Your Majesty!\" Xu Qian raised his head, his gaze burning brightly. \"The Book of Rites states: 'In the month of mid-autumn, the relevant officials are ordered to urge the people to harvest, to make sure to store vegetables, and to accumulate abundantly.' This advises the Son of Heaven to comply with the will of Heaven and conform to the seasons, without interfering with the farming schedule.","\"Now is but early spring, the time when all living things sprout and grow. Since the mid-autumn harvest season has not yet arrived, Your Majesty has specifically ordered the Imperial Astronomy Bureau to select an auspicious day for a single crop to perform the ceremony of an imperial harvest.","\"This is using the supreme status of the Son of Heaven to usurp the duties of the hundred gods below, and disrupt the order of the four seasons above! I fear that if word of this action spreads, the common people of the world will all imitate it. Seeking auspicious times will mess up the farming schedule, putting the cart before the horse, and damaging the very foundation of agriculture, Your Majesty!\"","His words were full of classical quotes and overly pedantic, but Yue Fuguang managed to understand the general idea. Ultimately, this was all caused by the trouble of having the Imperial Astronomy Bureau select an auspicious day just to dig up a few pots of potatoes, a crop they had never seen before.","In the end, these people simply felt that potatoes were unworthy of such a fuss, and that the Emperor was giving her too much face!","[Master, actually, if Little Zhu were to pick an auspicious day and time, it would definitely be better than whatever the Imperial Astronomy Bureau chooses.]","'Little Zhu, we can't do everything ourselves. We have to leave some things for others to do.' Otherwise, wouldn't these people lose their jobs? How could she live her days as a lazy salted fish then?","Besides, this wasn't just about picking a date.","As soon as his words fell, another official stepped forward. It was the Deputy Censor-in-Chief, Zhang Tingji, who was also the rival of the Censor-in-Chief, Feng Tang.","Back when Zhao Xu fell from power and was imprisoned, the two of them had been competitors. Zhang Tingji had even had a slightly higher chance of winning than Feng Tang.","He said, \"Your Majesty, although Lord Xu's words may be somewhat inappropriate, this humble subject believes there is reason in them. What exactly are potatoes? We have never even heard the name before.","\"Whether they can be widely planted is also unknown. Is it not somewhat improper to trouble the Imperial Astronomy Bureau to select an auspicious day for such a thing?\"","Yue Fuguang's brain automatically translated this. To put it bluntly, he was saying the Emperor was making a mountain out of a molehill. They hadn't even heard of these potatoes, so having the Imperial Astronomy Bureau pick a date for an unknown object meant it simply wasn't worthy!","Feng Tang's brows knitted tightly into a knot. This old coot Zhang Tingji was intentionally making things difficult for the Lord Junior Preceptor, wasn't he? If you want to say His Majesty is making a fuss over nothing, then just say it.","What was with him shooting side-glances at the Lord Junior Preceptor?","He covertly swept his gaze over his colleagues, becoming even more determined to pick an auspicious day to dig up the potatoes right in front of all the civil and military officials in the court.","He wanted to let all his colleagues know exactly what a massive blessing the Lord Junior Preceptor had brought to Great Yan!","Yun Tianxing, the Director of the Imperial Astronomy Bureau, who had heard the arguments, knew the inside story, and had even followed along to visit the Lord Junior Preceptor's farm, had observed the stars that very night and chosen a good day. He was just waiting to report back to His Majesty today.","He never expected that before he could even open his mouth, two people would jump out to drag them down.","He was so furious inside!","Stepping forward right before Feng Tang could, he said, \"You two Lords! The timing of the heavens is the pivot of yin and yang; good and bad fortune concern the destiny of our nation! Acting on an auspicious day is to pray that this seed of auspicious omen can be successfully promoted to bless our myriad of people.","\"How could this be a trivial matter? If we dig them up casually and offend the stars, bringing about disaster, who will bear the responsibility? Will you?\"","He threw down this massive accusation, crushing the two of them so much that they didn't know how to respond for a moment.","At this moment, another man named Huang Shouping stepped forward and said, \"Lord Yun is perhaps exaggerating! An auspicious omen is a sign of good fortune, something that cannot be obtained unless one possesses great wisdom, great virtue, and great luck.","\"Now, Your Lordship calls these unknown potatoes an auspicious omen. Is this not an overstatement?\"","Xu Qian also immediately reacted and loudly retorted, \"Offending the stars and bringing disaster? Lord Director, His Majesty is the true Son of Heaven. He shepherds the people on behalf of Heaven.","\"As long as he acts with benevolence and virtue, why should he fear the stars? If he rigidly adheres to divining good and bad fortune in every matter, that is not the conduct of a sage ruler!","\"Your Majesty, you should prioritize the state and the livelihood of the people. Such empty formalities should be dispensed with whenever possible!\"","\"Xu Qian!\" Emperor Mingxi's voice darkened, carrying a trace of displeasure. His gaze swept over the three men kneeling on the ground with slightly trembling bodies as he said, \"Are you accusing Us of being a superstitious, virtueless, and incompetent ruler?\"","The named Xu Qian immediately prostrated himself on the ground and said loudly, \"Please see clearly, Your Majesty. This humble subject did not mean that at all. I am merely acting out of a minister's heart full of loyalty to the sovereign, advising Your Majesty not to listen to false words.\"","\"Please, Your Majesty, stay close to virtuous ministers and distance yourself from vile characters. Absolutely do not listen to slander,\" Zhang Tingji immediately followed up.","'Little Zhu, are they making veiled attacks at me?'","[Master, they are outright calling you the vile character who spouts slander.]","Emperor Mingxi's heart sank, and he said sternly, \"You are insolent!\" The tiger had finally shown its teeth.","\"We wouldn't dare!\" Xu Qian, Zhang Tingji, and Huang Shouping slammed their heads against the ground with a loud thud.","The jade tablets in their hands struck the golden floor tiles, producing a crisp sound that made the entire grand hall seem even more dead silent.","\"May Your Majesty see clearly. We are wholeheartedly thinking of Your Majesty's best interests. Your Majesty strives for good governance, aiming to usher in a golden age.","\"However, to usher in a golden age, one must first prioritize practical matters, and secondary to that, superficial formalities. The miraculous effects of these potatoes are completely unheard of. Even if they can fill stomachs and save the people, what does that have to do with the exact hour they are dug up?","\"If future history books record that in a certain year and month, the Emperor observed the stars to dig up potatoes, Your Majesty... how will future generations judge you?\"","Emperor Mingxi was so angered by Zhang Tingji's words that he actually laughed. The Emperor's laugh was mixed with a bone-piercing chill, giving the grand hall an even more suffocating sense of oppression.","\"What a fine 'judged by future generations'!\" He stood up and walked to the edge of the imperial steps, looking down at Zhang Tingji from above, cold light flickering in his eyes. \"Minister Zhang, are you threatening Us?\"","'Little Zhu, not only is this guy making veiled insults at me, but now he's even threatening the Emperor. What's this guy's background?'","At this moment, Yu Chongshan stepped out. His back was perfectly straight as he said, \"May Your Majesty see clearly. For generations, the Yu family has been full of loyal subjects who serve the nation. The potatoes planted by the Lord Junior Preceptor are delicious and high-yielding.","\"We originally intended to present them to Your Majesty to save the myriad of people, but we never expected several lords to be so suspicious. I do not know if it stems from public interest or out of jealousy toward my granddaughter's good luck.\"","He looked at the few men disdainfully and said in a clear, resonant voice, \"The Lord Junior Preceptor descended to this world by divine decree. She is someone of great wisdom and virtue, and even more so, someone of great fortune.","\"What is so impossible about her obtaining potatoes that yield over thirty or forty shi per mu? You frogs at the bottom of the well looking up at the sky, there are so many things you have never seen. Does that mean they do not exist?\"","He deliberately downplayed the per-mu yield of the potatoes, afraid that someone would seize upon it as a handle to further attack Yue Fuguang.","Yue Fuguang's eyes, however, sparkled brightly. She felt that this impassioned little old man was absolutely awesome right now!","Feng Tang quickly chimed in, \"Lord Zhang, one cannot speak of ice to a summer cicada. I advise you all to read more books. As the agricultural texts say...\" Hearing the phrase \"read more books,\" Yue Fuguang instinctively completed the jingle in her mind: \"and read more newspapers!\""]},{"number":214,"title":"Chapter 214: What do you mean by \"kneeling quickly\"","paragraphs":["Right, if there is time in the future, maybe I should run a newspaper and control the mouthpiece of public opinion. I would like to see who would dare to speak ill of me then. I could expose them in minutes!","For civil officials, this was a way to kill without shedding blood!","Feng Tang mainly aimed to strike at Zhang Tingji, and in passing, he indiscriminately blasted Xu Qian and Huang Shouping. His verbal barrage lasted for the duration of a whole cup of tea.","Yue Fuguang smacked her lips, wondering why her mouth felt so dry!","[Master, this Zhang Tingji is Feng Tang's sworn enemy. He comes from the Zhang family of Jiangnan, a family of officials for generations, completely different from the grassroots Feng Tang.]","Feng Tang: Lord Artifact, is it possible that there is a more elegant name for grassroots called 'humble origins'?","He carefully peeked at Yue Fuguang's expression. The Junior Preceptor surely would not despise his humble origins and refuse to take him as a subordinate.","\"But I find Feng Tang more pleasing to the eye.\"","Feng Tang: Tears are about to fall!","Wu Yong: Hmph, the Junior Preceptor definitely finds me pleasing to the eye too.","He looked down at his plump belly and sucked it in hard. Hmm, he had lost weight!","[Indeed, Little Zhu also finds this Zhang Tingji an eyesore. The Zhang family has survived for hundreds of years, and it is not just because they have money and people.","It is also because they are quick to kneel. The successive family heads have a magic weapon, which is marriage alliances.","The Zhang family is good at reproducing, and their children and in-laws are spread all over the Great Yan Dynasty.]","\"Little Zhu, what do you mean by being quick to kneel?\"","[It means that in the final years of a dynasty, their Zhang family can always catch the last train of the new dynasty at the final moment.","This was the case in the current dynasty, the previous dynasty, and even further back.","The Zhang family even had a great-aunt who entered the palace in the previous dynasty. She was deeply favored by the last emperor for several years and even bore him a son and a daughter.","The son died along with the fall of the Tong family's dynasty, but the daughter changed her name and surname, entered the Zhang family as a Zhang daughter, and later married into an official family surnamed Tong.","This can be considered a disguised continuation of their branch of the Tong family bloodline.","Master, guess who her grandson Tong Jiye married later?]","\"Jiangnan, could it be related to Sima Jing? Speaking of Sima Jing, do you know how Bao Qianjun is doing now?","The emperor still does not know about his cousin's wild ambitions. The Bao family will not repeat their past mistakes, right!\"","[Master, during the time you warned them about the assassins kidnapping the bride, did you not indirectly remind them to be careful of the south?","Looking at Elder Lord Bao's demeanor, it seems the Bao family will be fine for now.","However, the person Tong Jiye married is indeed somewhat related to Sima Jing. His wife comes from the Shen family, the same Shen family as Shen Wanchuan.","After the Sima family's Great Wei fell, the successor was Shen Wanchuan's grandson. The Shen family's empire changed hands again in less than twenty years.","This new master is Tong Jiye's son, Tong Chengzong, whose state title was 'Great Zhou', historically known as the Southern Zhou.]","Hearing this, everyone else fell silent for a moment, except for Xu Qian, Huang Shouping, and Zhang Tingji, who were still arguing.","Especially the noble families—they never imagined that the Great Zhou, which their ancestors had overthrown, would be restored over a hundred years later. Although it sounded like the Great Zhou established by the Tong family's descendants was confined to a corner of Jiangnan, they had ultimately managed to restore their nation.","\"This dynastic change is really frequent enough. In less than a hundred years, the empire changed hands three times. The Tong family's century-long restoration effort actually succeeded in the end. This outcome is much better than that Murong Fu!\"","[Murong? Master, how did you know that the Tong family was replaced by the Murong family? This dynastic change is like an old lady's foot-binding cloth—long and stinky. We can talk about it in detail when we have time.]","Seeing the officials below who could not help but frown just like her, Yue Fuguang chuckled inwardly. It seemed that everyone's imagination was quite good; the mention of a foot-binding cloth made it seem as if they could actually smell it.","The system continued to spill the beans, [Did I not mention earlier that one of the reasons the Zhang family survived for hundreds of years was through marriage alliances? Master, do you not want to know which families they allied with?]","At this point, some people silently lowered their heads even further. It seemed that some of their families really did have daughters who married into the Zhang family, or wives from the Zhang family.","\"Did you not say there were a lot? I do not have the patience to listen. Besides, who they marry is decided by the family; it does not have much to do with these married-out daughters.\"","[Then I will just briefly mention a few. We will not bring up the ones who just lived peaceful lives.]","While some breathed a sigh of relief, they silently prayed in their hearts that their families would not be mentioned! Their humble households were not worthy of being brought up by Lord Artifact!","[The Zhang family's in-laws include the Sima family, though the one who married over was a concubine-born daughter, and she married a collateral branch member of the Sima family.","Furthermore, Shen Wanchuan's son also married the daughter of a cousin from a collateral branch of the Zhang family.","Next is Tong Jiye's son, Tong Chengzong, who later became emperor. From his time in the princely residence, he had a woman from the Zhang family as a concubine, and after becoming emperor, he conferred upon her the title of Consort Hui.","Master, guess who else they formed a marriage alliance with?]","Hearing this, the ruler and ministers of the Great Yan finally caught on to the pattern. The Zhang family continuously placed bets, and they bet right every single time. The known families who could ascend to the throne after the fall of the Great Yan were all in-laws of the Zhang family.","Could the Murong family be next?","The compound surname Murong was quite rare in the Great Yan Dynasty. If one really had to count someone with considerable power, there was only Murong Qian, the defending general stationed far away at the border of Jiaozhou.","Soon, their suspicions were confirmed when Yue Fuguang guessed, \"Is it the Murong family's turn next?\"","[Master guessed right, it is the Murong family. The future emperor of the Murong family is even a maternal grandson of the Zhang family.]","Yue Fuguang clicked her tongue, \"This Zhang family is truly an ever-victorious general at the gambling table. For mortals to reach such a level, they really have some skills. These officials of the Mingxi era who only look at what is in front of them are far inferior to them!\"","The ruler and ministers of the Great Yan had bitter expressions. The Little Immortal was scolding them for being short-sighted. Looking again at the few people in the center fighting like angry roosters, they suddenly felt their faces burn with shame!","[Master, let us not boost others' morale and diminish our own prestige. The reason the Zhang family can hit the jackpot every time is still by casting a wide net to catch fish.","Let alone the officials in the court, even the residences of Prince Ming and Prince Qi have Zhang family daughters.]","Wei Ping and Cai Xian's hearts stirred. The feigned-dead Prince Qi had already been secretly captured by them, and his backyard indeed had a concubine who came from a collateral branch of the Zhang family.","As for Prince Ming, who was being secretly monitored by them, it seemed he indeed also had a close senior maidservant surnamed Zhang, whose original registry was also in Jiangnan.","Looking at His Majesty's intentions, he still wanted to use Prince Ming as bait to fish out those two from Northern Li and Southern Zhao. It was said that Lan Xuan'er, in order to marry Prince Ming, was currently fighting for it with the Emperor of Southern Zhao.","Therefore, they could not reel in the net on Prince Ming just yet. However, a maidservant from the Zhang family should not be able to stir up any major storms either.","Although they thought this way, they still felt they should dispatch more manpower to keep an eye on this woman.","Emperor Mingxi looked at the eloquently speaking Zhang Tingji and sneered in his heart, but his voice was peaceful, carrying an unquestionable decisiveness as he said, \"I am not superstitious about auspicious times. I want to use this 'Imperial Digging' ceremony to inform the people of the world that the imperial court values this item more than pearls and jade!","Ordering the Imperial Astronomy Bureau to choose an auspicious time is also to tell the common people of the nation that the imperial court values this item just as it values the common folk of our Great Yan.","The Great Yan has received heaven's pity and been granted high-yield fine seeds, which is the blessing of the Great Yan.","Potatoes are the life-saving food for millions of commoners.\""]},{"number":215,"title":"Chapter 215: No Need to Burn Memorials and Offer Sacrifices to Heaven","paragraphs":["Feng Tang immediately responded, \"What Your Majesty said is correct. It is normal that Lord Zhang and the others do not understand. After all, Lord Zhang comes from a prominent aristocratic family in Jiangnan and has naturally never worried about food or clothing.","It is excusable that he cannot empathize with the suffering of the common people.\"","Yue Fuguang summarized his words in her mind: [It just means he's eaten too much to see that others are still starving and freezing. Empty talk ruins the country!]","Empty talk ruins the country! These words struck the hearts of the ruler and ministers of the Great Yan Dynasty like a heavy hammer, and everyone who heard them changed their expressions.","Especially those who usually liked to boast and talk big but had done little practical work; they gasped slightly. These words weighed on their hearts like a giant boulder—it was too heavy!","Emperor Mingxi, seated on the dragon throne, looked down from his high vantage point at the officials below whose expressions shifted several times. His fingers tapped lightly on the armrest, and the rhythmic thumping sound seemed to strike right at everyone's heart.","He only hoped that these people would take the Junior Preceptor's words to heart and constantly stay vigilant. The Great Yan Dynasty was at the crossroads of a tremendous transformation; what it lacked were capable ministers and competent officials, not subjects who only knew how to engage in empty talk.","He said, \"Beloved Subject Feng is right. As for what you beloved subjects said about not knowing what a potato is, I will not say much more to you all here.","Once the Directorate of Astronomy selects an auspicious day, you beloved subjects can dig them up with your own hands and see for yourselves whether the yield per acre questioned by Lord Xu, Lord Zhang, and Lord Huang has been exaggerated.\"","Hearing Emperor Mingxi's words, Yun Tianxing immediately stepped forward, unfurled a scroll of yellow silk, and reported loudly, \"Your Majesty, this humble official observed the celestial phenomena last night and deduced the calendar.","I have calculated that at the first quarter of the Si hour the day after tomorrow, the sun will reside in the east, bringing purple auspicious clouds from the east. Moreover, Chen belongs to earth and Si belongs to fire; fire generates earth. This perfectly aligns with the sign of sowing and harvesting. It is a time of supreme auspiciousness, most suitable for breaking ground!\"","Emperor Mingxi nodded slightly, his gaze turning to Yue Fuguang, who had just picked up a pastry and was about to take a bite.","Yue Fuguang: Should I eat it or should I eat it?","Catching from the corner of her eye the hundred officials holding their breath and watching her and Emperor Mingxi intently, Yue Fuguang thought for a moment and decided to hold the pastry firmly in her hands instead.","She couldn't lose her imposing manner. As for saving face, with the golden halo of the Little Immortal Lord on her, she wasn't afraid of losing face no matter what she did!","System: If the tips of your ears weren't red, Tongtong would have believed you!","Yue Fuguang decided to strike first, \"Does Your Majesty need something?\"","This was the first sentence Yue Fuguang had spoken while the court session was underway. It was also the first time most people had directly witnessed a sovereign-subject dialogue between their emperor and this Junior Preceptor.","Hearing Yue Fuguang's words, some people couldn't help but feel a strange sensation in their hearts, feeling as if the Junior Preceptor was acting a bit out of line, subverting the natural order.","Before the crowd could speculate further, they saw their emperor, who had just worn a face of ice, change his expression in a second. That warm smile, like a gentle spring breeze, was something they hadn't received even once in the dozen years they had served as his subjects.","They saw a smiling Emperor Mingxi say to Yue Fuguang, \"Fuguang, you heard Beloved Subject Yun's words just now. We will dig up the potatoes at the Fengtian Hall at the first quarter of the Si hour the day after tomorrow. Do you have any problems with this?\"","Some people were very satisfied with their emperor's performance. The items belonged to the Junior Preceptor, so it was indeed right to ask for the owner's opinion.","Those who were unaware frowned. Xu Qian couldn't help but speak up, \"Your Majesty, since digging up the potatoes is a major event, it should be solely decided by Your Majesty and the lords.","The Junior Preceptor is young. What could she possibly know about the harvesting of food crops? I'm afraid she might not even be able to tell the difference if chives and wheat were placed together.\"","[Little Zhu, this Xu Qian is deliberately targeting me, right?]","[Master, Little Zhu can feel this old geezer's deep malice towards you. Do you want me to strike him with a bolt of heavenly lightning to teach him a lesson?]","This time, there was no need for Yu Chongshan to step in. Yu Zhongchun, acting as a father, took the lead and rushed to the front. With a cold sneer, he said, \"What great arrogance, Lord Xu, to actually dare question Your Majesty.\"","He cupped his hands toward his colleagues and said, \"Although my daughter is young, she is exceptionally intelligent. I wouldn't go so far as to say she knows everything about astronomy and geography, but when it comes to agriculture, she is far superior to Lord Xu!\"","Wang Shouchen immediately stepped forward to show his support, saying, \"I can testify for Lord Yu on this point. Our Court of Imperial Agriculture has also received the methods provided by the Junior Preceptor regarding tilling, intercropping, and composting.","After testing, they have proven to be highly feasible. Barring any accidents, the lands cultivated using these methods this year will see a significant increase in grain yield.\"","Lu Qi also bowed respectfully to Yue Fuguang and said, \"The Ministry of Works also thanks the Junior Preceptor for providing the techniques for manufacturing agricultural tools, heated brick beds, and so on.\"","The most important iron-smelting technique involved confidentiality, so Lu Qi did not mention it. However, just the aforementioned contributions were already enough to surpass the majority of the people sitting here.","Subsequently, Dong Qianli of the Ministry of Revenue and Huo Ying of the Ministry of War also stepped in one after another to voice their support.","Cai Xian and Wei Ping were quite frustrated. The Junior Preceptor had clearly helped them the most, but because they had learned everything through eavesdropping, they couldn't speak of it publicly.","They could only watch their colleagues show off over there.","The others were all dumbfounded upon seeing this. When did all this happen? How come they didn't know anything about it?","If what these lords said was true, then this Junior Preceptor might really have an extraordinary background. Perhaps what the divine oracle said was true?","Meanwhile, Ji Hongming and Zhang Zhongping, who were also Ministers of their respective ministries, had red eyes. They hadn't realized it until they thought about it, but it turned out that they were the only ones who hadn't received any blessings from the Little Immortal Lord!","Was it because they rarely went out of their way to curry favor with those two little ancestors?","Zhang Zhongping glanced at his subordinate, Wu Yong. This kid was wholeheartedly devoted to the Junior Preceptor. Behind the scenes, the Little Immortal Lord and Lord Divine Artifact highly approved of him.","His Ministry of Rites still had a chance!","Wu Yong felt his hair stand on end under his superior's intense stare. However, thinking of his golden backer, he jiggled his chubby frame. He had nothing to fear!","Finally, the Crown Prince stepped forward and said, \"I also want to thank the Junior Preceptor for providing the method for producing cement. The cement used for building houses and paving roads saved many commoners during last year's snow disaster.\"","[Master, it turns out you have already done so much without even realizing it!]","A perfectly timed look of bewilderment appeared on Yue Fuguang's face. [I didn't know. I just mentioned it a few times to my grandfather and father at home, and handed the items over to a few officials. Has it really amounted to this much? You say I've done so much, do you think they will suspect my origins?]","Emperor Mingxi and his ministers felt their eyelids twitch. They had been so caught up in flattering him that they completely forgot about this detail. How careless of them!","Before anyone could react, Yun Tianxing from the Imperial Directorate of Astronomy immediately spoke up. \"My lords, you must not doubt it. The Junior Preceptor was born of divine decree, so he naturally possesses extraordinary traits. Wasn't the State Preceptor of the previous dynasty just as intelligent and blessed with immense fortune as our Junior Preceptor?\"","At the thought of that legendary State Preceptor from the previous dynasty, and then looking at their own Junior Preceptor, everyone suddenly felt that it all made perfect sense.","[Little Zhu, who is this State Preceptor of the previous dynasty?]","[Master, it is a long story about this State Preceptor. We can talk about it in detail when we have the chance. You still haven't answered me whether I can strike down that old geezer Xu!]","Yue Fuguang did not reply to the system. Instead, he first addressed Emperor Mingxi. \"It is entirely up to Your Majesty to decide. However, since Your Majesty has asked, I will only mention one thing.\"","He turned to Yun Tianxing of the Imperial Directorate of Astronomy and Zhang Zhongping, the Minister of Rites, and said, \"The auspicious time remains unchanged, and the ceremony shall be simplified. There is no need to burn a memorial to offer sacrifices to Heaven.\"","[Master, are you refusing to let them burn a memorial to Heaven because you are afraid that the moment you offer a stick of incense, the incense burner will explode right in your face!]"]},{"number":216,"title":"Chapter 216: Little Pearl, did you do this","paragraphs":["\"That's right, during the New Year, because I occupied the body of the Yu family's daughter, I could barely offer incense to them once. If I go again next year, the ancestral hall will probably explode!","During this New Year, I can only pretend to be sick and not go.\"","The Yu family father and sons, whose hearts had been hanging in their throats, immediately felt relieved. However, letting their granddaughter pretend to be sick was absolutely out of the question; there was no need for a child to do such a thing.","Emperor Mingxi and his ministers, on the other hand, felt a chill in their hearts. This served as a wake-up call for them: from now on, whenever it involved the Junior Preceptor, they had to listen to her opinion. It could save their lives!","The two officials immediately said, \"Yes, we have noted it down. Everything will be kept simple.\" They would just make the autumn harvest sacrifice grander.","\"My lords,\" the Emperor's gaze swept across the hall, \"the excavation will be handled by experienced farmers selected by the Court of Agricultural Affairs, and they will start at the 'auspicious hour' the day after tomorrow.","I and all of you ministers will be there in person to show our dedication to agriculture. Thus, are there any objections?\"","Emperor Mingxi's eyes looked sharply at Xu Qian. The question was directed at all the ministers, but the Emperor only stared at Xu Qian alone.","Xu Qian was so frightened by the Emperor's piercing glare that he froze in place. He then bowed deeply along with the others. This time, his voice carried a hint of trembling, \"Your Majesty is wise! I... have no objections!\"","The ministers chanted in unison, \"Your Majesty is wise, we have no objections!\"","As the crowd walked out of the outer hall, they heard the voice of the Divine Artifact Lord saying, [How could mortals withstand Master's incense offerings? Even the Heavenly Dao of this world cannot.","Even the Heavenly Dao doesn't dare to question Master, yet this guy surnamed Xu deliberately targeted Master. Little Zhu cannot swallow this anger.","Afraid of scaring people, Master didn't let me release lightning outside. Now that we are still in the imperial palace, these lords are experienced and knowledgeable, and with the previous experience, they definitely won't be scared by me.]","\"But the Emperor will definitely suspect that I am secretly hoarding lightning-summoning talismans. What if he makes things difficult for me?\"","Emperor Mingxi, who hadn't gone far, stumbled and was quickly supported by the Crown Prince. Without even looking, he knew that his imperial father had been hit hard by the huge blame thrown by the Little Immortal Lord.","Emperor Mingxi: I'm not, I didn't, don't talk nonsense! (Triple Denial JPG)","[That's really possible! How about I strike him with the lightning talisman and let it explode when he gets home? It can also help clear the filthy air of the Xu family.]","On her way out of the palace, Yue Fuguang occasionally greeted the colleagues passing by. Today, perhaps because a few lords had 'sung her praises', even the officials who had never spoken to her before would smile and nod in greeting when they saw her.","On the surface, Yue Fuguang nodded in return with the reserved manner of a little adult, but in her heart, she had already started chatting with the system.","\"Oh? What filthy things are going on in the Xu family? Quick, tell me about it.\"","[Master, this Old Bastard Xu perfectly matches the words beast in human clothing, shameless, devoid of honor, and brazen.]","Yue Fuguang nodded and commented, \"Little Zhu, you haven't been going to school with me for nothing these days. You know so many four-character idioms now.\"","The system wagged its non-existent tail. It originally wanted to show off a bit, but thinking of its task, it immediately gathered its thoughts and replied, [Of course, as a divine artifact, Little Zhu is only slightly inferior to Master.","However, Master, Little Zhu didn't wrong this old bastard. Don't be fooled by his appearance as an upright gentleman; in private, he is extremely shameless and despicable.","He's sleeping with his daughter-in-law!]","Hearing the words \"sleeping with his daughter-in-law\", the people scattered around who seemed to be passing by but were actually following her to enjoy the gossip all felt a chill of disgust in their hearts.","They were extremely contemptuous of Xu Qian.","In their positions, what kind of beautiful women couldn't they have? Was there a need to reach into their son's bedroom?","Some people shook their heads. After today's events, the Xu family's reputation was completely ruined!","\"Sleeping with his daughter-in-law? The Great Yan version of Jia Zhen?\"","[Yes, yes, that's him! But the object of his affair is not his son's legal wife, but a concubine. This dog even told that concubine that since concubines can be bought and sold, his actions don't count as incest.]","\"Little Zhu, remember to drop a huge lightning bolt on him and directly cripple him. I don't want to see him again tomorrow, it burns my eyes!\"","[Master, you can rest assured when Little Zhu handles things. I will definitely make him spend the rest of his life in pain on a bed. And Zhang Tingji, I sprinkled itching powder on him; he won't have a good time for this entire month. As for Huang Shouping...]","Before the system could finish speaking, a crackling sound of farting came from behind. Yue Fuguang turned around to look.","She saw Huang Shouping standing dozens of meters away, first looking at a loss, then his face turning bright red as he covered his face with the wide sleeves of his official robe and hurriedly fled to a less crowded place.","Before he could get far, someone couldn't help but burst into laughter. In the distance, Huang Shouping's footsteps became even more flustered amidst the laughter of his colleagues, and he almost tripped himself several times.","With a smile playing on her lips, Yue Fuguang asked, \"Little Zhu, did you do this?\"","[Yes, I did it, Master. Is Little Zhu awesome or what?] The voice was filled with joy, using a rising tone that begged for praise and compliments.","Yue Fuguang naturally wouldn't let the system down. A barrage of over-the-top praises almost made the system's code scramble, showing how profound her skills were—she usually just hid them well!","The people following behind: We've learned something new! We've learned something new! Next time, we'll try this on His Majesty to see the effect!","\"How long will his condition last?\"","[I used a small dose, so it will only last for today. As long as he doesn't eat or drink too much, he will be fine tomorrow. Hmph, he only dared to slander Master because he was too full.","And that Zhang Tingji, if he eats less, the itching might stop in half a month. If he eats and drinks his fill, he won't escape a full month of suffering.","Master doesn't blame me for taking matters into my own hands, right?]","Yue Fuguang said indifferently, \"I know you were just eager to protect your master. These are trivial matters. They are mere ants, a small punishment as a major warning is perfectly fine.\"","The crowd silently lit a candle in their hearts for those few people—they deserved it!","The reason the Little Immortal Lord hadn't taken action against them before was purely because she saw them as ants and couldn't be bothered to deal with them.","Now, there were those who were not afraid of death, bullying the little ancestor for her young age and dancing right in front of her face, not knowing that a mere crook of her finger could end their entire lives!","If they died, their Majesty wouldn't even help bury them.","Many people secretly rejoiced. Not killing them directly was truly the Little Immortal Lord's mercy! They would have to add two more sticks of incense when they went home to pray.","\"Little Zhu, elaborate on this gossip about Xu Qian sleeping with his daughter-in-law.\"","Yue Fuguang got into the carriage returning to the estate. Hearing his younger cousin start gossiping again, Yu Huaixian's ears perked up.","At the same time, he didn't forget to vigilantly scan the surroundings. Shen Chunying and the others did the same, as they all knew that when this ancestor started gossiping, she didn't care about the life or death of others.","She had offended quite a few people. What if someone couldn't think straight and stubbornly wanted to attack her?","This glance was quite revealing; there was actually a carriage following them at a leisurely pace. Having escorted the Junior Preceptor to and from court all these days, they had become familiar with the surrounding people and carriages.","At a glance, this carriage clearly belonged to Lord Wei of the Dali Court.","Looking again at the one in their family, they understood!","Shen Chunying thought of last night when she went to discuss with Yu Huaixian whether they should tell the Junior Preceptor about hearing her inner voice.","She still remembered how Yu Huaixian's look towards her suddenly changed at that moment. The look in his eyes went from looking at an ordinary colleague to looking at one of his own people."]},{"number":217,"title":"Chapter 217: The Pie in the Sky Drawn by the System","paragraphs":["Finally, giving her an appreciative look, \"Lord Shen, you only need to remember this: the Yu family will keep in mind those who are loyal to my younger female cousin. My cousin will certainly see it too.\"","Thinking of this, Shen Chunying and Yu Huaixian exchanged a glance, and both couldn't help but squeeze their horses' bellies. Seeing their actions, the driver Zhang Fang also raised his horsewhip.","Yue Fuguang, sitting in the carriage waiting to enjoy the gossip, suddenly felt the carriage speed up. She peeked outside through the gap in the curtains, and a smile crept up the corners of her lips, like a cat that had just stolen a fish.","[Master, this Xu Qian has a son named Xu Qi. Last year, during His Majesty's birthday festival, he took in a beautiful concubine.","This woman is named Luo Mei. She has fair skin, a beautiful face, and an exquisite, curvy figure. She won Xu Qi's deep affection, to the point where he spends almost every night in her room.","Because of this, it naturally provoked the dissatisfaction of Xu Qi's wife, Madam Chen. Thus, inner court battles are staged every day in the Xu residence.","When Xu Qian, as the father, was reprimanding his son in the study, telling him to exercise moderation, he coincidentally bumped into Concubine Mei who came to deliver soup. Xu Qian fell in one-sided love at first sight with her.]","'This Concubine Mei is young and beautiful, is she truly willing to submit to an old geezer like Xu Qian?' Isn't a young, handsome guy much more appealing?","[Has Master forgotten where Xu Qian comes from? The Ministry of Works! He is a colleague in the same department as your grandfather, and they used to be of the same rank.","Xu Qian had long considered Yu Chongshan's current position as the Vice Minister of Works to be his own in the bag. Who knew it would ultimately fall into the lap of Yu Chongshan, who was originally half-retired.]","'So he holds a grudge against my grandfather, and that led to today's drama?'","[Master guessed correctly. He believes the reason Yu Chongshan was able to be promoted to the Vice Minister position is entirely due to your rise.","And the reason this Concubine Mei entered the inner courtyard of the Xu family was also targeting Xu Qian, an official with real power in the Ministry of Works.]","'Another spy? They really are impossible to guard against! Since she was targeting Xu Qian, why didn't she directly enter Xu Qian's inner courtyard, but chose Xu Qi instead?'","[Because starting from last year, Emperor Mingxi, along with Wei Ping and Cai Xian, increased their precautions against the inner courtyards of important ministers. Whenever someone marries a wife or takes a concubine, that person's entire past will appear on the emperor's desk within a few days.","On the contrary, Xu Qi, who has not yet secured an official position in the court, became the best target. The imperial court would not investigate the origins of a concubine belonging to an official's son.]","'What a classic case of an ulterior motive! Are they coming for Great Yan's technology?'","[Yes, the spies they planted around Xu Qian detected changes in the Ministry of Works and suspected there was new technology.","However, the spies around Xu Qian had been unable to find a breakthrough to get concrete information, which is why they sent out this 'beautiful flower'.","Their purpose is to seize the opportunity to corrupt Xu Qian with beauty. It would be best if they could win him over; if not, they could still pry the information they want to know from his mouth.]","'Is this Concubine Mei not from Great Yan?'","[She is a pure Great Yan person, but the ones who paid to raise and train her were people from Northern Li. Master knows the original person in charge, it was that Xu Changyue.","After Xu Changyue was arrested by Great Yan, they replaced him with someone from Northern Yue.","This time entering the Xu family, she was also acting under the orders of Northern Yue.","Northern Yue originally wanted to gather information from Prince Ming, but unfortunately, he was first caught in the act of adultery by Lan Xuan'er, and then grounded—he still hasn't been released to this day.","With no other choice, they could only send someone into the Xu family's inner courtyard, which seemed the easiest to breach. A land of tender romance can be a hero's tomb, so burying a useless coward is certainly not an issue.]","'Did she succeed in the end?'","[Xu Qian only just got his hands on her right before the Lantern Festival. This Concubine Mei is still gently and carefully coaxing him, not daring to too obviously pry into his official business.]","'Does Xu Qi know that his old man is secretly tasting the forbidden fruit right in his own room?'","[Xu Qi doesn't know yet, but Madam Chen, who has absolute control over her own branch of the family, has already grown suspicious.","If it weren't for the accomplice—a servant planted by Northern Li around Xu Qian—helping to cover it up, this matter would have been discovered by Madam Chen long ago.]","'Since they are coming for the technology I provided, we can't just ignore it. Little Zhu, write this matter into a whistle-blower letter and place it on Cai Xian's desk.'","[Master, look, Little Zhu said this person deserves to be struck by lightning!]","Just as Yue Fuguang was preparing to have dinner, a sudden, deafening rumble echoed in her ears.","Cuizhu's hand, which was serving the soup, only trembled slightly before she steadily placed the bowl in front of Yue Fuguang.","She also instructed, \"Qingzhu, go and see where that noise outside came from. Don't dally around; come back immediately once you have news.\"","Despite saying this, Cuizhu already had some guesses in her heart. The commotion sounded like thunder, and looking at the time, wasn't it exactly when the officials finished their shifts and returned to their estates?","The news that Lord Xu Qian was struck unconscious by a bolt of lightning out of a clear sky just as he entered his estate's gates seemed to grow wings. It didn't take long for it to fly into thousands of households.","It also flew into the ears of Yue Fuguang, who was drinking her second bowl of soup.","[Host, do you want to see the miserable state of Xu Qian after being struck by lightning?]","'How can I see it? Can you even show me a live broadcast?'","[Not right now, but once we expose a bit more and upgrade to level four, maybe the Gossip System will have this feature.","I can show you a picture now.]","Yue Fuguang was not very confident in the functions her crippled system possessed. She could not help but question, \"Are you sure that once you upgrade to level four, you will be able to inherit all the functions of the Gossip System?\"","[Uh... As long as there is enough energy, I can repair myself! Host, just think about it. When the time comes, you can show these natives some videos from your hometown, and it will completely blow their minds!","And there is the Merit System. The higher the level, the more you, Ms. Yue Fuguang, as the host, can rely on the power of merit to do things that mortals cannot do, such as manifesting divinity in public.]","\"Manifesting divinity in public? Showing off is satisfying, but it costs way too many points!\" Was she spending points? No, she was spending her arms, her legs, her eyes, and her mouth.","[If the host relies on the power of merit, it would be just like a cultivator using their own spiritual energy to cast spells. You would be relying on yourself rather than those overpriced special effects bought from the system shop.]","\"You just said it is a cultivator's spell, and I am not a cultivator!\"","The reason Yue Fuguang was so obsessed with having her own body was also the hope that one day she could possess supreme power herself, rather than living in a borrowed shell like she was doing now.","[Hehe, this is the good news I want to tell you right now! Hurry, swallow the soup in your mouth. I am afraid you might spit it out when you hear the news.]","\"What good news? How could you hold it in until now?\" Yue Fuguang asked while finishing her last mouthful of soup.","System: Could I say that I only found out a few minutes earlier than you did?","[I was just afraid of disturbing your sleep!","Host, brace yourself. The news this system is about to share is about the question we asked the Main System a few days ago regarding the anomaly in your soul. Today, the Main System finally replied.]","Hearing its words, Yue Fuguang immediately smiled. \"That really is good news. Judging by your reaction, it is a good thing?\"","Seeing Yue Fuguang suddenly smile while eating the food in her bowl, Cuizhu, who was waiting on her by the side, silently made a mental note. A dish that could make her young lady smile while eating must be one of her favorites.","It had to be said, this was truly a beautiful misunderstanding."]},{"number":218,"title":"Chapter 218: Offering Incense and Worship, the Spirit Self-Molds","paragraphs":["[The Main System said that the host's lethargy and huge appetite, as well as feeling refreshed and healthy after eating and sleeping well, are partly due to the system consuming energy after the upgrade.","But the main reason is that the host has likely received the incense offerings from mortal believers, causing your divine soul to evolve toward that of an immortal god.","Look at the clay idols and wooden statues in temples and Daoist shrines. After enjoying the incense offerings of mortals year after year, who is to say they will not develop spiritual sentience one day? With good luck, they might even achieve godhood in this world.]","Hearing the system's explanation, Yue Fuguang's heart churned like a stormy sea, and a layer of cold sweat broke out on her back. She had actually received incense offerings without even knowing it!","\"System, I... I won't end up like them, will I?\" In her past life, she seemed to have heard that gods who achieved their status through offerings became dependent on incense, and their power was restricted by it.","This was not something Yue Fuguang, who liked to keep everything in her own hands, wanted to see.","[Of course not. First, there has not been enough time; second, the power of faith is not strong enough. The host's current situation can be understood as the incense nourishing your divine soul.","A powerful divine soul can reshape itself even without a physical body.]","Reshaping a physical body with the divine soul? Yue Fuguang stroked her plump chin. Being able to create a body according to her own wishes without spending points, this idea was absolutely brilliant!","So, when the system asked if she wanted to take a look at her divine soul, she agreed immediately without any hesitation.","After dismissing everyone from the room, Yue Fuguang closed her eyes and concentrated. Following the system's guidance, she saw a small ball of light shimmering with a faint golden glow, suspended in a pitch-black space.","That ball of light gave her a feeling of extreme intimacy. Was this her? Why was it different from what she had imagined?","Influenced by cultivation novels, she had thought it would either be a miniature version of herself, a sea of spiritual consciousness, or perhaps a white ball of light.","Her own, shining with golden light, looked exceptionally precious at first glance.","After she withdrew her consciousness, the system said, [Host, did you see it? That is your divine soul. When it grows a bit more and our level increases further, you will be able to cast spells relying on the Merit System.","The Merit System is equivalent to a magical artifact. With the help of this artifact, you can master supernatural powers.","If everything goes smoothly, during the Great Yan drought three years from now, you might not even need to pray for rain. You could just shout 'Let it rain,' and with your words acting as law, sweet dew would truly fall.]","\"How come this is different from the cultivation novels I have read? Do you not have to form hand seals to summon rain? Just shouting for it to come is way too awesome!\"","[You said it yourself, those are novels. Of course there is a difference from reality!","Host, trust me. As long as your divine soul continues to grow stronger, your ideal body with bones of white jade, spirit like autumn waters, and eyes like stars, along with the absolute best cultivation aptitude...","You might be able to achieve all this without relying on a massive amount of points, and perhaps without even needing to do too many missions after leaving this world.]","Yue Fuguang lay back on the bed, adopting the perfect posture of a slacker. \"System, I am feeling a bit stuffed from this massive pie in the sky you have drawn for me today.","Spit it out, what do you want?\"","Afraid the system might go too far, she immediately added, \"We have already leaked enough information. Any more, and the entire civil and military court will suspect the two of us are chatterboxes!\"","For the sake of realism, the two of them always rambled on about this and that, making it seem like a normal conversation. Otherwise, she could summarize the mission in just two sentences every time.","It was still because her influence was not strong enough. Otherwise, she could just lay her cards on the table, and they would still carry out her orders properly.","[Uh... how about you lend me some more points, Host? We have saved up over thirty thousand these past few days. Once today's mission points arrive, we will break fifty thousand, so...]","Yue Fuguang was speechless for a moment. It had spent all this time painting a glorious picture of the path to godhood for her, and it turned out it was all just for points!","Thinking that the system repairing its data would also benefit her, she said, \"I will give you ten thousand. I still need to save some for the limited-time ninety-percent-off sale when the store opens!","When will the system store be available? Have you received any news on your end?\"","Hearing that it would get ten thousand, the system suddenly felt that the pie it had just drawn for the host was totally worth it!","Speaking of the store, it recalled how it had waited several days for a reply after asking the Main System a question. This was the first time it had been so slow, leading it to guess that the Main System's data must have suffered significant damage from that attack.","So it replied, [There is no news from the Main System yet. I reckon it will not be too soon.]","\"Alright then. Leave the picture of Old Bastard Xu getting struck by lightning for me, and you are dismissed!\" Yue Fuguang rolled over, changing from lying on her stomach to lying on her back.","She called up the system panel and carefully admired the picture of Old Bastard Xu getting struck.","Tsk, tsk, tsk. After just one glance, Yue Fuguang could not help but click her tongue. Too tragic!","Xu Qian's official uniform hung on his fat body like a torn rag. His exposed skin was a grayish-black color and was even emitting green smoke.","This green smoke definitely carried the scent of roasted meat!","Crispy on the outside and tender on the inside, making it look like a cultivator undergoing a heavenly tribulation.","While Yue Fuguang thought it looked like a cultivator undergoing a tribulation, the rumors outside did not see it that way.","Rumors in the streets all said that Xu Qian must have done something so wicked that it angered both heaven and the people, provoking the heavens to send down a lightning punishment to discipline him!","As for this rumor, regardless of whether others believed it or not, there were a few people who believed most of it.","One was Concubine Mei, who had been having an illicit affair with Xu Qian. She thought that her incestuous relationship with her father-in-law was what brought about the lightning punishment.","Would she be the next one to be punished? So she went overnight to find her accomplice, the undercover servant boy named Shunzi in Xu Qian's courtyard.","The two conspired to sneak into the study tonight while Xu Qian was unconscious. Regardless of whether they could find any useful information, they would run away first thing tomorrow morning.","It could be said that even though she was scared half to death, Concubine Mei was still very dedicated to carrying out her mission as a spy.","Yue Fuguang could not help but shake her head and sigh. She was the ultimate workhorse! Even with her life threatened, she did not forget to pull off one last job before leaving.","The others were Huang Shouping, who had been farting incessantly since leaving the court today, and Zhang Tingji, who had been itching all over his body.","When Zhang Tingji and Huang Shouping met, they both saw each other's miserable state. Though they did not say it out loud, they could not help but mutter in their hearts.","Their current situation was clearly abnormal. They had sought out Sun Huajing, the head physician of the Imperial Hospital. After checking their pulses separately, he only shook his head. \"I cannot cure it, I cannot cure it!\"","He was just an imperial physician, not an immortal god. How could he undo the methods of Lord Divine Artifact?","Sun Huajing: I did not know I was this capable!","Huang Shouping looked awkwardly at Zhang Tingji, who was standing ten meters away, covering his mouth and nose, and occasionally scratching himself all over. \"Brother Zhang, is our situation because we offended that person?\"","He pointed his finger in the direction of the Yu Manor.","Zhang Tingji really wanted to shake his head in denial. The rise of the Yu family did not align with the interests of their Zhang family. Under his family's orders to investigate the situation of Prince Ming, he was also doing everything in his power to suppress the Yu family, especially that Junior Preceptor who was currently riding high.","He guessed that the latter instruction was mostly because the clan leader was acting on someone else's request.","After all, even if the eldest son of the Yu family, Yu Qingyu, had rejected the Zhang family's marriage proposal, the family would not necessarily insist on suppressing the Yu family's momentum just because of that."]},{"number":219,"title":"Chapter 219: Why Was the Judgment Made That the Liu Family's Daughter-in-Law Died by Hanging Herself","paragraphs":["At this moment, the itching all over his body made the words of denial on the tip of Zhang Tingji's tongue turn into, \"My thoughts are the same as yours, brother. That person might really be someone of significant background.\"","His itching, much like Huang Shouping's foul flatulence, had started right after the morning court session ended.","He knew his colleagues well enough; if they wanted to deal with him, they wouldn't use such prank-like methods.","Moreover, no one could poison them so accurately right in the imperial court. They simply didn't have the skill for it.","Most importantly, the doctors and witch doctors in his manor were completely helpless against it, and neither of them showed any signs of being poisoned.","The witch doctor, much like Sun Huajing, just kept shaking his head at him and bluntly stated that this was not the doing of a mortal.","Not the doing of a mortal? Looking across the entire Great Yan, the only person who barely had any connection to gods was that Junior Preceptor who had descended to the world by divine oracle.","And the three of them had targeted her at every turn during today's morning court...","Zhang Tingji waved his hand to dismiss the idle servants, then took a step forward... before taking half a step back, saying, \"Brother Huang, I believe that even if she wants to punish us, it shouldn't last too long. His Majesty is still watching!\"","Huang Shouping looked utterly unwilling. \"Brother Zhang, I only spoke up in support during today's morning court because I listened to your words, and now I've ended up in such a state...\"","Before he could finish his sentence, he felt a hot current rush from his abdomen all the way down to his tailbone, and a gushing wave of gas erupted with an indescribably foul stench.","His face was filled with grief and indignation. \"With me like this, how am I supposed to attend court tomorrow?\"","After saying that, without even glancing at Zhang Tingji, who had covered his mouth and nose and retreated dozens of meters away, he angrily flicked his sleeves and left the Zhang Manor.","As Huang Shouping hurried home, he made excuses for himself. All things considered, he had no grudge against the Yu family. His words during today's morning court were all instigated by Zhang Tingji.","Now, he planned to turn back before it was too late and go to the Yu Manor to apologize.","Therefore, while Yue Fuguang and the system were making their work plan for the next month, Cuiyu came to report that Lord Huang Shouping had come to visit, asking if she wanted to see him.","Yue Fuguang waved her hand. \"No!\"","However, remembering that the medicine the system had given him would lose its effect tomorrow, she added, \"Take him to my grandfather or father and see what this Lord Huang is visiting for so late at night.\"","[Host, could this guy surnamed Huang be here to apologize?]","'If he is, then he must suspect that his condition has something to do with us. It seems he isn't stupid.'","[If it weren't for the fact that this person died early and had no chance to participate in the later political chaos of Great Yan, I wouldn't have let him off so easily!]","Yue Fuguang turned around to hide her smiling face. At first, the system still remembered that it was a merit system, constantly advising her and urging her to be good.","Ever since they started enjoying gossip and doing tasks, it had slowly revealed its true nature. With all this fighting and killing all day long, who could have guessed that it was actually a merit system!","If it weren't for the constraints of the merit system that prevented them from casually harming people, they wouldn't even need Emperor Mingxi to take action; the two of them could have precisely eliminated some of the killable targets in their tasks.","Although they couldn't complete all the tasks, for thirty percent of them, as long as they solved the people creating the problems, the problems would be solved! And the points would be theirs!","Why bother nagging day after day! It was exhausting!","The word exhausting didn't even stay in Yue Fuguang's mind for more than a second before her soft snoring began to sound.","Above the Yu Manor, or rather, the Bright Moon Pavilion, a mass of green energy invisible to the mortal eye gathered from all directions, slowly forming a funnel shape that hovered above Yue Fuguang's bedroom.","Then, that green energy flowed slowly like water into Yue Fuguang, who was lying on the elaborate canopy bed, sleeping with a peaceful expression on her face.","System 07, which was in a semi-shutdown state in the system space, did not see that a small section of data in its code was slowly recovering.","The next day, just as Yue Fuguang stepped into the gates of the Hongwen Academy with Yu Ningxuan and Yu Ningxin, they ran straight into the Fourth Prince, whose face was flushed red with hidden anger.","'Little Zhu, how did this guy heal from his injuries so quickly? Could it be that the executioner went easy on him?'","Qian Gui, who had personally carried out the punishment by imperial decree, was currently accompanying the emperor at court. Standing quietly in attendance, he suddenly couldn't help but shiver, and his body seemed to grow a bit heavier.","That was the blame Yue Fuguang had just pinned on him!","[Master, you forgot. Fourth Master Xie's mother comes from South Yue. Although Concubine Xin's medical skills are not as good as Lan Xuan'er's, they are not much worse.","Treating his superficial wounds wouldn't take much effort.]","'If you hadn't mentioned it, I would have forgotten that there was this seemingly invisible concubine in the emperor's harem.","Could her year-round feigning of illness be to hide her medical skills?'","South Yue was famous for both medicine and poison. Many doctors, such as Zhang Huajing from the Imperial Hospital, had once gone to South Yue for further studies.","'The emperor really isn't picky at all. He even dared to take a royal daughter of South Yue into his harem.'","Seeing Yue Fuguang arriving from afar, Wei Ping had just lifted his foot to go out and welcome her when he heard this sentence.","Wei Ping promptly withdrew his foot!","Cough! How was he supposed to relay what he had just heard to His Majesty!","Emperor Mingxi: He regretted issuing the decree to the officials that whenever you hear the Junior Preceptor's inner thoughts, you must relay them word for word.","Sometimes, certain contents really had no significance for his decision-making! They would only anger him!","[Concubine Xin is actually the current Emperor Gan Sheng's cousin-aunt. When Concubine Xin entered the palace, Emperor Mingxi had only been on the throne for a few years.","In order to consolidate his imperial power, he naturally expanded his harem. More than half of your little classmates' mothers entered the palace during those years.]","Xie Zhiwei, who originally had a face full of annoyance, showed a momentary flash of hostility upon seeing Yue Fuguang. He quickly lowered his head, cupped his hands toward Yue Fuguang, and said, \"Zhiwei greets the Junior Preceptor!\"","His mother had told him to apologize when he saw Junior Preceptor Yue, but the faint pain coming from his buttocks made it impossible for him to utter any words of apology.","Yue Fuguang merely nodded at him as a greeting.","With her current status, she didn't need to feign politeness with anyone just to save face.","Her likes and dislikes were displayed clearly, and no one would step forward to say anything about it.","During the morning class, Wei Ping brought out many cases and told them to the students like stories.","Yue Fuguang also gained a superficial understanding of Great Yan's laws, though, of course, Wei Ping's detective stories were much more captivating than the laws themselves.","For the first time, Yue Fuguang did not doze off in class.","Looking at the Junior Preceptor with bright eyes, listening earnestly to the stories... to the lesson, Wei Ping couldn't suppress the smile at the corners of his mouth no matter how hard he tried.","Thinking of his colleagues saying that the Junior Preceptor loved to doze off in class—that simply didn't exist in his class!","Cough! Although his own role in the cases had been refined and beautified by him... the reasoning process and the punishments of the cases were entirely accurate!","Look, the Junior Preceptor was even raising her hand to ask a question. Ignoring the raised arms of the Seventh Prince and the others, Wei Ping only spoke to Yue Fuguang, \"Does the Junior Preceptor have any questions for this humble official?\"","\"Lord Wei, in the case you just mentioned about the Liu family's daughter-in-law hanging herself, what considerations was your judgment based on?\"","Wei Ping replied, \"Junior Preceptor, this case actually happened on the day of the Lantern Festival. Due to official duties, this humble official did not go to the scene."]},{"number":220,"title":"Chapter 220: Hurry up and find a way to clear Lord Shaoshi's name","paragraphs":["The on-site investigation was conducted by Lord Hu, who led the yamen runners and the coroner. Later, I reviewed their autopsy report and the on-site investigation records.","The conclusion that the Liu family's daughter-in-law committed suicide was based on the following points: the deceased's toes were naturally pointing downward, and there were no external injuries on her body.","There was only one strangulation mark on her neck, slanting upwards in a pulling shape.","There was a footstool beneath the deceased, lying not far from the body. The hemp rope used for the suicide was tied in an ordinary dead knot.","The room was clean and tidy, with no signs of a struggle and no missing valuables.\"","Yue Fuguang nodded. After a moment of thought, he asked again, \"Then, Lord Wei, have you verified the relationship between the Liu family's daughter-in-law, her husband, and other relatives?","Was the height of the footstool exactly reaching the position beneath the deceased's feet? Have the scratches on the crossbeam been examined?\"","Seeing that Yue Fuguang cared a lot about this case, Wei Ping couldn't help but ask, \"Does the Junior Preceptor feel that there is something suspicious about the Liu family's daughter-in-law hanging herself?\"","Yue Fuguang did not hide anything and directly voiced his doubts, \"Lord Wei mentioned that Madam Liu had two daughters and loved them dearly.","Madam Liu's husband is the only son in the family, and he has three older sisters who are already married.","However, her parents-in-law, as well as the children's father, did not like the two girls.","Madam Liu should have been very clear that if she were gone, her two daughters' lives would only suffer more harsh treatment.","It is said that a mother's love makes her strong. Without a fatal reason, Madam Liu would absolutely not abandon her two daughters and choose to die.","Furthermore, on the day of the Lantern Festival, she even took her children to the lantern fair, bought lanterns for her two daughters, and bought a wooden hairpin that she liked for herself.","Her eldest daughter once said that her mother had bought gifts, and they had agreed to take them back to their maternal grandparents' house the next day.","Also, the wooden hairpin she bought was found in her embrace, not on her head.","All of the above indicates that it was impossible for the Liu family's daughter-in-law to suddenly want to commit suicide.","In my opinion, this should be a murder disguised as a suicide.\"","Hearing Yue Fuguang's analysis, Wei Ping suddenly felt it made perfect sense. They had only focused their attention on the visible evidence on the surface.","But they forgot to carefully investigate the deceased's various behaviors before her death, which were completely inconsistent with someone so desperate as to commit suicide!","'Little Zhu, help me check if this Liu family's daughter-in-law was murdered?'","[Master, wait a moment, it will be done soon!] Fortunately, this case happened in the capital city, Shangjing, and the data of its Gossip System had been restored a little bit, so it wouldn't cost it much energy.","The recess had not yet ended when the system's message arrived. As soon as its voice saying [Master, I found it!] came out, some people who were originally chatting instantly quieted down.","The Seventh Prince and the Eighth Princess even returned to their seats and silently picked up a book.","Seeing this, the Fourth Prince, who had just come in from outside, couldn't help but sneer, \"Seventh Brother, I have only heard of reciting backwards fluently, but I have never heard of reading backwards fluently! Hahahaha.\"","Hearing him say this, the Seventh Prince realized that he was holding his book upside down!","His face immediately flushed with embarrassment, and he turned his head away, ignoring the mocking Fourth Prince.","Seeing his silent demeanor, Xie Zhiwei suddenly felt bored.","This Seventh Brother was a bit strange today. If it were in the past, he would have definitely argued with him a few times. Being so well-behaved today, could it be because...","He glanced toward Yue Fuguang's position and felt even more bored, instantly shuffling back to his seat feeling a bit down.","Even his fifth and sixth brothers had gone to the next class, while he, as an older brother, was still studying with little kids. Xie Zhiwei suddenly felt that his life was bleak!","'Little Zhu, how did the Liu family's daughter-in-law die?'","Having read so many detective novels in his previous life, he finally had the opportunity to put what he had learned into practice this time. Yue Fuguang couldn't help but feel a bit eager. Was armchair strategy actually useful?","[Master guessed right, the Liu family's daughter-in-law died from murder!]","Before it could continue, Yue Fuguang immediately expressed dissatisfaction with the system's wording, 'System, I wasn't guessing, it was deduction, deduction!'","[Alright, alright, the host is deducing, not guessing, okay!]","[Master, who do you guess the murderer is?]","'Someone from the Liu family, or rather, her husband?'","[How did Master guess... deduce that?]","The gossip-loving crowd, including Wei Ping, was also very curious. The Junior Preceptor seemed to already have an answer in his heart.","'Didn't Wei Ping say it? The room was clean and tidy, no valuables were missing, and the deceased had no defensive wounds.","The Liu family can be considered a moderately wealthy household, with servants and a gatekeeper. Outsiders generally wouldn't be able to sneak in.","Even if they managed to enter the Liu family, it wouldn't be just to kill a daughter-in-law who had no say in her in-laws' house.","Therefore, I presume it was committed by an acquaintance, and the deceased's husband is the most suspicious. Little Zhu, just tell me if your Master is right or not!'","[Hehehe, Master is completely right. The murderer is the deceased's husband, Liu Dalang, Liu Hong. That night, while his wife was fast asleep, he sneaked from his study into his wife's room.","He used a pillow to smother her until she fainted, and then hung her up to create the illusion of suicide by hanging.","If Wei Ping goes to check the scratches on the beam and compares the height of the footstool as you said, he will find the clues.]","After a burst of joy in his heart, Wei Ping felt a wave of shame and embarrassment. He prided himself on being very skilled in interrogating and investigating cases, but he never expected to be blinded by such a small case!","Just as he was thinking, he heard Yue Fuguang say, 'It seems that Wei Ping's professional skills need to be improved. I remember you have quite a few relevant books there.","He probably wouldn't understand the overly advanced ones. Give me the Collected Cases of Injustice Rectified written by Song Ci. I'll find a chance to give it to him to read, so there will be fewer unjust and false cases.","I like the phrase \"Speak for the living, assert the rights of the dead\" the most.'","[This is simple. In two days, it will be Wei Ping's thirty-fifth birthday. Master can give him the book as a birthday gift.]","Yue Fuguang nodded and praised, 'Good idea!'","Wei Ping was even more ecstatic in his heart, secretly giving a thumbs-up to the Lord Divine Artifact, and thanking the Little Immortal Lord over and over again!","Collected Cases of Injustice Rectified, being highly praised by the Little Immortal Lord, was clearly no ordinary book.","Grinning from ear to ear with his teeth showing, while his heart felt like it was being scratched by a cat in anticipation, Wei Ping wished tomorrow could be his birthday.","Wearing this grinning and teeth-baring expression, before he even reached the Dali Temple office, the news that Lord Wei Ping was suspected of having contracted a strange illness had already spread like wildfire.","Previously, there was Huang Shouping who kept passing foul-smelling gas, and Zhang Tingji who had to take a leave of absence because his whole body was itching. Now came Wei Ping. Some of the lords accepted it well, but others couldn't help feeling anxious and panicky!","Lord Wei had just returned from teaching at the Hongwen Pavilion. As for who was at the Hongwen Pavilion today, it went without saying for everyone.","Wu Yong, Feng Tang, and the others rolled their eyes at their colleagues who were acting like easily frightened birds. Their Junior Preceptor would definitely not take the blame for Lord Wei's condition.","In order to clarify the situation, they coincidentally headed towards the Dali Temple and happened to run head-on into Cai Xian, who was hurrying over.","The few of them cupped their hands in greeting. Without needing to say much, they all knew each other's purpose for this trip.","As soon as Cai Xian entered the door and saw Wei Ping's look, he couldn't help but say, \"I thought the rumors were wrong, but it turns out they're true! What did you hear from that person to make you put on such an expression?\"","Feng Tang said with a hint of condemnation, \"No matter what Lord Wei heard, you are being too frivolous. Now there are rumors outside that your illness was caused by the Junior Preceptor!","Hurry up and think of a way to clear the Junior Preceptor's name!\""]},{"number":221,"title":"Chapter 221: The Hatred of Child Murder and the Resentment of Physical Destruction","paragraphs":["Wu Yong pursed his lips and said to Wei Ping, whose rank was several levels higher than his own, \"Yes, Lord Wei. Although the Junior Preceptor doesn't fear these things, it still doesn't sound good, does it?\"","Wei Ping felt quite embarrassed after hearing them explain the ins and outs of the matter. He hurriedly recounted what had happened during the lecture earlier.","He added, \"I will take my men to the Liu family's residence shortly. Once the case is resolved, I will naturally clarify to the public that I received guidance from the Junior Preceptor today.","It was only because I was so astonished that I had such an expression.\"","Cai Xian, who often collaborated with Wei Ping on cases, had a flash in his eyes. No, he knew Wei Ping too well. A mere case wouldn't cause him to make such an expression; there must be something else going on.","So, he gave Wei Ping a sidelong glance and said, \"Old Wei, look, we've been colleagues for so many years, and now, because of the Junior Preceptor, we're all tied to the same rope.\"","He pointed at Feng Tang, Wu Yong, and the others, continuing, \"If you have something going on, you can't hide it from us. Whether it's good news or bad news, we'll face it together.\"","Feng Tang immediately caught on and nodded repeatedly, saying, \"Yes, yes, yes! Lord Wei, just speak your mind. We will definitely help if we can!\"","Wu Yong was a bit dazed, but he followed the crowd and nodded along.","Wei Ping thought to himself: I'd be a fool to believe you! Especially that old fox Cai Xian, he's incredibly shrewd!","Knowing he couldn't hide it—and frankly, not intending to—Wei Ping was actually itching to show off to those in the know!","He coughed lightly and said with a face full of joy, \"I heard the Junior Preceptor say that in a few days, for my birthday, she will give me a wondrous book called the Collected Cases of Injustice Rectified as a birthday gift!\"","Hearing that the Junior Preceptor was going to give Wei Ping a birthday gift, Cai Xian and the other two exchanged glances. Their eyes confirmed it—they were all burning with jealousy!","Not only did the Junior Preceptor remember this guy's birthday, but she also planned to give him a gift. How could the three of them, whose birthdays were still months away, not be jealous?","Full of envy and jealousy, they slowly surrounded Wei Ping. If they hadn't remembered that they were in the government office, and on Wei Ping's turf at that, he would have definitely been in for a beating!","At the very least, Cai Xian, as a Minister, wouldn't just stand by and watch his smug face without doing something!","Cai Xian was not just a Minister, but the Minister of Justice. With him in charge of the Ministry of Justice and Wei Ping heading the Court of Judicature and Revision, they were practically in the same line of work.","Collected Cases of Injustice Rectified—just hearing the name meant it was right up their professional alley!","He chuckled twice, finally unable to resist rubbing his hands together, and decided to try the diplomatic approach first.","So he discussed it with Wei Ping, saying, \"Lord Wei, once you get the book, could you lend it to me to read?\"","Wei Ping initially wanted to feign refusal to negotiate some benefits for himself, but then he heard Cai Xian continue, \"Look, given my relationship with the Junior Preceptor,","when my birthday comes in two months, I might also receive a gift. When that time comes, I will definitely share it with you, my good brother.\"","Wei Ping thought about it and realized it made sense. The Junior Preceptor was actually very easy to get along with and treated all of them quite well. This old fellow Cai Xian might really manage to score a birthday gift.","However, thinking of Cai Xian's special hobby, he couldn't help but say, \"What if the Junior Preceptor gives you a recipe? Like how to make some kind of pie!\"","Cai Xian was speechless!","It really wasn't impossible!","But at the thought of the fragrant, crispy, and crumbly meat pie, Cai Xian silently swallowed his saliva and said seriously, \"Does Lord Wei think the crumbly meat pie is not fragrant, not crispy, or not delicious?\"","The day after the Junior Preceptor taught him the recipe, he was demanded by a group of colleagues to bring the food that even the Junior Preceptor praised so highly for them to taste as well.","So, these people had eaten plenty of his pies under the guise of tasting them.","Before Wei Ping could say more, Wu Yong, who was swallowing his saliva, chimed in, \"The Junior Preceptor's recipe is naturally excellent. The crumbly meat pie is absolutely superb. I find it incredibly delicious.\"","Cai Xian felt as if he had found a kindred spirit and suddenly found the chubby Wu Yong much more pleasing to the eye. \"Lord Wu also thinks it's delicious, right!\"","He then glanced at Wei Ping again. \"Be straightforward, just tell me if it's a yes or no!\"","Wei Ping looked at the sky outside and, not wanting to entangle with him any further, readily agreed, \"Alright, it's a deal.\"","He cupped his hands to the group and said, \"Gentlemen, I still need to take my men to investigate the Liu family's residence, so I won't keep you any longer!\"","Wu Yong looked somewhat enviously at Cai Xian and Feng Tang, who were leaving with Wei Ping. It was a pity that this case had nothing to do with his department, otherwise he could have tagged along to watch the fun!","Wei Ping acted very quickly. By the time Yue Fuguang finished her classes, the officials passing by her hurriedly cupped their hands and bowed to greet her from afar.","Her two older sisters looked at her with starry eyes all the way, but Yue Fuguang was completely bewildered, her head full of question marks.","After listening to the system's explanation, she finally understood the whole story, which was related to the case from that morning.","Just because of this minor case, the Junior Preceptor's persona of being a godlike detective was inexplicably established!","Upon returning to the Yu Manor, Yue Fuguang ate and drank her fill, and then fell into a food coma from all the carbs. She hadn't slept for long when she heard the system calling her.","[Host, Chonghua and Zhou Yunxin are dead, and Bai Yu is dead too!]","\"They're all dead? When did this happen, and how do you know?\"","[Just over the past two days. I was checking the point balance just now and suddenly noticed that the points had increased by six thousand.]","\"Three people, so that's two thousand points per life. Isn't that a bit low?\"","[It's not low at all. Zhou Fushan was only one thousand five hundred, and Xu Changyue was three thousand. The others were even less than those two. The points might be higher when the Prince of Qi and the Prince of Ming die.","So getting six thousand points for these three is already pretty good! These don't even count towards the mission points; they are considered extra rewards, so you should be content, Host!]","Where you sit determines where you stand. She wasn't surprised at all that the system was speaking up for its own company. However, thinking about it, what it said made some sense. It was free points, and having some was better than having none.","So she asked about another matter. \"How did they die? Did Emperor Mingxi do it?\"","[After Bai Yu was secretly captured from Xie Zhiyao's marriage alliance procession by the men Huo Ying sent, he was locked up in the heavenly prison for interrogation and died from the torture.","As for Chonghua, when the Emperor heard that Zhou Yunxin was dead, he felt it would be meaningless to keep Chonghua alive, so he finished him off with his own hands.]","Yue Fuguang nodded. \"Taking revenge personally is indeed the only way to satisfy one's hatred. By the way, if Zhou Yunxin didn't die by the Emperor's hands, did she die of illness?\"","[Consort De did it. She poisoned her with One Day Heartbreak.]","\"Consort De? She seems to be just like the Fourth Prince's mother, Concubine Xin, an invisible person in the imperial palace. I've never even seen her.\"","[Master, Concubine Xin feigns illness all year round, and Consort De constantly practices vegetarianism and recites Buddhist scriptures without ever leaving her small Buddhist hall. Naturally, you wouldn't see them.]","Hearing the system call her Master, Yue Fuguang's eyes shifted, and she followed up on its words, asking, \"What kind of deep grudge does Consort De have against Zhou Yunxin?\"","[The enmity of murdering her child and ruining her health. Consort De's original name was Bai Weiyin. Not only did she have a beautiful name, but she was also extremely beautiful herself.","After she entered the palace, she indeed took away a lot of Emperor Mingxi's favor from Zhou Yunxin. From the very beginning, she was hated and envied by Zhou Yunxin, becoming a thorn in her side that had to be removed.","Only a few months after entering the palace and receiving favor, Bai Weiyin became pregnant. Later, according to the imperial physicians, it was a male fetus.","At this time, the Ninth Prince was only a year old. Zhou Yunxin was afraid that Bai Weiyin's son would take away the Emperor's favor from her own son, just as Bai Weiyin had done to her.]"]},{"number":222,"title":"Chapter 222: When you think about it, they are all her 'masters' wives'","paragraphs":["\"...when she was over six months pregnant, she was given an abortion drug. Because the drug was so potent, the fully-formed male fetus was miscarried, and Consort De's body was permanently damaged, rendering her unable to ever bear children again.\" 】","\"As expected, palace schemes are always bloody. Emperor Mingxi is such a scumbag! He is the root cause of it all.\"","【Master, do you want Little Zhu to cripple him?】 Yue Fuguang rolled her eyes. Just look at you, do you even resemble a merit system anymore!","Even if they were 'immortals', crippling a nation's emperor would still negatively impact the smooth progress of their mission.","Currently, the stability both inside and outside the Great Yan court was the most advantageous for them. Talking about personal morality with an emperor was like trying to teach morals to a rogue.","She wasn't that stupid.","Not to mention the distant past, just look at those capable emperors of the Xia Kingdom—which one of them didn't have flaws in their personal morality? Emperors were a species that simply couldn't be judged by the standards of ordinary people.","She believed her mind hadn't been warped by the sweet romance novels she read in her past life. Expecting an emperor to be devoted to one woman was the biggest joke of all.","Emperor Xiaozong of Ming, Zhu Youcheng: Then what am I?","Yue Fuguang: Your nephew from a collateral branch succeeded the throne because you had no heir, and your son was murdered and still had to take the blame. What do you think you are?","Reining in her wandering thoughts, Yue Fuguang decided that although she didn't plan to lay a hand on Emperor Mingxi, she could still scare him a little to make him behave.","Perhaps she had been thinking for a bit too long, as the people outside were anxiously pacing back and forth. Only then did she say unhurriedly, \"Let's wait and see. If he drafts concubines again, we'll confiscate his reproductive rights.\"","The inner palace was managed by the Empress Dowager and the Empress, so she couldn't criticize the inner palace. Otherwise, Emperor Mingxi would definitely use it as an excuse to push all the blame for poor management onto Empress Xu.","Therefore, it was better to stop him from holding a draft and let him make do with the current women in his harem.","【Alright then, let's give him one more chance. Hehehe, confiscating reproductive rights is what I do best!】","Yue Fuguang thought to herself, of course you're good at it, you've already taken away quite a few people's rights! Eunuch Qian has gained quite a few fellow comrades.","For ancient men, being unable to produce offspring was as agonizing as losing their lives. Moreover, this kind of pain was continuous, far more torturous than a swift death by the blade.","She believed the emperor would behave for a while and focus on governing the country properly, which would also allow her to complete her mission sooner.","Yue Fuguang was essentially treating the emperor and his officials as beasts of burden. She provided the technology, and they were responsible for development. It was a flawless plan!","Far away in the imperial palace, Emperor Mingxi, who was just thinking about slacking off and dumping the memorials in front of him onto the Crown Prince, suddenly shuddered. A chill rose from the soles of his feet.","He quickly dismissed the thought of slacking off and going to the inner palace to relax.","【Master, do you want to know whose hands Consort De's 'One Day Heartbreak' poison came from?】","Yue Fuguang thought for a moment. The only poison master they knew was Du Zhongxian from Nanyue, so she said, \"Don't tell me this 'One Day Heartbreak' is another one of Du Zhongxian's creations?\"","The system was a bit disappointed. The entire white dumpling in the system space wrinkled together, very dissatisfied with Yue Fuguang's correct guess. Who chats like this?","No wonder she was a wealthy, beautiful woman but still a single dog for twenty years in her past life. She was truly single by her own sheer ability!","Yue Fuguang suddenly felt her nose itch. She had a sneaking suspicion that someone was gossiping about her!","Although the host didn't play along as expected, thinking of the mission, the system cheered itself up. Making its voice sound as cheerful as possible, it continued: 【Master is so smart, you guessed it right away.】","\"Isn't this Du Zhongxian a bit too prolific? Given his status in the 'poison world', shouldn't his poisons be extremely hard to come by? How come his poisons are everywhere?","From the Great Yan court down to the common people, how many have been harmed by his 'works'?\"","【There actually is a reason for that, but we won't talk about that today. The poison was made by Du Zhongxian, but the poison in Consort De's hands wasn't bought from him.","The bottle in her hand was given to her by Concubine Xin. Furthermore, the abortion drug that Zhou Yunxin used to harm Consort De back then was also secretly delivered to Zhou Yunxin's hands by Concubine Xin.","Between Zhou Yunxin and Concubine Xin, one committed the murder while the other handed over the knife.】","\"Hearing you say that, does it mean the poison that killed the Crown Prince and the Emperor was also provided by Concubine Xin?\"","The system, which had been about to burst into laughter, suddenly choked on its words upon hearing Yue Fuguang's deduction. The words stuck in its throat, neither going up nor down. It felt so stifled!","Sometimes, having a host with too much 'experience' wasn't a good thing!","It suddenly missed the royal court. Back then, its host was a perfect sounding board, allowing it to fully indulge its desire to spill the tea.","The system was relatively emotionally stable. It gathered its feelings, forced itself to perk up, and said: 【That's right, she was the one who ordered someone to secretly deliver it to Zhou Yunxin.】","Afraid that Yue Fuguang would steal its thunder again, the system continued to output: 【She is also the only person in the inner palace who knows who the Ninth Prince's biological father is.","Her feigned illness isn't entirely fake either. Since she makes poison, it's inevitable that her body would be eroded by the toxins, so naturally, she isn't as healthy as an ordinary person.","However, recently, Emperor Mingxi has been sending her the fruits and vegetables produced in your greenhouse, and her health has slowly been improving.】","Yue Fuguang could already imagine how spectacular Emperor Mingxi's expression would be when he found out about this!","Thinking this in her heart, she didn't forget to add a sarcastic remark, \"The Emperor is surprisingly nice!\"","【Master, that head palace maid beside Concubine Xin named Yue Ying is actually a fully intact man.】 The system felt that the host's words weren't enough to anger the emperor to death, so it continued dropping bombs.","\"A man? The Emperor has been cuckolded again? Is the Fourth Prince's father...?\"","Her use of the word \"again\" was quite brilliant, sending a chill down the spines of the people listening outside!","【That's not the case. Xie Zhiwei is the Emperor's biological karmic debt collector, there's no mistake about that.","However, this Yue Ying hasn't been idle either.","He has bedded more than half of the palace maids in Xinrong Palace. Because Concubine Xin is the only high-ranking concubine residing in that palace, this news has never leaked out.","Those maids and eunuchs are all from Nanyue as well, so Xinrong Palace is essentially Nanyue's private turf within the Great Yan imperial palace. This is the result of the hard work of two generations—Gan Sheng and his father.】","\"Not only has the Emperor's court been infiltrated like a sieve, but his inner palace hasn't fared any better! Under such circumstances, it's quite impressive that the Great Yan managed to hold on for another eight or nine years!\"","【Yue Ying's contribution in all of this is paramount. The poisons all passed through his hands and were transferred several times according to his plan before reaching Zhou Yunxin.","This man is also a master at making and using poisons himself. He is an honorary disciple of Du Zhongxian, and Concubine Xin's poison skills were taught by him. Although the two are of similar age, they actually hold the titles of master and apprentice.】","\"No wonder he was able to bed more than half the maids in Xinrong Palace.\" Thinking of this, a strange thought suddenly popped into Yue Fuguang's mind.","She couldn't help but ask, \"Doesn't Concubine Xin feel awkward ordering these maids around? Technically, all these maids could be considered her 'master's wives'!\"","【Hahaha, Master is absolutely right!】 The system was completely awed by its host's train of thought!","【Also, the few young palace maids beside the Fourth Prince are all Yue Ying's daughters. Technically speaking, these people are also the Fourth Prince's elders, hahahahaha!】","When the system mentioned the palace maids, Yue Fuguang naturally thought of the eunuchs. \"Then the eunuchs beside him wouldn't happen to be Yue Ying's spawn as well, would they?\""]},{"number":223,"title":"Chapter 223: One is a Fake Palace Maid, the Other is a Fake Eunuch","paragraphs":["[There is one. Host, do you remember what Little Fuzi told you a few days ago? He discovered a eunuch named Xiao Yinzi secretly asking around about you.","He also mentioned that this Xiao Yinzi's identity was suspicious?]","\"I remember. He said Xiao Yinzi entered the palace right around the same time he did, and the two had interacted privately. Ever since Xiao Yinzi was transferred to serve in the Fourth Prince's palace, it was like he had become a completely different person.","This little eunuch was also secretly snooping for information about me.\"","[He wasn't wrong at all when he said Xiao Yinzi seemed like a different person. After the Xiao Yinzi he knew entered the Fourth Prince's palace, he was replaced by the current one, who looks eighty to ninety percent like him.","However, this Xiao Yinzi is just like his father: one is a fake palace maid, and the other is a fake eunuch.]","\"Is Emperor Mingxi indirectly helping Yue Ying raise his wife and child?\"","[The Fourth Prince is surrounded by his own people. Otherwise, as an unfavored prince with no real power, how could he accomplish those great things later on?","I have to say, among the emperors of the six nations, Gan Sheng is indeed an outstanding figure when it comes to scheming. His plot almost succeeded.]","Yue Fuguang nodded in agreement.","Among the emperors of the six nations, the only one who could compare to Gan Sheng in terms of craftiness and deceit was that short and squat emperor of Dongyi.","The conversation between Yue Fuguang and the system was soon presented on Emperor Mingxi's desk.","Crash! Clang!","Since Yue Fuguang wasn't present, Emperor Mingxi let loose and vented his anger.","The Crown Prince and Qian Gui exchanged a glance. Both felt that it was better for the Junior Preceptor to be enjoying the gossip in the royal court; that way, no matter how angry His Majesty was, he would have to hold it in.","Unlike now, where the two of them were the only punching bags present. They might very well suffer collateral damage at any moment!","The two lowered their heads, one lower than the other, trying hard to minimize their presence.","Xie Zhiyan looked at the tips of his shoes and his blue four-clawed python robe, sighing inwardly. His outfit today seemed a bit too bright, which wasn't conducive to turning invisible!","Sure enough, just as this thought crossed his mind, Emperor Mingxi's voice came from above, \"Crown Prince, go tell your mother to manage the inner palace well.","Especially...\"","Thinking of Yue Ying's possible methods, the Empress's people might not necessarily be of use against him.","He turned and ordered Eunuch Qian, \"Qian Gui, go find Shadow Two. Have him bring some men to keep a close watch on Xinrong Palace. Don't let a single fly escape from there!\"","The Great Yan imperial palace suddenly became relaxed on the inside but strict on the outside, with all areas heavily monitored by Emperor Mingxi's men.","Faced with the sudden appearance of countless watching eyes, Yue Fuguang didn't panic in the slightest.","She still leisurely led her two older sisters as they strolled toward the Hongwen Pavilion.","[Host, hasn't Old Master Yu found a study companion for you yet?]","\"It's not that he hasn't found one. It's just that there are too many wolves and too little meat. There are only two spots, but the number of male and female applicants combined is nearly a hundred. Tell me, how is he supposed to choose?\"","[Then does the host have any candidates in mind?]","\"I do, but I'll confirm it once I see them in person.\"","Tomorrow was the auspicious day selected by the Imperial Astronomy Bureau for digging up the potatoes. Commoners and the families of officials would all be present.","The location was at the Fengtian Hall, which was also the only place where commoners could get up close to the imperial palace buildings.","During every major sacrifice, to show the royal family's desire to share joy with the people, they would open up Fengtian Hall, the closest building to the inner palace within the Imperial City.","In Yue Fuguang's eyes, this was just the royal family wanting to show off and needing a free audience!","Upon arriving at the Hongwen Pavilion, Yue Fuguang didn't follow her two sisters to class. Instead, she was stopped by the Minister of Rites. After the situation was explained to her, she headed east, following Zhang Zhongping toward the outer perimeter of the palace city.","[Host, does this count as an advance rehearsal for tomorrow's event?]","Yue Fuguang silently replied, \"Of course it's an advance rehearsal! Right now, the streets and alleys of the entire capital city are spreading the news that Great Yan has discovered a crop that yields a thousand catties per mu.","Just watch, I bet more than half the people in the capital will flock over tomorrow.\"","When the two arrived at Fengtian Hall, Yue Fuguang found that she was once again the last to arrive. The monarch and officials of Great Yan had already lined up neatly.","Hundreds of people stood solemnly. Even the official uniforms they wore were ninety percent new. If you asked Yue Fuguang how she knew, it was because she saw that several impoverished officials standing at the back of the line weren't wearing their old uniforms today.","Yue Fuguang didn't feel the slightest bit of awkwardness for making people wait. Zhang Zhongping led her all the way to the front. As she passed the group of royals, she saw that even the long-bedridden Prince Ming had shown up today, sporting a pale face.","Prince Kang, who had been reprimanded, grounded, and demoted in title by His Majesty... Oh, he should be called Prince Jing now, Jing as in quiet.","Prince Jing had also come. As a senior member from the youngest branch of the family, this Prince Jing looked only a few years older than Emperor Mingxi and was exceptionally well-maintained.","It was just that the way these two looked at her was a bit strange. If looks could speak, their eyes would surely be hiding thousands of words.","Yue Fuguang had no interest in deciphering their thousands of words and didn't let her gaze linger on them for even a second.","Finally, she stood side by side with the Crown Prince. In front of them was Emperor Mingxi, standing on the jade steps.","With everyone present, Minister of Rites Zhang Zhongping and the Head Envoy of the Imperial Astronomy Bureau, Yun Tianxing, began to rehearse according to the schedule.","Although it was said that there was no need to offer incense, the Emperor had already done so before Yue Fuguang arrived. In front of the large incense burner, Xuanmingzi temporarily took on the role of the incense-watching boy.","Going through the entire procedure, even with the heaven-worshipping paper-burning segment omitted, took more than two hours. Even though she had a great physique now, standing completely still was much more tiring than walking for two hours.","Yue Fuguang turned around with a world-weary expression, only to see that some of the elderly officials, who were about the same age as her grandfather, hardly showed any signs of fatigue.","She couldn't help but secretly praise them: these old officials had incredible standing skills!","[Host, the morning court session lasts for two to three hours. This little bit of time is nothing to these old officials who are used to standing.","You're just finding it hard to transition from an easy life to a demanding one; you lack exercise.]","\"Don't you think it's because it's boring? Without any gossip to distract me, of course I get more and more tired the longer I stand.\"","[The big gossip naturally has to be saved for tomorrow.]","\"What's that?\" Yue Fuguang asked, looking in a certain direction.","Yu Chongshan followed his granddaughter's gaze and saw that inside and outside the grand hall named the Pavilion of Rare Treasures within the palace city, guards holding halberds stood in three layers inside and out.","The armor on these guards and the weapons in their hands actually looked better than the equipment of the escort guards who accompanied Xie Zhiyao for her political marriage.","The leader of these men was Shen Kang, someone she recognized. Seeing Yue Fuguang looking over, he cupped his hands in a respectful greeting from afar.","Before Yu Chongshan could reply, the Crown Prince behind them spoke up, \"The Pavilion of Rare Treasures is currently holding those eight pots of potatoes that were moved from the Junior Preceptor's residence yesterday.\"","\"It's holding potatoes? I thought it was holding some sort of treasure belonging to His Majesty!\"","Xie Zhiyan smiled mysteriously and lowered his voice slightly, saying, \"The things in this Pavilion of Rare Treasures all center around the word rare.","If you're talking about real treasures, those are only found in my imperial father's private vault.\"","As a son, Xie Zhiyan didn't hesitate in the slightest to sell out his own father.","Emperor Mingxi: Having you is truly my blessing!","Seeing that Yue Fuguang remained unmoved, he couldn't help but ask, \"Does the Junior Preceptor want to go in and take a look?\""]},{"number":224,"title":"Chapter 224: Do You Think Heaven Understands","paragraphs":["Yue Fuguang looked at his sparkling eyes and felt that this child must have been bullied by his old man, which was why he wanted to throw his father under the bus.","If she went in to take a look, how could she leave without taking some souvenirs with her?","Thinking of the contributions she had made to the Great Yan, going in to take a look wasn't out of the question. After all, her five-hundred-cubic-meter storage ring was still quite empty.","Yue Fuguang didn't possess the good quality of seeing through things without pointing them out. She asked directly, \"Did His Majesty bully you?\"","Xie Zhiyan was clearly taken aback by Yue Fuguang's directness. But thinking of the Junior Preceptor's personality, he instantly felt relieved and answered just as directly, \"Not me, but my mother, the Empress.\"","With huge scandals repeatedly breaking out in the inner palace, all related to his imperial father's concubines, his dad was obviously a bit triggered!","Yue Fuguang instantly understood. Thinking of the gossip she and the system had leaked last night, it was no wonder the Emperor had a face longer than a donkey's today.","The forced smile he squeezed out when he saw her was truly hideous!","However, for him to push all the blame onto the Empress was a bit too much! An emperor who didn't know how to reflect on himself clearly needed her to knock some more sense into him.","\"I'm a little tired today. How about you accompany me tomorrow? His Majesty wouldn't disagree, right?\"","With the Crown Prince here to throw his dad under the bus, he would definitely know which items inside were the most precious. Space was limited, so she would only take the most expensive ones!","\"By the way, Crown Prince, there will be many commoners tomorrow. Could enemy spies infiltrate the crowd? Do you have any preventive plans for the planting of sweet potatoes, corn, and potatoes?\"","Xie Zhiyan's face immediately turned serious. He replied, \"Please rest assured, Junior Preceptor. The first batch of seeds will all be planted in the imperial estates.","The second batch is planned to be planted first by the important ministers in the court, and then the imperial court will purchase the harvest from them to distribute as seeds to the commoners.","While the court and the public maintain strict information confidentiality, security measures around the fields and borders will also be increased to ensure that the superior seeds do not flow out.\"","Yue Fuguang nodded. It would be difficult to prevent them from leaking out entirely, but as long as the Great Yan could maintain an absolute lead for two or three years, relying on their current financial resources, they could build a strong and well-equipped army.","It wouldn't matter if the seeds leaked out after that. By then, according to her plan, it would be time for the Great Yan to expand its territories!","The great drought three years from now wouldn't just strike the Great Yan. It would be a natural disaster sweeping across all six nations, affecting the entire region, even though the severity would vary from country to country.","Natural disasters would breed man-made calamities.","The chaos would officially begin three years from now!","Thinking of her increasingly robust divine soul, she recalled the system telling her that many officials were worshipping her statues in their homes. Her incense offerings came precisely from these people.","Once the potatoes were dug up tomorrow, her reputation as the Junior Preceptor would become even more resounding. When autumn arrived and the sweet potatoes, corn, and potatoes made their debut, which commoner who relied on the land for a living wouldn't worship her?","Yue Fuguang, who originally didn't want to be famous and only wanted to complete her missions from behind the scenes, now acted like a star eager for fame because of the benefits the incense offerings brought to strengthening her divine soul. She was just afraid that others wouldn't know her name.","Time passed quickly. In the blink of an eye, it was the first quarter of the Chen hour the next day. Yue Fuguang stood beside the Crown Prince once again. Both faced east, watching the slowly rising sun gradually illuminate the entire land.","In front of them was a high terrace with jade steps. Upon it sat a large three-legged bronze cauldron, engraved with intricate patterns and texts.","Below it was a large incense altar. In the middle of the altar sat an incense burner, from which three thick, long incense sticks leisurely emitted wisps of blue smoke.","Slightly below the incense burner, on the left and right sides, offerings of the three sacrificial animals, tea, fruits, and pastries were placed.","Although Yue Fuguang and the others didn't need to offer incense anymore, the Ministry of Rites still didn't dare to omit the incense, candles, and sacrificial offerings meant for respecting heaven and earth.","Behind them was a dense crowd of people stretching as far as the eye could see. The system showed her a bird's-eye view. Starting from the Fengtian Hall and radiating outward, densely packed heads filled every street and alley of the capital city of Shangjing, extending for miles outside the city walls.","This crowd rivaled the foot traffic of certain famous tourist spots and train stations during the National Day holiday! As far as the eye could see, it was just people!","There were high-ranking officials and noblemen, as well as commoners in plain clothes. Old people held the hands of children, and women followed their husbands. Families brought their entire households, all craning their necks to look forward.","In reality, all they could see in front of them were motionless heads, and more heads.","Many people sat on the ground and began to eat their morning meal.","\"System, we still underestimated the allure that high-yield superior seeds have for the commoners. Nothing has even happened yet, and there are already so many people.","I don't even dare to imagine what the scene will be like when the corn and sweet potatoes are harvested.\"","[To the commoners, how could anything that fills their stomachs be a trivial matter! The people from your world are just too well-fed, which is why they forget that there are still many people starving.]","Yue Fuguang smacked her lips. Those words were truly irrefutable. The greatest hardship she had suffered in both of her lifetimes combined was during those days at the Zhou family.","At that time, the system was afraid she would kick the bucket, so it even took out loans to feed her. Strictly speaking, she hadn't actually gone hungry for many meals.","Following Eunuch Qian's loud and clear announcement of \"His Majesty arrives!\", Emperor Mingxi slowly walked out from the side hall.","At once, the officials turned solemn, and the commoners bowed their heads.","The moment Emperor Mingxi stood still, the resounding cheers of \"Long live the Emperor\" rose and fell like ocean waves, surging from the palace to the imperial city, and extending all the way from the imperial city to the outer city.","Wherever the sound passed, tens of thousands of commoners fell to their knees in prostration, like wheat being harvested.","However, the hundreds of officials of the Great Yan only bowed to Emperor Mingxi.","In previous years, on such grand occasions, they would have had to kneel and prostrate as well. But for some unknown reason, His Majesty had actually exempted them from this grand ceremony today.","Some people cast a glance in Yue Fuguang's direction. Could it be out of consideration for her?","Although Yue Fuguang really wanted to be famous right now, she didn't want to stand out like a sore thumb at a time like this. She was extremely satisfied that the officials could perform a bowing salute just like her.","\"Rise!\" Emperor Mingxi clearly used his inner energy for this word. It spread far and wide, as if he had used a loudspeaker.","At the very least, the commoners at the front all heard it.","Although the segment where the Emperor and the officials offered incense was skipped, the Ministry of Rites dared not be careless when it came to sending a message to the Heavens during the sacrifice.","Yesterday, they finally won Yue Fuguang's approval to keep the program of burning the sacrificial memorial to the Heavens, simply going through the motions.","Considering the presence of the commoners, it was understandable that the imperial court wanted to make things a bit more sacred and solemn.","Yue Fuguang agreed to it; as long as they didn't make her offer incense, it was fine.","Otherwise, to maintain her absolute authority, she would have had to blow up the incense burner!","The Minister of Rites solemnly unrolled the sacrificial memorial and began to read it aloud.","We humbly submit that the Sovereign of Vast Heaven nurtures all living beings and oversees all categories of life. Now, as the early spring farming begins and the southern fields are opened. Your subject risks death to report: the green jade is offered upon the purple altar, and the dark liquor is laid out in the pure temple. We dare to present our utmost sincerity, reaching up to the high heavens...","To be honest, with Yue Fuguang's shallow knowledge, she only understood a little bit of it. However, listening to Zhang Zhongping's rhythmic and cadenced reading, she actually found it quite hypnotic.","We only hope that the Imperial Heaven will show mercy, and the Sovereign Earth will manifest its spirit, granting us a year of abundant harvest, and blessing our multitudes of people. So that the granaries may be full and the people may know propriety and righteousness, and the world within the seas may be peaceful and bear your great blessings.","Your servant, overwhelmed with utmost trepidation and reverence, respectfully presents this memorial to be heard.","By this time, Minister Zhang's throat was noticeably dry. Fortunately, he managed to finish reading the letter to the Heavens before his voice cracked.","\"Little Zhu, do you think the Heavenly Dao can understand this?\"","[Master, before your memories were sealed, you could understand it too. Deities interpret a sacrificial memorial not by its words, but by the faith, sincerity, devotion, and reverence it carries.]"]},{"number":225,"title":"Chapter 225: Dig and Dig, Digging Potatoes","paragraphs":["The crowd's hearts stirred. As they watched Emperor Mingxi personally cast the sacrificial manifesto into the great cauldron to burn, their reverence deepened.","Those who had shrines at home thought to themselves that they must remind their families to be absolutely respectful and devout when offering Incense to the Little Immortal Lord.","Next came Emperor Mingxi's verbal decree to the civil and military officials, as well as the commoners.","In the middle of the Si hour, the thrilling moment to harvest the potatoes finally arrived.","As sixteen strongmen carried eight large vats of potatoes onto the high platform, a restless commotion began to ripple through the crowd.","Especially among the common folks, whose minds had been lulled to sleep by the sacrificial manifesto and the decree, they were instantly jolted awake. Each of them craned their necks, wishing they could stretch forward a few more meters.","A cacophony of voices rose and fell. If one listened closely, words like \"They're digging!\" and \"So many pots!\" could be heard.","The officials who were in the know were thrilled, their faces flushed with excitement, but they managed to maintain their composure. They thought to themselves that a yield of thirty shi should be possible.","Those who were completely clueless only fared slightly better than the commoners when they saw the large vats being carried up.","They remembered clearly how Yu Chongshan had stated with absolute certainty in the great hall that this thing called a potato could yield at least twenty to thirty shi per mu.","Compared to the two or three shi per mu yield of rice and wheat, if this potato was truly edible, even if it tasted a bit inferior, the Junior Preceptor deserved to enjoy the Incense offerings of ten thousand households.","Some in the crowd had burning gazes, while others had flickering, uncertain eyes. As they looked at the potato pots on the high platform and the small figure of Yue Fuguang standing below them, it was hard to tell what they were thinking...","The sixteen strongmen retreated to the side. From the back came Wang Shouchen leading the way, followed by two officials from the Court of Agricultural Administration, and over twenty people dressed as old farmers and rural squires.","Were these the witnesses Emperor Mingxi had found among the people? Truth be told, it was a good idea.","The potato yield was so vastly different from the current grain yield of the Great Yan Dynasty that if they didn't find some influential commoners and squires from the local areas, some people might genuinely not believe it.","Yue Fuguang was invited onto the stage. Zhang Zhongping was seen handing a tool resembling a trenching spade to Emperor Mingxi, bowing as he said, \"Your Majesty, please dig the first spade for our Great Yan!\"","Placed in front of Emperor Mingxi was a pot containing the best-growing potato plant. Although its leaves were turning yellow, the plant was massive. Everyone guessed that there must be quite a few potatoes growing underneath.","Emperor Mingxi couldn't help but tighten his grip on the tool Yue Fuguang called a trenching spade. Having seen his fair share of great storms, even he couldn't help but feel a bit nervous at this moment.","The palm gripping the spade was slightly sweaty, and his heartbeat was a few beats faster than usual.","Just as Emperor Mingxi's spade was about to touch the potato vines, he reflexively glanced at Yue Fuguang, who was looking at him with a calm expression, holding a spade of her own, waiting for him to start digging.","Yue Fuguang said, \"Rest assured, Your Majesty, the potatoes in your vat weigh at least three catties. You won't lose face. Hurry up and dig!\"","[Exactly! It's just digging up a potato, why dawdle! If he saw rice that yields fifteen or sixteen shi per mu, wouldn't he be too scared to harvest it?]","Fifteen or sixteen shi? And of a precious grain like rice!","The Junior Preceptor had seemingly provided their Great Yan with rice that could yield six or seven shi per mu, which was already excellent. As for rice that yielded fifteen or sixteen shi, they... they weren't... envious, really!","Yue Fuguang: If your eyes weren't so red with jealousy, I might have believed you!","Hybrid rice was inherently unsuitable for saving seeds, and the high-yield rice seeds she had deliberately chosen from the system mall would produce less than half the yield of Great Yan's native rice in the second year.","Therefore, she only planted some in her own Sancha land far off at the border. This would not only solve the food problem for the garrison troops but also trick any lawless scoundrels who dared to steal her rice.","[Host, do you think that when your rice is harvested, if someone really steals it to plant, they'll regret it to death?]","Its host was far too devious. It knew that the rice plants would still grow exceptionally well in the second year, but they simply wouldn't produce any rice grains.","The more hope it gave people in the early stages, the more despair it would bring them later on.","\"Taking without asking, is that my fault?\"","Meanwhile, Emperor Mingxi, whose heart had been tense and anxious, was instantly refreshed by the interruption of these two little ancestors. He returned to being that calm and majestic emperor.","Yue Fuguang: The emperor seems to be developing into a glutton for punishment; a little scolding and he's full of energy!","With Yue Fuguang's endorsement, Emperor Mingxi felt completely at ease. He smiled and said, \"Fuguang makes a good point. Then I shall start digging!\"","As for the people on the stage, apart from Zhang Zhongping and Wang Shouchen, who were accustomed to it and thought nothing of it, the others saw the casual way the Junior Preceptor spoke to their emperor.","Not only did His Majesty not take offense, but he also responded with a chuckle. They all couldn't help but be shocked, quickly lowering their heads to hide their expressions.","There were many rumors in the streets about this legendary Junior Preceptor who had descended upon divine decree. Seeing her today, she was indeed extraordinary.","Although they couldn't quite put it into words, they felt she was different from them mortals, especially the lotus mark on her forehead, which shimmered with brilliance in the sunlight.","It made those who saw it feel an urge to bow down and worship her.","Incense: It is indeed me exerting my power!","Emperor Mingxi had obviously practiced beforehand. Using the trenching spade, he first loosened the soil along the edges, then grabbed the potato vines with his left hand and gave a forceful pull.","Instantly, six or seven earthy-yellow potatoes at the roots of the plant were pulled out. The large ones were the size of an adult man's fist, while the small ones were the size of a child's fist.","Ah!","Hiss!","Oh!","Upon seeing what was beneath the seedlings, various gasps echoed around Yue Fuguang.","Tears even welled up in the eyes of those old farmers. They didn't cry out loud; they just wept silently, occasionally wiping the corners of their eyes with the sleeves of their ill-fitting clothes.","Their eyes, however, were completely glued to the potatoes in Emperor Mingxi's hands.","This scene made Yue Fuguang, who dreaded seeing people cry the most, feel a surge of sorrow. No matter where, life was never easy for the common folk.","The people here were especially pitiful; their only wish year-round was simply not to go hungry.","Wang Shouchen and the other officials weren't doing much better. Although they had anticipated this, seeing the potatoes dug out of the soil one by one still brought tears to their eyes.","\"Your Majesty, quickly weigh them!\" Prompted by Wang Shouchen, Emperor Mingxi's slightly trembling hands immediately plucked the potatoes off one by one and wiped away the dirt on them.","He gently placed them into the exquisite weighing pan beside him, and Wang Shouchen stepped up without hesitation to weigh them immediately.","His hands were shaking non-stop, and it was only with Zhang Zhongping's help that he managed to finish the weighing.","Three catties and two taels!","\"Three catties and two taels!\" Zhang Zhongping immediately shouted in a hoarse voice.","\"Three catties and two taels!\" Someone began to relay the message, and voice after voice passed on the weight of the first potato plant.","The commoners knelt on the ground to thank the heavens. Among the officials, some also kowtowed to the sky, while others bared their teeth, looking up at the sky with vacant eyes, as if there were potatoes up there too.","The more normal ones started dancing with joy, such as Wu Yuanjing and Ling Yinghua.","As for her grandfather, father, and uncles, they flashed their white teeth and grinned foolishly at her, their faces full of shared pride.","Yue Fuguang looked at the people going crazy with joy on and off the stage and frowned.","If these were potatoes from her hometown, this weight would indeed be quite a lot. But these were produced by the system, the best of the best, and the yield was supposed to be higher than those from her hometown."]},{"number":226,"title":"Chapter 226: So little, how are you going to eat it","paragraphs":["Moreover, it had been irrigated with the Spiritual Rain. If the yield didn't increase, wouldn't her Spiritual Rain Talisman have been a total waste of money!","\"That's not right. Why is the yield so low!\" Her muttering wasn't loud, but the people on the platform and those in the front rows below all heard it.","Gah! The people who were just laughing heartily choked on her words, letting out a sound like a duck honking.","Three catties and two taels was considered low? Judging by the plants, a single mu of land could easily grow over two thousand of them. Even with a conservative estimate, the yield per mu would be nearly fifty piculs!","The Junior Preceptor still thought it was too little. Truly, immortals did not understand the affairs of mortals.","Before the crowd could react, Yue Fuguang raised the trenching shovel in her hand and dug into the soil, digging out...","Eh? Sure enough, she dug out three more potatoes from the soil, two large and one small, and placed them on the scale, signaling Wang Shouchen to continue weighing them.","Wang Shouchen's hands trembled as he mechanically lifted the steelyard scale. Because of his shaking hands, he failed to find the balance mark several times. It was Zhang Zhongping who stepped up again, and with their cooperation, they finally got it right.","Emperor Mingxi leaned over to look at the weight, and then, with a slightly cracked voice, he shouted, \"Four catties and three taels!\"","\"Four catties and three taels!\"","\"Four catties and three taels!\"","Four catties and three taels! It was passed on thousands of times, spreading by word of mouth all the way to the outskirts of the city without a single mistake, which was a miracle in itself.","Hearing this weight, Yue Fuguang saw another scene transmitted by the system: hundreds of thousands of commoners were all kneeling on the ground, thanking the heavens for bestowing this life-saving grain.","At this moment, the system's highly displeased voice reached everyone's ears. [Master, these people are blind! It was clearly you who bestowed these excellent seeds, yet they only remember to thank the Heavenly Dao.","Does It deserve it? Watch me go settle the score with It! I guarantee I'll beat Its soul right out of Its body!]","Gah!","Someone was so frightened they hiccuped. After their initial shock, Wang Shouchen, Zhang Zhongping, and the others very obediently bowed to Yue Fuguang.","\"Thank you, Lord Junior Preceptor, for finding these excellent seeds for the people of Dayan!\"","\"Thank you, Lord Junior Preceptor, for finding these excellent seeds for the people of Dayan!\"","......","\"Thank you, Lord Junior Preceptor, for personally planting these excellent seeds for Dayan!\"","Um, the person in front, please keep in formation. The word 'finding' was quite appropriate, but as for 'personally planting,' there was no need to bring that up!","\"Lord Wang, Lord Zhang, please rise quickly! All you lords, please rise as well!\"","Old Mr. Wang was already in his sixties. Having him kneel to her made her feel somewhat unaccustomed, but as an 'immortal,' she had to appear exceptionally calm.","Especially since Yu Chongshan and his son were still kneeling below, and further away in the pavilion, the female members of the Yu family, led by Old Madam Yu, were accompanying the Empress Dowager, the Empress, and others.","It looked like they also wanted to stand up and follow suit in kneeling. The family members of other high-ranking officials were doing the same, regardless of anything else, they just needed to follow the lead of the lords of their households.","Of course, not everyone knelt. A small number of them looked at their kneeling colleagues in confusion, and someone let out a quiet sneer, \"Lord Zhao, you're following the crowd again!\"","Zhao Shen didn't even spare a glance at this fool. Couldn't he see that the first, second, and third-rank officials in front had all knelt? What right did a mere fifth-rank official like him have to put on airs? Just because his rank was low, was he not afraid of being stripped of his position!","You cannot discuss ice with a summer insect. Following the crowd was the ultimate survival method in the imperial court.","This survival tool had saved him many times, and he definitely hadn't chosen the wrong side this time either!","Besides, the Lord Junior Preceptor truly deserved their gratitude.","Just as the crowd rose, Emperor Mingxi and the Crown Prince, father and son, bowed simultaneously to Yue Fuguang. \"I, on behalf of the millions of citizens of Dayan, thank Fuguang for your life-saving grace!\"","\"Thank you, Lord Junior Preceptor, for your life-saving grace!\" Xie Zhiyan bowed deeply, even more respectfully than Bao Zihui offering a toast at his wedding.","As expected of a martial artist, his body was so flexible. In her past life, she could never have managed such a movement.","At a time like this, the fact that this was the first thing to pop into Yue Fuguang's mind meant she was genuinely a bit envious!","The people who had just been sneering at Zhao Shen were dumbfounded when they saw the actions of the Emperor and the Crown Prince!","Their Emperor and His Highness the Crown Prince treated Junior Preceptor Yue with such courtesy, not discounting her contributions regarding the potatoes in the slightest.","Then what they had just done...","Suddenly, their legs felt a bit sore, and they really wanted to kneel. What was going on!","With this beginning, there was no need to say more about what followed. Originally, the Ministry of Rites had brought in local squires and experienced old farmers from the villages and towns around Shangjing City to serve as witnesses and to have them dig up the potatoes themselves. This was meant to prepare them to promote the potatoes in the future upon their return.","Unexpectedly, they didn't even get a chance to lay a hand on them.","After the Lord Junior Preceptor and their Emperor worked together to dig up a vat of potatoes, the officials standing below swarmed over.","They begged the Emperor to let them participate in this potato-digging work that was so beneficial to their physical and mental health.","Of course, the elderly officials led by Wang Shouchen, as well as young and robust officials like Wei Ping, spoke very implicitly. The above was just Yue Fuguang's automatic interpretation of their words.","Zhang Zhongping closed his eyes. It was a mess, a total mess. How were they supposed to proceed with the rest of the schedule!","He glanced again at Wang Shouchen, who had already started digging the soil with his bare hands. For some reason, his own hands began to itch with the urge to join in.","Yue Fuguang caught a glimpse of Zhang Zhongping, who had been hesitating a second ago, using his nimble footwork and slender physique to quickly squeeze his way to the front of a large vat the next second.","She almost failed to maintain the unfathomable expression on her face. Minister Zhang had truly executed the phrase 'if you can't beat them, join them' seamlessly.","One second he had a look of deep-seated grievance, and the next he transformed into a groundhog, digging out an extra-large potato and grinning like a fool.","The Left Vice Minister of Rites looked at his Minister, who was laughing like an idiot, and silently took on the responsibility of the remaining procedures.","Looking at the potato vats that were almost completely emptied, he swallowed hard and told himself, 'I am carrying the banner for the Ministry of Rites. Today's ceremony cannot go on without me!'","Emperor Mingxi looked at his pillars of the state, who were buzzing around the seven large vats, arguing noisily over who got to dig first and whose potato was bigger.","He silently turned his back. He did not see Cai Xian, who had almost half his body leaning into the vat.","He did not see Wei Shouyi, whose head and face were covered in dirt. He did not see Ling Yinghua, who had one of his shoes squeezed off in the crowd. He did not see...","His ministers were all elegant and well-mannered pillars of the state!","Young, low-ranking officials like Wu Yong stared blankly at the big shots squabbling on the jade steps.","The intensity of this was even greater than their performance in the imperial court. It seemed that their superiors had been holding back when they verbally sparred in court.","With the enthusiastic help of the various lords, the eight vats of potatoes were 'smoothly' harvested, yielding a total of thirty-six catties and eight taels.","As soon as the news spread, the crowd fell silent at first, and then erupted like a boiling pot. The cries of the spectating commoners truly made it sound like a massive funeral procession!","After a period of futile effort to complete the remaining procedures, the Left Vice Minister of Rites followed his Minister and joined the celebrating crowd, crying and laughing at the same time!","[Master, they're acting like this just because they dug up a few dozen catties of potatoes. Is it really necessary?]","\"I don't know! Little Zhu, mortals have a good saying: you may not understand it, but you should respect it!\"","[Alright, potatoes do indeed have many advantages. People say they're hard to store for a long time, but that's just because they're using the wrong methods. Just like sweet potatoes, if you dry them into potato slices or make them into potato flour, can't they be kept for a long time?","They are both a vegetable and a staple grain. By the way, Master, four of these vats should belong to you, right? How do you plan to eat them?]"]},{"number":227,"title":"Chapter 227: How dare they disagree","paragraphs":["The words \"how do you plan to eat them\" exploded in everyone's ears. They were so busy being happy that they actually forgot half of the potatoes belonged to the Junior Preceptor!","Those who originally only had tears welling up in their eyes couldn't hold back anymore upon hearing this, and their tears streamed down.","It was fine for those who knew Yue Fuguang had saved potato seeds for them, but for those who didn't, it felt like someone was slicing off their flesh—their very own flesh.","\"Tonight, we'll have potato stewed with beef, hot and sour shredded potatoes, crispy potato pancakes, spicy cumin potato wedges, hot and sour potato noodles...\" As Yue Fuguang listed over a dozen dishes, quite a few people disappointingly gulped, their stomachs suddenly rumbling with hunger.","Yu Chongshan looked rather melancholic at the dozen or so catties of potatoes he was carrying. This meager amount probably wouldn't be enough for his granddaughter to devour tonight!","The Crown Prince was the most quick-witted. He leaned in close to Yue Fuguang and asked, \"Lord Junior Preceptor, since the potatoes have been successfully harvested today, shouldn't we proceed with a tasting?\"","\"A tasting?\" What was there to taste? Hadn't she already eaten them before?","Looking at Xie Zhiyan's eager eyes, uh... it seemed they really hadn't tasted them yet.","Glancing at the commoners outside the field who hadn't dispersed but were instead gathering closer, she continued, \"Since I was the one who found the potatoes, naturally, I should be the one to taste them.\"","She gazed at the Great Yan commoners in the crowd, each dressed in coarse cloth, their skin tanned dark from years of hard labor.","The originally sorrowful eyes of these young and old people were reignited by the new crop, the high-yielding potatoes, filling with a vibrant will to live.","She paused for a moment, and ultimately addressed the crowd, \"Potatoes have a high yield. The imperial court has just planted them for the first time this year. Once we figure out the planting patterns and save enough seeds...","...we will start promoting them among the commoners next year. Everyone, go back and tend to your fields well. If you want a bountiful potato harvest, it will still depend on the fertility of the soil.\"","Hearing her state so affirmatively that they would be able to plant them next year, several elders took the lead and knelt to thank Yue Fuguang.","\"This humble old man thanks Lord Junior Preceptor for this life-saving grain!\"","\"Thank you, Lord Junior Preceptor, for your life-saving grace!\"","Thank you...","\"Everyone, please rise!\"","Facing the massive crowd kneeling before her, Yue Fuguang looked incredibly calm, perhaps even a bit aloof—that is, if one ignored the fact that she was curling her toes so hard in sheer embarrassment she could have dug a three-bedroom apartment in the ground!","\"It's time to head back!\" Walking briskly as if riding the wind, she headed towards the palace. It really wasn't easy to become famous; first and foremost, one needed a thick skin.","[Master, didn't the Emperor and the others discuss having the court officials plant them first next year, and only promoting them to the commoners after saving enough seeds?]","The monarch and officials of Great Yan: Right, right, right, that's exactly what we agreed upon earlier!","\"I suddenly changed my mind. Next year, we'll slowly start promoting them from the capital. As for the seeds, we can just go cast a couple of spiritual rain showers on the imperial estates.","Wouldn't that boost the yield? Besides, if I want the commoners to plant them first, would they dare disagree?\"","Yue Fuguang swept her gaze over the people around her.","Wherever her eyes landed, everyone silently lowered their heads, not daring to meet her gaze.","Yet their hearts were pounding wildly. When the Junior Preceptor looked at them so calmly, it was truly terrifying! Scared to death.jpg","Once Yue Fuguang turned around, Emperor Mingxi and his officials exchanged a glance. Whatever the Junior Preceptor decided, they naturally had to execute it to the letter!","After the silent exchange of glances between the monarch and his subjects, Emperor Mingxi leaned over and asked, \"Fuguang, you just mentioned promoting them to the commoners next year. Will all three types of grain be promoted together?\"","Yue Fuguang shook her head. \"It's better to divide it by region. Elder Lord Wang has inspected the trial planting areas for the seeds; he knows best what is suitable to plant where.\"","After thinking for a moment, she couldn't help but remind him, \"Your Majesty, it would be best to establish a promotional team to travel across the country and properly disseminate the knowledge related to these improved seeds, lest someone takes the opportunity to mislead the commoners.","Ideally, you should also publish a newspaper once or twice a month to increase the promotion of the seeds and the imperial court's policies.\"","\"A newspaper? What is that?\" Emperor Mingxi heard this new term for the first time and asked with some curiosity.","Yue Fuguang then explained what a newspaper was, how to run one, and what its benefits were. This could be considered the longest speech she had given since arriving in Great Yan.","Emperor Mingxi and the officials listened with continuous gasps of amazement, a shrewd light flickering in their eyes. A newspaper—the mouthpiece to control public opinion!","Imperial power rarely reached the rural villages, but with this newspaper, and by setting up newspaper reading stations everywhere, even illiterate commoners would be able to learn about the court's decrees in a timely manner.","Especially the agricultural knowledge provided by Yue Fuguang, which could be published in the newspaper for the commoners to learn. As long as they reaped the benefits from what they learned in the newspaper,","they would take the initiative to seek out the newspaper for information, without worrying about obstruction from those with ulterior motives.","Having finished discussing one serious matter, Emperor Mingxi automatically switched the topic to another: what were they going to eat later?","\"Fuguang, how about your potatoes be cooked in the imperial kitchen? We, the monarch and officials, can taste them together, which will also facilitate future planting.\"","What the heck did tasting them have to do with facilitating planting?","However, she was a kind person, so she didn't expose the Emperor's flimsy excuse. \"Your Majesty, the dishes I want to make are not something the imperial chefs know how to cook.\"","\"That is but a trivial matter. I will immediately send someone to the Yu Manor to invite your cook.\"","He said he would send someone immediately, but in reality, the person dispatched to the Yu Manor was already almost at its gates.","The one sent to invite the cook was Shen Kang. Emperor Mingxi had promised his nephew an extra seat at the table later.","Since his imperial uncle promised to save him a seat, Shen Kang went wild with joy. Riding his prized horse that could \"travel a thousand miles a day,\" he dashed madly toward the Yu Manor as if his life depended on it.","Finally, he wouldn't have to stand while others sat, or watch while others ate. Of course Shen Kang had to seize this rare opportunity!","Seeing that Emperor Mingxi was dead set on hosting a meal, Yue Fuguang just treated it as a working lunch and followed the crowd toward the Hall of Delicacies.","Looking at the massive crowd, Yue Fuguang tossed aside the concern of whether there were enough potatoes. Anyway, she wasn't the one treating them, so it wasn't her place to worry.","Still, she couldn't shake the feeling that she had forgotten something!","Trailing behind her, Xie Zhiyan's eyes flickered slightly. He wanted to remind Yue Fuguang of the word \"treasury,\" but seeing his royal father walking side by side with the Junior Preceptor, he shrank back.","Thinking of his royal father's future plans for the Junior Preceptor, it seemed even better than a trip to the treasury. Although she was a \"deity\" descended to the mortal realm,","since she was walking in the mortal world, she couldn't lack the corresponding status and position. Being offended by an idiot like his fourth brother must absolutely never happen again!","It didn't take long before the monarch and officials of Great Yan smelled and saw the rich aromas of the potatoes cooked into various dishes.","Why was it smelling and seeing instead of eating?","It was simply because there were too many mouths to feed and not enough food. Some of the officials witnessed the deliciousness of the potato dishes but had no chance to even take a bite.","Of course, this did not include Yue Fuguang and His Majesty the Emperor, who were eating so heartily that their mouths were glistening with oil.","Just as Yue Fuguang was feasting with the Emperor, the news that Great Yan had a miraculous grain yielding five thousand catties per mu spread through the crowds, from one to ten, and from ten to a hundred. In just a few days, rural villages and towns hundreds of miles away had all heard this monumentally good news.","Dozens of miles outside the capital, in a town named Shangxi, there was an ordinary grocery store called Chen's Groceries.","It was noon, yet a group of commoners were neither working nor eating; instead, they were all gathered in front of Chen's Groceries."]},{"number":228,"title":"Chapter 228: Major epidemics often follow great disasters.","paragraphs":["\"Old Man Chen, how many statues of the Junior Preceptor do you still have today? I've been waiting for a good while, and I must invite one back home today no matter what.","My wife is giving birth in the next couple of days. If I don't invite the Junior Preceptor home, I won't have peace of mind!\"","A man in the crowd wiped the sweat from his forehead, desperately squeezing to the front, and asked Old Man Chen in the shop with an anxious look.","Someone behind him pulled him back and said, \"Liu Tietou, get up. The Junior Preceptor is in charge of farming. For your wife's delivery, you should pray to Madam Jinhua. What's the use of seeking out our Junior Preceptor?\"","\"Exactly! The Junior Preceptor is the god of grain. Tietou, don't add extra burdens to the gods.\"","Someone \"kindly\" pointed the way for Liu Tietou, \"Tietou, in Oil Press Alley, Mafuji has statues of Goddess Jinhua. Go there to invite one.","The Ma family's carving craftsmanship has been passed down for several generations, so you can go invite one with peace of mind.\"","Liu Tietou shook his head like a rattle drum. \"No! Old Man Chen is someone who has seen the Junior Preceptor up close. I trust the statues he carves!\"","Who cares if you trust him or not? We trust him ourselves!","Old Man Chen was truly lucky. With so many people around, he somehow managed to squeeze to the very front and even got the chance to kowtow to the Junior Preceptor. Now, he doesn't even need to run his grocery store anymore. Just by carving the statues of the Junior Preceptor full-time, he can feed his whole family.","Such scenes of \"inviting gods\" were constantly taking place in the villages and towns surrounding the capital of Shangjing, and there was a trend of it slowly spreading outward.","And along with the popularity of inviting gods, \"A Hundred Ways to Eat Potatoes\" also became widely circulated in the streets, describing the deliciousness of potatoes as something found only in heaven and unmatched on earth.","There were no less than a hundred poems written to describe the delectable taste of potatoes. As for the poems, they were naturally penned by the esteemed officials who had seen and smelled them but had never actually tasted them.","Many down-to-earth verses were even compiled into nursery rhymes by thoughtful individuals for children to sing.","\"System, the sensation in my divine soul has become more distinct these past two days.\"","[Host, this means that your words from that day were not spoken in vain. Many people remembered your appearance. Now, the statues and portraits of you on the market don't differ much from your actual self.]","If things continued this way, when the once-in-a-century great disaster in the eighth year of Yuankang truly arrived, the host might not even need many rain-summoning talismans and could resolve most of it relying on her own power.","\"Have you prepared the prescription?\" Yue Fuguang didn't think that far ahead, but instead focused on the upcoming task.","[Rest assured, my data has generated the formula based on the existing types of herbs in Great Yan, and the selected herbs are all the most common and ordinary ones.]","\"Then let's begin!\"","Meanwhile, in the imperial court, the Minister of Revenue, Dong Qianli, was reporting to Emperor Mingxi on the statistics of the money and grain expended by the imperial court for the snow disaster earlier that year.","The expenditure of nearly one million taels of silver was the amount spent even after early preparations had been made to reduce losses.","In the original timeline, the state treasury was empty. Even if the imperial court had taken out more than half of its silver, it still would have been unable to provide relief to all the disaster victims. The financial crisis caused the relief efforts to lose momentum, which consequently triggered multiple rebellions.","After reporting the expenses, Dong Qianli continued, \"Your Majesty, during the early stages, the freezing weather made excavation difficult, leaving many corpses still buried under the collapsed houses.","Now that spring has arrived and the weather is warming up, although various prefectures and counties have intensified their excavation efforts, due to limited manpower, the dead cannot be buried in time. This humble subject fears that this might lead to... an epidemic!\"","Although Dong Qianli was extremely reluctant to say those two words, he had consulted the Imperial Academy of Medicine and also had years of experience dealing with various natural disasters.","He knew full well that those corpses were the source of disease. If not handled promptly, the consequences would be unimaginable.","[Master, after a great disaster, a great plague is bound to follow.]","Emperor Mingxi's heart tightened. Dong Qianli's speculation was not unreasonable to begin with, and now even the Divine Artifact Lord was saying so. Emperor Mingxi could not help but wonder if this had occurred in the original timeline...","\"Not enough manpower? I remember the refugees should still be in the temporarily built relief shelters, right? Aren't these all ready-made laborers?","Is the imperial court just feeding them watery porridge every day for free? Don't they know how to provide relief in exchange for labor? Those who want to eat their fill will naturally work actively.","As for those who want to be lazy and refuse to work, just give them enough water to feel full so they won't starve to death. It's such a simple matter.\"","Yue Fuguang felt that her current way of speaking sounded quite like the bosses of certain companies in her past life. However, if she didn't do this, those hardworking people who originally could have eaten their fill would be dragged down as well.","If this dragged on any longer and the epidemic became rampant, resulting in the deaths of too many people like before, it would affect the calculation of her task points. Therefore, she had to intervene in this matter.","Especially the children and the elderly. In these few prefectures, the population loss after that epidemic almost caused a generational gap.","Losing a massive amount of the population even before the drought arrived was absolutely unacceptable!","Relief in exchange for labor? Dong Qianli's eyes lit up. It wasn't that he hadn't thought of it, but the laws and regulations of the imperial court were set as such.","It had never been done in previous years, so naturally, he didn't dare to propose it lightly.","But now that it was proposed by the Junior Preceptor, he couldn't help but look up at His Majesty. Emperor Mingxi subtly nodded his head.","[Exactly. The roads here are so poor. You're feeding these people for nothing, yet you don't know how to take the opportunity to pick out some hardworking and willing ones to repair the roads.","You should also let them earn more rations for their families, which is much better than starving together with those lazy bums.]","Everyone looked embarrassed. Since ancient times, disaster relief had always been like this: the imperial court distributed porridge, and the commoners awaited aid.","They had never thought of using this labor force to do anything else.","After all, building bridges and paving roads had traditionally been done by the imperial court assigning corvée labor to the commoners. The officials responsible for disaster relief had no authority to do these things, as it involved issues of jurisdiction.","If the Junior Preceptor hadn't pointed it out today, even if someone had thought of it, such as Dong Qianli and the others, they wouldn't have dared to speak up easily.","\"By the way, Little Zhu, you just said that after a great disaster, a great plague is bound to follow. Did you mean that an epidemic will break out in the upcoming prefectures and counties of Great Yan?\"","[Master guessed correctly. Because the cases of the four major families were solved in time, the relief efforts for Great Yan's snow disaster this time were also timely, and far fewer commoners died compared to the original timeline.","However, just like in the original timeline, the epidemic is inevitable! I just don't know if it will be like before, where so many people died from the epidemic that nine out of ten houses in many villages and towns were left empty!]","The epidemic is inevitable? Nine out of ten houses empty!","Hearing these words, many officials stumbled on their feet. A few elderly officials would have definitely fallen if they hadn't been supported by their colleagues beside them.","If one were to ask what they feared the most in governing the country, the plague would definitely take a spot in the top three.","The main reason was that the plague killed too many people, was too difficult to control, and it didn't distinguish between the noble and the lowly! Whoever caught it would die!","Emperor Mingxi's face turned even more ashen. He had just obtained high-yield fine seeds and was preparing to accumulate strength relying on the immortal grain, and then fully display his ambitions.","He hadn't even been happy for a few days before he was suddenly told that a plague would break out in Great Yan, and the kind that would leave nine out of ten houses empty at that. Who could endure this!","He didn't erupt on the spot solely because the accumulated prestige of the two ancestors was too heavy, and there were also a few mature and prudent officials who reacted first, staring at him with burning gazes.","Emperor Mingxi: I don't dare to move, I completely don't dare to move!","Ahem! Of course, We are not afraid of them. After all, these people are the pillars of the imperial court, Our right and left hands. Their opinions cannot be ignored, cannot be ignored..."]},{"number":229,"title":"Chapter 229: A Disaster Both Natural and Man-Made","paragraphs":["Thanks to the book friend Zheng Luoyun of Tianji City for rewarding 10 chapter-urging talismans, here is a special bonus chapter.","For those who lost control of their facial expressions, their inner emotions were written all over their faces. They were utterly terrified, yet no one doubted the truthfulness of the two ancestors' words.","System: No helping it, this is what you call a good reputation!","Yue Fuguang lowered her head and played with the jade beads in her hands, kindly asking the question that was on everyone's mind.","\"Little Zhu, why are you so certain that an epidemic will inevitably break out in Great Yan? Hasn't the imperial court already started digging up and burying the corpses? Although spring has already begun, a few days' delay with the bodies shouldn't matter, right?\"","Many people frantically nodded in their hearts. Yes, yes, yes! If we act a bit faster and mobilize the commoners, we can definitely finish disposing of the corpses before the weather gets hot and they start to rot.","[Master, it is because this epidemic that sweeps across multiple provinces and counties in Great Yan is both a natural disaster and a man-made calamity. As for the natural disaster aspect, the sovereign and ministers of Great Yan have already minimized its impact. However, the man-made calamity has not been resolved. Therefore, Little Zhu says that the epidemic will definitely arise!]","\"There's a man-made calamity in this too? The Four Great Families were the man-made calamity during the snowstorm, and there's another one in the epidemic?\"","Emperor Mingxi gripped the golden armrest tightly with his right hand. The carved dragon head on the silver-plated gold armrest of the dragon throne showed faint signs of deforming.","Dragon armrest: You win, you're strong. You don't dare offend those two ancestors, so you take your anger out on a dead object like me. Is there not a single breathing soul who will speak up for me?","Everyone: Why are there so many people scheming behind the scenes? Not a single one of them rests. Just how fragrant is the Xie family's throne? Exactly how many people want to replace them?","Emperor Mingxi: I'd like to know too!","[Master, this time the epidemic is primarily man-made, and secondarily a natural disaster. If someone hadn't deliberately mixed infected individuals among the refugees, it wouldn't have led to the epidemic breaking out simultaneously in multiple places later on with such ferocity. The True Records of Great Yan records that in the early spring of the fifth year of Yuankang, epidemics broke out in multiple provinces. It also describes the tragic devastation with the phrases 'entire households perished' and 'families completely wiped out'!]","Entire households perished! Families completely wiped out!","These words continuously looped in the ears of the sovereign and ministers of Great Yan, and the entire grand hall fell dead silent. Cai Xian, who had been reporting on the subsequent trial matters of the Four Great Families, opened his mouth, only to find that he couldn't make a single sound.","Elder officials like Bao Yuanjun, Wu Yuanjing, and Wang Shouchen even staggered back two steps, their violently trembling bodies caught just in time by the people behind them.","The abnormal behavior of these people was noticed by certain observant individuals, making them even more certain that something they were unaware of was happening in this royal court.","Otherwise, Minister Cai's requested final trial and sentencing for the Four Great Families could be considered quite standard; it was impossible for so many people to have such massive reactions all at once.","The strange behavior of these people couldn't simply be explained away by saying they were 'having an episode'!","Imperial Physician Sun Huajing claimed that some of them had hidden ailments, but why did they find that so hard to believe!","The hissing sounds of sharp intakes of breath and the gasping noises that sounded like people were dying made it feel as if they were in a snake pit or at a memorial service.","Yue Fuguang was right in the middle of it all. If she still couldn't notice that something was wrong with them, her playing deaf and dumb would be too obvious!","\"Little Zhu, what's wrong with these people? Cai Xian just wants to use torture on the family heads, so why are they making those faces?\"","[I don't know! Could it be because the torture methods he mentioned are too cruel?]","\"Could it be even more cruel than branding, the nail chair, rat torture, or the paper-on-face suffocation? Look at them, their faces have all gone pale!\"","Everyone looked utterly bewildered upon hearing these punishments. Why did the hair on their bodies stand on end just from hearing the names!","Although they had their doubts, they didn't have time to dwell on what on earth those things were. The most urgent task was to dispel the suspicions of these two ancestors.","Ling Yinghua was the first to step forward and say, \"Reporting to Your Majesty, this humble subject believes that Minister Cai's words are somewhat inappropriate. Although the Four Great Families are at fault, those who deserve death should be killed, and those who deserve trial should be tried. However, wouldn't the abuse of severe torture raise suspicions of extracting confessions through force?\"","Shang Xuewen also stepped out of the ranks and said, \"Your Majesty, this humble subject feels that Chancellor Ling's words are reasonable. My fellow colleagues surely share the same thoughts as this lower official.\"","He pointedly looked at a few officials whose facial expressions had been the most obvious.","Those few people immediately caught on and bowed one after another, saying, \"We second the motion. Minister Cai's proposal is truly frightening!\"","As they spoke, they even wiped the cold sweat from their foreheads. It seemed they really were quite frightened!","[The benevolence of women! These officials are too pedantic, especially that Chancellor Ling! If the people of the Four Great Families hadn't been caught now, the commoners of these provinces wouldn't have known peace for the next few years!]","Ling Yinghua: Who did I provoke? I just came out to smooth things over, so how did I get called out and scolded!","He looked at Emperor Mingxi with a bit of grievance. Emperor Mingxi pressed a hand to his lips. How novel! Even I don't dare talk back when I get scolded, do you think you'd be an exception!","Shang Xuewen and the others silently stepped back and hid within the ranks. Lord Divine Artifact can't see me, can't see me!","Ling Yinghua: No loyalty at all! Who did I do this for!","Emperor Mingxi: You'll get used to it!","Ling Yinghua: I can't get used to it at all!","\"It's normal. Some old fogeys just read too much and turn their brains rigid! Let's not talk about them. Tell me, who exactly does this man-made calamity refer to?\"","[Master wants to intervene in this matter?]","\"Little Zhu, haven't you noticed that your master's divine power is slowly recovering?\"","[Master possesses divine power in a mortal body?]","\"Not quite to that extent. I can just do some things that mortals cannot. However, I've only recovered a tiny sliver, so it's normal that you didn't notice.\"","[Master, that's not right. Your physical body is just that of an ordinary mortal, so how could your divine power recover? How can a mortal body withstand Master's divine power?]","\"It's because I have received the power of incense offerings. With my primordial spirit controlling this mortal vessel, I can perform extraordinary feats.\"","[Then what does this have to do with you interfering in the epidemic?]","\"Little Zhu, where do you think my incense offerings come from?\"","Wu Yuanjing and the others, who offered three sticks of incense to Yue Fuguang at home every day, silently thought to themselves: Could it be because of the incense we offer?","\"Naturally, it comes from the mortal commoners. By taking care of this matter, I can consider it settling the karma.\"","They finally understood. The Little Immortal Lord had recovered a bit of divine power because of their offerings, but she was anxious to settle this karma.","She wanted to cut ties with them! That absolutely wouldn't do!","The sovereign and his ministers exchanged a glance, everything understood without words.","Since the Little Immortal Lord wouldn't board their boat, they would board hers. The incense must not be broken, and the offerings would not lessen. If she settled the karma today, they would renew it tomorrow, renew it abundantly!","It seemed it was time for the title of Junior Preceptor to resound throughout all of Great Yan! Perhaps her title as an Immortal Lord could also slowly spread...","With the offerings from the millions of commoners in Great Yan, and the imperial court funding the construction of temples everywhere, creating a flourishing stream of incense, how would the Junior Preceptor ever be able to cut off this karma!","Wanting to wash her hands of them and run away at the drop of a hat like she did before? That definitely wouldn't do!","[Then how does Master want to handle this? Although Little Zhu brought some panaceas and miraculous medicines, there are so many mortals that it won't be enough.]","Bros, please move your wealth-bringing little hands and urge for more updates. The stats are getting worse and worse. Don't let chapters pile up before reading, or the book will die! Thank you, folding hands in respect."]},{"number":230,"title":"Chapter 230: A Stroll in the Eastern Market","paragraphs":["\"Just give me the prescriptions that mortals can use, and I will hand them over to the Emperor myself. Besides, the epidemic hasn't broken out yet. If we catch the culprit behind this, won't we resolve the crisis of a large-scale outbreak?","Furthermore, with the prescriptions we provide, as long as Dayan handles it properly, they can solve it on their own.\"","[What if they don't handle it properly?]","\"Then it can only be said that this is Dayan's destiny. We don't help trash!\"","The monarch and officials of Dayan were all secretly rubbing their hands together in anticipation. They were determined to do this well and show the Young Preceptor that they were not trash!","If she helped them change their fate, they would definitely be able to catch it!","\"Little Zhu, first tell me who is behind this epidemic.\"","[Master, this person has some connection with that cross-dressing head palace maid, Yue Ying.","The one who led people to disguise themselves as traveling merchants to come to Dayan, secretly captured some of the disaster victims, locked them in a cave, and infected them with the epidemic is Yue Ying's senior martial brother, Qi Ming.","He is acting on the orders of the Emperor of Yue, Gan Sheng. It's a pity that he is too far away, so we can't eliminate Gan Sheng, the biggest mastermind behind the scenes!]","\"So it was done by Southern Yue? This is a biological weapon on a national level. This style of doing things is very similar to certain countries!\"","Gan Sheng again! Emperor Mingxi's liver ached just hearing this name now!","He gritted his teeth, thinking that one day, he would definitely capture this Gan Sheng and bring him to Dayan to dance for him!","[The fact that this epidemic could bloom in multiple places is not only led by Southern Yue, but the people of Eastern Yi also had a hand in it behind the scenes.","Even the Sima family opened the door of convenience for the Eastern Yi people. Without them cleaning up the trails, no matter how stupid the monarch and officials of Dayan were, they should have noticed it.]","The Sima family again. This sentence echoed in the hearts of the monarch and officials of Dayan. Emperor Mingxi pressed his lips tightly together. His layout against the Sima family was not yet complete.","It was not yet time to reel in the net. He noted down this debt and would eventually settle the score with Sima Jing!","\"The Sima family again. Did Sima Jing harbor treasonous intentions this early? I heard that because Bao Qianjun offended him, the Emperor ordered Bao Qianjun to return to the capital to report on his duties?\"","[The Emperor has poor eyesight, mistaking pearls for fish eyes, and treating treacherous people as loyal subjects. Do you want to remind him, Master?]","\"Let's talk about it later. Let's resolve the matter with Qi Ming first, as well as the Eastern Yi people.\"","[Qi Ming is currently hiding in the Zui Lai Ju restaurant in the East Market of Shangjing City, waiting to rendezvous with Yue Ying.","According to the timeline, after the two of them meet, Qi Ming will get something from Yue Ying and head straight to Bingzhou. The first source of infection for the epidemic was created by him in Bingzhou.","Then the 'poisonous people' will travel all the way from Bingzhou to Yizhou, spreading the epidemic wherever they go.","As for Xingzhou closer to the south, that is the work of the Eastern Yi people. The Southern Yue people created cholera, while the Eastern Yi people created dysentery.","The Sima family will lift the coastal blockade, and the Eastern Yi people will land from the small port of Haiqing County, which is under the jurisdiction of Dongling Prefecture in Yingzhou.","How do you plan to catch them, Master?]","\"East Market. What kind of place is Zui Lai Ju?\"","[Zui Lai Ju is a famous restaurant in the East Market. Its behind-the-scenes boss is a Southern Yue person, and it is also a spy stronghold planted by Southern Yue in Shangjing City.","It was even established by Yue Ying himself, and his two sons are hidden inside.]","\"Little Zhu, what if I go to Zui Lai Ju for my lunch today?\"","[Then you should bring more people, Master. Several of the Southern Yue assassins who tried to assassinate you are hiding in this stronghold.]","\"No need to worry. Not to mention that my divine power is recovering, with you here, who would I be afraid of?","It just so happens that my escort team today is also the strongest lineup, with Zhang Fang and the Shen sisters all present.\"","Seeing the two ancestors finalize their itinerary, the monarch and officials of Dayan did not dare to delay their 'dining'. With a sweep of Emperor Mingxi's gaze, Qian Gui immediately stepped forward and shouted, \"If there are matters to report, speak now; if not, the court is dismissed!\"","Just as an unperceptive official wanted to step out of the ranks, he was quickly pulled back by a sharp-eyed colleague beside him.","With this brief delay, Emperor Mingxi had already lifted his foot and walked out of the hall.","[Master, the Emperor is walking so fast, could it be that he urgently needs to pee?]","The well-prepared Qian Gui had already firmly supported Emperor Mingxi's arm. The master and servant steadily walked out of the hall without messing up a single step.","Although they were fast, Yue Fuguang's voice still reached their ears, \"Little Zhu, don't always make fun of the Emperor. He can't hear it anyway, so the only one you're tormenting is me, your master.","Be careful of making it a habit here. If you accidentally slip up when we return to Lingxu Mountain, Master won't spare you.\"","[Hehe, Master, aren't we in the mortal realm right now? Once we return to the Immortal Realm, Little Zhu will definitely be able to change it!]","The system clenched its little fists in its space, refusing to admit that its friends from the Imperial Examination System and various Learning Systems were already disdaining it for speaking vulgarly!","One person and one system talked and laughed as they walked out. It was only after her carriage went far away that the Crown Prince, leading Wei Ping, Cai Xian, Huo Ying, and others, appeared at the palace gates.","Xie Zhiyan said, \"My lords, let's arrange things as we just agreed. We must ensure the safety of the Young Preceptor.\"","Huo Ying said, \"Rest assured, Your Highness. My men have already disguised themselves as diners and gone ahead to Zui Lai Ju.\"","Saying that, he turned to Cai Xian and added, \"This humble subject and Minister Huo will be at the Fu Man Lou restaurant right across from Zui Lai Ju. As soon as there is any movement on the Young Preceptor's side, we will rush over immediately.\"","This was the reasonable excuse for their appearance that they had discussed. Not dining at Zui Lai Ju would also reduce the Young Preceptor's suspicions.","Xie Zhiyan said, \"Very well! You go ahead, and Lord Wei and I will follow shortly.\"","The East Market was the commercial high street of Shangjing City. Where there was trade, there would naturally be disputes, so the Dali Court, the Ministry of Justice, and the Shangjing City Prefecture Office all set up a small administrative office there.","Today, it was justifiable for him and Wei Ping to inspect the East Market office. As for bringing a bit too many people, there was naturally a reasonable explanation for it.","Meanwhile, Yue Fuguang had already brought a group of thugs... escorts to the entrance of the East Market.","A wide bluestone road stretched forward, flanked by all kinds of shops on both sides.","In the fabric shop, the shelves and counters were filled with rolls of silk and cotton cloth. A young shop assistant was picking up a bolt of blue cloth to introduce it to a customer.","Next door was a shop selling porcelain, with bowls, plates, and various vases neatly arranged on the shelves. Through the window lattice of her carriage, Yue Fuguang saw several pieces of lacquerware displayed on the counter. They were extremely exquisite, not much inferior to those in her storehouse.","Thinking of the storehouse, she finally remembered what she had forgotten!","She had agreed with the Crown Prince to visit the Emperor's private treasury. How could she have forgotten!","While thinking about the Emperor's private treasury, Yue Fuguang's eyes strayed to the stalls set up by peddlers on both sides of the road.","One of the steamed bun peddlers was standing behind a steaming bamboo steamer. The buns in front of him were all white, tender, and lovely.","If she didn't have to save her stomach for Zui Lai Ju, she would have liked to have a few right now.","\"Would you like to try one, My Lady?\" Shen Chunying couldn't help but ask when she saw Yue Fuguang's gaze lingering on the buns for too long.","\"I'll go buy them.\" Yu Huaixian ran out from who knows where, not even wiping the sweat off his forehead, and volunteered, lifting his foot to walk towards the bun stall.","\"Second Brother Xian, it won't be too late to buy them on our way back.\" If they bought them now but didn't eat them, wouldn't they get cold very quickly?","\"Also, isn't today your day off? Why did you come running over here?\""]},{"number":231,"title":"Chapter 231: Immortal Really","paragraphs":["Officials of Great Yan had two days of rest a month. However, the guards in Yue Fuguang's retinue, despite being officials of Great Yan and drawing a salary from the imperial court, answered only to her.","Therefore, she gave each person four days off a month, with the leave schedules all arranged by Zhang Fang and the Shen sisters.","She remembered Yu Huaixian saying that today was his day off.","[Master, for an immortal, you're getting quite accustomed to eating mortal food.]","\"Little Zhu, your master is merely adapting to local customs. The spiritual fruits and vegetables of the immortal realm certainly have their own flavor, but the worldly food of this mortal realm also has its unique charm.\"","Yu Huaixian smiled and said, \"I had nothing to do, so I came to the East Market for a stroll and just happened to see your carriage.\"","He wouldn't dare admit that his granduncle had sent a message home, saying that their cousin was coming out to catch an enemy \"spy\" today and ordering him to provide close protection.","Zhang Fang and the others had good martial arts skills, but the family didn't dare entrust their cousin's safety entirely to outsiders.","His grandfather and the elders had instructed him that in times of danger, he was to be his little cousin's human shield. He could be injured or even die, but his cousin couldn't lose a single hair!","Yu Huaixian didn't think there was anything wrong with the elders' instructions. After all, she was the golden child of the Yu family. With her around, the Yu family would have nothing to worry about for three generations.","Besides, his little cousin was an Immortal Lord descended to the mortal realm. As long as he had one breath left, she would definitely have a way to save him. He was just that confident!","While Yu Huaixian was still fantasizing about being a human shield for his immortal cousin, his sleeve was tugged by Shen Dongxue beside him.","Yu Huaixian turned to look at her in confusion, only to see one, two, three... twelve shocked faces behind him.","What was going on? Why did they have such expressions? Did something happen that he didn't know about while he was chatting with his cousin just now?","He silently questioned his colleagues with his eyes.","Zhang Fang quietly pulled him a few meters away and whispered breathily in his ear, \"An immortal! Really?!\"","The question was directed at him, but his eyes were darting toward Yue Fuguang's carriage.","Yu Huaixian was taken aback by his question and mirrored their shocked expressions. \"You guys didn't know?!\"","The shock of the group turned into bewilderment. 'Were we supposed to know?'","'We had no idea! No one told us!'","The crowd was speechless, but Yu Huaixian read the meaning in their eyes.","He silently turned around, his back to them, and then flashed a massive grin, baring his teeth and gums. Suppressing tears of laughter, he hurriedly rubbed his face with his hands.","He didn't dare let these guys, who were all brawn and no brains, know that he was laughing at them.","To think that even the usually clever Shen sisters had been kept in the dark.","By the time Yu Huaixian turned back around, he had already put on a serious face.","The crowd understood; this guy must have been secretly laughing at them just now!","However, for the sake of the answer that was practically bursting out, they endured it!","Yu Huaixian nodded vigorously at the dozen or so people, then secretly pointed a finger toward the sky.","The meaning was self-evident.","The guards: So everything we've been hearing is true! It's not that the Junior Preceptor is comparing herself to an immortal, she is a real immortal!","The crowd thumped their heads in frustration; they should have figured it out sooner!","Only this made the abnormal behavior of all the court officials make sense!","Then was their guard team of several dozen people just... decorations by the Immortal Lord's side?","Whether they were decorations or not, everyone made up their minds to cling tightly to the Immortal Lord's golden thigh for a hundred years without letting go!","Yu Huaixian rather unkindly admired his colleagues' ever-changing expressions in silence. Their faces shifted from feeling utterly lost to sudden enlightenment, then to excitement and inexplicable thrill. If it weren't for the fact that they had already started scaring passersby, even making two chubby, pink-cheeked children cry, Yu Huaixian really wouldn't have bothered to remind them: your facial expressions are out of control, bros!","Yue Fuguang paid no mind to the silent exchanges among the guards outside, still looking at the scenery along the way with great interest.","Passing by a farmer selling vegetables, Yue Fuguang saw several baskets of fresh wild greens in front of him. Thinking of shepherd's purse dumplings, she decided that on her next day off, she could visit the estate to check on the progress of the villa's construction and the planting of fruit trees and flowers.","Most importantly, she could go over and cast a localized spiritual rain to help them survive and grow as quickly as possible.","A little further past the vegetable farmer was a peddler carrying a shoulder pole. Both ends of the pole were hung with small items like needles, thread, and combs.","Yue Fuguang couldn't help but think of the disappearance case involving Gao Ming. Whenever young girls or young wives were said to have eloped, eighty percent of the time, the partner was a peddler.","Peddlers: In the end, it's our profession that takes all the blame!","The East Market was very bustling today. There were many pedestrians on the street, including both luxuriously dressed people and commoners in plain clothes.","She even saw a few scholars wearing the attire of provincial graduates. Judging by their accents, they were all from out of town. Had they come to the capital a year in advance to prepare for the exams?","Early next spring would be another year for the metropolitan examination. It wouldn't be surprising if a few new metropolitan graduates emerged from among these people next year.","At this moment, the soft, sweet voices of children begging their parents to buy toys drifted into her ears, along with the hawking of various stalls. A few porters carrying goods walked briskly through the crowd, repeatedly shouting for people to make way.","Occasionally, a carriage would pass by. The crisp ringing of the bells on the carriage frame mingled with the peddlers' cries, the haggling of shoppers, and the footsteps of people walking by.","This filled the entire street with a vibrant atmosphere. Who could have imagined that in less than a month, a plague would break out everywhere, affecting even the capital at the foot of the Son of Heaven, leaving the people in a state of panic.","[Master, looking at this peaceful scene, it's hard to imagine what it will be like in a month when the plague runs rampant, people's livelihoods are ruined, the population withers, and everyone fears for their lives.]","\"Little Zhu, the scene you described won't happen. We caught Qi Ming, one of the main culprits, today. Even if Gan Sheng wants to send someone else, I don't think Emperor Mingxi is someone to be trifled with.\"","Emperor Mingxi: I have already sent a message by carrier pigeon, ordering people to infiltrate Nanyue and stir up trouble. I believe that in a few days, Gan Sheng will be so overwhelmed with his own mess that he won't have time to worry about Great Yan.","She believed that after the maneuvering of the monarch and his officials, along with their previous instigations, even if the temporary alliance formed by the four countries didn't break down immediately, there wouldn't be any more major joint movements.","To think they dared to make a move against their Junior Preceptor—did they really think they wouldn't fight back?","The group continued down the street, and the variety of shops on both sides increased.","Yue Fuguang saw a blacksmith shop nearby. She could hear the clinking sound of iron being forged inside, and a few newly made kitchen knives and agricultural tool parts like hoes were hanging at the door.","[Master, are these agricultural tool parts the standard models you gave to the Ministry of Works?]","\"They should be. I wonder how effective these new agricultural tools are for the commoners.\"","Wang Shouchen, who was following a few hundred meters away, had the most right to speak on this. To sum it up in one sentence: all the commoners who used them said they were great!","He had visited a few households, and enshrined in their main halls were portraits or statues of the Junior Preceptor.","Before the sacrifice five days ago, the commoners had only set up memorial tablets in their shops. But ever since the commoners standing at the very front had seen the Junior Preceptor's true face that day, they had all eagerly brought back statues or portraits to worship.","Aside from the imperial court officials, the earliest people to worship the Junior Preceptor were the commoners who manufactured and used the agricultural tools.","Wang Shouchen glanced at the blacksmith shop they were passing by. He was ninety percent sure that this shop must be worshipping the Junior Preceptor."]},{"number":232,"title":"Chapter 232: Was poppy shell added to these meat dishes","paragraphs":["Further ahead was a pastry shop. A sweet aroma wafted from within, and standard pastries like walnut cookies and mung bean cakes were displayed on the counter.","This sweet fragrance made Yue Fuguang even hungrier!","She couldn't help but ask, \"Second Brother Xian, are we almost at Zuilai Restaurant?\"","Yu Huaixian smiled and said, \"Seventh Sister, you must be hungry. Look, what's that?\"","As they conversed, the carriage happened to stop in front of a shop.","Yue Fuguang looked through the lattice window and saw the three large golden characters for 'Zuilai Restaurant' sparkling in the sunlight.","It was a three-story wooden building, taller and grander than the shops on either side. A large, conspicuous signboard hung above the entrance, flanked by strings of red lanterns on the left and right, giving it a very festive look.","By the door stood hitching posts and a wine flag bearing the three large characters for Zuilai Restaurant. Like the plaque, the calligraphy was vigorous and powerful, clearly the work of a master.","A waiter stood at the entrance of the restaurant. Seeing guests arrive, he hurriedly stepped forward to greet them.","Led by Yue Fuguang, the group walked into the ground-floor dining hall, which was furnished with many square tables and long benches.","Most of the tables were occupied, making the place seem quite lively.","Against the wall was a wooden counter. The shopkeeper stood behind it, holding an abacus and flicking the beads from time to time.","Seeing the group's attire, he immediately knew they were distinguished guests.","He was extremely attentive in his greeting, though of course, before he could even reach Yue Fuguang, he was sent away by Yu Huaixian and the others.","Yue Fuguang noticed several jars of wine on the shelves behind the counter, labeled with red paper bearing the names of the wines. She wondered how their taste would compare to the white liquor she planned to brew this year.","Judging by their clothes, the diners in the hall were all wealthy. It made sense; Zuilai Restaurant was considered one of the top three restaurants in the East Market.","Without some wealth, one wouldn't come here. She observed many people eating while conversing in low voices. Like teahouses and taverns, this place was a hub for information. Nanyue had chosen this as one of their strongholds—truly a clever calculation.","To her surprise, Yue Fuguang saw a couple of stir-fried dishes on some tables. Zuilai Restaurant certainly lived up to its role as a spy network; they had already brought stir-fried dishes, which were currently only popular among the upper echelons of the Great Yan Dynasty, to their tables.","Although the young waiter saw that Yue Fuguang was young, her clothes and entourage told him that this young lady wearing a veiled hat must be a noblewoman from a prominent family.","Not daring to be negligent, he noticed her turning her head to look at the nearby tables. He guided the group toward the second floor up a relatively wide staircase that was swept quite clean.","As they walked, the young waiter introduced, \"Noble lady, our humble establishment has recently introduced a new style of cuisine called stir-frying. You can order a few dishes to try later.","These stir-fried dishes are different from stews, the taste is...\"","He had originally wanted to boast about it as usual, but considering this lady's attire, she had surely eaten stir-fried dishes before.","So he sheepishly stopped himself and began recommending other signature dishes.","Like the third floor, half of the second floor consisted of private rooms. Most of the doors were closed. Occasionally, a waiter carrying a tray of food would open a door to enter, revealing even more elegantly dressed guests sitting inside.","Yue Fuguang chose the second floor because it was crowded and 'lively.' She didn't request a private room. For one thing, a private room only had one large table, and her guards naturally wouldn't be willing to eat at the same table as her.","She couldn't just let them watch her eat. She wasn't used to it, and it wouldn't help her show grace and win over their loyalty.","More importantly, a private room would only have her own people, which wasn't conducive to her 'stirring up trouble'!","Yue Fuguang's group occupied three tables by the window. Looking out from the second-floor window, they could perfectly see the signboard of Fuman Restaurant across the street.","With these two restaurants opening right across from each other, if they weren't owned by the same family, they were definitely bitter rivals.","There were no menus here; instead, a glib-tongued waiter who was adept at reciting dish names introduced the options to her.","Listening to him rattle off a string of dish names made Yue Fuguang even hungrier, so she said, \"Bring a few of your signature dishes to each table, along with some stir-fried dishes. No wine.\"","They would have to fight later, and she was afraid that drinking wine would affect their performance.","As for the lack of wine, Zhang Fang, Xu Chunshan, and the others didn't feel disappointed. After all, the 'Pear Blossom White' bestowed by the Junior Preceptor suited their tastes much better.","Having tasted Pear Blossom White, drinking any other wine now would seem rather bland!","Cuizhu, Shen Chunying, Shen Dongxue, and a few other women sat at the table closest to Yue Fuguang. Among this group of beauties, Yu Huaixian was the only man mixed in.","Faced with the women's eye-rolls, Yu Huaixian remained as steady as a mountain, his face not flushing in the slightest.","So what if he was a single speck of green amidst a bed of flowers? Who asked this table to be the closest to his cousin?","They were outside now, not at a family banquet, so he naturally wouldn't agree to eat at the same table as Yue Fuguang.","The absolute status and majesty of the Junior Preceptor was something their family had to carefully uphold.","Yue Fuguang felt that although both were second children in their respective branches, Brother Boming, who was one year older than the seventeen-year-old Yu Huaixian, was still far inferior to him in terms of composure.","Everyone in the group knew exactly what they were here for. Being on their first proper mission, they couldn't help but feel a little nervous.","They were afraid that outsiders might spot a flaw and ruin their cousin's plan.","While waiting for the food, Yu Huaixian took the lead in breaking the silence. \"Seventh Sister, your brother is riding on your coattails today to be able to eat so many dishes at Zuilai Restaurant.\"","He said this in a pitiful tone. Although the Yu family's ancestors had only become wealthy a few generations ago, the elders managed their businesses well, and the descendants all lived comfortably.","When the family was divided, her grandfather, as the legitimate eldest son, took the lion's share, but with his care, her second great-uncle's family also received a substantial portion.","No matter how you looked at him, Yu Huaixian didn't seem like someone who couldn't afford to eat at Zuilai Restaurant. But looking at his expression and the reactions of the others, she knew her second cousin wasn't lying.","So she probed, \"Why, are the dishes here very expensive?\"","\"Aren't they! Just the dishes you ordered just now will cost no less than fifty or sixty taels of silver per table.\" His monthly allowance in the past hadn't even been that much.","It was only after following his cousin for over a month that his purse had bulged. His grandfather had tripled his monthly allowance, making it the highest among all the brothers in the two branches!","Even Brother Boming couldn't compare to him. Who asked him to be by Seventh Sister's side now!","\"If it's that expensive, the taste shouldn't be bad!\"","Yu Huaixian nodded. \"I guarantee you'll want more after eating. This shop relies on repeat customers.\"","As everyone chatted, the dishes were quickly served. Yue Fuguang first took a bite of stir-fried pork with bamboo shoots, and couldn't help but pause her chopsticks.","Seeing Yue Fuguang stop her chopsticks, the others also froze with their hands extended in mid-air.","Yue Fuguang thought for a moment, then picked up a chopstick-full of wild vegetables. She nodded silently and proceeded to try the rest, taking a bite from each of the ten dishes.","She frowned. 'Little Zhu, help me check if poppy husks were added to these meat dishes.'","[Please wait a moment, Master... Master, there are indeed poppy husks in them.]","'No wonder Second Brother Xian said this place mainly relies on repeat customers, and that people want more after eating. It turns out the root cause isn't the taste, but this thing causing mischief!'","[The Emperor and the officials are too incompetent. This harmful thing has already made its way onto the dining tables of the Great Yan people, and they are still completely unaware.]"]},{"number":233,"title":"Chapter 233: We'll take action after the people inside have eaten and drunk their fill.","paragraphs":["Regarding the Divine Artifact Lord's bombardment of the Emperor and the civil and military officials, Shen Chunying and the others still felt quite guilty hearing it. However, the moment they thought about the true identity of the person they were following, they instantly calmed down!","As long as they clung tightly to the Junior Preceptor's thigh, not even His Majesty could touch them.","Emperor Mingxi: Do you still remember whose officials you are, whose salaries you receive, and whose authority you are under!","The guards: We all listen to the great Junior Preceptor!","\"Today we will uproot this place. When the time comes, I'll give Wei Ping and the others a hint. I hope these people can be a bit smarter!\"","Separated from the Zuilai Tavern by just a street, a straight-line distance of no more than three hundred meters, Wei Ping was currently accompanying the Crown Prince.","The two of them heard Yue Fuguang's words crystal clear! He gave the Crown Prince an awkward smile.","Wei Ping: Thank you, Junior Preceptor, for thinking of me in everything!","[Master, judging from this, Nanzhao isn't the only one aware of the effects of imperial rice. Nanyue is even using it in their meals, so they must understand it very well.]","\"Little Zhu, you forgot that Nanyue has the world-renowned Du Zhongxian. It shouldn't be surprising that they could discover the effects of imperial rice.\"","Wei Ping and Xie Zhiyan exchanged a glance. So the poppy shells the Junior Preceptor mentioned were actually imperial rice?","Both of them utterly detested that substance. After understanding some of its effects, the ruler and his minister had broken out in a cold sweat.","Especially after conducting experiments on death row inmates in the heavenly prison and seeing those people eventually reduced to a miserable state, neither human nor ghost, it caused them to lose sleep for days.","His Majesty immediately issued an edict prohibiting the cultivation of even a single stalk of imperial rice within the borders of Great Yan. Violators would be severely punished, and serious offenders would be charged with treason.","Under such severe penalties, the ruler and his minister originally thought it had been completely eradicated in Great Yan. They never expected that the Nanyue scoundrels would blatantly put it into their meals.","Xie Zhiyan's eyes turned ruthless. \"Lord Wei, is there any better excuse than this?\"","Wei Ping only paused for a moment before understanding the Crown Prince's intention. He immediately sent someone to invite the Market Director of the East Market. They still needed an informant, so he set his sights on Cao Cang, the manager stationed at the East Market.","Meanwhile, on Yue Fuguang's side, having confirmed that poppy shells were added to the meat dishes, she said to the guards, \"The vegetable dishes here are cooked passably well. As for the meat dishes, not only do they lack a bit of flavor, but they also don't seem very fresh. It's best not to eat them.\"","[Master, isn't your excuse a bit too perfunctory and forced? Look at the way they are staring at the meat dishes; can they really resist eating them?]","\"I have fulfilled my duty to remind them. As to whether they listen or not, it's entirely up to their own free will.","Little Zhu, you know that your master has always respected the fate of others and refrained from bearing their karma.\"","Before the others could react, Yu Huaixian and Shen Chunying quickly moved all the meat dishes from Yue Fuguang's table and their own tables to the empty table next to them.","Without saying much, they proved with practical actions that they had taken her words to heart.","They didn't know what poppy shells were, but the name 'imperial rice' had echoed throughout the entire Great Yan a year ago. The imperial court's determination to eradicate it could be seen from the severe punishments.","Addictive, leading to a fate worse than death. Just thinking of these words, the meat dishes on the three tables were cleared away in mere moments.","[Master, these people are quite sensible!]","\"Those who aren't sensible wouldn't be kept by my side, right?\"","[But compared to those little immortals on Mount Lingxu, they are still far behind.]","\"Little Zhu, there is a difference between immortals and mortals. How can you compare them?\"","As Yue Fuguang's group chatted while eating, the forces of the other two parties had already quietly locked down the area, ensuring that not even a fly could escape from the Zuilai Tavern.","Cao Cang and the East Market Director, Jin Ming, didn't dare to strike up a conversation with the Crown Prince, so they quietly asked Wei Ping, \"Lord Wei, at what time should we take action?\"","They had just been summoned without being told a specific time. The two of them, especially Jin Ming, were so anxious that they were almost sweating.","Wei Ping glanced at him and said, \"We will take action after the people inside have eaten and drunk their fill.\"","They actually had to wait for the people inside to eat and drink their fill. Being seasoned officials, the two naturally wouldn't think Lord Wei was just being kind-hearted.","There must be some special person inside, and their status definitely wasn't low.","At this moment, they were even more curious about who exactly was sitting inside, capable of making Wei Ping and the Crown Prince wait until they finished their meal before making a move.","It couldn't be that His Majesty was inside, could it!","In another alley, although Cai Xian and Huo Ying hadn't communicated with the Crown Prince and Wei Ping, they could basically guess each other's thoughts.","Making that ancestor handle matters on an empty stomach—never mind how the Little Immortal Lord would react, just the Divine Artifact Lord alone could scold them to death.","Being targeted by the Divine Artifact Lord, or having it speak ill of them in front of the Junior Preceptor—neither of these was something they wanted to see!","On Yue Fuguang's side, having eaten a stomach full of vegetarian dishes, her belly was barely full, but her mouth was craving more. She thought about quickly finishing the matters here and then going elsewhere to find something delicious.","Thus, she reached for the coin pouch at her waist but couldn't feel it. Looking down, not only was the coin pouch hanging at her waist missing, but a piece of jade pendant with excellent translucency had also vanished without a trace.","So she said, \"Zhang Fang, Chunying, my coin pouch and jade pendant are gone!\"","Shen Chunying said, \"My Lord, could they have been stolen?\"","Her voice was particularly loud, successfully alarming the guests in the adjacent private room.","Zhang Fang also said, \"Please wait a moment, My Lord. Your subordinate will go find the shopkeeper and immediately lock down the Zuilai Tavern. That thief won't be able to escape!\"","\"Little Zhu, this script isn't right. I said my things were gone, and they determined it was stolen without even questioning if I just remembered wrong?\"","[Master, these are the kind of good subordinates you want. Those who dare to question you absolutely cannot be kept by your side.]","The guards' hearts tightened. The reason they believed her so readily was only because they knew their Lord's purpose in doing this. Under normal circumstances, they might have actually asked an extra question.","Wouldn't that have angered the Divine Artifact Lord, making it doubt their loyalty to the Little Immortal Lord?","If they were driven away from the Little Immortal Lord's side, not to mention how others would view them, they themselves would be sick to death with regret.","Cuizhu helped Yue Fuguang stand up. As she turned her head, she happened to see Cai Xian and Huo Ying about to enter the Fuman Restaurant opposite them.","\"Miss, it's Minister Cai and Minister Huo.\"","Yue Fuguang looked in the direction she was pointing and also saw the two of them looking up towards their side.","The two smiled and cupped their hands in greeting to her, then lifted their feet and walked towards the Zuilai Tavern.","[Host, these two are quite cunning. In order to make their appearance seem reasonable, they pretended to head to the restaurant opposite.]","\"Isn't it better to be reasonable? It saves us trouble and won't make us look too stupid. Otherwise, where would the 'Immortal Lord's' face be?\"","Huo Ying, Cai Xian, and Zhang Fang brought the shopkeeper of the Zuilai Tavern upstairs together.","Before coming upstairs, Zhang Fang had already quickly informed the two of the course of events.","After both sides exchanged greetings, Cai Xian said, \"Junior Preceptor, please wait a moment. This trivial matter can be left to this subordinate and Lord Huo.\"","Shen Dongxue handed Yue Fuguang a cup of warm tea. Yue Fuguang took a sip before saying, \"I'll have to trouble you two Lords.\"","Huo Ying and Cai Xian bowed and said, \"You flatter us! Does the Junior Preceptor have any other instructions?\"","Yue Fuguang thought for a moment and said, \"My intention is to search the entire Zuilai Tavern.","I heard there is a guest courtyard behind the restaurant. Perhaps the thief is hiding there.\"","Cai Xian nodded in agreement. As he turned around, his expression instantly became stern and grave. He unleashed his full aura, pressing down so heavily that the shopkeeper of the Zuilai Tavern didn't even dare to lift his head."]},{"number":234,"title":"Chapter 234: Moonlight Just Watches Quietly as They Perform","paragraphs":["Hearing Yue Fuguang suggest searching the backyard, he was already so frightened that he broke out in a cold sweat, cursing that blind little thief a thousand times in his heart.","Upon hearing Zhang Fang's reason for looking for him, he already had a suspect in mind, as this wasn't the first time that person had stolen from a guest.","He never expected to kick a steel plate today! This little girl was actually some high-ranking official!","In the Great Yan Dynasty, who else could be a female official with such an esteemed status other than the famous Junior Preceptor?","With a hasty glance just now, he seemed to have faintly seen that iconic lotus mark on her forehead!","The shopkeeper's mind suddenly became active. Thinking of a certain possibility, a sense of determination instantly filled his chest!","He clenched his hands hidden in his sleeves, doing his best to suppress his increasingly excited, thrilled, and somewhat contorted face.","He stole a glance at Yue Fuguang's guards, secretly assessing their combat power against the people in the backyard and calculating their odds of winning.","Cai Xian looked at the shopkeeper, whose legs were trembling from a bold decision, and said coldly, \"Shopkeeper He, a thief has committed a robbery in your inn. Do you know where this thief is now?\"","Huo Ying also said, \"I have heard that multiple thefts have occurred in your inn. Don't tell me you don't have a suspect in mind.\"","Shopkeeper He cupped his hands and bowed, his face full of flattery as he said, \"My lords, this humble one... this humble one indeed has someone in mind. That person is currently staying in Room Bing-Three on the first floor of the backyard.\"","Cai Xian and Huo Ying exchanged a glance, both able to tell that this shopkeeper was being dishonest.","Without them needing to waste their breath, he took the initiative to lead everyone to the backyard. No matter what treachery he was hiding, it played right into their hands.","The two slightly turned sideways and glanced at Yue Fuguang, who was sitting upright there.","Yue Fuguang understood clearly in her heart. Naturally, she also noticed the shopkeeper's seemingly respectful demeanor, which actually concealed an ever-growing malice toward her.","Since this was one of the strongholds of Nanyue, and Shopkeeper He was deliberately leading them there, the backyard must not be simple.","Just as Cai Xian was wondering whether they should wait for the Crown Prince and Wei Ping, he saw Yue Fuguang stand up and say, \"My lords, why don't we follow the shopkeeper to the backyard and have a look.","Whether it is or isn't, a search will tell us.\"","Seeing that Yue Fuguang had made a decision, the two bowed and agreed.","Shopkeeper He also took the opportunity to raise his eyes and quickly size up Yue Fuguang. After confirming her identity, he made an inviting gesture to the group in a seemingly humble and flattering manner.","Just as the group headed toward the backyard, the outside of Zuilai Inn had already been completely surrounded by the Crown Prince's men.","Xie Zhiyan said to Wei Ping, \"Lord Wei, send some men out to keep a close eye on the nearby intersections, just in case the people inside escape through a secret tunnel.\"","After the incident with Bai Yu and the Prince of Qi, they were all on higher alert, guessing that Zuilai Inn might have a similar secret tunnel.","At this time, a 'diner' ran out of Zuilai Inn. The man came before the Crown Prince, bowed, and quickly reported, \"Your Royal Highness, just now, the Junior Preceptor and the two Ministers, Cai and Huo, took their men and followed Shopkeeper He to the backyard.","Minister Huo suspects there is an ambush in the backyard.\"","The Crown Prince's gaze sharpened. Without time to overthink, he immediately ordered, \"Quickly, follow me inside to protect the Junior Preceptor! Wei Ping, I'll leave the capture of the criminals to you.\"","\"Yes, sir!\"","The two of them led their men and charged inside. Just as they approached the screen wall of the backyard, they heard the clash of weapons and shouts of killing coming from within.","\"Quick, charge in!\"","Wei Ping, holding a steel blade, took the lead and charged in, shouting loudly, \"The authorities are handling a case! Surrender at once!\"","\"Lord Wei!\"","\"Your Royal Highness!\"","\"Junior Preceptor!\"","\"Minister Cai, Minister Huo, why are you here?\"","The Crown Prince and Wei Ping put on an act of a chance encounter, their expressions completely on point.","\"We were just about to ask you that. Why is Lord Wei here? And with so many men?\"","Cai Xian's acting skills were equally impressive.","Yue Fuguang quietly watched them perform. She kept a serious face and didn't speak because she had to... hold back her laughter!","The two sides successfully joined forces, yet they pretended not to know the other was there, probing each other's purpose for coming. It was truly hilarious.","Yue Fuguang nodded secretly. As expected of veteran actors, their expressions and words were perfectly executed, and no one dropped the ball.","The few of them protected Yue Fuguang as they retreated to the side. Then, they bowed and saluted the Crown Prince, saying, \"The two of us agreed to have lunch at Fuman Restaurant across the street today.","We didn't expect to happen upon the Junior Preceptor...\"","Cai Xian recounted the sequence of events to the Crown Prince and the others. Huo Ying continued, \"Your Royal Highness, this humble minister believes that the origins of this Zuilai Inn must be problematic.","That shopkeeper just now was clearly targeting the Junior Preceptor.\"","Yue Fuguang also nodded and said, \"What Minister Huo said is correct. Shopkeeper He's hidden weapon was indeed aimed at me. If Chunying and Dongxue hadn't reacted quickly,","he might have actually succeeded.\"","Xie Zhiyan asked, \"Does the Junior Preceptor suspect that this person is connected to the previous assassins?\"","\"Indeed, I do have suspicions in that regard.\"","Wei Ping also chimed in, \"The Junior Preceptor's guess is not unreasonable. Because of the potatoes, the people of the Great Yan Dynasty are exceptionally grateful to you. Only those previous assassins would think of killing you instead of thanking you.\"","By this time, the fighting in the courtyard had ended. Everyone in Zuilai Inn, from the shopkeeper down to the waiters and guests, had been captured.","The Crown Prince ordered, \"Search all the rooms. If you find any suspicious individuals or items, report it immediately.","Also, pay attention to checking for hidden rooms and secret tunnels.\"","Cai Xian asked, \"Do Your Royal Highness and Lord Wei have other important matters here?\"","The Crown Prince signaled for Wei Ping to explain, so Wei Ping said, \"Minister Cai might not know this, but I and His Royal Highness came here because we received a secret report from the Market Director here and Manager Cao Cang.","Manager Cao recently hosted a banquet for his friends here and discovered that the meat dishes at Zuilai Inn seemingly contained imperial poppy.\"","Wei Ping spread his hands. \"His Majesty attaches great importance to this matter. Whether true or false, I and His Royal Highness had to bring men to investigate.","Coincidentally, we ran into the Junior Preceptor and the two ministers.\"","Huo Ying suddenly realized, \"So that's how it is. This further proves that this Zuilai Inn is definitely not simple.\"","The Crown Prince said disapprovingly, \"The two ministers were too reckless today. How could you bring the Junior Preceptor into such danger?\"","The two hurriedly bowed and said, \"Your Royal Highness's reprimand is justified. It was our lack of careful consideration.\"","Yue Fuguang quickly interjected, \"Your Royal Highness, don't blame the two ministers. It was I who insisted on coming here.\"","[Master, something is wrong. Wei Ping said the Market Director and Manager Cao sent a secret report. Let's not talk about this Manager Cao for now, but the Market Director of the East Market should be named Jin Ming, right?]","\"Does Little Zhu know this Jin Ming?\"","[According to the records, this Jin Ming is a major 'drug lord.' He is also one of the behind-the-scenes owners of Zuilai Inn. How could he report that the food here is laced with imperial poppy?","He wouldn't even have time to cover it up fast enough. To him, this Zuilai Inn is a goose that lays golden eggs.]","\"Jin Ming is a major drug lord! And the behind-the-scenes owner of Zuilai Inn? Didn't you say this Zuilai Inn belonged to Nanyue?\"","The Crown Prince and the others thought: Yes, isn't it a Nanyue stronghold? How did it become Jin Ming's property?","Jin Ming's ancestry was traceable; they were all people of the Great Yan Dynasty. Could the Jin Ming before them be a fake?","It wasn't that they were overthinking. Ever since the incident with Qian Gui's family, these people's imaginations had grown wilder, immediately thinking of body doubles.","The group couldn't help but secretly scrutinize Jin Ming, but they couldn't figure out anything from it."]},{"number":235,"title":"Chapter 235: Seize Jin Ming at once","paragraphs":["At this moment, Jin Ming was not as calm as he appeared. His cooperation with the Nanyue people had always gone smoothly, and he never expected that the addition of Imperial Rice to the meat dishes would be noticed by Director Cao.","It should be known that because the cultivation of Imperial Rice was banned in Great Yan, very few people had ever tasted it.","If he had known earlier that Director Cao was familiar with this substance, he would have finished him off long ago to prevent any future troubles!","Standing next to Jin Ming, Cao Cang suddenly shivered. He couldn't help but pull his cloak tighter, muttering in his heart about why the wind still felt so chilly even though spring had already arrived.","He was completely unaware that Jin Ming, with whom he often drank on ordinary days, was already plotting to take his life.","[Master, the original owner behind the Zuilai Tavern was indeed Jin Ming. This property was handed down from his ancestors. It didn't go by this name before, and it only consisted of the front tavern.","Later, when he started cooperating with the Nanyue people, he changed the name to Zuilai Tavern, and the courtyard in the back was bought at that time as well.]","'So the Nanyue people use this place as a stronghold. Does he know everything about Qi Ming and the assassins?'","[He knows about the assassins. In fact, he was the one who used his official position to inquire about your itinerary.","As one of the owners, he has his own people planted in the Zuilai Tavern, so he naturally knew when a big shot from Nanyue arrived.","He has also met Qi Ming, but he doesn't know the true purpose of Qi Ming's trip to Great Yan.","As a Great Yan citizen, even though he betrayed his country for glory and wealth, the Nanyue people still keep their guard up against him.","Ultimately, this man was only looking for wealth at first. Later, when he realized he had boarded the Nanyue people's pirate ship and couldn't get off, he had no choice but to go down that dark path to the very end.]","Despicable! Xie Zhiyan felt a surge of anger in his heart. This bastard Jin Ming was receiving a salary from Great Yan and holding an official position in Great Yan, yet he was helping Nanyue harm his own country!","This kind of traitor who bites the hand that feeds him is even more detestable than Nanyue's spies and assassins. What those people did could only be said to be serving their own masters; they belonged to different countries and had different interests.","There was no such thing as who was more righteous.","But Jin Ming was not among them. He deserved to die!","\"Qi Xiang, take Jin Ming down for me!\"","\"Yes, Your Highness!\"","Before Jin Ming could even take out the dagger hidden on his body, he was captured by Qi Xiang, an officer of one of the Crown Prince's Six Guards.","He could only beg for mercy repeatedly, \"Your Highness, I am innocent! I am innocent!\"","The Crown Prince sneered, \"Innocent? As the Director of the Eastern Market, how could you not know that Imperial Rice was added to the meat dishes at the Zuilai Tavern?\"","He then turned to Wei Ping and said, \"Lord Wei, interrogate him thoroughly. Even if he doesn't know everything, he is still guilty of dereliction of duty!\"","[Master, hasn't the silly Crown Prince gotten a bit smarter? Although he hasn't figured out Jin Ming's true background, now that the man is captured, there's no fear that he won't spill everything he knows.]","Xie Zhiyan: Should I say thank you for the praise from Lord Divine Artifact?","Just then, the search party began to report back one after another. They had found several suspicious individuals and confiscated dozens of pounds of Imperial Rice.","Furthermore, they discovered a secret passage and a hidden room in the premium guest room labeled Jia.","Hearing about the secret passage, Jin Ming immediately widened his eyes. He knew about the hidden room, but when was the secret passage dug? Manager He had never mentioned this to him.","He An, who was already pressed against the ground with a face full of dirt, closed his eyes. Jin Ming was a Great Yan citizen; how could they possibly reveal their escape route to an outsider?","\"Bring the guest registry here!\"","At Xie Zhiyan's command, someone immediately handed over the guest registry. Wei Ping also leaned in to check it together. He only took one glance before saying to the Crown Prince, \"Your Highness, the number of people is wrong. Three are missing.\"","\"Does Lord Wei know which three are missing?\"","Wei Ping spread out the list of people they had just recorded and verified it before replying, \"Your Highness, Qi Ming and his two servants are missing.\"","[Master, it turns out Qi Ming really hasn't left Shangjing yet. This man is quite bold, even checking in under his real name.]","'As long as he doesn't expose the true purpose of his trip, even if he checks in with his real name, no one will suspect anything.'","Prior to this, to the ruler and ministers of Great Yan, he truly wasn't considered any sort of big shot.","Yue Fuguang was afraid the targets would escape and didn't want these people to dawdle any longer, so she asked, \"Lord Wei, were these three staying in the premium room with the secret passage?\"","Wei Ping glanced at the check-in information and confirmed, \"Indeed, they were staying in that room.\"","\"Then since they knew about that secret passage, they must be inextricably linked to the Zuilai Tavern. They might even be big fish.\"","The others nodded, fully agreeing with the Junior Preceptor's speculation.","Just as the group was about to follow the secret passage to chase the suspects, Shen Kang walked in with a smug and complacent look on his face. Seeing the Crown Prince and Yue Fuguang,","he immediately bowed and said, \"Shen Kang greets His Highness the Crown Prince, Lord Junior Preceptor, and the other lords.\"","The Crown Prince looked at his cousin and smiled. \"Judging by your expression, Cousin Kang, did you reap some harvest outside?\"","Shen Kang smiled and replied, \"Just as Your Highness expected, we caught three people running out of a tunnel in an abandoned courtyard by the roadside, two intersections away from here.","Guessing that they might be connected to the Zuilai Tavern, we brought them to Your Highness.\"","[Master, the skinny man standing at the very back, dressed as a servant, is Qi Ming, the orchestrator of the plague in Great Yan.]","'This person is indeed a bit smart, but unfortunately, not quite enough. I believe Wei Ping and Cai Xian will be able to tell that there's something wrong with him.'","Since the mission was complete, there was no need for her to worry about what followed. Thus, Yue Fuguang bowed out after a successful job, leading her guards straight to the Fuman Restaurant across the street.","Having eaten a stomach full of vegetarian food earlier, she was hungry again. Since she was already here, she decided to have another meal.","Once everyone sat down, Yue Fuguang asked, \"Zhang Fang, do you guys really not need to go back and treat your injuries first?\"","She saw that the few of them had merely sprinkled some medicinal powder on their wounds and casually bandaged them with cloth strips. It was extremely sloppy.","They didn't even furrow their brows, acting as if the injuries weren't on their own bodies.","Zhang Fang replied, \"Please set your mind at ease, My Lord. We are fine.\"","He smiled and moved his injured left arm, saying, \"This little injury won't even delay our daily training.\"","Xu Xiaoman also smiled and chimed in, \"My Lord, let alone these grown men, even for me, this minor injury won't affect my daily work.\"","[Master, for martial artists, this minor injury is no big deal, but wound inflammation and festering are the true culprits that endanger their lives.]","'You mean bacterial infection?'","[Yes, exactly that. These mortals still don't know that the reason for the flesh rotting at the wound is the lack of proper disinfection.","This leads to bacterial infection, festering flesh, and high fever with convulsions. On the battlefield, many people are not directly killed by the enemy.","Instead, they die from the backward medical treatment afterward.]","'Speaking of disinfection, it reminds me of our white liquor. If distilled a few more times, wouldn't it also have this effect?","But wouldn't wiping a wound with that stuff hurt like hell?'","[A moment of pain is better than losing one's life!]","Zhang Fang and the others secretly nodded. Compared to their lives, no matter how much it hurt, they had to endure it.","As for the white liquor the Junior Preceptor mentioned, it should be the Pear Blossom White bestowed upon them. That stuff could disinfect wounds?","Maybe they should try it when they get back? Although the Junior Preceptor said it needed to be distilled a few times and they didn't know how to do that, using it undistilled shouldn't cause any problems either.","[Are you going to remind the Crown Prince and the others about alcohol being able to disinfect wounds, Master?]"]},{"number":236,"title":"Chapter 236: Dad, You Left Your Son Here","paragraphs":["Yue Fuguang thought for a moment. Opposite her, in the Zuilai Restaurant, the Crown Prince and his companions, who had been listening to all of this, exchanged glances. Just as they thought the Junior Preceptor would not agree...","...they heard her say, \"Although I don't like some of the behaviors of the Great Yan soldiers, they are still the people of Great Yan. Since I have received the incense offerings from the people, I will help them one last time. I'll find some time to remind the Crown Prince.\"","[It's a pity that with the knowledge and conditions of mortals, they can't produce sulfonamides and penicillin using traditional methods like they can with artemisinin. If they had these two miraculous anti-inflammatory drugs, the casualties among the wounded on the battlefield could be reduced by at least half.]","\"Little Zhu, do you have any stock of these things left?\"","[Master, to us immortals, these things are just like rubble and sand, so I don't have much in stock. Do you want to use them?]","\"Prepare a little for me. Isn't my second brother going to the Sancha region in two months to look after my cotton fields? I'll have him take some just in case.\"","[Should we give him the spiritual elixirs as well?]","\"If mortals use spiritual elixirs and can't control the dosage properly, their bodies will explode and they will die. Divide one Rejuvenation Pill into twenty portions, and give him two of those portions when the time comes.\"","[With these portions of Rejuvenation Pills, even if Yu Boming only has one breath left, taking one will bring him back to life. If he still dies with this, it just means he's too useless, and you can't be blamed, Master.]","When the crowd heard that a tiny piece of a pill could bring someone back to life, their eyes turned red with jealousy. They wanted it!","Yu Huaixian was even more envious. That fool Yu Boming was just going to look after a cotton field for their little cousin. He could do that too!","While the Crown Prince and his companions wanted the pills, they also caught the key points: what were artemisinin, sulfonamides, and penicillin?","Especially the latter two, which could reduce soldiers' casualties. Huo Ying, the Minister of War, had even redder eyes.","Just a moment ago, he was pulling at the Crown Prince asking for alcohol, but now he was staring at him eagerly, wanting penicillin and sulfonamides!","The Crown Prince thought: Do I look like I know what those things are? Even with alcohol, we still have to work hard on the word 'purification'.","\"By the way, Little Zhu, the Sancha region is close to Western Qiang and Northern Li. Do you have any smallpox vaccines in stock?\"","[Does Master mean to vaccinate the soldiers going to the Sancha region to prevent smallpox?]","\"Exactly. If these people are vaccinated before they go, they won't have to fear the smallpox virus ever again.\"","Vaccination, and never fearing smallpox again!","Clang, crash!","Hearing these words, Zhang Fang's hand holding a bowl trembled. The bowl fell onto the table, rolled to the ground, and shattered into two pieces.","Under the table, Shen Chunying quickly kicked his leg. Crack! Alright, the sound of his leg bone snapping brought Zhang Fang completely back to his senses.","Yue Fuguang stole a glance at the little movements under the table and chuckled inwardly. The way martial artists 'woke' each other up was truly simple and unpretentious.","Zhang Fang hurriedly stood up and cupped his hands in apology, \"Please forgive me, Lord Junior Preceptor. This subordinate has been impolite!\"","Yue Fuguang said lightly, \"It's fine. You are injured and your movements are inconvenient. I am not an unreasonable superior.\"","On the Crown Prince's side, Wei Ping looked at the Crown Prince gripping his arm so hard it hurt, yet he didn't dare to make a sound.","Not to mention the Crown Prince, even among the few of them, whose family hadn't lost relatives to smallpox!","They just didn't know if Great Yan could produce the vaccine the Junior Preceptor mentioned.","Hopefully, it wouldn't be like penicillin and sulfonamides, leaving them with empty joy.","[Master, I just checked. Five thousand doses of the vaccine are not enough. How about letting the Imperial Hospital make it themselves?]","Yue Fuguang said, sounding slightly helpless, \"That's the only way. We still have over two months. From development to live trials, with Sun Huajing's medical skills, there should be enough time.\"","After finishing this matter, Yue Fuguang said no more and peacefully enjoyed her second lunch.","Meanwhile, Emperor Mingxi and a group of ministers, who quickly received the news, were pacing back and forth excitedly in the Emperor's Hall of Mental Cultivation.","Each of them looked exactly like ants on a hot pan.","They wanted artemisinin, sulfonamides, and penicillin; they coveted the miraculous elixir that could bring the dead back to life; and they were determined to develop the method to prevent smallpox.","Ji Hongming, who had lost a relative to the poison of smallpox just last year, couldn't help but ask Emperor Mingxi, \"Your Majesty, I wonder when the Junior Preceptor will be able to share the method with us.\"","Emperor Mingxi was also very anxious himself, but seeing the burning gazes of all the officials, he could only pretend to be composed and comfort them, telling them not to rush.","\"Since the Junior Preceptor said she would give it, she will not go back on her word. She knows what she is doing and will certainly not delay the time for the second son of the Yu family and the others to head to the Sancha region.\"","Saying this, he looked towards Yu Chongshan and said, \"My dear minister Yu, the Junior Preceptor hates trouble the most. She will most likely hand the items over to you to pass on. Since there's nothing else today, why don't you leave work early?\"","Ordered by the emperor to leave work early, Yu Chongshan was more than willing. Without any hesitation, he bowed and saluted, \"Your Majesty, then this humble minister will take his leave first.\"","After Emperor Mingxi nodded in agreement, he cupped his hands to his colleagues, \"Thank you for your hard work, gentlemen!\"","With that, he walked away briskly under the envious gazes of his colleagues. Perhaps because he was walking too fast, the spiritual jade pendant given to him by Yue Fuguang swayed at his waist, catching everyone's eyes.","The crowd gritted their teeth. This old guy managed to show off again!","Although they secretly cursed Yu Chongshan for showing off, they knew very well in their hearts that if they were in his position, they would show off even more than he did.","The two brothers, Yu Zhongchun and Yu Shuchun, looked at each other. Watching their father's retreating back, they really wanted to say, 'Father, you left your sons here, please take us with you!'","Equally jealous, Ji Hongming patted his subordinate's shoulder and said earnestly, \"Shuqin, the Ministry of Revenue still needs you. Have the accounts for the fund allocations of the various ministries been sorted out?\"","Yu Shuqin cupped his hands to his superior and said, \"My Lord, they have been sorted out. I used the bookkeeping method taught by my niece, and all the accounts are clear at a glance.\"","The seemingly complex items were handled quickly and accurately using those methods, saving him a lot of effort.","In his heart, he was actually grateful that his niece had thoughtfully considered every aspect for his son. Noticing the envious gazes his colleagues cast his way, Yu Shuchun unconsciously straightened his back!","Speaking of which, Emperor Mingxi understood Yue Fuguang's temper quite well; she was indeed someone who hated trouble.","She truly planned to hand the method of cowpox vaccination, the production method of artemisinin, and a prescription for epidemic diseases over to Yu Chongshan, letting him pass them on.","The favors and merits she didn't need shouldn't be wasted; giving them to the Yu family was just perfect.","As soon as she walked into the Yu Manor, she heard that her grandfather had returned early from work. After a moment of thought, Yue Fuguang understood the reason behind it.","Since she had decided to take the items out, she was also a straightforward person and headed directly to the main hall.","Just as she stepped through the courtyard gate of the main hall, she saw Yu Chongshan standing with his hands behind his back, looking at a few sprouting flowers and plants below the hall.","Seeing her come in, he smiled and said, \"I heard Fuguang went to the East Market. Quickly tell Grandfather, is the East Market fun?\"","Yue Fuguang walked over, pinching the newly sprouted little buds of the plants, and nodded, \"It's quite lively. I even brought back a lot of snacks for Grandfather and Grandmother. Grandfather, you should try some.\"","Flowers and plants: Will some kind soul please speak up for the lives of us poor plants!"]},{"number":237,"title":"Chapter 237: How about going to the manor for a visit tomorrow","paragraphs":["The grandfather and granddaughter walked arm in arm toward the main hall. As soon as Yu Chongshan heard that his granddaughter had brought him back some snacks, he immediately said with delight, \"Fuguang is so thoughtful. This old man must have a good taste of them.\"","Yue Fuguang smiled and said, \"Then let's go to Grandmother's place and enjoy them together.\"","Yu Chongshan chuckled, \"Alright, we'll listen to our Fuguang.\"","The grandfather and granddaughter chatted and laughed as they headed toward Old Madam Yu's courtyard. Meanwhile, Old Madam Yu had already received the news of their arrival.","As soon as the two entered, they were greeted by a table full of tea and pastries, all in Yue Fuguang's favorite flavors.","Yu Chongshan deliberately acted jealous, \"Madam, why isn't there the yellow pea pudding that your husband likes?\"","Old Madam Yu rolled her eyes at him. \"Are the pastries your granddaughter brought back for you not enough for you to eat?\"","\"Here!\" Saying that, Old Madam Yu served him a bowl of spiced tea. \"Didn't I prepare your favorite tea for you?\"","How was this tea? This was practically a bowl of seasoned soup! Fortunately, she usually had various herbal drinks or honey water to drink, so she didn't have to torture her own mouth with this kind of tea.","The system also could not help but complain, [Master, bear with it a little longer. Once the tea trees you planted on the mountain are ready for harvesting, we will roast the tea leaves ourselves.]","Yu Chongshan and Old Madam Yu exchanged a glance. They had long noticed that their granddaughter was very resistant to the tea of Great Yan, so they never made her drink it on normal days.","They just wondered what the roasted tea mentioned by Lord Artifact would be like, and how its taste would differ from the current tea of Great Yan.","\"Speaking of tea trees, we have to make a trip to the estate. The newly planted tea trees, fruit trees, and flowers all need to be nourished by spiritual rain to ensure they all survive and grow quickly. Otherwise, I won't be able to drink any pre-Qingming tea,\" she thought to herself.","[Rest assured, Master. Leave it to Little Zhu. I guarantee not a single one will die!]","Hearing about the spiritual rain, both Yu Chongshan and the old madam felt their hearts stir. Such a miracle—should they follow their granddaughter to go see it when the time came?","Thus, Old Madam Yu said, \"Fuguang, the crops, fruit trees, flower bushes, and tea trees on your estate have all been planted. When will you find time to go take a look? While you're at it, you can see if anything is missing and needs to be added.\"","Yue Fuguang thought for a moment and said, \"Grandmother, have someone dig a large pond near the villa. I want to plant lotus flowers.\"","Looking as if she had expected this, Old Madam Yu smiled and said, \"Grandmother guessed you would want to plant those. I have already ordered people to dig the pond, and the lotus has been planted as well.\"","Yue Fuguang had not expected Old Madam Yu to be so thoughtful. She smiled and said, \"Grandmother still loves me the most. Why don't we go to the estate tomorrow to take a look?\"","Seeing the expectant look in the old madam's eyes, she continued to invite her, \"Grandmother, how about you come with me to the estate to relax?\"","Old Madam Yu smiled lovingly and patted her hand. \"That sounds wonderful. Grandmother hasn't gone out for a walk in a long time. Tomorrow, I'll follow my granddaughter out to stretch my bones and joints. Who knows, I might even live a few years longer.\"","Seeing the grandmother and granddaughter chatting so livelily while leaving him out in the cold, Yu Chongshan could not help but feel a bit jealous. \"You two are planning to leave this old man behind and go have fun by yourselves!\"","The old madam said with a hint of disdain, \"What's wrong with me going out to play with our granddaughter? Aren't you going to work tomorrow?\"","Though her words were tough, seeing her husband's unhappy face, she coaxed, \"Next time you have a day off, we'll take you along to play.\"","Yu Chongshan shook his head. If he waited until next time, who knew if his granddaughter would summon the rain again? \"I will ask His Majesty for a leave of absence tomorrow and go to Fuguang's estate to check on the construction progress of the roads and the villa. This can also be considered official business.\"","That works too? Yue Fuguang could tell that this little old man was dead set on tagging along with them to have fun.","However, it would be good to have her grandfather, a professional, go over and take a look, just in case someone wasn't doing their job diligently and tried to fool her.","So she nodded and said, \"Then Grandfather must help me take a good look and push the progress. It would be best if it could be completed before summer arrives. Then we can go there to escape the summer heat.\"","Old Madam Yu also joined in the fun, \"Yes, yes, yes. You go and push them. Don't delay our granddaughter's summer retreat.\"","Seeing the grandmother and granddaughter chiming in with each other and arranging his tasks for tomorrow so clearly, Yu Chongshan nodded in helpless amusement. \"Alright, alright, it won't be delayed.\"","The person in charge of the project was a trusted subordinate he had personally selected. He wouldn't feel at ease leaving the construction of his granddaughter's estate to just anyone either.","That subordinate was also a master of mechanisms. If it weren't for the need to covertly install a few life-saving mechanisms for his granddaughter, with the manpower invested by the Ministry of Works and the readily available construction materials, it definitely would have been completed within three months.","Seeing that this matter was settled, Yue Fuguang spoke again, \"Speaking of this, it suddenly occurred to me, isn't Second Brother setting off for the Sancha Region in late May?\"","Yu Chongshan thought to himself, Here it comes!","Although he was excited in his heart, his face remained calm and collected. He just smiled and nodded, saying, \"I received a letter from the steward the day before yesterday. The cotton seeds, rice, and wheat have all finished being sown.\"","\"He also mentioned that your tools are incredibly useful and have saved them a lot of effort.\"","\"Your second brother will set off in late May and arrive by early June. That will be exactly when the cotton reaches its flowering and fruiting season. Otherwise, without anyone keeping an eye on it, your father, your uncle, and I wouldn't be at ease.\"","The batch of seeds Fuguang had previously given to the imperial court included cotton seeds. However, it would take at least a year or two of cultivation and practical experience before they could be successfully distributed and grown nationwide.","Therefore, his granddaughter's vast cotton fields were especially important to the Great Yan Dynasty.","An initial workforce of five thousand men had been sent over. When the harvest season arrived, His Majesty intended to dispatch another five thousand.","This meant his granddaughter would command a force of ten thousand men. Even though they were officially imperial troops, everyone knew that they were effectively a private army bestowed upon Fuguang by the Emperor.","\"That region is too close to Northern Li and Western Qiang, where smallpox outbreaks are common. I managed to obtain a method for preventing the disease from a maritime merchant friend of mine. I plan to inoculate Second Brother and the others with this smallpox vaccine before they depart. That way, they won't have to fear the disease anymore.\"","Yu Chongshan remained relatively composed, but Old Madam Yu abruptly grabbed Yue Fuguang's hand. \"Fuguang,\" she asked, her voice trembling with excitement, \"is what you say true? Is there truly a way to prevent smallpox?\"","Seeing his wife's agitated expression, Yu Chongshan was reminded of their fifth child, who had died of the very same disease. The boy had been barely three years old when he passed away, and his wife had nearly followed the child to the grave from sheer grief.","\"Grandmother, I am ninety percent certain that the method works. Once a person is inoculated, there is an over ninety percent chance they will never contract smallpox.\"","\"Over ninety percent! That's more than enough! It's enough!\"","She held tightly to Yue Fuguang's hand, her face etched with sorrow. \"You actually had a Fifth Uncle once. He was taken from us by smallpox.\"","Wiping away her tears, she continued, \"He was only three when he left us. My heart still aches whenever I think of him. He was such a sweet and obedient boy from the day he was born, far more affectionate and sweet-talking than your father or any of your other uncles...\"","The old madam clung to Yue Fuguang's hand, rambling on for quite some time. Yue Fuguang listened attentively. For the elderly woman, even though more than twenty years had passed, the agonizing pain of losing her son had never faded from her heart.","\"My dear, you must be tired. Come, have a cup of honey water to soothe your throat first.\"","Afraid that her grandmother would drown in her sorrow, Yue Fuguang deliberately changed the subject. \"Grandfather, speaking of the smallpox vaccine, I also have a prescription for treating cholera and a method to cure dysentery.\"","As she spoke, she reached into her pouch and pulled out three pieces of paper."]},{"number":238,"title":"Chapter 238: Master, Are We Not Planting the Golden Lotus Anymore","paragraphs":["Yu Chongshan, who had been extremely thrilled to hear all this, couldn't help but twitch his mouth fiercely when he saw his granddaughter casually stuffing such an important prescription into her snack bag.","Indeed, there was a difference between immortals and mortals. What was a heaven-defying treasure to them was probably less important to his granddaughter, this little immortal lord, than her favorite daily pastries.","Yue Fuguang felt quite helpless about it too. She just wasn't used to hiding important things in her robes or sleeves like the people here did.","Since there was no school today, she hadn't brought her schoolbag and could only pretend to take it out of her pouch.","Yu Chongshan took a look but couldn't quite understand it. To produce the item on the prescription, he would still need to find Imperial Physician Sun Huajing.","So he stood up and said, \"Fuguang, this item is far too important. Grandfather will enter the palace to seek an audience with His Majesty right away. The sooner we settle this, the sooner we can develop it. We absolutely cannot delay the day your second brother and the others set off.\"","He had to go now; if His Majesty found out, he would be dragged out of bed even in the middle of the night.","\"Thank you for your trouble, Grandfather.\"","Yue Fuguang was getting more and more comfortable being a hands-off boss. It felt more like the Emperor and his officials were working for her!","Although they were building their own country, she was reaping the real benefits. It was practically an effortless victory!","At present, the Great Yan Dynasty was actually being led by the nose by her. The policy decisions in the royal court and the tasks handled by the various officials were all being carried out, either overtly or covertly, based on her inner thoughts.","Her grandfather waved his hand, his heart filled with profound comfort. \"It is Grandfather, the Yu family, and the imperial court who should be thanking you.\"","Saying that, a sly glint flashed in his eyes. \"If I hand this over today, Grandfather can also comfortably go to the estate with you tomorrow to relax.\"","Yu Chongshan had it all figured out. When he asked His Majesty for leave, he would absolutely not mention a word about the spiritual rain. Otherwise, a whole string of people would definitely follow them.","At most, he would come back and tell them whether the spiritual rain tasted sweet or not.","Yu Chongshan didn't return until late at night. The lights in the imperial palace and the Imperial Academy of Medicine also stayed lit throughout the entire night.","The next day, before the morning assembly even began, the Emperor issued a baffling decree, ordering the prefectures and counties near the capital city to hand over sick cows infected with cowpox.","The imperial court would help treat them uniformly without charging any medical fees.","In ancient times, cattle were crucial means of production and the most important property for many farming households. This out-of-the-blue order immediately sparked a lot of speculation and hesitation.","However, none of this had anything to do with Yue Fuguang and the others, who had stolen a half-day of leisure.","For their outing today, apart from the men who had to go to school or attend court, all the female members of the family had come along to relax.","The Yu family's procession consisted of six carriages, moving at a very slow pace.","This was because the old master and Yue Fuguang each had their own carriage and were sleeping so soundly that they were oblivious to the passing of time.","Yu Chongshan was catching up on sleep because he had left the palace in the middle of the night yesterday.","Yue Fuguang simply needed a lot of sleep. Whether in her past life or this one, her habit of getting drowsy the moment she got into a vehicle hadn't changed a bit.","The convoy swayed and bumped along for two hours before arriving at their destination.","As soon as she got off the carriage, Yue Fuguang saw that the fields and hillsides, which had been a faint light green during her last visit, were now fully clothed in lush greenery.","The air was filled with the fresh scent of earth and vegetation.","The dewdrops on the grass blades hadn't completely vanished yet, and as the sunlight pierced through the morning mist and shone upon them, looking from afar...","They twinkled like stars on a green canvas.","Yue Fuguang stretched comfortably. She still preferred nature. When summer came, she would definitely stay here for a while.","Everyone pretended not to see her behavior, which was quite unbecoming of a noble lady.","They could see that the smile on the child's face was much more genuine than usual; she must truly love this place.","But thinking about it, it made sense. Wasn't it said that immortals liked to live in seclusion in otherworldly mountains and forests, leading a carefree life like idle clouds and wild cranes?","It was truly a grievance for Fuguang, an immortal lord, to live in the noisy city!","Yue Fuguang was unaware of the fleeting guilt in her family's hearts. She just smiled as she watched Yu Ningxuan mimic her actions and stretch as well.","\"Second Sister, don't you feel relaxed all over after doing that?\"","Her smile sparkled in the sunlight, and the lotus mark on her forehead also shone brightly.","Yu Ningxuan thought to herself that her Seventh Sister was looking more and more like a heavenly immortal. Even though she was standing right beside her, she gave off an indescribable ethereal feeling, as if mountains and seas separated them, and she could soar into the sky at any moment.","Thinking such groundless thoughts in her heart, she replied, \"It really does. I feel like my bones and muscles have all stretched out.","You have no idea. To come out and play today, I rushed my homework yesterday, and my hand and shoulders got stiff from writing.\"","On the days Yue Fuguang attended court, the sisters Yu Ningxuan and Yu Ningxin still had to attend classes at the Hongwen Academy as usual. To take a leave today, they naturally had to finish their homework in advance.","\"When I have free time, I'll teach you a few ways to exercise, Sister. As long as you keep practicing, I guarantee you'll live a long and healthy life.\"","Not to mention Tai Chi, the Five Animal Frolics, and the Eight Section Brocade, even those fitness methods in the system that cost a few dozen points could help people strengthen their bodies and prolong their lives if practiced well.","\"Really? That's wonderful! I will definitely learn them properly when the time comes!\"","Yu Ningxuan knew very well that not a single item her Seventh Sister brought out was ordinary.","The Fourth Madam, Madam Bao, nudged Yu Ningrong. The foot Yu Ningrong had just lifted fell back down.","Madam Bao sighed helplessly in her heart. Her daughter cared too much about her pride. Because of past events, Fuguang hadn't pursued the matter, but she remained somewhat distant towards them.","However, her husband, the Fourth Master, was currently working under Fuguang, so their branch of the family was naturally considered Fuguang's people.","Regardless of her daughter's attitude, as long as they were respectful to Fuguang and maintained the loyalty the Fourth Master spoke of, they wouldn't miss out on the benefits they deserved.","As for whether an uncle and aunt showing loyalty to their niece would cause them to lose face?","Madam Bao scoffed inwardly. This was a blessing that countless people begged for but couldn't get; how could they be so ungrateful as to disdain it?","Thinking of the banquet invitations she had recently received from various madams addressed specifically to her, she couldn't help but feel delighted. In the past, such invitations would never have been sent to her.","All of this was thanks to Fuguang.","Today, she was originally supposed to attend a gathering hosted by Madam Liu, the wife of a Ministry of Rites official. Because she had to follow Fuguang to the estate, she could only send someone to explain why she had to cancel.","According to her senior maid's report, when Madam Liu and the other ladies heard the reason, they couldn't hide the envy on their faces.","Madam Bao felt happy and wanted to do something to contribute, so she said to Old Madam Yu, \"Mother, I see the wild vegetables in the fields are fresh and tender. Why don't we pick some to make soup?","I remember Fuguang likes to drink shepherd's purse and meatball soup.\"","Old Madam Yu nodded. \"The fourth daughter-in-law is very thoughtful. Make some small wontons as well. Fuguang didn't eat much for breakfast; she'll be hungry soon.\"","Hearing this, Madam Bao became even happier and immediately said, \"Mother, I will take the maids to pick some right away. It will be ready in no time.\"","As she spoke, she called the young maids to fetch the tools.","When Yue Fuguang heard they were going to dig for wild vegetables, her interest was immediately piqued, and she rubbed her hands together, ready to join in the fun.","Seeing this, the system hurriedly stopped her. [Master, did you forget that we need to go plant the golden lotus? It's already the middle of the Chen hour.","If the Chen hour passes, you'll have to wait until tomorrow to plant it.]"]},{"number":239,"title":"Chapter 239: So you intended to let them get caught in the rain.","paragraphs":["Yue Fuguang gently patted her forehead, almost forgetting about this matter. This golden lotus wasn't just pretty to look at; it was also an incredibly precious medicinal herb.","Every part of it was a treasure.","It was one of the few plants from the cultivation world that could be grown in the mortal realm, where there was no spiritual energy.","It had a specific habit: it had to be planted during the hour of Chen, between seven and nine in the morning, and right after planting, it required spiritual energy to nourish it and help it take root.","Yue Fuguang played with a green jade stone in her hand, slightly larger than a quail egg. Its translucency was even better than the spiritual jade hanging at Yu Chongshan's waist.","This was the spiritual stone she had hoarded back then, perfectly suited to nourish the golden lotus.","\"Grandfather, Grandmother, I brought the lotus seeds. I'm going to the pond to plant them first.\"","The two elders knew she was talking about the golden lotus, but they didn't know how Fuguang's golden lotus differed from the ones in the pond at the back mountain of Baoye Temple.","\"Let's go, Grandfather and Grandmother will go with you.\"","Yu Chongshan smiled and said, \"When your grandfather was young, I even sneaked to the pond at the back mountain of Baoye Temple to pick lotus seeds.\"","Old Madam Yu added, \"The back mountain of Baoye Temple your grandfather mentioned also has a few golden lotuses planted there. They only bloom a few flowers every year.","Over all these years, the lotus pond hasn't grown many new lotuses, which shows how delicate and hard to raise golden lotuses are.\"","Speaking of this, Old Madam Yu laughed again. \"Because of stealing lotus seeds, your grandfather was punished by your great-grandfather to kneel in the ancestral hall for a whole night.\"","As for the part about getting spanked with a board, she saved her old man's face and didn't mention it to their granddaughter.","Hearing his old wife expose his embarrassing past, Yu Chongshan was displeased and forced himself to save face, saying, \"Who was I doing it for? If it wasn't for you saying you wanted to eat fresh lotus seeds when you were pregnant with our third child.","At that time, only the golden lotuses at Baoye Temple had lotus seeds, otherwise, I wouldn't have gone to pull a tooth from the tiger's mouth.\"","Back then, if it weren't for his good martial arts skills, he would have almost been caught red-handed by the martial monks in the temple.","Even so, he didn't escape a beating when he got home. Poor him, he was already a father of several children at that time!","\"My golden lotus is much better than the ones at Baoye Temple,\" she said as she took out nine lotus seeds from her pouch. They sparkled like round golden beads.","The two elders each picked one up to look closely, and couldn't help but praise, \"It is indeed better than the lotus seeds at Baoye Temple. The lotus pod I sto... ahem, picked back then only had five lotus seeds inside. They were pale gold and not as plump as this one.\"","[Master, your grandfather has quite a good eye. This golden lotus is no ordinary item. In the world today, only the two of us, master and servant, can grow it successfully.]","Not an ordinary item? No wonder!","Yu Chongshan secretly thought to himself that once the golden lotus grew, he would have to send more men to help his granddaughter guard it, in case she encountered someone like him... ahem! In case she encountered someone unafraid of death.","The group soon arrived at the pond, which was only separated from the courtyard garden by a wall. Looking ahead, the pond was about five or six mu in size.","Stones were placed around it, and flowers and grass were planted, though they hadn't grown yet in this season.","Seeing the effort put into it, one could foresee that in the season of warm spring and blooming flowers, this place would definitely be a beautiful sight.","Old Madam Yu pointed to a spot in the west and said, \"Fuguang, the flower farmers planted white and pink lotuses over there.\"","\"Then we'll plant the golden lotuses in the east. Later, we can open a small door in this courtyard wall, so we can see the lotus pond as soon as we step out.\"","Golden lotuses were domineering and naturally had to be kept far away from those regular lotuses, otherwise, the latter wouldn't survive.","Walking to the east side, Yue Fuguang casually scattered the nine lotus seeds in her hand into the pond water. Finally, she tossed the spiritual stone in her hand into the water as well. Feeling it wasn't enough, she tossed in three more with a plop, plop, plop, before stopping.","Seeing their granddaughter throw such high-quality spiritual jade into the water, the two elders couldn't help but feel a bit of heartache, but they said nothing.","The items belonged to their granddaughter, so naturally, she could do whatever she wanted with them.","As people get older, they should meddle less so as not to annoy the younger generation.","Besides, since Fuguang did this, there must be a reason for it.","Yu Chongshan thought a bit more. He looked around and felt relieved. Fortunately, as soon as they arrived, the manager had cleared out all the irrelevant people.","Except for their respective attendants, no one saw the treasures their granddaughter threw into the water.","'Little Zhu, activate the spiritual stones to help the golden lotus grow.'","[Received!]","The couple exchanged a glance. It turned out that such beautiful stones were called spiritual stones, not spiritual jade as they had thought.","So the growth of this golden lotus actually relied on such good things for nourishment.","That made it much more delicate and precious than the golden lotuses at Baoye Temple!","Not long after planting the golden lotus, Lady Bao sent someone with a message, saying the wontons were ready.","Yue Fuguang happily ate two small bowls of shepherd's purse and pork wontons, suddenly feeling energized again.","\"Grandfather, Grandmother, I want to go up the mountain to check on the tea trees and fruit trees.\"","[Master, we can sneakily make it rain spiritual rain on the mountain. The sun is perfect today. A sun shower will let us see a rainbow on the mountain.]","'Little Zhu, that's a good idea. Later, I'll bring all the guards we brought along up the mountain, so they can take the opportunity to get caught in the rain.'","[Master, Zhang Fang and the other injured ones are following too. You didn't object. Are you planning to let the spiritual rain heal their injuries?]","'Exactly. I noticed that Cuizhu, Chunying, and Dongxue all have hidden injuries from practicing martial arts. Getting caught in a rain shower will be good for them.'","Yue Fuguang linked her arm with Old Madam Yu's and smiled at Lady Zhang and the others, \"Grandfather, Grandmother, Mother, Aunts, do you want to go up the mountain to have a look together?\"","[Master, you're just climbing a small dirt hill. Do you need to bring the whole family?]","'Little Zhu, you don't know this. If I don't drag them along, when it rains later, my mother and grandmother will definitely hide in their rooms.'","[So you were planning to make them get caught in the rain all along.]","'Of course! Your master is smart, right! Getting drenched in your spiritual rain for a while has effects not much worse than a Body Strengthening Pill.'","Praised by Yue Fuguang, the system proudly puffed out its round little body in the system space and said arrogantly, [Little Zhu's spiritual rain can not only help plants grow.","Even if mortals drink it, it only brings benefits without the slightest harm.]","'Now that you mention it, after today, won't the weeds on the mountain and in the fields grow wildly alongside the crops and fruit trees?'","The system said nonchalantly, [What's there to fear? Just pull them out when they grow. Weeds that grow up drinking spiritual rain are top-quality fodder.","Master, absolutely do not waste them!]","'It's impossible not to waste them. I can't exactly tell Grandfather and Grandmother that these weeds are great treasures, even more nutritious than soybean cakes and rice bran.'","Yu Chongshan chuckled inwardly. Rest assured, Granddaughter, Grandfather promises not to waste a single bit.","He would have to send a trusted confidant to handle this matter, and he couldn't keep it from His Majesty either.","Not bringing him along to plant the golden lotus, not bringing him along to catch the spiritual rain... Yu Chongshan could imagine how resentful His Majesty would be when the time came. But there was no fear, he had a backup plan.","Sitting steadily in the Golden Throne Room, Emperor Mingxi, who was still listening to the courtiers in the hall arguing endlessly about how to handle the accomplices of the Four Great Families, suddenly let out a soft sneeze.","He casually picked up the tea in front of him and took a small sip, gesturing for them to continue bickering, while he could just use this opportunity to slack off for a bit.","Emperor Mingxi's thoughts instantly flew outside the hall. He wondered what delicious food Fuguang would make at the estate today..."]},{"number":240,"title":"Chapter 240: Is the Size of Zhuangzi Incorrect","paragraphs":["Catching a glimpse out of the corner of his eye of the crown prince, who was visibly distracted below the dais, Emperor Mingxi had a sudden thought: Should he let the crown prince go take a look?","Anyway, looking at his son, his body was still here, but his soul had probably wandered off a while ago.","\"Imperial Father, this isn't very appropriate, is it!\"","Xie Zhiyan had just arrived at the Hall of Mental Cultivation and was about to dive headfirst into the vast ocean of memorials when he never expected his imperial father to suddenly suggest he go to the Junior Preceptor's estate to see what she was doing.","Although the crown prince also really wanted to cast aside the endless memorials and go out to clear his head right now, having him go to the Junior Preceptor's estate...","It always felt a bit like he was tailing and spying on her.","\"Crown Prince, your marriage with the Shen family's girl has already reached the stage of requesting the wedding date, which happens to require a wild goose. Why don't you go hunt one?\"","There happened to be a large river next to Fu Guang's estate where wild geese often appeared. For the crown prince to pass by her estate to hunt a goose for his wedding would be perfectly justifiable.","\"Imperial Father, hasn't the Imperial Astronomy Bureau already set the wedding date for the ninth of next month?\"","The crown prince's grand wedding was a major event for the entire Great Yan court. All the civil and military officials in the court would start preparing their wedding gifts six months to a year in advance.","\"Although the wedding date has already been set, the procedure of going to the bride's home to request the date hasn't been done yet. The wild goose is indispensable!\"","Originally, the Ministry of Rites had already prepared one, but if the crown prince personally hunted one, who could say it was wrong?","Seeing his son dawdling, Emperor Mingxi impatiently said, \"Just tell me, do you want to go or not!\"","As soon as he saw his imperial father's expression, the crown prince very obediently said, \"I'll go. Your son will go right away.\"","Saying that, he cupped his hands to Emperor Mingxi and walked out of the hall. His quick little steps were so fast, it was as if a dog were chasing him from behind!","Meanwhile, Yue Fuguang, oblivious to the fact that the crown prince had been shooed over by his own parent, was still leading her large family, huffing and puffing their way up a mountain!","From a distance, this mountain didn't look very high, but once they actually started climbing, it proved somewhat strenuous for the madams and young ladies who rarely stepped out of their inner courtyards.","They had only reached halfway up the mountain, and all the masters, old and young, except for her and Yu Chongshan, were sweating profusely from exhaustion.","\"Grandmother, Mother, Second Aunt, Fourth Aunt, let's rest here for a while.\"","These few were older after all, unlike Yu Ningxuan and her sisters, who, although tired, could still hold on if they really had to keep climbing.","The spot on the mountainside where they stopped had a small platform. A small pavilion was built on it, and judging from the timber, it should be newly constructed by the Ministry of Works.","At this moment, everyone sat in the pavilion and looked down the mountain, where they could just see the bustling construction site at the foot.","A construction team of seven or eight hundred people was quite spectacular.","It wasn't noticeable at the foot of the mountain, but once up on the mountain, looking down from a commanding height, Yue Fuguang quickly realized something was wrong.","She couldn't help but ask Yu Chongshan, who was sitting beside her drinking tea, \"Grandfather, isn't the size of the estate a bit off right now? It looks like it's being built according to the sketch I drew.","But isn't it a bit too big?\"","She didn't know much about building materials in ancient times, but the main gate of the manor had already begun to take shape, and its scale seemed somewhat inappropriate!","Yu Chongshan smiled mysteriously and lowered his voice, \"Fuguang saw it too?\"","Yue Fuguang looked at Yu Chongshan with a puzzled face. It seemed the old master had known all along. Since he knew but didn't say anything, there must be an inside story.","Seeing that although no one moved, their ears clearly perked up, he continued softly, \"All the building materials and scales were personally arranged by His Majesty.\"","He pursed his lips toward the foot of the mountain and said, \"The scale is being built according to the standards of a Prince of the First Rank, and the materials are even comparable to the Crown Prince's Eastern Palace.\"","\"This...\" Except for the person involved, Yue Fuguang, and Old Madam Yu, who had seen her fair share of great storms.","The other female family members of the Yu family were all so shocked that their eyes went wide. Constrained by etiquette, they hastily used the silk handkerchiefs in their hands to cover their mouths, clutching their chests with their other hand.","Seeing everyone's expressions of shock turning into sheer dumbfoundedness, Yue Fuguang found it quite amusing, imagining that beneath their handkerchiefs, her aunts and sisters were all forming uniform, large O shapes with their mouths.","\"Father, our Fuguang, Fuguang she...\" Second Aunt Yu was a bit too excited to know what to say. The word Prince swirled around the tip of her tongue, but she didn't dare utter it aloud.","Fourth Aunt Yu's face was also filled with excitement, and her hands, gripping Yu Ningrong's, were sweating slightly.","Seeing her mother's excited expression, Yu Ningrong thought it looked exactly like the time she found out her father had gotten a principal sixth-rank official post.","In the end, she didn't say anything to spoil the mood.","The other sisters were also flushed red, and Yu Ningxuan's dimples deepened even more as she smiled.","After her excitement subsided, Madam Zhang still couldn't help asking Yu Chongshan, \"Father, is this truly His Majesty's intention?\"","Seeing that her father-in-law had clearly known this all along, did her husband know that their daughter had the prospect of becoming a Prince of the First Rank?","And a female Prince at that! Throughout history, there had been quite a few female generals, and even female marquises, but the only one fortunate enough to become a Prince was their family's Fuguang!","Looking at his eldest daughter-in-law's excited yet disbelieving expression, and then at the female family members gazing at him with eager anticipation, only his own wife remained somewhat calm.","He couldn't help but tease Old Madam Yu, \"The children don't believe my words. Madam, hurry up and validate me.\"","Old Madam Yu lightly patted her husband's arm. \"You're teasing the children again, old man.\"","Then she said to everyone, \"Just keep it to yourselves. You must absolutely not go out and speak nonsense.\"","At the same time, she held Yue Fuguang's chubby little hand and said, \"Besides, what is my granddaughter not worthy of being?\"","She was an Immortal Lord! To be a Prince in their mortal realm was already a grievance to her.","Sure enough, just as Old Madam Yu thought this, the grand complaints of the Divine Artifact Lord echoed in her ears.","[Master, it's just a mortal Prince, is it worth them being so happy?","We don't even care for the position of Emperor, so why would we think highly of the position of a Prince?]","'Whether it's a Prince or not doesn't matter, but the courtyard at the foot of the mountain looks like it's being built quite nicely.'","[Master has forgotten, your Immortal Palace was what you call beautiful. This courtyard at the foot of the mountain isn't even as good as the place where the spirit cranes, the mounts of minor immortals, live.","Not to mention the spirit flowers that bloom for a hundred years without withering, and the spirit fruits that can prolong life when eaten. Not a single one of those could survive being planted here.]","'Little Zhu, we have to do as the locals do. Although this place isn't as good as our Immortal Palace, it has a different kind of charm.'","[If Master likes it, then Little Zhu will plant some immortal herbs in your courtyard that can survive in the mortal realm. Although they aren't as beautiful as spirit flowers, these mortal flowers and grasses are truly a bit too tacky.]","Everyone's hearts skipped a beat. How could they have forgotten? This precious golden lump was an Immortal Lord. How could a deity care for a mortal position? Even the position of a Prince couldn't compare to a minor immortal sweeping a deity's courtyard.","With the shot in the arm that the Yu family was about to produce a Prince, everyone suddenly felt filled with energy.","As they walked along the mountain path, it was as if there was wind beneath their feet.","The people following behind to protect Yue Fuguang's safety also had various thoughts in their minds, but the flush on their faces, which was no less than that of the Yu family members, showed that their inner hearts were not calm either.","Especially Yu Mochun and Yu Huaixian, these two Yu family members. The sharp glint in their eyes could almost rival the sun in the sky.","They didn't walk together with their family members, but instead followed behind with the escort guards. It could be said that the two of them had a very clear understanding of their own roles."]},{"number":241,"title":"Chapter 241: Open the Door, Free Trade","paragraphs":["Falling behind at the back, the Shen sisters, Liu Wei, and Xu Xiaoman silently gripped each other's hands tightly.","Their Great Yan was about to produce a female Prince. As the Prince's guards, as long as they remained loyal and stayed by Her Highness's side for the rest of their lives, those men wouldn't dare utter a single word of complaint.","Yue Fuguang stood at the summit, looking down in all directions. As far as her eyes could see, it was all her land, planted with the highest-yielding crops in Great Yan, as well as fruits and vegetables that didn't even exist here before.","They would all become seeds to be planted throughout the entirety of Great Yan. She refused to believe that with enough food, she couldn't complete the natural disaster population preservation quest worth 188,000 points.","If she really couldn't complete it, then it would be because Emperor Mingxi and the officials of Great Yan had failed in their promotion and management.","She wouldn't mind replacing useless beasts of burden with a batch of capable ones!","Since Great Yan couldn't push forward with land reform, she planned to wait until the natural disasters passed and then take a drastic measure, directly launching industrialization tailored to Great Yan's national conditions.","With her high-yielding premium seeds, the people of Great Yan would no longer have to fear starvation.","Those who lost their land could all go work in factories, completely breaking away from their dependence on the land.","Once the neighboring countries were conquered, they would serve as ready-made granaries!","Especially Nanyue and Nanzhao, where crops ripened two or three times a year, what excellent granaries they would make!","Then there were Beili and Xiqiang, where animal husbandry could be developed. As for Dongyi, the fishing industry and maritime trade would be left to them.","It could be said that before even taking the first step, Yue Fuguang had already clearly arranged what these countries should do a hundred steps down the line!","Reaching this point in her thoughts, Yue Fuguang seemed to hear a super loud shout echoing in her ears: Open the door, free trade!","Amused by her own thoughts, she couldn't help but say, \"Little Zhu, the weather is so nice. How about a shower of rain to add to the fun?\"","The Crown Prince, who was nearing the top of the mountain, suddenly heard the Junior Preceptor's inner voice and couldn't help but think: It's such a beautiful spring day, yet this ancestor wants to make it rain for fun!","Did all immortals have this kind of thought process?","In his mind, the court musicians and dancers, who had long been left idle by his imperial father and were previously used for entertainment and amusement, involuntarily surfaced.","Over the past half year, whenever his imperial father was in a good mood, he would either summon his key ministers to discuss state affairs or enjoy a lavish feast. In the past, there used to be a third option: strolling through the inner palace.","Ever since being secretly criticized by these two ancestors, his imperial father had been so frightened that he rarely visited the inner palace anymore.","He couldn't help but look up at the sky. A moment ago, the spring sunshine had been bright and beautiful, and the fragrant grass lush.","The next moment, the wind and clouds shifted, signaling an impending mountain storm! Fierce winds howled!","He couldn't suppress an inexplicable sense of shock in his heart. Was this the mighty power of a deity?","Just as this thought crossed his mind, a strong gust of wind swept past, and the dark clouds overhead grew thicker and thicker.","When the entire sky and earth changed color, fine and dense threads of rain began to fall from the heavens.","Xie Zhiyan halted his steps and gazed into the distance. This rain was truly a custom creation of the Little Immortal; it was only falling over their patch of land and the mountain peak.","The Yu family and the guards behind Yue Fuguang were no less shocked than the Crown Prince!","Immortals controlled the laws of heaven and earth. The shifting of winds and clouds was dictated by just a single word from them.","If they hadn't had reservations, they truly would have wanted to kneel and worship in awe.","Yu Huaixian and a few others standing guard at the outermost perimeter silently opened their mouths wide. How could letting the rain fall on their bodies be as effective as drinking it straight into their mouths?","Zhang Fang and a few others who had been injured yesterday even silently removed their bandages. They didn't know if it was just an illusion, but the moment their wounds touched the rainwater.","They instantly stopped aching and itching, and even showed signs of slowly healing.","The men exchanged glances and silently kept their mouths shut. As long as no one asked, they absolutely wouldn't breathe a word about it!","[Master, how is this amount of rainfall?]","\"Not bad. The rain covers all my fields. In a few months, these will be the best batch of seeds in Great Yan.\"","[Huh, why is Xie Zhiyan here? This fool is actually holding an umbrella.]","Yue Fuguang turned around to look, just in time to see the Crown Prince lifting the hem of his robe, striding over with a tall and straight posture, while an attendant beside him held up an umbrella for him.","\"Nice umbrella. Not a single drop of rain fell on him.\"","Dark lines formed on Xie Zhiyan's face. How could holding an umbrella in the rain earn him the title of fool from Lord Divine Artifact?","Seeing the Junior Preceptor's agreeing expression, were these two ancestors sure they weren't targeting him?","[If he finds out about the effects of this rainwater afterward, will he regret it to death? Hahahaha!]","The system's laughter, clearly enjoying the drama without minding the consequences, made Xie Zhiyan feel uneasy. Then he looked at the Yu family standing in the spring rain with faces full of enjoyment.","It was only the beginning of spring, yet not a single person was holding an umbrella. The female family members were just letting the rain drench them like this. Were they really not afraid of the cold? Or was there something peculiar about this rain?","Recalling what Lord Divine Artifact had said about the rainwater's effects... If it said he would regret it, then he absolutely would regret it!","Xie Zhiyan wasn't one to agonize over things either. Regardless of the effects, he decided he might as well get drenched first. Otherwise, he really might miss out on a heaven-sent opportunity.","He pushed away the umbrella over his head and said, \"Since the Junior Preceptor is not using an umbrella, Zhiyan naturally must keep you company.\"","The reasoning was very strong, so Qi Xiang did not dare to urge him further.","Seeing the Crown Prince's arrival, everyone respectfully bowed in greeting.","\"How does His Royal Highness have the leisure to come here?\"","Yue Fuguang looked at the bow and arrows carried by the attendant behind him. Was he here to hunt?","Her mountain had been cleared out. Aside from wild game like pheasants and rabbits, there was no large prey.","[He was lucky enough to catch our spiritual rain. If he had this kind of luck in his past life, he wouldn't have been left with the title of Fragrant Crown Prince.]","Xie Zhiyan: Can't my luck turn around? Having the two of you is my greatest blessing!","The Crown Prince tried hard to force a blush onto his face and said, \"For my marriage with the daughter of the Shen family, requesting the wedding date requires a wild goose. I had some free time today, so I specifically came to try my luck.\"","He pointed to a large river overgrown with reeds not far from the foot of the mountain and said, \"I heard that wild geese often roost in that reed marsh.","I happened to pass by the estate and remembered that the Junior Preceptor was here today, so I came over to take a look.\"","Yue Fuguang nodded. \"So that's it. I almost forgot, the ninth day of the fourth lunar month is the Crown Prince's wedding day.\"","She then smiled and added, \"It is very thoughtful of the Crown Prince to think of personally hunting a wild goose to present to the bride.\"","It was evident that the Crown Prince was quite satisfied with his future Crown Princess.","The Crown Prince, teased by her slightly playful smile, no longer needed to force it, his face had genuinely begun to flush red.","Xie Zhiyan hurriedly changed the subject, saying, \"The rain is getting heavier. Junior Preceptor, Lord Yu, your clothes are getting wet. Should we take shelter from the rain, or head straight down the mountain?\"","Everyone shook their heads in their hearts. Taking shelter from the rain was absolutely out of the question.","Although the rainwater soaked their heads and faces, they didn't feel the icy chill of a typical early spring rain at all.","The rain wasn't hot, but it gave them the sensation of bathing in a hot spring.","Yu Chongshan smiled and said, \"There is no need to take shelter. Spring rain is as precious as oil. How about we take advantage of this spring shower and walk slowly down the mountain?\"","Yue Fuguang nodded. \"Heading down the mountain now will get us back just in time for lunch.\"","[Master, your plan was almost ruined by this stupid Crown Prince.]","\"He who does not know is not to blame. You can't expect a mortal to understand the ultimate truths of heaven and earth like an immortal.\"","Although Xie Zhiyan, bearing the title of stupid Crown Prince, had been scolded by Lord Divine Artifact once again, he couldn't muster even the slightest bit of anger at this moment.","To have the fortunate encounter of being drenched in such rain, what did it matter if he was scolded a few times?","Therefore, looking from afar, this group of people descending the mountain appeared exceedingly bizarre.","Not only was their descent slower than their ascent, but the refined mood they lacked when going up the mountain had suddenly appeared while getting soaked in the rain on their way down."]},{"number":242,"title":"Chapter 242: He also wants to watch a play, so let's see how the emperor changes his expression","paragraphs":["The Crown Prince led the way, followed by Yu Ningxuan, Yu Ningxin, and the other sisters. They spent their time admiring flowers, searching for herbs, and composing poetry.","In short, their main focus could be summed up in one word: dawdling!","Old Madam Yu, Madam Zhang, and her sisters-in-law were actually walking much more briskly now than when they first climbed the mountain, yet they insisted that the rainy mountain path was treacherous and they needed to walk slowly.","[Master, what kind of luck do these people have? If they keep walking like this while I gather the clouds and bring the rain, they will be drenched from head to toe.]","\"Why else do you think I dragged the whole family up the mountain? It was all so they could get rained on in a perfectly reasonable way. Just do your job and make it rain, and let them get soaked.\"","The group finally dawdled until the clouds parted and the rain stopped before returning to the estate.","\"Do not wash these clothes. Pack them away carefully in a box for me.\"","This exact instruction echoed in quite a few rooms. The maids did not understand, but they respected the orders!","Seeing how much importance their masters placed on this, they all carefully packed the clothes away. As for what they were actually thinking in their hearts, no one could tell.","After a hearty lunch, the crowd, who should have been exhausted, were instead brimming with energy.","Yu Chongshan said he was going to check on the growth of the crops in the fields, while Yu Ningxuan and the other girls said they wanted to follow Madam Zhang and the others to dig for wild vegetables.","Madam Zhang said with a smile, \"I noticed that Fuguang quite enjoyed the dishes made with shepherd's purse today, and so did Father and Mother. Why don't we dig up some more before heading back to the manor?","We can also bring some back for the Master and the boys to try something fresh.\"","Old Madam Yu nodded in agreement, very satisfied with her eldest daughter-in-law's quick wit.","The Crown Prince, who had originally planned to go catch wild geese, couldn't help but change his mind upon hearing this. Although his imperial mother and imperial grandmother hadn't had the chance to get rained on,","they absolutely could not miss out on the wild vegetables nourished by the spiritual rain.","He was just wondering what excuse he could use to join the vegetable-digging team without seeming out of place, when he heard Old Madam Yu ask, \"Fuguang, are you going out to play with your mother and aunts, or are you going to rest for a while?\"","This child had a habit of taking afternoon naps, rain or shine. Old Madam Yu had already ordered a young maid to make her bed, so she was merely asking out of courtesy.","\"Grandmother, I'm sleepy. I want to sleep for a bit.\"","The Crown Prince relaxed. Once Yue Fuguang went for her nap, he didn't even need to find an excuse; Yu Chongshan had already ordered someone to prepare the tools for him.","The next time Emperor Mingxi saw his son, it was in the Empress Dowager's palace.","From the doorway, he could hear the cheerful laughter coming from inside the hall. \"Crown Prince, I heard that you came back covered in mud. Did you fail to catch any wild geese and fall into the river instead?\"","Faced with his imperial father's teasing, Xie Zhiyan didn't even have to open his mouth before he heard the Empress Dowager say, \"Which blabbermouth did the Emperor hear this from?\"","She glared crossly at the attendants beside the Emperor.","Qian Gui, who was standing behind the Emperor, thought: I am truly wronged! I am wherever His Majesty is. Even if I wanted to blabber, I wouldn't have any gossip to share!","Emperor Mingxi raised an eyebrow and looked at the Crown Prince, saying, \"Crown Prince, you tell me. Is that not the case?\"","Seeing his imperial mother speak up for his son, Emperor Mingxi suddenly felt a sense of falling out of favor. Could it be that he was no longer his imperial mother's favorite son?","He refused to believe it!","Xie Zhiyan chuckled inwardly. He just wondered if his imperial father would still have this calm, spectating expression once he revealed the truth.","He, too, wanted to watch a good show and see how his imperial father's face would change.","The Crown Prince bowed and said, \"It is exactly as Imperial Father said. I was indeed covered in mud when I returned to the palace.\"","\"The Crown Prince should be a role model for all subjects in the world. Your etiquette is not only a matter of personal cultivation, but it also concerns the order of the state and the image presented to the world.","The Crown Prince's status is noble, so your adherence to etiquette and proper conduct must be even more rigorous. There is no room for any negligence. This is both a safeguard of your status and an example for the people of the world...\"","Emperor Mingxi spoke with great fervor. How long had it been since he had lectured his son so thoroughly and satisfyingly?","It seemed like it had been since the Junior Preceptor appeared...?","Xie Zhiyan bowed and listened quietly, silently watching him perform. The happier his imperial father was speaking now, the harder the slap to his face would be later.","He just didn't know if his imperial father would still have the face to eat the things he brought back.","Waiting until Emperor Mingxi had finished his passionate speech and picked up his teacup to moisten his throat, Xie Zhiyan finally said, \"Imperial Father's reprimand is correct. I will not do it again next time.\"","He deliberately smiled with a hint of embarrassment. \"It was also my recklessness today. I thought about how Imperial Grandmother, Imperial Father, and Imperial Mother didn't have the chance to get caught in the rain.","So I figured it would be good for you to taste the wild vegetables that had absorbed the rainwater.\"","\"What rain? What wild vegetables?\"","Emperor Mingxi was taken aback by his seemingly nonsensical words.","Why did he suddenly have the lingering illusion that he was about to be tricked!","The Empress Dowager gave a mischievous smile and said, \"Crown Prince, repeat what you just told your imperial grandmother and imperial mother to your imperial father.\"","\"Yes.\" The Crown Prince turned to Emperor Mingxi and said, \"Following Imperial Father's orders, I...\"","Emperor Mingxi gritted his teeth and said, \"So, the Little Immortal Lord and the Divine Artifact Lord brought down a spiritual rain upon the estate!\"","He clenched his fists. \"This spiritual rain not only helps the crops grow, but even people who get caught in it will find their bodies growing stronger?\"","\"That is indeed the case. Not to mention myself, but Song Xiang and the guards who accompanied me, some of them had hidden injuries and old wounds from years of martial arts practice or running errands, and all of them have shown signs of improvement.\"","It wasn't just signs of improvement; they were mostly healed.","However, the Crown Prince didn't dare to say that, afraid that his imperial father wouldn't be able to handle the shock!","\"My clothes were drenched in the rain. After changing my attire, I thought about how Imperial Father, Imperial Grandmother, and Imperial Mother had missed out on enjoying the spiritual rain. However, you could eat some of the wild vegetables, which would also have some effect.\"","As the Crown Prince spoke, Emperor Mingxi's expression shifted continuously, making for quite a spectacular sight.","His face was now slightly flushed with embarrassment. \"Your clothes were dirtied while digging for wild vegetables?\"","Xie Zhiyan nodded. Emperor Mingxi forced himself to salvage his dignity, putting on a look of great comfort as he said, \"My son is kind and filial. Even when you are away, you do not forget your grandmother and parents at home.","As your father, I am deeply gratified. Later, I must properly taste my son's filial piety.\"","Xie Zhiyan suppressed the urge to roll his eyes. Seeing the excuse his imperial father forced out just so he could eat more and take a larger share, he admitted that he had truly learned something new!","Today, his imperial father had taught him another lesson through his own words and deeds, and the tuition fee was the plates of wild vegetables served by the Imperial Kitchen.","Just as he picked up a chopstick full of fresh and tender wild vegetables, Emperor Mingxi suddenly thought of something and asked the Crown Prince, \"Your wet clothes...\"","\"Eunuch Zhao has already placed them in Imperial Father's washroom.\" Eunuch Zhao, whose full name was Zhao Tuo, was the head eunuch responsible for Emperor Mingxi's daily washing and grooming.","The Crown Prince could still vividly recall the indescribable expression on the eunuch's face when he heard his request, an expression of wanting to speak but not daring to.","Emperor Mingxi couldn't care less if the eunuch beside him suspected his son had something wrong with his head. In any case, the moment the Crown Prince mentioned it, he understood immediately.","Overjoyed, he couldn't help but praise, \"These wild vegetables are fresh, tender, and delicious, possessing a unique flavor of their own. Imperial Mother, Empress, you should both eat more.\"","The Empress Dowager looked at her precious eldest son, momentarily speechless. Had he forgotten whose palace this was and who had brought these things back?","The Empress Dowager placed a shepherd's purse dumpling into the Crown Prince's bowl with her chopsticks, saying with a loving expression, \"Zhiyan, you should eat more too!\"","The imperial family had just finished their dinner, and before Emperor Mingxi could even take a sip of his digestive tea, he heard a eunuch report that Lord Yu Chongshan was requesting an audience with His Majesty.","Emperor Mingxi, who was fully satiated and felt his body in much better shape, instantly made his smile vanish.","Without even lifting his lowered eyes, he said calmly, \"Let him in.\""]},{"number":243,"title":"Chapter 243: The small statue appears to be a Jianghu figure.","paragraphs":["Seeing the Emperor's expression, the Empress Dowager realized he was venting his anger, but no matter what, Yu Chongshan was Yue Fuguang's grandfather.","If the Emperor dared to disrespect him today, the Little Immortal Lord would return the favor tenfold tomorrow.","Since she often came to her palace for meals, she knew more about Yue Fuguang. She might look amiable, but she did not have a good temper.","And no matter what the Yu family was like in the past, they were now under her protection. What was the difference between slapping Yu Chongshan's face and slapping the Junior Preceptor's face?","\"Emperor,\" the Empress Dowager only called out to him. With the tacit understanding they had built over many years as mother and son, he naturally knew what she was thinking.","He was just feeling a bit unhappy in his heart. If he really uttered harsh words to Yu Chongshan because of this matter, wouldn't it clearly show his dissatisfaction with the Junior Preceptor? That would be asking for a beating!","Even if all the civil and military officials in the court knew about this, he would be the one in the wrong.","\"Rest assured, Mother, your son knows his limits.\" Emperor Mingxi instantly put away his little bit of emotion.","While the mother and son were talking, Yu Chongshan had already been led into the main hall by a eunuch.","After bowing and paying his respects to the four members of the imperial family, Yu Chongshan explained the purpose of his visit.","Emperor Mingxi stood up abruptly. \"Is what you say true, my beloved minister Yu?\"","Yu Chongshan bowed and said, \"Reporting to Your Majesty, I would not dare to speak nonsense.\"","Saying this, he took the item he had brought from the eunuch behind him, offered it with both hands, and said, \"The item is here. Your Majesty can take a look for yourself.\"","Qian Gui originally wanted to go over, take it, and present it to Emperor Mingxi, but was stopped by him. With a wave of his hand, the Emperor said, \"Beloved minister Yu is one of our own. I want to personally see the token of appreciation he has brought for me.\"","Hearing such words, if Yue Fuguang were here, she would definitely get goosebumps and be reminded of the phrase 'sharing a bed like brothers'.","Yu Chongshan respectfully placed the box in his hands on the low table in front of him.","Opening the box, inside were two exquisite white porcelain bottles used for holding wine.","Each bottle held about two catties.","Emperor Mingxi impatiently opened the stopper and brought the mouth of the bottle close to his nose to sniff it. Those who didn't know better would think it contained some peerless fine wine!","As if smelling it wasn't enough, Emperor Mingxi couldn't help but comment, \"The scent is fresh and elegant. It truly is spiritual water.\"","He turned his head and looked at Yu Chongshan with satisfaction, saying, \"Beloved minister Yu, you are very thoughtful!\"","Yu Chongshan repeatedly said he didn't dare claim the credit. He knew clearly in his heart that the Yu family's current status was entirely due to his granddaughter.","As the head of the family, what he needed to do was maintain the right attitude. At a time when the family was prospering, it was even more important to stick to their duties. As the saying goes, they couldn't get carried away, nor could they cause trouble or bring a bad reputation to his granddaughter.","While his granddaughter acted freely in the front, he would clean up the aftermath in the back. The Yu family was not afraid of trouble, but there was no need to bring unpleasantness upon themselves over trivial matters.","After Emperor Mingxi invited him to sit down, he said, \"Today, the Crown Prince returned and told me the whole story. I was originally a bit disappointed about missing this opportunity.","I never expected that not only would I get to eat the wild vegetables the Crown Prince brought back, but now I can also drink the spiritual rainwater you specially prepared for me.","Beloved minister Yu, you are my trusted pillar of the state, a true loyal subject!\"","Yu Chongshan immediately looked excited, his face flushing bright red. His eyes were full of loyalty as he looked at Emperor Mingxi, and he said, \"I do not deserve such excessive praise from Your Majesty!","The matter happened so suddenly, so I could only resort to this makeshift plan of having the old servant catch the rainwater with a basin.\"","A trace of an awkward smile appeared on his face as he added, \"As long as Your Majesty does not mind it!\"","Emperor Mingxi waved his large hand. \"You are mistaken to say that, beloved minister Yu. This contains not only spiritual rainwater but also your loyalty. I know it all!","You are well aware of how important the Junior Preceptor is to our dynasty.\"","Saying this, Emperor Mingxi raised the teacup in his hand. \"In the future, our Great Yan will still have to rely on the Junior Preceptor and you, my beloved minister Yu!\"","Yu Chongshan immediately stood up, cupped his hands, and said, \"Your Majesty's words are too heavy! I am truly unworthy.\"","\"Sit, quickly sit down, beloved minister Yu.\" He then turned to the Crown Prince and said, \"Crown Prince, serve tea to the venerable official.\"","\"Your Majesty, you must not! The Crown Prince is the heir apparent of our dynasty, the future ruler. How can he serve tea to a humble subject like me!\"","Emperor Mingxi said nonchalantly, \"Sit peacefully, beloved minister Yu. As a member of the younger generation, it is only proper for him to serve tea and pour water.\"","Seeing that the Emperor's family was determined, Yu Chongshan said no more and could only accept the gesture.","He then brought up another matter. \"Your Majesty, Fuguang mentioned that the weeds growing in the fields, because of the spiritual rainwater, are also excellent forage. What do you think...\"","This matter couldn't be kept a secret. Including the forests, there were over two thousand acres of farmland and mountainous terrain. Their family's tenant farmers alone would be too busy to pull all the weeds.","Yu Chongshan also had a bit of a selfish motive; he was worried that if too much time passed, the weeds would absorb the soil's nutrients, affecting the growth of the grain and vegetables.","Seeking outside help was the best solution.","\"There's such a thing?\" A look of joy appeared on Emperor Mingxi's face.","There was the Great Yan racecourse in the suburbs of the capital. If the horses were fed forage that had absorbed spiritual rainwater, then...","\"Crown Prince, go notify the manager of the imperial estate. Have him send people to weed the Junior Preceptor's fields. Tell them to be careful and absolutely not damage the grain seedlings.\"","Xie Zhiyan immediately received the order, and Yu Chongshan took his leave as well.","Before leaving, he not only received a chest of rewards but also several boxes of pastries, which the Empress Dowager explicitly stated were for Yue Fuguang.","\"When it comes to pastries, the ones made in the Empress Dowager's palace are truly the most delicious.\"","Yue Fuguang placed several plates of pastries on the table, inviting her sisters to eat, and picked a peach-blossom-shaped one for herself.","Yu Ningxuan took a small bite and praised, \"Not only are these pastries delicious, but their appearance is also top-notch.\"","Yu Ningxin nodded in agreement.","Yu Ningzi said, \"The house has been bustling these past two days. The officials coming to visit Grandfather are an endless stream, and everyone who comes always brings pastries.","Grandmother has enough over there to open a pastry shop.\"","Yu Ningxuan said, \"For the past few days, Grandfather has been staying in the tearoom as soon as he finishes his official duties, and those visiting officials head straight for the tearoom too.","Could it be that Grandfather recently acquired some extraordinary fine tea?\"","Yue Fuguang chuckled softly in her heart. The old man hadn't acquired good tea; he had acquired good water.","Good tea needed to be paired with good water. She guessed that the bit of spiritual rainwater the old man had secretly collected was probably almost entirely consumed by these waves of visiting officials over the past few days.","While the sisters were talking, Qingzhu suddenly came to report, \"Miss, someone from the Old Master's courtyard has come to deliver a message, inviting you to meet him in the tearoom.\"","\"Grandfather is calling for me. Do you know who his guests in the tearoom are today?\"","Yue Fuguang bid farewell to her sisters and, while walking towards the outer courtyard's tearoom, asked the young servant boy leading the way.","The young servant boy was about seven or eight years old and looked very clever. Seeing Yue Fuguang ask, he didn't hide anything.","He replied in a crisp voice, \"Reporting to Miss, those who came to visit the Old Master today are Minister Huo, General Wei, Court Physician Song, and an unfamiliar young man.\"","The young servant boy frowned and said, \"From what this humble one observed, that person looks like someone from the martial arts world.\"","Yue Fuguang chuckled aloud. \"You know how to observe people? Have you seen people from the martial arts world before?\"","The young servant boy blushed with shame at Yue Fuguang's laughter and said embarrassedly, \"Miss, our family has many guards, and most of them come from the martial arts world.","After seeing them so much, I just...\"","He scratched his head. \"That person is very similar to Lord Zhang Fang, so he must be someone from the martial arts world.\"","Yue Fuguang nodded. Zhang Fang was indeed a typical martial artist. Although he had entered officialdom, he still carried an aura of the martial arts world. Here with her, in an environment far from the true officialdom and relatively free,","it really wouldn't be that easy to wash away his martial arts world traces in such a short time.","Before even entering the tearoom, Yue Fuguang could hear Yu Chongshan's hearty laughter coming from inside."]},{"number":244,"title":"Chapter 244: With my status, who dares to look down on me except my sworn enemies","paragraphs":["\"Grandfather, what were you discussing with these gentlemen? You all seem so cheerful.\"","Yue Fuguang pushed the door open and entered, holding a small jar of tea leaves.","Coming to the tea room, and to avoid drinking the tea laden with too many additives, Yue Fuguang had brought her own 'provisions', carrying a small jar from her personal stash.","\"Fuguang is here, please, have a seat.\"","Upon seeing her enter, the several men all rose and bowed in greeting. \"We pay our respects to the Junior Preceptor. We apologize for the intrusion.\"","\"Gentlemen, please be seated.\"","She then addressed Yu Chongshan, \"Grandfather, this is the tea I brought.\"","Placing the tea jar on the tea table, she continued, \"This tea is different from the compressed tea cakes of Danyan. Would you and the gentlemen care to try it?\"","\"That would be splendid. I happen to have some plum-blossom snow water sent by Minister Wang the other day.\"","He retrieved a pink porcelain bottle from beneath the tea seat. \"Fuguang, shall we use this snow water to brew the tea?\"","\"Excellent!\"","She took the bottle and said, \"Grandfather, allow me to prepare the tea.\"","After she set the water to boil, Yu Chongshan finally explained the reason for summoning her.","\"Fuguang, this is Dai Yuxing, a young master of martial arts. With the Crown Prince's wedding approaching, the capital is teeming with all sorts of people. Your grandfather specially asked Judge Song Xingzhou to find a skilled hand to protect your safety. His Majesty is also aware of this matter.\"","Recently, street brawls and fights had become frequent, and the entire capital was seething with undercurrents. His Majesty also feared that people from several nations might take advantage of the Crown Prince's wedding to stir up trouble again.","Especially the assassination attempts targeting Yue Fuguang. The several nations involved might have developed mutual suspicions, as there had been no recent action. But for them to give up completely was likely impossible.","\"Dai Yuxing pays his respects to the Junior Preceptor!\"","Dai Yuxing appeared to be around twenty years old. The page boy had said he resembled Zhang Fang, and upon seeing him now, Yue Fuguang immediately felt the page boy had a keen eye.","The two men weren't alike in looks—Zhang Fang was bold and rugged, while the man before her was tall and slender, with handsome features that were nearly as striking as described by clichés.","Moreover, he carried an innate air of chivalrous righteousness.","Yue Fuguang nodded, made a gesture of invitation, and said, \"Young Master Dai, there's no need for such formality. Please, sit.\"","She then asked Song Xingzhou, \"Judge Song, has His Majesty made any arrangements regarding Young Master Dai?\"","Song Xingzhou knew she was inquiring about an official position for Dai Yuxing, as those serving as guards for the Junior Preceptor were never without rank or credentials.","\"His Majesty's intention is to leave it entirely to the Junior Preceptor's discretion.\"","Song Xingzhou couldn't help but feel a twinge of envy. Zhang Fang, who was under his jurisdiction, was now almost at his own rank, and now another Dai Yuxing was being sent.","His Majesty was clearly indicating that the Junior Preceptor could bestow official positions at will—a privilege in Danyan that not even the Crown Prince possessed.","Yue Fuguang lowered her gaze in brief thought, then looked at Dai Yuxing and asked, \"Young Master Dai, are you acquainted with Zhang Fang?\"","\"Yes. His master and my master are close friends, so we are fairly familiar with each other.\"","\"Compared to him, who is stronger?\"","Dai Yuxing was momentarily taken aback by her direct question. Wasn't it said that those in official circles preferred to speak in roundabout ways?","Even though this Junior Preceptor was young, the fact that the Minister of War treated her with such respect spoke volumes about her exalted status.","Facing someone of such high position, regardless of age, Dai Yuxing dared not let his guard down.","So he had been mentally prepared and had run through various scenarios—just not one where the Junior Preceptor would be so blunt.","This one was even more 'forthright' than those of the martial world!","His mind racing, Dai Yuxing pondered many things in an instant. Meeting Yue Fuguang's clear, bright eyes, vast as the brilliant moon, his response was equally honest and confident.","\"Within fifty moves, I am confident I could wound him. Within a hundred, I could certainly capture him alive.\"","\"In that case... you shall hold the same rank as Zhang Fang, Deputy Fifth Grade Protector. He will be the Left Protector, and you the Right.\"","In the Danyan court, left took precedence over right. Even though Dai Yuxing's martial skills might surpass Zhang Fang's, Zhang Fang was, after all, the 'veteran'.","She couldn't let a newcomer immediately outrank him.","Yue Fuguang glanced at the panel showing this person's favorability value, which was actually sixty-one. If not for his nearly passing favorability score, she might not have kept him.","After all, she was more inclined to have another valiant, heroic, and supremely skilled female knight by her side.","Upon hearing that the Junior Preceptor was immediately granting him a Deputy Fifth Grade position, Dai Yuxing was stunned for a moment. Although he had heard from his master that Zhang Fang also held Deputy Fifth Grade, Zhang Fang had been in the capital for over two years.","He had heard of the hardships Zhang Fang faced during those years. His current position was also due to good fortune, luckily encountering the highly esteemed Junior Preceptor.","Otherwise, who knows how long he might have languished.","Since entering the Junior Preceptor's residence, Zhang Fang, while maintaining normal correspondence with them, had refused to say a single word about this Junior Preceptor.","He had originally planned, upon arriving in the capital, to find an opportunity to ask Zhang Fang to arrange an introduction to the Junior Preceptor. Little did he expect that upon just entering the city, he would encounter thieves attempting to steal the potatoes.","He had contributed significantly to capturing that person. He never imagined the court's reward would be to directly recommend him to the Junior Preceptor who had produced the superior potato seeds.","And at their very first meeting, the Junior Preceptor had immediately granted him a Deputy Fifth Grade position.","Thinking of this, Dai Yuxing suddenly stood up, solemnly bowed deeply, and said, \"Dai Yuxing thanks the Junior Preceptor for your high regard!\"","Then he knelt on one knee, looked at Yue Fuguang, and declared clearly, \"Dai Yuxing hereby swears an oath to follow the Junior Preceptor unto death.\"","Yue Fuguang was taken aback by his series of actions, feeling a touch of awkwardness.","Dai Yuxing's pledge of loyalty was filled with the air of the martial world. But since he was from that world, even though she had given him an official post, wasn't this 'submission' a bit too swift?","Was she some kind of classic trope blocker? She never encountered scenarios where she could show off, put someone in their place, and then win their loyalty.","Was it because she lacked the protagonist's halo?","She never met subordinates who were arrogant and unruly.","[Host, if you encountered that kind of arrogant, defiant subordinate who felt terribly wronged serving a 'child' like you, would you take them on?]","Yue Fuguang didn't hesitate for a second, shaking her head mentally. 'Am I some kind of masochist? Talented people are plentiful. Who has the patience to insist on hanging themselves on one particular tree!","With my status, aside from mortal enemies, who would dare look down on me!'","Everyone sat down again. Yue Fuguang began steeping the tea, while Huo Ying and the others discussed the recent chaos in the capital.","\"Regarding the thieves attempting to steal the potatoes, over several incidents, we have successively captured more than twenty people, not counting those who escaped.\"","Speaking of this, Huo Ying's face was full of worry.","Just those eight pots of potatoes had attracted so much covetous attention. If they were to find out that the imperial estates and the Junior Preceptor's fields held many more...","Even deploying the entire capital garrison to protect these superior seeds might not guarantee absolute safety.","No wonder His Majesty and the others had discussed early on to plant all those potatoes in the vegetable gardens opened up at the Pacification Office.","From the very beginning, those dozen or so pounds of potato seeds were bait.","And these big and small fish had truly taken the hook! But weren't there too many of them? It's impossible to catch them all!","\"Minister, do you know the origins of these people?\"","Yue Fuguang currently lacked the ability to set up protective formations around her estate, so she couldn't help but worry about the safety of the seeds planted in her fields.","\"Minister Cai and Vice Minister Wei have interrogated several. Some have tight lips. So far, we only know there are people from our Danyan, as well as from Northern Li and Southern Zhao.\""]},{"number":245,"title":"Chapter 245: Is It Really Good to Suddenly Add Extra Scenes","paragraphs":["Seeing Huo Ying only mention those few families, Wei Shouyi couldn't help but interject, \"In my opinion, Lao Wei, the remaining families aren't clean either. Who wouldn't want a high-yield seed that produces a thousand catties per mu!\"","His face beaming with admiration, he looked at Yue Fuguang, \"Our Dayan is lucky to have the Junior Mentor. They don't have this luck, so of course they'd come to steal it!\"","Not only did they want to steal the potatoes, but they also wanted to take the Junior Mentor away.","According to reports from Dayan's spies placed in various countries, the Zhaiyue Alliance had changed their orders from assassination to capture alive—they intended to snatch the Junior Mentor from Dayan!","Dai Yuxing was looking at her with the same expression.","Yue Fuguang: Now she found the reason why his favorability rating towards her was passing, despite him being someone who had only recently come to the capital!","'Little Zhu, do you know what's going on?'","[Master, according to the original historical timeline, during the Crown Prince's wedding, all sides were in motion. During that period, hundreds of spies from various countries and factions infiltrated the capital.","They also committed several major cases. These cases seemed unrelated but were actually interconnected.","Now, with the added incentive of the potatoes, the number of people in the capital with ulterior motives is surely even greater now.]","Oh!","While Yue Fuguang was communicating with the system, Wei Shouyi, sitting next to Dai Yuxing, let out an almost inaudible gasp of pain from his throat.","Dai Yuxing's hand was gripping his thigh like a vise. If not for the habit of not showing emotions, cultivated from long exposure in front of the Junior Mentor, he would have cried out loud!","Wei Shouyi covertly shot a fierce glare at Dai Yuxing.","If this kid didn't rein in his expression soon, it would arouse the Junior Mentor's suspicion.","So young and inexperienced after all! All the repeated instructions given before coming were forgotten!","His hand also clamped onto Dai Yuxing's arm, giving it a hard squeeze. Good, his thigh was finally liberated!","'They committed major cases too? Who did it?'","[The perpetrators included You Tan, Tianxing Lou, and Fengyu Ge. As for the masterminds behind them, several countries and certain factions within Dayan are all implicated.]","'Tianxing Lou and Fengyu Ge? Are they assassin organizations like You Tan?'","[More or less. However, what's different about Fengyu Ge compared to You Tan and Tianxing Lou is that some of its assassins are not fixed personnel.","Many who work for Fengyu Ge are 'temporary workers'—these are 'anyone' drawn by the hefty bounties.","They could even be assassins from You Tan or Tianxing Lou taking on side jobs. Some people do one job and never commit another crime, which is why Fengyu Ge assassins are the hardest to catch.","Among the assassins who attacked you, Master, on East Main Street last time, several were hired by Xie Qi at a high price from Fengyu Ge.]","'Fengyu Ge, how very good! Then do you know where these organizations' headquarters are?'","[Little Zhu can only sense the general locations. You Tan's main headquarters is in Nanyue, Tianxing Lou's is in Beili.","As for Fengyu Ge, it exists in all six kingdoms, operating independently yet interconnected.]","'Leave the ones in other countries aside for now. Find the headquarters of Dayan's Fengyu Ge and figure out a way to uproot it!'","[Master, Fengyu Ge's connections are too extensive, involving other prefectures in Dayan. Should we report it to the Emperor?","According to records, on the night after tomorrow, when it's dark and windy, Fengyu Ge will join forces with You Tan to set fire to the Hundred Herb Garden warehouse.]","'Why would they burn the herb garden warehouse?'","Yu Chongshan and Huo Ying exchanged a glance; they thought of the captured Qi Ming.","[Nanyue intends to create a plague in Dayan, so of course they'd first cut off one of Dayan's largest medicinal herb warehouses. However, now that Qi Ming is captured, their plans might change.]","Whether they change or not, protecting the medicinal herb warehouse is absolutely necessary. They needed to report this information to His Majesty as soon as possible.","'Can you pinpoint the location of Fengyu Ge's headquarters? Regardless of whether their plans change, let's destroy it first!'","Yue Fuguang spoke with great force. She had to be forceful—this Fengyu Ge was her mission, and among the dozen or so Jianghu tasks, it was the most urgent one that needed completion.","[Master, Fengyu Ge's headquarters is located underground in a three-courtyard residence on Jiming Lane in the capital.","The owner of this residence is none other than a property of the Cao Gang in the capital. It houses subordinates of the gang leader, Cao Hu.]","'The Cao Gang? This matter couldn't also be related to the Sima family, could it?'","[The Sima family is one of the financial backers behind Fengyu Ge. The Cao Gang's Cao Hu is merely a scapegoat pushed to the forefront by Fengyu Ge.","The true master of Dayan's Fengyu Ge is named Luo Feng. He also has a twin brother named Luo Yu, who works under Cao Hu's command. The person living in that courtyard is him.]","'Luo Feng, Luo Yu? What are their backgrounds?'","[Their mother is named Luo Xue, the master of Luoxia Manor in Xingzhou, also a famous female knight-errant in the Jianghu.]","Luoxia Manor!","None of them had imagined that the young master of the famous Luoxia Manor, one of the Five Mountains and Six Manors of Dayan, was actually the master of Fengyu Ge!","And with both the Sima family and the Cao Gang implicated, they had to be on guard and eliminate them as quickly as possible.","'Is Luo Xue involved in Fengyu Ge's affairs?'","[Luo Xue is unaware. Luo Feng became the master of Fengyu Ge by inheriting his master's legacy.","His master's name is Feng Yang.","He hails from the Feng family of Xiqiang, and by lineage, he is considered an uncle of Feng Wuchang.","Therefore, Dayan's Fengyu Ge is considered a branch of Xiqiang's Fengyu Ge.]","'Never mind who's behind him for now. Let's destroy their headquarters first. As for whether the operation on the night after tomorrow will still happen as in the original history, that depends on Wei Ping, Cai Xian, and the others.'","While listening to the words of the Little Immortal Lord and the Divine Artifact, a few of them sipped the freshly brewed tea Yue Fuguang had poured for them.","The tea liquor was clear and bright, with a faint floral scent mingled with the aroma of tea upon smelling. The first sip was slightly bitter and astringent, not particularly remarkable, but upon careful tasting, it left a lingering fragrance in the mouth with a sweet aftertaste.","Faced with such fine tea, several of them had no mind to savor it carefully.","Of course, Song Xingzhou, who was already on his third cup, was an exception. He unilaterally declared in his heart that he would only drink this kind of tea from now on!","[Master, it's starting to rain outside.]","Yue Fuguang's eyes shifted. 'This rain comes at a good time. A little thunder on a rainy day isn't too much, is it?'","[Master, are you thinking of having Little Zhu strike Fengyu Ge's headquarters with lightning?]","'Little Zhu, this time your master will take action personally. Let's see if this tiny bit of divine power I've recovered can blast open the rats hiding underground.'","Upon hearing this, a few of them quickly took their leave. They wanted to hurry to Jiming Lane for a front-row seat to watch the show.","This suited Yue Fuguang perfectly. Handing Dai Yuxing over to her grandfather, she hurriedly made her way towards her own Mingyue Pavilion.","'System, why did the mission suddenly change? Adding scenes so abruptly, is that really okay?'","[Host, we have altered the original historical timeline's plot too much, so the system missions have changed accordingly.","Look, introducing high-yield seeds naturally leads to corresponding problems, which in turn trigger corresponding missions.","Although the mission is a bit urgent, compared to those systems that demand task completion within an hour, mine is really quite reasonable!","The Merit System is the conscience of the system world, no doubt about it!","'I think you just want to earn my points!'","Even though she said this, Yue Fuguang still let the system deduct 888 points.","Immediately afterwards, a stream of unfamiliar information rushed into her mind. Yue Fuguang's steps didn't falter in the slightest.","If her soul hadn't been nourished by incense offerings to become exceptionally strong lately, she wouldn't have dared to receive the thunder technique enlightenment while walking so recklessly."]},{"number":246,"title":"Chapter 246: Thunderbolt","paragraphs":["Upon reaching the second floor, Yue Fuguang opened the window and looked into the distance. Even though it was just the second floor, one could still see quite far.","\"System, are you sure they're plotting something right now?\"","[Host, today is the best opportunity. If we miss today, these people will scatter everywhere, and it'll be hard to catch them.]","\"First, help me locate the underground entrance of the Cao family's villa.\"","It seemed that this was the first time she was going to do some work herself to earn points.","Yue Fuguang closed her eyes slightly and carefully felt. The Lightning Method of Bestowing Wisdom that she had bought from the system at a friendly price emerged in her mind.","\"After absorbing so much incense power, let me try what it feels like to have extraordinary power!\"","Yue Fuguang raised her chubby right hand, and several cute dimples appeared on the back of her hand. It didn't look like a hand that could control extraordinary power at all.","But as Yue Fuguang's will moved, faint purple lightning threads instantly appeared on her fair and tender little hand.","As the lightning crackled, the flickering lightning threads wrapped her entire right hand.","\"System, I feel like the direction we're going in is wrong. Shouldn't I be pretending to be a god with the system's props? How come I've developed extraordinary power myself as things progress!\"","At first, when the system told her about it, she didn't have much of a feeling. Then the system stole the Lightning Method from the mall's backend and resold it to her, which gave her incense power a use.","Even with the lightning threads flickering on her hand, Yue Fuguang still had a sense of unreality.","[Host, at most, you're like those Taoist people who attained the Way on ancient Earth, with the ability to control the wind and rain, and manipulate thunder and lightning. After all, you're still a mortal with a physical body. We won't develop in the direction of cultivating immortality. The environment here doesn't allow it. However, just this little ability is enough to make you the only true god in this world!]","\"System, you said I can control the wind and rain and manipulate lightning, but I can't do that yet!\"","[Well... that's an additional cost!] It sold the abilities of wind, rain, thunder, and lightning separately because it was afraid that if it was too expensive all at once, the host wouldn't buy it. Besides, thunder comes with an electric arc. Even if the host doesn't buy the method of manipulating lightning, it doesn't affect her ability to show off!","Yue Fuguang knew what the system was up to and didn't want to haggle. She then changed the topic and said, \"Is the location set? I'm going to... not, I'm going to cast a spell!\"","[Host, you fly with confidence, and the system will follow behind you...]","As the system's strange and off - key electronic voice sang, Yue Fuguang clumsily made a hand gesture.","A strange yet familiar power in her body flowed along her arm to her fingers. Yue Fuguang gently pointed in the direction of the Cao family's villa.","Crack! Crack!","Boom! Boom!","Suddenly, thunder roared over the capital. Purple lightning flashed like snakes in the gray - black clouds, illuminating the faces of those who were either terrified or shocked.","Suddenly, it was like it had found its prey and pounced on a certain place.","Boom! Bang! Bang!","Thunder exploded, breaking down walls and houses, and a deep pit was blasted on the ground.","Cai Xian and Wei Ping, along with a group of civil and military officials summoned by Huo Ying, were standing on the roof of a mansion in the distance, watching all this happen.","They were instantly stunned.","\"Brother Yu, hold me up. My legs are a bit weak!\" Dong Qianli grabbed Yu Shuchun's arm as if it were a life - saving straw.","Ji Hongming, Zhang Zhongping, and other civil officials were no better. Their calves were trembling.","Their memories of the thunder still remained on the night of the Five - Country Competition during the Longevity Festival.","The Little Immortal Lord was much gentler then!","Everyone took turns looking into the Cao family's yard through the telescope made by the Crown Prince's glass workshop.","They saw a huge pit still smoking. Except for a few walls at the entrance of the three - courtyard mansion, nothing else was intact.","And the houses of its next - door neighbors were safe and sound!","It could be said that the strike was quite precise, without involving any innocent people.","\"How is it?\" Ling Yinghua, Wang Shouchen, and several other senior officials standing below waiting for the news couldn't help but ask when they saw the stunned people on the roof.","Poor them, being old, they couldn't even get a good view when watching the show. The second - hand news was also late, which made them almost jump up in a hurry.","Zhang Zhongping climbed down the ladder clumsily. Usually, he was very particular about etiquette, but at this moment, he was a bit embarrassed.","Bao Yuanjun asked first, \"My Lord, did the thunder really strike the Cao mansion?\"","Just now, the electric snakes were swimming right above their heads, so close that it seemed they could touch them with their hands.","\"The houses have collapsed, and there's a pit about five or six meters wide and bottomless on the ground.\"","As for the people inside, they could only wait for the news after Wei Ping and Cai Xian, who had gone to arrest them, had investigated.","The others came down from the roof one after another. They didn't go into the house but just stood in the corridor, each holding a cup of hot tea, neither drinking nor speaking.","They were all lost in their own thoughts.","The power of heaven is unpredictable. This is the real power of heaven!","They witnessed the whole process of the thunder and the terrifying lightning crashing down on the ground. The shock was much greater than that of those who only saw the pit.","Just as everyone was silent, Wei Shouyi suddenly said, \"The Young Master has always been so gentle to us!\"","Yu Shuchun said, \"My Fuguang is the kindest and most gentle immortal.\"","Luo Feng and Luo Yu: Why don't you take a look at our miserable state before saying that!","In the Imperial Study, the emperor and the crown prince were also talking about this.","\"Prince, you said you saw lightning flashing on the Young Master's hand through the telescope, and she just gently pointed at the Cao mansion, and then thunder roared. Are you sure you saw it clearly?\"","Xie Zhiyan nodded affirmatively. \"Father, I saw it clearly. This time, it was really the work of the Little Immortal Lord.\"","Emperor Mingxi sat back on the imperial throne. Both father and son thought that the Young Master had finally started to use her abilities as an immortal.","\"Prince, do you think it's right to offer incense to the Young Master?\"","Xie Zhiyan's eyelids twitched. He was very afraid that his father would be afraid of the immortal's power and do something stupid at this time.","He replied without hesitation, \"Naturally, it's a good thing. It's a blessing for the Dayan Dynasty and for our father - son pair. Father, without the immortal, you and I wouldn't have many years to live.\"","Did his father think that once the arrow was shot, it could be taken back?","Not to mention among the officials, even the enthusiasm for offering incense to the Young Master among the common people couldn't be suppressed by them.","Should they stop planting good seeds? Should the Dayan Dynasty stop developing? Or was his father tired of living?","Xie Zhiyan secretly thought that his father mustn't be so ungrateful and do something like crossing the river and then removing the bridge. Otherwise...","\"Father, those three people are our examples. You...\" It's best not to have any inappropriate thoughts.","After being reminded by the crown prince, Emperor Mingxi suddenly broke out in a cold sweat. Right, right, he couldn't even think about it!","\"Prince, I remember you said Fuguang wants to visit my treasure house. After tomorrow's court session, you two go there and pick out some good things.\"","Emperor Mingxi finally calmed down slowly. He felt embarrassed and scared about the thought that had just flashed through his mind."]},{"number":247,"title":"Chapter 247: The Pavilion of Wind and Rain","paragraphs":["He couldn't help but talk more, saying, \"I heard it was Wei Ping's birthday yesterday, and Yue Fuguang gave him a book.","Cai Xian was at the Wei residence yesterday, and the lamp in the Wei family study didn't go out all night.\"","Emperor Mingxi took a sip of tea and continued, \"During the morning court today, I saw the two of them. Though they looked tired with dark circles under their eyes, their spirits were unusually high.","I wonder what exactly that book contained to make them so.","With your wedding less than half a month away, I'm curious what grand wedding gift Yue Fuguang will give you then.\"","Actually, Xie Zhiyan had also been looking forward to this for a while, but one couldn't force such things. Anything from the Junior Mentor would be good.","While the father and son were discussing the book gifted by Yue Fuguang, Wei Ping and Cai Xian were using their newly learned methods to investigate at the Cao residence.","The next morning at court.","Wei Ping, holding his hu tablet, stepped out of the ranks, bowed, and memorialized, \"Your Majesty, your subject Wei Ping has a report.\"","\"Permission granted!\"","\"Reporting to Your Majesty, yesterday evening, your subject, in cooperation with Minister Cai, investigated the Cao residence destroyed by the heavenly thunder.","Our investigation found the resident was a supervisor from the Canal Gang named Cao Yu. We also discovered a secret chamber within the deep pit blasted open by the thunder.","Inside the chamber were thirteen individuals. Seeing their suspicious behavior and the large quantity of prohibited standard-issue weapons they carried, we took them all into custody.","After your subject and Minister Cai interrogated the group throughout the night, we confirmed three leaders among them. One is Luo Feng, the young master of the Great Yan Fengyu Pavilion, also the elder brother of the Canal Gang supervisor, Luo Yu.","The other two are Zuo Qianming, the Left Commander of the Dark Character Division of You Tan in Great Yan, and Qu Shengwu, the Right Commander of the same division.\"","As soon as his words fell, they immediately sparked discussions among the hundred officials in the court.","You Tan, Fengyu Pavilion, and Tianxing Tower—the three largest, most mysterious, and most troublesome assassin organizations across the six kingdoms.","Which official in the court did not know of them?","Who would have thought that yesterday's terrifying thunder had actually exposed major figures from both the You Tan and Fengyu Pavilion organizations.","Some people secretly glanced towards Yue Fuguang, sitting steadily on the high platform, as everyone had witnessed her command the heavenly thunder for her own use during the Longevity Festival banquet.","Although the Junior Mentor's thunder that day was far less spectacular than yesterday's, it didn't stop some from suspecting this thunderclap was peculiar.","Yue Fuguang was not afraid of their scrutiny, still drinking her tea when she pleased and watching the show.","\"Are you certain the captured individuals are assassins from Fengyu Pavilion and You Tan?\"","Wei Ping said, \"The three confessed personally. It cannot be false.\"","Thanks to the Junior Mentor's Truth Elixir. Last time he interrogated those assassins, he only used less than half a pill.","This time, after applying various torture instruments to no avail and them still refusing to talk, he had no choice but to use this precious pill.","In less than half the time it takes to drink a cup of tea, they confessed everything. If not for the small dose and the effects wearing off quickly, those three might have started recounting stories from their childhood, like peeping at widows bathing.","Emperor Mingxi looked serious. \"Did you ascertain the reason for their gathering?\"","At this point, Cai Xian stepped forward to report, \"Reporting to Your Majesty, according to the confessions of the three, they were holding secret talks in the Cao residence chamber yesterday. The matter discussed was to set fire to the Hundred Herb Garden warehouse tomorrow at the hour of the rat (midnight) and...\"","\"And what?\" Emperor Mingxi's authoritative voice sounded from the throne.","Cai Xian glanced up quickly and stole a look at Yue Fuguang. Yue Fuguang thought to herself, \"Sure enough — it was aimed at her.\" The development of the historical timeline was beginning to deviate because of her appearance.","\"Setting fire to the Hundred Herb Garden, because we captured Qi Ming and ruined their scheme, was thus downgraded from the main assault to a feint.","The target of their operation this time is the Junior Mentor and the potato plants grown at the Xuanwei Estate.\"","Bang!","\"What audacity! They dare to target our dynasty's Junior Mentor and the potatoes!\"","Emperor Mingxi's large hand slapped the armrest of the dragon throne with a bang, startling the officials in the hall so much they dared not breathe loudly.","Yue Fuguang, however, couldn't help but glance at Emperor Mingxi's slightly trembling hand. This was a case of showing off feeling great in the moment, but only you know the pain in your hand!","[Master, the Emperor's hand has turned red!]","「Is the dragon throne gold-plated or pure gold? Could the Emperor have dented it with that slap?","That chair, though uncomfortable to sit on, is quite exquisitely made with vivid carvings. It would be a shame if it got damaged.」","Great Yan's ruler and ministers: Wait, our two esteemed figures, isn't your focus a bit off?","There are assassins targeting the Junior Mentor, aren't you concerned at all?","The ruler and ministers exchanged glances. Could it be that their bait wasn't enticing enough to pique the interest of the chatterbox divine artifact?","Cai Xian pressed on, \"According to the confession of You Tan's Right Commander Qu Shengwu, the one who attempted to abduct Chu Qiuyue that time was Left Commander Zuo Qianming.","And Zuo Qianming confessed that the assassination attempt on the Junior Mentor on the night of the Lantern Festival was carried out by Qu Shengwu.\"","Ignoring the hushed discussions among the civil and military officials, Wei Ping added, \"The true purpose of their operation this time, with the feint on the Hundred Herb Garden, was actually to abduct the Junior Mentor and steal the potato seedlings.","The plan was finalized five days ago, but Zuo Qianming and Qu Shengwu had a dispute over the mission objectives, leading to yesterday's secret meeting.\"","\"What dispute? Minister Wei, tell us.\"","Wei Ping bowed and said, \"Reporting to Your Majesty, according to their confessions, these two developed a rift after the failed mission to abduct Chu Qiuyue.","Zuo Qianming suspected that Qu Shengwu deliberately leaked mission information, causing his mission to fail.","His aim was to use the mission to eliminate him, ascend to his position, and single-handedly control all You Tan assassins in the northwest region of Great Yan.\"","Master, it seems your words last time took effect. Indeed, suspicion and discord arose among the You Tan leaders because of it.","「That's also because they inherently distrusted each other, coupled with conflicting interests. Planting just a small seed of doubt can escalate power struggles.」","Wei Ping continued, \"This time, Fengyu Pavilion's Luo Feng was responsible for stealing the potatoes, while Zuo and Qu argued over who would be responsible for abducting the Junior Mentor and who would set fire to the Hundred Herb Garden.","Both wanted to go to the Yu residence to abduct the Junior Mentor, especially Zuo Qianming. He wanted to personally ask the Junior Mentor about her source of information.\"","\"Hmph! How bold these villains are! Do they think our dynasty's several hundred thousand troops are mere decorations? Abduct the Junior Mentor—what are their intentions? Has it been clarified who is behind them?\"","\"All three claimed to be acting on the orders of a mysterious buyer. That person wore a veil, obscuring their features, and their voice sounded like that of a middle-aged man.\"","Emperor Mingxi pondered for a moment. \"Is Fengyu Pavilion's Luo Feng connected to the Canal Gang?\"","This was a sensitive topic. Everyone knew under whose jurisdiction the Canal Gang fell. In recent years, the smooth operation of water transport and the stability of the Canal Gang were part of Sima Jing's political achievements.","Sima Jing oversaw the administration of the Jiangnan region. This Cao Hu was said to have long pledged allegiance under him, hence their obedience. And his position within the Canal Gang, backed by Sima Jing's support, remained as solid as Mount Tai.","Before Wei Ping and Cai Xian could reply, someone stepped forward and said, \"Your Majesty, in your subject's humble opinion, this matter cannot possibly be related to the Canal Gang.","The Canal Gang is located far away in the Jiangnan region. If it were involved, Fengyu Pavilion's stronghold should be in Jiangnan, not in Shangjing City.","The Cao residence is merely the most insignificant one among the numerous properties the Canal Gang owns in Shangjing City and throughout Great Yan.","Folks, move your lucky little hands to give this a like for more updates, thank you! Fist bump!"]},{"number":248,"title":"Chapter 248: Hermaphrodite","paragraphs":["Seeing that Emperor Mingxi showed no reaction, he continued, \"Luo Yu, the brother of Luo Feng, misused public resources for private gain, lending them to his sibling to serve as a base for an assassin organization. I privately believe that the Cao Gang was unaware; it was solely the doing of Luo Yu himself.\"","Another official stepped forward and said, \"Your Majesty, I believe Minister Xue is correct. Over the years, the Cao Gang...\"","[Master, the person behind this Cao Hu is not only Sima Jing; he has another master, Xiyan, the ruler of Western Qiang.","This time, Luo Feng was acting on the orders of the Fengyu Pavilion from Western Qiang to steal the high-yield potato seeds.","As for capturing you, it was a joint plot by Gan Sheng and Xiyan. They received information that you possess even better things here.","Because the spies' rank was not high enough, they only knew that capturing you would make obtaining the high-yield seeds easy.]","\"Do they think that after having sent people to assassinate me before, I would still be willing to cooperate with them?","Little Zhu, if someone really comes to abduct me, we might as well go with them.\"","[Does Master intend to go personally to eliminate those two?]","\"They have made attempts on me several times. What's improper about us taking their lives?\"","[Master, mere mortals, even if they are emperors of the mortal realm, are nothing but ants of a slightly higher status. Why trouble yourself to go personally?","Once my divine power recovers a bit, I can take their lives even from thousands of miles away. Please be patient, Master.]","\"Alright then. I'm not really one to endure the hardships of long journeys either. When my divine power recovers enough to control an aircraft and soar through the nine heavens, then I might travel to the other kingdoms.\"","Wu Yong in the crowd: Please take me with you JPG.","He unconsciously sucked in his increasingly plump waist and bulging belly, feeling for the first time in his life the impulse to lose weight.","A gleam flashed in Emperor Mingxi's eyes. Soaring above the nine heavens—how exhilarating that must be!","Places close to the sky, I wonder if other immortals live there.","As for being called an ant or the like, Emperor Mingxi thought that familiarity breeds indifference; he was already numb to it.","These two ancestors can do whatever they please, as long as it's not directed at him.","Master, beyond the five kingdoms that surround Dayan in this world—across the deserts and the Gobi to the west, the oceans to the east, the high mountains and vast marshes to the south, and the grasslands to the north,","there are vast lands and dozens of countries and tribes, with customs, cultures, and cuisines all different from here.","Although this world is much smaller compared to my Lingxu Mountain, it is indeed worth a visit.]","The Dayan monarch and his ministers exchanged glances. There was such a vast world beyond the six kingdoms?","Vast lands—they wanted them!","Abundant resources—they wanted them!","A large labor force—they wanted them!","\"By the way, Little Zhu, does Sima Jing know Cao Hu's true background? How much does he know about this operation by the Fengyu Pavilion?\"","[Master, Sima Jing naturally knows Cao Hu's background. It was precisely because Cao Hu had Xiyan backing him that he caught Sima Jing's eye.","As for the plans to steal the potatoes and abduct you, he was not directly involved but was aware of them.","The Sima family provided financial support to the Luo brothers through Cao Hu, and the Fengyu Pavilion helped him eliminate rivals.","That Xue Zhipan who stepped forward earlier to claim the Fengyu Pavilion had nothing to do with the Cao Gang is a Langzhong in the Ministry of Personnel, responsible for capital inspections.","He is Sima Jing's man. The information about the potatoes and you was also leaked to Sima Jing through him.","The Dayan branch of the Fengyu Pavilion originated from the Feng family of Western Qiang and is also under their control. Therefore, although Luo Feng is the Pavilion Master of the Fengyu Pavilion, he and his brother Luo Yu sometimes have to take orders from Cao Hu.","The true master of the Dayan Fengyu Pavilion is still the old Pavilion Master, Feng Yang.]","\"These relationships are truly tangled! This Xue Zhipan's eyes are shifty. Since he's Sima Jing's man and is also defending Cao Hu, could he be involved too?\"","[Master, the world is like a giant chessboard, with intricate connections. Various forces may seem unrelated on the surface, but secretly they are often intertwined.","Take this Xue Zhipan for example. He has indeed secretly pledged allegiance to the Sima family and has received considerable 'tribute' from Cao Hu.","But for money, he didn't just leak information to Sima Jing; he sold the same information to multiple parties.","Youtan, the Tianxing Tower, and even several major noble families in Dayan—he sold them all.]","\"I didn't expect that. This man looks unremarkable but actually knows so many channels?\"","[Luo Feng's mother, Luo Xue of the Luoxia Mountain Villa, is a close friend of He Qisha from the Seven Swords Manor, and this He Qisha is Xue Zhipan's brother-in-law.","Most of his information about the Jianghu comes from his brother-in-law.","And matters of the court, he informs He Qisha, which then spreads throughout the Jianghu sects.","Thus, there are no secrets in the Dayan court.]","Emperor Mingxi gritted his teeth. No secrets in the Dayan court—it truly lives up to its name as a sieve!","At this moment, he wished he could tear Xue Zhipan limb from limb, but until he thought of a pretext to deal with him, he had to endure a little longer.","\"So, because of this Xue Zhipan's promotion, I've become the target of several assassin organizations? He actually dares to trade information about this immortal lord for money.","I'm afraid he'll earn the money but won't live to spend it!\"","[Don't be angry, Master. This Xue Zhipan doesn't have many days left to live.]","\"Oh? Why do you say that, Little Zhu? This Xue Zhipan looks only about forty. The saying that mortals have short lives refers to commoners. He's an official, well-fed and fat—how could he be short-lived?","Is there something going on? Tell me quickly, I'm dying of boredom at this morning court!\"","Everyone immediately pricked up their ears as well, using one ear to enjoy the gossip and the other to listen as this Xue Zhipan and another person loudly extolled Sima Jing's hardships in governing Jiangnan and the Cao Gang's meritorious service in court.","[Master, the day before yesterday, Xue Zhipan secretly met with the Third Star Pavilion Master of the Tianxing Tower. They are old acquaintances, and the meeting place was chosen at the Huichun Pavilion.","During their transaction, they were overheard by the Drunken Rakshasa, who was disguised as a dancing girl. She learned that the Tianxing Tower intended to steal the potatoes.","She then sprinkled the secret drug 'Seeking Fragrance' on them. Just from the name, you can tell this drug is a tracker.","Ordinary people can't smell anything from this drug; even an old hand like the Third Star Pavilion Master didn't notice.","After they left, the Drunken Rakshasa followed the Third Star Pavilion Master and discovered a Tianxing Tower safe house in Shangjing City.]","Drunken Rakshasa! Wei Ping and Cai Xuan exchanged glances. They had been searching for this woman for a long time, and she had escaped right under their noses twice.","They thought the situation was tense and she must have left Shangjing City to lay low for a while, but she never left!","\"It's this Drunken Rakshasa again. I heard a while ago that Wei Ping and the others have been looking for this person. She's actually connected to the Xue family too.","They still haven't caught her?\"","[Of course not. Master, have I ever told you that this Drunken Rakshasa is of dual nature?]","\"Dual nature? You haven't mentioned this before.\"","[Because the Drunken Rakshasa is of dual nature, Wei Ping and the others only know her female side. They don't realize that each time she escapes, she changes into her male form.]","How infuriating! Wei Ping clenched his fist. While pursuing the Drunken Rakshasa, he had indeed encountered a handsome, elegant scholar.","And Cai Xuan encountered someone dressed as a shop assistant, carrying a food box, clearly out delivering meals for a customer.","The two exchanged glances. After court, they needed to find a painter to sketch the appearances of those suspicious individuals they had seen!"]},{"number":249,"title":"Chapter 249: Seven Swords Manor, Sunset Glow Manor","paragraphs":["\"Let's ignore this Drunken Rakshasa for now. Continue talking about Xue Zhipan. Was he also tracked by the Drunken Rakshasa and then killed?\"","[He obviously looks like a court official, so the Drunken Rakshasa didn't track him for the time being, because after he left the Huichun Pavilion with the master of the Sanxing Pavilion, he turned back from the side door.","That night, besides the master of the Sanxing Pavilion, Xue Zhipan also met with his nephew from the Seven Swords Villa who had come to the capital, He Qisha's third son, He Huan.","The wine they drank was laced with 'Ruochenxin'. This drug is fine on its own, but once the person engages in sexual intercourse, they will definitely die within ten days if they don't take the antidote in time.]","\"So this Xue Zhipan only has six or seven days left to live? Who wants to kill them, or rather, who wants to kill He Huan?\"","[Master, you also saw that the killer was aiming for He Huan?]","\"Because of Du Zhongxian, this poison immortal, I've recently read some novels and biographies of famous poison and medical experts from the Six Kingdoms.","Whether it's 'Xunfangzong' or 'Ruochenxin', they are both three words. This poison should be the work of the three-word poison doctor Li Sanming.","His poisons are best known not for their toxicity, but for their high price, because of their excellent concealment.","To deal with an official like Xue Zhipan who has no experience in the martial arts world, there's no need to use this kind of poison.","So it can only be aimed at He Huan.\"","[That's right. The excuse He Huan used to come to the capital this time was to find medicine for his severely injured father, He Qisha.","In fact, he was looking for his uncle's help.","His father, He Qisha, was plotted against and severely injured, and his condition is incurable. He wants to hand over the family business to his eldest son, He Heng. He Huan is unwilling to accept this, so he asked his uncle for help and asked him to introduce him to the Tianxing Pavilion.]","\"He Huan approached the Tianxing Pavilion. Is he hiring a killer? Is his target his eldest brother, He Heng? Another drama of fighting for the inheritance!\"","[Yes and no. He does want to bribe the killers of the Tianxing Pavilion to help him eliminate his eldest brother He Heng and his second sister He Jin.","But he also wants to join the Tianxing Pavilion himself.","He wants to rely on the power of the Tianxing Pavilion to help him suppress those in the Seven Swords Villa who are dissatisfied with his succession.]","\"I understand that he wants to get rid of the heir He Heng, but why won't he even spare his sister He Jin?\"","[Because He Jin is the strongest among the three siblings in both martial arts attainments and villa management.","She is also deeply loved by He Qisha, so if He Heng is gone, the successor must be He Jin.]","\"So this He Huan is just the last resort that He Qisha didn't choose, a useless piece of trash?\"","[Master is right. This person is ambitious but incompetent. Being encouraged by someone with ulterior motives, he really thinks he can control the huge business of the Seven Swords Villa.]","\"Then who poisoned him?\"","[It's the people from 'Panshan'. Master, the organization behind the Drunken Rakshasa is Panshan. They aim to subvert the imperial power and support their own forces to take over.","The one who severely injured He Qisha is Panshan, and the one who wants to kill He Huan is also Panshan.","And the person Panshan wants to support is He Qisha's younger brother, He Jiuyang.","He Jiuyang has long joined Panshan, and he has secretly cooperated with Luo Feng. Luo Feng helped him kill the siblings He Jin and He Heng.","He helped Luo Feng force Luo Xue to abdicate, and Luo Feng inherited the Luoxia Villa.]","\"What is their purpose in doing this? To plant a base in Dayan?\"","[Master, look at the geography of Dayan.]","As the system spoke, a map of the mountains, rivers, and geography of the Six Kingdoms suddenly appeared before everyone's eyes.","The mountains, rivers, land, and towns shown in the map were all drawn vividly, like a miniature version of the real thing.","Most importantly, this map covered the scope of the Six Kingdoms. The sharp-eyed Huo Ying saw the garrison defenses of the Six Kingdoms at the first glance!","This was a treasure map that the Dayan Dynasty had spent decades trying to obtain but failed. Its value far exceeded that of a treasure map.","The moment the map appeared, the monarch and officials of Dayan all widened their eyes, leaning back in a tactical maneuver as a conditioned reflex of shock.","A few older ones, especially the two cabinet elders who rarely spoke and acted as mascots in the court, and who had even been ignored by Yue Fuguang, were so shocked by the map that suddenly appeared in front of them, with every blade of grass and tree seemingly within reach, that their legs went weak and they almost fell to the ground.","It was also because of these two that the strange behavior of others stepping back or leaning forward had a reasonable explanation.","Emperor Mingxi steadied his mind and asked with concern, \"Prime Minister Cai, Prime Minister Bao, are you two beloved officials alright? Are you hurt?\"","Others, eager to clear themselves of the suspicion of being frightened just now, also voiced their inquiries.","The people standing behind the two, like the Ministers of the Six Ministries, acted even harder.","Lu Qi said, \"I was really scared to death just now. Seeing the two adults like this, my legs also went weak.\"","Ji Hongming chimed in, \"I was so scared that I stepped back and almost bumped into Minister Zhang.\"","Zhang Zhongping said, \"Seeing Minister Ji step back, I also dodged.\"","Cai and Bao looked at each other, and Elder Cai bowed and said, \"Replying to Your Majesty, we are fine. Just now, because I am old and frail, my legs went weak for a moment. Elder Bao was implicated by me and wanted to help me, but he almost fell together with me.\"","Emperor Mingxi nodded and said, \"Men, grant the two cabinet elders seats.\"","After the two thanked him and sat down, in this brief moment of speaking, Huo Ying, who had been standing still, seemed to have calmed down on the surface.","In fact, his brain was running rapidly, trying to memorize the defense situations of some important passes in the Five Kingdoms.","If one looked closely, they would find that Qian Gui, who had been standing behind Emperor Mingxi, was gone.","[The two cabinet elders are so pitiful. They still have to come to court at this age. The emperor really doesn't know how to respect the elderly!]","Emperor Mingxi, who had been called out again, was already numb. Forget it, forget it. The divine artifact adult can scold him if she wants, as long as she leaves this map up for a while longer.","What does it matter if he gets scolded a few more times!","\"Little Zhu, the emperor neither respects the old nor loves the young. Look at your master, me, waking up early and staying up late to attend court at the age of nine. This is employing child labor!","Forget it, let's not talk about him. Is this thing you released the map of the Six Kingdoms? Where is Dayan?\"","Following Yue Fuguang's question, the other five kingdoms gradually shrank, while the mountains and rivers of Dayan grew larger, and the towns and roads leaped onto the map.","\"Lord Liu, why are you always looking up?\" An official in the crowd asked his colleague next to him in a low voice.","It wasn't just Lord Liu; many officials in front of and behind him were also slightly looking up. Was it really okay to look directly at the Emperor's face like this?","\"Lord Li, I've been keeping my head down for too long, and my neck is a bit sore. I'm looking up to relieve it!\"","While dealing with his colleague, Lord Liu looked up towards Emperor Mingxi, his eyes darting around, not looking at the Son of Heaven at all.","There were quite a few people who had the same behavior as him.","[Master, look here is the Seven Swords Villa, and here is the Luoxia Villa.]","Following the system's words, a green mountain range was circled, and inside was exactly where the Seven Swords Mountain was located.","Another place near the west, where there was still some wind and snow even at the end of March, was circled, and the name was marked as Luoxia Mountain Range.","\"Oh, this Luoxia Villa is close to Western Qiang in the west, and not far from the Savage Mountain of Nanzhao in the south.\"","[Master also saw that the geographical locations of these two villas are special, which is why Panshan and Fengyu Pavilion want to control them.","Their plans were noticed by the Tianxing Pavilion, who had come into contact with He Huan. Next, the three parties will fight over this, and the capital will be lively!]","\"Weren't the brothers Luo Feng and Luo Yu captured by Wei Ping and his men? Even if the Fengyu Pavilion wins, there will be no one left to inherit Luo Xue's estate, right?\""]},{"number":250,"title":"Chapter 250: Has Someone Switched Babies Again","paragraphs":["[Ah, how could Little Zhu forget this? Even though Luo Feng has a pair of children, a son of four and a daughter of two, he and his nominal wife have no children of their own.","With the young pavilion master Luo Feng captured, his master, Old Pavilion Master Feng, might have to support a child of a few years old to take the position, and these children are his grandson and granddaughter.]","\"So how did things develop originally?\"","[Originally, Luo Feng wasn't struck out by Master's heavenly lightning, so naturally he wasn't captured either.","Xue Zhipan died because he didn't take Tianxing Tower's antidote in time. And He Huan escaped disaster because he was a pawn Tianxing Tower wanted to support.","After He Qi died, He Heng and He Jin siblings were besieged by their uncle and younger brother, eventually fleeing Seven Swords Mountain with injuries, only to reappear years later.","And Seven Swords Mountain fell into the hands of Tianxing Tower, later Tianxing Tower cooperated with Panshan, becoming a lingering disease of Great Yan.","Two years later, Luo Xue died of illness, Sunset Mountain smoothly fell into Luo Feng's hands, Wind and Rain Pavilion was backed by Sunset Mountain Villa, truly growing bigger and stronger in Great Yan, and really created quite a bit of brilliance.","Officials in the Northwest Circuit were frequently assassinated in the few years before Great Yan's subjugation. By the two years before the subjugation, half of them had already been replaced by their people.]","Hearing this, Emperor Mingxi broke out in a cold sweat. Half of the officials in the Northwest Circuit were people from Wind and Rain Pavilion, how was that different from being in the hands of Western Qiang?","Then wouldn't Western Qiang invading Great Yan be like entering an uninhabited land?","Huo Ying carefully recalled the map he had just seen. There was a small path connecting Sunset Mountain Villa and Western Qiang, and its extension led to Savage Mountain!","Savage Mountain, and further ahead was the location of Nanzhao's fine iron ore vein...","A sharp light flashed in Huo Ying's eyes. If they could rely on Sunset Mountain Villa, could they seize the iron ore on Savage Mountain at the right time?","His subordinates had secretly brought back some iron ore, which was finer than any iron ore found within Great Yan's borders, making it impossible for him not to covet it.","Lu Qi, the Minister of Works, had the same idea. As the Minister of Works, he naturally wanted to take good materials for himself.","\"Great Yan is really a piece of fat meat. To get it, these neighbors really racked their brains. No wonder it really perished later.","With the intentional calculating against the unintentional, continuous internal problems, an incompetent monarch, party struggles, traitors and national thieves, speculators and rebels, plus natural disasters, it gathered all the necessary conditions for subjugation.","Great Yan perishing was not unjust!\"","The ruler and ministers of Great Yan felt sorrowful in their hearts. Some couldn't help but take their seats according to the number, wondering if they were part of the party struggles or speculators, surely they weren't rebels.","It was just that no one admitted to being a traitor or national thief, after all, they still had to save face!","[Master, don't sigh yet, I just saw something fun.]","\"What fun thing? By the way, hasn't today's court session lasted a bit long?\"","In order to hear the follow-up, Zhang Zhongping, the Vice Minister of Rites, resolutely stepped forward. After getting the emperor's permission, he began to report in detail on the various matters of the Crown Prince's wedding.","You Mingmin, the Minister of the Court of State Ceremonial, had a thought. If Minister Zhang finished speaking and the two ancestors still hadn't finished, he would continue to report on the arrangements for the foreign delegations attending the Crown Prince's wedding.","In short, they had to drag it out and not let the court session end just like that.","[Master, ignore them for now. The thing I want to talk about is somewhat similar to your experience.]","\"Someone switched children again?\" Yue Fuguang reflexively thought of the true and false wealthy daughters.","It couldn't be that someone else crossed over to another world like her and also brought a quest system!","[Yes, someone's child was switched. I just found out by following Luoyu's line.","He is actually not Luo Feng's twin brother at all. At that time, Luo Xue actually gave birth to twins of different sexes, not two boys.]","\"Where is the girl who swapped identities with Luoyu now, is she still alive?\"","She wouldn't be a bitter cabbage like the original host, would she?","[Master, you definitely won't guess who she is. Not only do you know this person, but you're also quite familiar with her. She is someone by your side.]","\"Cuizhu, Cuiyu, Qingzhu, Chunying, Dongxue, Xiaoman, Liu Wei? The people around me who fit the age and I have more contact with are just these.","Could it really be one of them?\"","[Is Master unable to believe it? Little Zhu also looked several times before confirming that Shen Dongxue is Luo Xue's daughter.","The person whose identity was replaced by Luoyu.]","\"Since Dongxue is Luo Xue's daughter, without Luo Feng in Sunset Mountain Villa, wouldn't she be the ironclad future heir?\"","[Is Master going to help Shen Dongxue get her identity back?]","\"Of course. Even if Dongxue wasn't my guard, since I know about this, I would definitely help her get back the identity she deserves.","Moreover, Dongxue is my person now, how could I not help?","And Luo Xue's death from illness, there must be something fishy about it, right? Dongxue must be helped, and Luo Xue must be saved too.\"","Everyone in their hearts felt a burst of envy. Being recognized as one of their own by the Junior Preceptor was great!","Not only helping themselves, but even their relatives, they would lend a hand.","Many people's minds wavered. How could they hug the Junior Preceptor's golden thigh?","As for the crisis of Sunset Mountain Villa, they were a bit worried at first, but now that the Junior Preceptor was going to intervene, that trace of worry vanished completely.","Song Xingzhou, the Director of the Guest Courtyard, looked at Emperor Mingxi. This Shen Dongxue came out of their Guest Courtyard and now held an official position in the court.","If she could smoothly take over Sunset Mountain Villa in the future, it would also be a center of influence for the court in the Northwest Circuit.","Emperor Mingxi naturally understood Song Xingzhou's meaning. What he had to do was watch quietly. If the Junior Preceptor wanted people, give people; if she wanted power, give power. Anyway, he just had to do a good job in logistics support.","After the morning court session, returning to the Yu Mansion, Yue Fuguang ate and drank her fill, then called the Shen sisters over.","After the two sat down, she said, \"Chunying, I once heard you say that Dongxue is not your biological sister, is that true?\"","Chunying said, \"My lord has a good memory. There are four siblings in my family. Above Chunying are twin brothers Xiayu and Qiushan.","I heard my parents say that when I was one year old, I had a high fever from catching a cold that wouldn't go down. My parents had no choice but to take me into the city to see a doctor. It was also at that time that they found Dongxue, who was frozen purple, in a snow pit on the mountain.","My parents couldn't bear it, so they brought her home and she became the fourth child in our family.\"","Shen Dongxue also said, \"My parents brought me home and always raised me the same as my brothers and sister. In Dongxue's heart, they are my biological parents.\"","She had a good relationship with her sister Chunying. Besides sisterly affection, she was also grateful to her sister in her heart. If it wasn't for her sister's illness, she might have frozen to death in that heavy snow years ago.","Although she was an adopted child and a girl, the Shen parents always treated her equally with their other children.","Although the family was not rich when she was young, the whole family got along harmoniously. Shen Dongxue felt that she hadn't suffered much, and she was very satisfied with her current life.","Yue Fuguang looked at Shen Dongxue and said, \"Dongxue, have you ever thought about finding your biological parents?\"","Shen Dongxue paused, nodded, and then shook her head. She said, \"My lord, from the time I can remember, my parents never hid my background from me."]},{"number":251,"title":"Chapter 251: From Idol to Mother-in-Law","paragraphs":["They also asked me the same question, and even gave me the clothes and baby blanket I had back then to keep for myself.","Dongxue had guessed that perhaps they abandoned me because I was a girl, but Dongxue has her current parents and older siblings to love her.","I don't want to look for them anymore. In Dongxue's heart, the grace of giving birth is not as great as the grace of raising me.","To give birth to her and then throw her away, and on a deserted snowy mountain at that—the person who abandoned her never intended to leave her a way to survive.","If it weren't for her parents, she would have died long ago, so she has already repaid the debt of her birth.","\"If your birth mother didn't know of your existence, and you were maliciously switched after birth, would you still think so?\"","\"What? My Lord, are you saying Dongxue was switched?\"","They remembered clearly that the predecessor of the Lord before them was also maliciously switched, which led to the later descent of the Immortal Lord.","Shen Dongxue naturally thought of this too, but she was relatively lucky to have met her current parents and her loving brother and sister.","She asked, \"Who did the malicious switching that My Lord mentioned? Do my birth parents know?\"","Did they want to acknowledge her? If they treated the fake as a treasure like the third branch of the Yu family did, then she definitely wouldn't acknowledge them.","She made up her mind; even if they wanted to acknowledge her, she was still the child of the Shen parents, the fourth child of the Shen family, Shen Dongxue.","\"Your birth mother is still unaware to this day. Do you remember the sudden thunder that struck when it rained yesterday?\"","The two nodded. Not only did they remember, but they also knew that it was a mere point of her finger that summoned the heavenly thunder.","Recalling the lightning flashing on the Lord's hand at that time, the sisters still felt a palpitation in their chests and infinite admiration and submission toward the Junior Preceptor.","\"The heavenly thunder destroyed the Cao residence, and over a dozen people were captured, among them a pair of Luo brothers, Luo Yu and Luo Feng.","They are the eldest and second sons of Luo Xue, the master of Sunset Villa.","This Luo Feng is also the Young Pavilion Master of the Wind and Rain Pavilion.\"","\"Wind and Rain Pavilion? One of the three largest assassin organizations in the martial arts world, and its Young Pavilion Master is actually the eldest son of Sunset Villa?\"","Shen Chunying's eyes widened. As children of the martial arts world, who didn't know the Wind and Rain Pavilion that spanned the six kingdoms, and Sunset Villa, one of the Five Mountains and Six Villas of Great Yan?","Shen Chunxue also said, \"Lord Junior Preceptor may not know, but this Sunset Villa is only a hundred miles away from our hometown, and it has a great reputation among the commoners in the surrounding prefectures and counties.","It's because their master, Luo Xue, is not only a renowned heroine in the martial arts world, but also a great philanthropist known for her local charity.","I never expected them to be involved with the notorious Wind and Rain Pavilion!\"","Shen Chunxue's face showed unconcealable disappointment; the childhood idol of the sisters was the heroine Luo Xue.","Seeing her expression, Yue Fuguang curled her lips into a smile, \"I haven't finished speaking yet, don't be disappointed just yet.\"","[Master, if you dawdle any longer, won't these two stop being fans and turn against her!]","The sisters' bodies stiffened involuntarily. Although they didn't understand what the divine artifact meant by \"stop being fans and turn against her,\"","they knew they were being impatient. They smiled embarrassedly, sat up straighter, and quietly waited for the Junior Preceptor to continue.","\"The brother Luo Yu is not Luo Xue's biological son; he is the baby boy who was switched with Dongxue.","Back when Luo Xue gave birth, she didn't know she had a boy and a girl, rather than twin sons.\"","Hearing this, Shen Chunying's face flushed red, while Shen Dongxue's face gradually turned pale.","Shen Chunying's voice trembled a little as she said, \"So, Heroine Luo is Dongxue's birth mother?\"","Shen Dongxue also looked at her in disbelief. How could Heroine Luo, whom the sisters admired most in their childhood, be her birth mother!","Yue Fuguang said affirmatively, \"That's right, Luo Xue is Dongxue's biological mother, and she is unaware of Dongxue's existence.","The ones who switched the children were the midwife and a maid in the Luo mansion, and they were all acting under the orders of Yin Shuangcheng.","As for this Yin Shuangcheng, he is Luo Xue's husband, Dongxue's biological father, and the live-in son-in-law of Sunset Villa.\"","\"Her biological father switched the children? Even a vicious tiger won't eat its cubs, and Dongxue is his biological daughter. He actually...\"","He actually threw her into the mountains, and on a snowy day at that. He didn't leave this daughter any way to survive!","Shen Dongxue had tears welling up in her eyes. Hearing that she was switched by her biological father didn't make her too sad.","After all, she felt nothing for that Yin Shuangcheng. Without expectations, there could be no disappointment.","Her sadness was just heartache for Luo Xue. Such a valiant heroine actually met such a scumbag, and this scumbag was her biological father.","Shen Dongxue held her sister's hand, which was trembling slightly with anger, and asked Yue Fuguang, \"My Lord, what is the matter with that Luo Yu?\"","\"According to investigations, this Yu is your half-brother, the son Yin Shuangcheng had with another woman.\"","She sighed slightly and said, \"Yin Shuangcheng married into Sunset Villa. He has seven brothers in his family, and he is the fifth.","The first year was fine, but later, after living comfortably in the Luo family, his mind became restless. Taking advantage of Luo Xue being out on business,","he watched plays, listened to music, and visited brothels. Later, a high-class courtesan became pregnant with his child. Originally, Yin Shuangcheng just wanted to have a child with his own surname.","He didn't expect that at this time Luo Xue was also found to be pregnant, and later it was discovered to be twins. So he harbored thoughts he shouldn't have had.","He brought a midwife from his hometown, sent away the loyal maids, and used a secret medicine to make both women give birth at the same time.","After you were born, the midwife directly announced it was a son. By this time, Luo Xue had already fainted from exhaustion, and what followed was Yin Shuangcheng switching the children.","Because you were born at a manor when Luo Xue was out on an inspection tour, it was relatively close to the mountain where you were abandoned.","Yin Shuangcheng switched the children overnight and personally threw you onto the mountain.\"","\"My Lord, this matter must be told to Villa Master Luo.\"","Shen Chunying gnashed her teeth. They absolutely could not let that man surnamed Yin off easily!","Yue Fuguang nodded, \"It will definitely be told. Luo Feng has been captured and will undoubtedly die, so Shen Chunxue will be the sole heir of Sunset Villa.\"","[Master, don't you plan to tell Shen Chunxue that Luo Feng, like his scumbag father, also has a son and a daughter outside?]","\"Why tell her? The grandson and granddaughter of the old pavilion master of Wind and Rain Pavilion are destined not to be on the same path as her, nor can they enter the same family.","With them alive, do you think Pavilion Master Feng would spare Chunxue, the person competing with his grandson for the inheritance?\"","The sisters' hearts sank. Getting involved with the Wind and Rain Pavilion, what would the imperial court think?","Shen Dongxue said somewhat hesitantly, \"My Lord, Luo Feng's matters won't implicate Villa Master Luo, will they?\"","\"No.\" She looked at Shen Dongxue and said, \"Luo Xue is unaware of Luo Feng's affairs. I will naturally protect Sunset Villa. Do you want to acknowledge Luo Xue?\"","Shen Dongxue immediately knelt on one knee, \"Dongxue thanks My Lord on behalf of Villa Master Luo for your protection.\"","Her hanging heart settled slightly. As long as My Lord took action, Sunset Villa would absolutely be fine.","Yue Fuguang chuckled lightly, \"Looking at you, it seems you are going to acknowledge her?\"","She nodded in satisfaction. \"Get up quickly. Sunset Villa's geographical location is special. If you manage it well, you will naturally achieve great things.\""]},{"number":252,"title":"Chapter 252: Treading on Snow, Leaving No Trace","paragraphs":["Shen Dongxue stood up somewhat embarrassedly and said, \"My Lord, this subordinate wishes to acknowledge Manor Lord Luo, but I don't want to return to Sunset Manor just yet.\"","\"You don't want to return? Why not?\"","Luo Xue was not yet forty years old this year. In modern times, this would be the age to strive for a career, but in ancient times, at this age, one could already step down and enjoy playing with grandchildren.","\"This subordinate wishes to stay by My Lord's side for a few more years. Manor Lord Luo manages Sunset Manor very well, and there is no need for Dongxue right now.\"","Shen Dongxue felt that the time she had spent with My Lord was still short, and their bond was still a bit thin.","She wanted to stay by My Lord's side for a few more years, and it wouldn't be too late to return to Sunset Manor once she had firmly hugged this golden thigh.","By following Yue Fuguang here, she was also indirectly contributing to Sunset Manor. With My Lord as a backer for the manor, it would be more useful than ten of her going back.","Yue Fuguang was indifferent to this, \"Whatever you want, just discuss it with Luo Xue when the time comes.\"","After the Shen sisters left, the system couldn't help but ask, [Host, aren't you going to tell Shen Dongxue that Yin Shuangcheng died two years ago?]","\"We don't need to say it, Luo Xue will naturally tell her when she comes. Besides, I think Luo Xue did the right thing.","Discovering that her scumbag husband cheated and conspired with outsiders to switch her child, she decisively killed him. I must give her a thumbs up for her methods and decisiveness!\"","[Indeed, Yin Shuangcheng had a secret rendezvous with his lover and was robbed and killed by mountain bandits on the way. She even used the banner of avenging her husband.","Wiping out that bandit den was truly satisfying.","Even when Luo Yu personally went to investigate, she didn't find any clues.]","\"Luo Xue was just afraid that her husband would suffer, so she gave him some extra money when he traveled and conveniently asked him to collect some rent.","The news was found out by the mountain bandits, and they not only robbed him but killed him on the spot. This was all an accident, it can only be said that Yin Shuangcheng had bad luck.","Carrying a large sum of money and daring to take his old lover sightseeing, if he didn't die, who would?\"","[Hearing that Luo Yu was caught, Luo Xue must be overjoyed. Previously, because she feared the power of the Water Transport Gang and Sima Jing, she didn't dare to lay a hand on this person. Even when looking for her daughter, she had to indirectly ask others for help.","Now that the fake son is caught and the real daughter is found, it's simply cause for celebration.]","\"System, don't forget that her biological son, Luo Feng, was also caught, and it's the kind where death is certain.\"","[Because of the inheritance issue of Sunset Manor, their mother-son relationship has long existed in name only.","Luo Feng knew that his father had an illegitimate family and even switched his own sister.","For his own interests, he could still be as close as family with that family of three. Such a son is not worth having!]","\"Qingzhu, hasn't Taxue returned yet?\"","It truly lived up to the saying, you can't talk about people, and you can't talk about falcons either.","Just as Yue Fuguang asked about Taxue, two black dots came with the wind in the distance.","When they flew closer, the one leading was none other than that silly bird brought as tribute from Western Qiang, which shamelessly insisted on following Yue Fuguang during Emperor Mingxi's birthday celebration!","After it stuck to Yue Fuguang, it couldn't be driven away, and the emperor's beast park couldn't keep it either. Ultimately, Yue Fuguang reluctantly accepted it as a little brother... little sister, and named it Taxue.","\"Miss, it's Taxue, and it brought back an eagle? Falcon!\"","Qingzhu happily went to open the window for Taxue.","\"Qingzhu, go get some fresh meat for them.\"","[Host, you complain about the trouble of keeping it, but you are the one who feeds it the most diligently, even giving it Spirit Beast Pills.","Look at how fat Taxue has become!]","\"So what if she's fat, it doesn't stop her from bringing back a son-in-law for herself!\"","Yue Fuguang had already seen that the gray peregrine falcon behind Taxue, which was a circle larger than her, was male.","Could the other party have taken a fancy to Taxue's plumpness and followed her knowing she had good food?","Then she had to make Taxue look good. With a thought, the remaining half of a Spirit Beast Pill that Taxue had left over appeared in her hand.","As soon as the pill appeared in her hand, the two feathered creatures immediately became restless, especially the newcomer, who spread its long wings.","It couldn't help but flap twice, blowing a natural breeze over.","Yue Fuguang's face darkened, and she scolded, \"Taxue, control your guy, or I'll kick you both out of the house!\"","Yue Fuguang wasn't afraid she wouldn't understand. Having eaten Spirit Beast Pills a few times, Taxue, who was already exceptionally smart, had her IQ tested by the system.","She already had the intelligence of a three or four-year-old child.","Sure enough, upon hearing this, Taxue ignored the Spirit Beast Pill and directly slapped... clawed the peregrine falcon, knocking its head sideways.","The peregrine falcon, which lost a few feathers after being hit by Taxue, immediately became obedient.","Yue Fuguang was very satisfied with Taxue's husband-taming method; it was simple, crude, and effective.","She divided the half Spirit Beast Pill into five unequal parts, picking the largest one for Taxue and the smallest one for the newcomer.","For her own child, she had to make sure Taxue always maintained an absolute advantage in martial power to secure her unquestionable family status.","Dividing half a pill into several parts wasn't Yue Fuguang being stingy. This was a Spirit Beast Pill, which, as the name suggests, was for spirit beasts.","Taxue and the others were mortal beasts; if they ate too much at once, they would explode and die.","Look at this newcomer. Even with the smallest piece, after eating it, it already started acting like it was drunk, fluffing up into a big furball, with the skin under its wings turning pink.","Yue Fuguang patted its head with her hand, \"Newcomer, don't sleep yet. From now on, you'll follow Taxue's name and be called Wuhen.","I am your master, you must be obedient in the future, or you'll be kicked out of the house.\"","Taxue and Wuhen, it sounded like a family. Yue Fuguang was very satisfied with her naming skills.","She then said to the exceptionally excited Taxue, \"Taxue, manage Wuhen well. Our family implements a guilt-by-association system. If one bird makes a mistake, the whole family is exiled. Do you understand?\"","Yue Fuguang's threatening words were full of a Japanese officer flavor, bah! Before the system could speak, she despised herself first.","Taxue tilted her bird head, her beady eyes rolling around, clearly looking like her CPU wasn't enough.","[Host, look at Taxue's confused look, can she understand what a guilt-by-association system is?]","\"She'll know after eating a few more Spirit Beast Pills.\"","Yue Fuguang threw a piece of fresh meat brought by Qingzhu to Taxue, \"Eat quickly, eat full so you can work.\"","[Host, do you want Taxue to deliver a letter to Luo Xue? I estimate Luo Xue should have already received the carrier pigeon message about Luo Feng and Luo Yu being caught.]","\"My message to Luo Xue is mainly about Dongxue. Getting the news early should make her feel better.","She can also think carefully about how to deal with the subsequent matters on the way. I'm only responsible for ensuring the mother and daughter reunite; I don't want to meddle in anything else.\"","No one should expect her to worry any more.","[Host, you want to slack off again! The entire Great Yan Dynasty, from the emperor to the officials, is busy working for you, yet you are lying flat at home.]","\"What do you mean working for me? Can they rely on an outsider to build their own country?","Just tell me, did they get any benefits from working? I provided technology, seeds, and predicted the future for them; they didn't suffer any losses.","Isn't it right to enshrine me?\"","This enshrinement was real, the kind with incense!"]},{"number":253,"title":"Chapter 253: Eliminate the root cause to prevent future trouble.","paragraphs":["\"Besides, the mission belongs to both of us. Tell me, isn't it awesome to get points just by eating melons and enjoying the gossip?\"","The system thought about it and agreed. Furthermore, their persona was that of immortals descending to the mortal realm to experience trials. If the host was too approachable and did too much, it really wouldn't be appropriate.","The current situation was just fine. It immediately flattered her, [Host, the emperor and all the officials are acting as your beasts of burden. You are so incredibly awesome!]","Yue Fuguang tilted her head up, put her hands on her hips, and said arrogantly, \"Of course. Working for anyone is still working, but the most important thing is that I pay them well!","Also, the map you displayed today was much clearer than the one during the potato sacrifice. Has your data recovered a bit more?\"","[Host, it's not data recovery. I leveled up again!]","\"You leveled up? Why didn't you say so earlier? Hurry up and tell me what new functions you have.\"","The function to see merit and luck that appeared last time had been fun for a while. After looking at all the civil and military officials in the court, she had long since gotten bored of it.","[The Gossip System's inner voice can now cover a radius of one kilometer, and it can be directed at up to three hundred people. The Merit System can now show a person's specific merit value.","It is much more precise than at level three, when you could only see the color of their merit and luck.","Most importantly, there is now a live-streaming function!] Although this live-streaming had some restrictions, having it was better than not!","Not bad, not bad. For a crippled system to get new functions with every upgrade, Yue Fuguang was already very satisfied!","The number of targets for the directed inner voice leak had grown from one hundred and fifty to three hundred, doubling in size. In the future, when encountering grand occasions, she could develop even more usable believers!","As for the live-streaming, she could use it to show off when the opportunity arose, giving these backward ancients a little shock!","The next day, just as Yue Fuguang finished her morning classes and had lunch, she was preparing to take a short nap.","Then she saw the Crown Prince walk in.","\"Crown Prince, shouldn't you be preparing for your grand wedding? How do you have the free time to come to the Hongwen Pavilion?\"","For the Crown Prince's wedding, although the Ministry of Rites handled the procedures, as the groom-to-be, he still needed to learn the wedding etiquette.","After all, it was his first time getting married, and he had no experience.","The last time the Great Yan Dynasty had such a grand occasion was when his parents got married, which he didn't have the chance to witness himself, so of course he had to learn!","The Crown Prince smiled and said, \"It's raining today, so the afternoon equestrian class is canceled. I just happened to have some free time, so I came to invite the Junior Preceptor to stroll through my royal father's private storehouse with me.\"","Upon hearing the Crown Prince's words, never mind Yue Fuguang, the surrounding princes, princesses, and study companions all gasped in shock.","Stroll where?","His Majesty's private storehouse!","Was that a place just anyone could go?","The Crown Prince even used the word 'stroll', which was quite audacious.","Yue Fuguang stood up, instructed her two older sisters to return to the manor first, and then said to the Crown Prince, \"Alright, let's go see what good things His Majesty has hidden away.\"","Seeing her relaxed demeanor, as if she were going for a stroll in her own backyard, everyone was a bit dumbfounded!","These two, truly one dared to suggest it, and the other dared to agree!","Did His Majesty even know you were going to his private storehouse?","Emperor Mingxi: I didn't know? Could this son who favors outsiders even get in otherwise?","He would never admit to death that, in order not to be looked down upon by these two \"ancestors\", he had secretly ordered Eunuch Qian yesterday to place some of his favorite treasures into the private storehouse to keep up appearances.","[Master, what is there to see in a mortal's private storehouse? There are no immortal herbs, spiritual materials, precious artifacts, or immortal pills. Taking them is useless!]","\"Little Zhu, I am currently a mortal little girl. Don't you think it would be strange if I didn't like these things?\"","Xie Zhiyan: It truly is a grievance for these two ancestors!","[Master, should we tell the Crown Prince and the Emperor that Shen Dongxue is Luo Xue's daughter?]","\"Of course we have to tell them. Otherwise, once Feng Yang finds out about Dongxue's existence, he will definitely make a move against her so that his grandson can inherit the Luoxia Villa.","I don't want to worry too much about it, so the imperial court will have to pay a little attention and help keep an eye on Luoxia Villa.\"","Xie Zhiyan silently committed this to memory. Understood. He would pass down the orders to have people help the Junior Preceptor keep an eye on things.","[Does Master want to use the Emperor's hand to eliminate Feng Yang?]","\"What else? If we just strike him dead with lightning right away, Luo Feng and Luo Yu alone wouldn't be able to uproot all the other strongholds of the Wind and Rain Pavilion in Great Yan.\"","[Are there strongholds that Luo Feng, the young pavilion master, doesn't know about?]","\"Feng Yang will definitely hold something back. However, how much they can dig out will depend on the interrogation methods of Wei Ping and Cai Xian.","Little Zhu, can you confirm where Feng Yang is hiding right now?\"","[Master, Feng Yang is currently hiding in Fahua Temple, a hundred miles outside the capital city of Shangjing. You would never guess what his current identity is.]","Yue Fuguang's lips curled up. \"I guess he is either the abbot, the gatekeeper of the Sutra Pavilion, or an inconspicuous sweeping monk.\"","Here it comes, here it comes, what a classic trope!","[Master, you actually guessed wrong this time! Feng Yang is currently neither a sweeping monk nor the monk guarding the Sutra Pavilion.","He is now just an ordinary old lay Buddhist who is temporarily residing in the temple, devoted to Buddha.","However, the abbot of Fahua Temple is his Left Protector, and the gatekeeper of the Sutra Pavilion is his Right Protector.","The sweeping monk is his armed guard.","What they are guarding is not the scriptures inside, but the massive amount of treasure in the secret chamber beneath the Sutra Pavilion, all obtained by the Wind and Rain Pavilion through years of murder and robbery.]","Xie Zhiyan nodded inwardly. He noted it all down. As soon as he got out of the private storehouse, he would notify the two ministers, Wei Ping and Cai Xian, to arrest them.","He would just say that Luo Feng confessed it. Otherwise, if they waited for the Junior Preceptor to remind them, Feng Yang might run away upon seeing the bad situation, and it would be hard to catch him!","While Xie Zhiyan was thinking about how to arrest them without alerting the people in the temple, Yue Fuguang started chatting with the system about other things.","[Host, how should we deal with Luo Feng's two children?]","\"If it were me, I would prefer the approach from my hometown: pull up the weeds by the roots to leave no future troubles. After all, having one story of the Orphan of Zhao is enough.\"","[Do you have the heart to do that? Have you forgotten how you died?]","\"How is that the same? A saying I have always praised is, 'If they are not of our kin, their hearts must be different.' These two children have always been raised by Feng Yang and his daughter.","In fact, they are Western Qiang people. Besides, didn't you check that the lives of these two are worth eight hundred points in the system's mission bar?","With lives worth eight hundred points, you don't even need to look at the original history to know they deserve to be killed!\"","Yue Fuguang's words left System 07, whose Merit System had temporarily gained the upper hand due to the upgrade, completely speechless.","The two of them walked all the way to the main entrance of the private storehouse.","From the outside, it was a tall and sturdy building, looking like it had about eight or nine rooms.","The walls were thicker than elsewhere and looked very new with a gray hue, probably because they were coated with cement.","The main doors were three meters high, made of an unrecognizable wood that felt incredibly solid. A massive iron lock hung on them, and the windows used iron bars for lattices.","As for the security forces, there were two guards at the door, and guards stationed at the surrounding intersections.","There were also two squads of guards patrolling back and forth, with ten men in each squad.","Just as the two stopped at the entrance, two minor officials in green robes ran over. After inspecting the warrant Xie Zhiyan handed them, one signaled the other to help open the storehouse doors together.","\"These two minor officials in green robes must be people Emperor Mingxi trusts very much to be able to guard his storehouse doors.\"","[Of course they are trusted by the Emperor! It's just a pity that the Emperor's blindness when it comes to judging character remains as stable as ever.]"]},{"number":254,"title":"Chapter 254: The Night-Shining Pearl is Toxic","paragraphs":["[The one on the left is called Qian Bao. He is the eldest grandson of the emperor's wet nurse. True to his name, he is the treasure of the Qian family.","Unfortunately, with the emperor as his backer, this person has been spoiled since childhood, developing a lawless temperament.","Lining his own pockets and treating the emperor's private treasury as his own storehouse, pocketing many good things—these are just minor offenses.]","Treating the emperor's private treasury as his own is considered a minor offense?","\"Then what is a major offense?\" Is he trying to ascend to heaven?","Yue Fuguang asked while following the Crown Prince inside, casually casting a discreet glance at the fawning Qian Bao.","This man's days were numbered!","The private treasury was vast, four or five meters high, lined with many dark wooden shelves and chests.","The air smelled of wood and old things.","Xie Zhiyan must have been a frequent visitor, as he skillfully found an incense burner on an empty table in the middle.","Before long, a faint scent of plum blossoms reached Yue Fuguang's nose, gradually diluting the stale air in the storehouse.","[Of course, it's raiding the emperor's home!]","Xie Zhiyan's hand trembled, almost dropping the jade ruyi in his grasp.","Xie Zhiyan felt helpless in his heart. The Divine Artifact Lord spoke so... so boldly!","Under the heavens, only the emperor raided others' homes. Who would dare to raid the emperor's home?","Yue Fuguang had the same doubt. \"Little Zhu, are you sure you didn't say it backwards? Qian Bao, a minor seventh-rank official, raiding the emperor's home?\"","[Master, Little Zhu is not speaking nonsense. Before the allied forces of the three nations broke into the imperial city, this Qian Bao used the convenience of his position.","Along with another minor official named Fei Wu and a few guards on duty at the private treasury, he secretly transported all the good things out of the private treasury.","Later, during the internal chaos of the imperial city, he gathered a group of eunuchs to rob and steal from various palaces, making off with a lot of valuables.","Does this not count as raiding the emperor's home?","The pair of jasper paperweights crafted by Master Mo, which the emperor liked most in the Hall of Mental Cultivation, ultimately fell into his hands.]","At this moment, Yue Fuguang rested her hand on a wooden shelf. The bottom tier of the shelf displayed beautifully shaped bottles of various colors—white, cyan, and multi-colored.","Unfortunately, after leaving this world, to Yue Fuguang, these things would be no different from ordinary flower vases.","Just like the calligraphy and paintings placed on the top tier, if antiques do not carry relevant history, what difference is there between them and other objects?","Therefore, she hadn't placed a single painting, calligraphy work, or bottle in her storage ring's collection. It was better to leave the civilization of this world right here.","Yue Fuguang merely admired them briefly before turning to walk further back. As she turned, she acutely noticed a flash of bright yellow passing by the open door of the private treasury.","With a guess in her heart, she couldn't help but agree with the system, \"That is indeed no different from a raid. This Qian Bao looks honest and simple-minded; I didn't expect him to be such a bold and treacherous person inside.\"","[Master, don't be fooled by his appearance. Don't be deceived by how cautious and timid he acts in front of you and the Crown Prince right now.","Little do you know, behind the scenes, relying on the fact that the emperor drank his grandmother's milk, he bullies his colleagues at work. It's only because you two came today; if someone of a lower status came, they wouldn't even get to see him.","To enter this door, one would have to give a lot of bribes.","Outside the palace, he bullies men and oppresses women, committing many evil deeds. Despite his ugly appearance, it doesn't stop him from liking beauties.","And he is not picky about gender. He is a regular customer at both the Spring Hiding Pavilion and the Spring Painting Pavilion.]","Yue Fuguang came to a jade shelf. The jade wares on the shelf gathered the colors of the rainbow, and each piece was of premium quality.","Some were carved into various shapes, including jewelry and ornaments, while others were just raw stones waiting to be carved and polished.","On the next tier down, there were a few bronze objects with dark green rust on them.","A few paintings hung on the wall here, depicting landscapes, flowers, and birds. The paper looked a bit old, and there were seals stamped on them; they must be the work of masters.","Yue Fuguang thought for a moment and still picked a few beautiful paintings of flowers, birds, fish, insects, and landscapes, holding them in her arms.","Seeing that she had found things she liked, Xie Zhiyan walked over and said, \"Lord Junior Preceptor, I will help you put them in the chest.\"","She looked in the direction Xie Zhiyan pointed. On the ground next to the incense burner table, several large chests had been placed at some point.","It must have been Xie Zhiyan who brought them for her to put things in.","\"He plays that wildly? If I remember correctly, those two pavilions are also industry leaders, housing many top-tier courtesans and male escorts. They are genuine money-squandering dens.","How can a tiny seventh-rank official like him afford to frequent such places, even if he has some family wealth?","Does his family own a mine?\"","Yue Fuguang guessed that his theft of items from the emperor's private treasury must have occurred during the later years of Emperor Mingxi. The emperor was still vigorous and energetic now; surely Qian Bao wouldn't dare to do it yet?","Yue Fuguang continued walking inward. On a shelf, she saw some weapons.","A sword rested in its scabbard, a bow hung on the wall, and next to the bow was a quiver containing a few feathered arrows.","\"Little Zhu, give me the blueprints for the repeating crossbow when we get back.\"","[Master, I also have the blueprints for a siege crossbow here. Do you want them?]","\"We are not laying siege to any city right now. Keep them for yourself for now.\"","Standing to the side, Xie Zhiyan really wanted to say that laying siege was only a matter of time, and there would definitely be a chance to use the siege crossbow.","Unfortunately, he didn't dare to utter a single word.","However, he quickly got over it. With the repeating crossbow, this trip to the private treasury was already very fruitful, not to mention learning about a national pest.","He had heard quite a few bad rumors about his imperial father's wet nurse, Madam Liu's in-laws. Last spring, the second branch of the Qian family, living in the suburbs of the capital, was even sued at the county office for embezzling their neighbor's land.","For his imperial father's sake, the county magistrate handled the matter leniently. If his subordinates hadn't encountered it while running errands, he wouldn't have known about it.","His imperial father indeed indulged the families of his two wet nurses, Madam Liu and Madam Wei, a bit too much!","Several large chests were placed in the corner with their lids closed. Not knowing what was inside, she looked at the dust accumulated on them, then at her own moon-white gauze dress, and Yue Fuguang's curiosity instantly vanished.","Xie Zhiyan walked up to a shelf on her left, picked up a small box, and opened the lid. Inside was a round bead; it was light green and not very bright.","He said to Yue Fuguang, \"Lord Junior Preceptor, please look. This is a luminous pearl sent in as tribute by a foreign state.\"","Yue Fuguang looked at the pearl. Upon hearing the name 'luminous pearl,' her legs moved faster than her brain, unconsciously stepping back two paces.","Seeing her reaction, Xie Zhiyan's hand paused. Suddenly, he felt as if the pearl in his hand weighed a thousand catties. No, he couldn't hold it up anymore!","\"Lord Junior Preceptor, do you think there is a problem with this pearl?\"","He tossed the pearl back into the box. His movement no longer retained the careful caution he had when he first picked it up.","\"Little Zhu, help me scan this. Is this luminous pearl made of fluorite, willemite, or a radioactive uranium mineral?\"","Yue Fuguang shook her head. \"I don't know if there is a problem with this pearl, but when I was at the Daoist temple, I heard that the light from some luminous pearls is toxic.","Even if a healthy person stays with it for a long time, it can cause illness, even terminal illness.\""]},{"number":255,"title":"Chapter 255: Very Good, Very Criminal","paragraphs":["Cancer-causing—isn't that a terminal illness? Even with advanced modern medicine, it hasn't been completely conquered, let alone in ancient times with backward medical practices. One could only wait for death.","Of course, she wasn't afraid. Inside her storage ring, there was more than one type of pill that could counteract it.","[Master, this thing is not fluorite. Little Zhu detected that its composition is complex, and right at this moment, it is continuously emitting radiation. It is definitely carcinogenic.","To put it bluntly, whoever stays close to it for a long time will die.]","Xie Zhiyan's body stiffened, his face turning pale for a moment. His voice was a bit dry as he said, \"This is the birthday gift sent by Beili this time.","There are three in total. One is in the storehouse, one is in my grandmother's sleeping quarters, and one... is in my imperial father's sleeping quarters.\"","His hands trembled slightly. \"Imperial Father likes it very much and often takes it out to play with.\"","It seemed he had found the reason why his currently robust-looking imperial father would fall severely ill a few years later!","[Master, if the Emperor frequently plays with this thing over the next few years, it wouldn't be surprising if he doesn't live past fifty.","Even if he isn't poisoned to death in the end, he will die because of the luminous pearl.]","'Little Zhu, the main point is, does Beili know this thing is poisonous?'","Indeed, Xie Zhiyan couldn't help but wonder as well: did Beili know this thing was poisonous?","And did the Beili royal family use this item themselves?","Xie Zhiyan's eyes flickered. It was time for the spies in the Beili imperial palace to make a move!","[If Master wants to know, you can order someone to investigate the symptoms of Beili royal family members before their deaths from illness. Perhaps you will find something.]","'Forget it, I'm not that curious!'","The Emperor and the Crown Prince would investigate; she just needed to wait for the fruits of their labor.","Thinking this in her heart, she said aloud, \"The Crown Prince can mention it to His Majesty. I've only heard rumors about this, so whether to believe it or not is up to His Majesty's own decision.\"","[If he doesn't believe it, he can just wait for death. Master, if the Emperor doesn't listen to advice and falls ill because of it, you must not use a pill to save him!]","Emperor Mingxi, who was hiding in the duty room next door eavesdropping, ground his teeth secretly when he heard this. What do you mean by 'doesn't listen to advice'? You should at least advise me before saying that!","Just letting the Crown Prince mention it to me! If it weren't for the fact that these two ancestors had the golden aura of immortals and could never be wrong, who would have thought that such a beautiful pearl was poisonous!","\"Zhiyan will definitely persuade Imperial Father to destroy this harmful poison pearl!\"","Xie Zhiyan, as if avoiding the plague god, stayed far away from the shelf holding the pearls along with Yue Fuguang. They walked toward a row of low shelves further inside.","The shelves were covered with velvet cloth, and several ivory carvings were displayed on them.","There was a picture of a group of immortals carved from a whole ivory tusk, as well as seals carved from small pieces of ivory.","Next to them were a few rhinoceros horn cups of varying shades.","There were also exquisite ornaments made of giant clam shells, each piece extremely beautiful.","Yue Fuguang: The things on this row of shelves are all very beautiful and very 'criminal'!","She picked two of each item. Since it wasn't 'illegal' here, she would stock up on some goods first.","On the bottom layer were several brocade boxes. She opened them one by one, and Yue Fuguang was almost dazzled by the things inside.","Various beautiful gemstones and pearls were packed together in boxes. Yue Fuguang brought over a medium-sized red sandalwood box from next door.","Pink, sea blue, lake blue, yellow, red... grabbing a handful of each. Yue Fuguang looked at her small, chubby hands, which could only grab a few fingernail-sized gems at a time, and couldn't help but grab two more handfuls.","There were also pearls of various shades and sizes; she took some of everything.","Looking at a box full of treasures, she felt instantly satisfied.","Yue Fuguang suddenly realized that she hadn't thought about her unspent fifty million in a long time.","On the wooden shelf against the wall was a row of boxes. Opening them, she saw that they contained complete sets of exquisite tea sets.","There were purple clay ones with smooth teapot bodies, and white porcelain ones with extremely thin cup walls.","Yue Fuguang wouldn't use tea sets that others had used, but that didn't stop her from collecting them.","Next to the tea sets were complete sets of the Four Treasures of the Study. The most attractive were the various inkstones. Without standing on ceremony, she picked out a few good ones.","Especially the ink sticks that emitted a faint fragrance, engraved with golden characters. Each ink stick was beautifully crafted, looking very much like a work of art.","Yue Fuguang noticed that there were also a few wooden boxes on the shelf.","Opening them, she found complete sets of ancient books inside. The pages were yellowed, but the ink marks were still clear.","Next to the book boxes were piled several rolls of maps, tied with silk cords.","When it came to maps, whose could be clearer and more effective than the maps transmitted in real-time by the system? These maps, as long as they weren't treasure maps...","...she had absolutely no interest in them.","The innermost room had a lower temperature, and various medicinal herbs were displayed on the shelves. There was lingzhi in jars, ginseng in brocade boxes, and deer horn wrapped in oiled paper.","Soaking in a wooden barrel in the corner were several animal skeletons—tiger bones!","Yue Fuguang nodded. Very good, very 'criminal'!","Xie Zhiyan stopped in front of an iron chest.","Inside the chest were neatly stacked weapon catalogs and blueprints for various devices. The papers depicted the structure of the Great Yan's crossbows.","On the wooden shelf next to it were corresponding models: foldable scaling ladders, various types of machinery, etc. The workmanship was very exquisite, but the items were too outdated.","Yue Fuguang saw that Great Yan's crossbows were still single-shot, and the range probably wasn't very far.","'Little Zhu, it seems Great Yan doesn't have repeating crossbows. I could make an extra one to give to the Crown Prince as one of his wedding gifts.'","Hearing that Yue Fuguang would give him a repeating crossbow as a wedding gift, Xie Zhiyan felt inexplicably excited.","Smiling, he walked up to a shelf and opened a huge box containing various pelts.","He picked up pure white, fiery red, and purple fox pelts and said, \"Lord Junior Preceptor, these pelts have no mixed colors and would look quite beautiful made into winter clothes. Do you like them?\"","As he spoke, he opened another box containing several fur cloaks.","There were pure white fox furs, as well as spotted leopard skins.","On the shelf next to the fur clothes were several headpieces, some inlaid with jade and others embedded with pearls, which matched the fox fur cloaks quite well.","Yue Fuguang felt that Xie Zhiyan's aesthetic taste wasn't bad, so she happily accepted his goodwill.","By the time they left the Emperor's private storehouse, Yue Fuguang and Xie Zhiyan were followed by ten people carrying five large chests.","'Little Zhu, do you think the Emperor will cry when he finds out I took so many of his treasures?'","[Little Zhu thinks the Emperor is not that stingy.]","Emperor Mingxi, hiding in the duty room, nodded in satisfaction. Although the Divine Artifact sometimes spoke infuriatingly, it still had a good eye.","I am a generous emperor. Let alone five chests, even if it were ten, I wouldn't feel the slightest bit of heartache.","Compared to his own life and the Xie family's empire, these were not worth mentioning.","Who knew that just as he thought this, he heard the Divine Artifact continue, [Look at how many treasures from his private storehouse were taken home by Qian Bao.","I didn't see him feel the slightest bit of heartache over that either.","Didn't Master just ask how someone from Qian Bao's background could afford to frequent top-tier brothels like the Hidden Spring Pavilion and the Painted Spring Pavilion?","The answer lies here. Guarding the Emperor's massive private storehouse, would he be afraid of lacking money to live it up? And when I say he stole from the private storehouse, it's not something that happens years later.","It started not long after he took the job!]","Emperor Mingxi: I take back what I just said!","Emperor Mingxi turned his head and saw Qian Bao, gagged and tied up tightly, tossed on the floor in the corner.","His eyes were filled with completely undisguised, chilling killing intent."]},{"number":256,"title":"Chapter 256: Laozi Has a Backer, a Big Backer","paragraphs":["That dog, stealing things right from under his nose!","It was only in the past half year that he had made a fortune and his private treasury was filled. A few years ago when he was still poor, this dog must have embezzled quite a lot!","Emperor Mingxi couldn't help grinding his teeth. As the emperor of a nation, the silver he had saved up was actually taken by this dog to please girls and gigolos!","A total disgrace, an absolute disgrace!","\"The Emperor's private treasury is like his own home, taking whatever he wants to spend! This private treasury might as well be renamed the Qian Family Treasury.\"","Emperor Mingxi, already furious to the point of ascending to the heavens after being backstabbed by someone he trusted, had his heart suddenly stabbed again by Yue Fuguang.","It hurt!","Walking shoulder to shoulder with Yue Fuguang, the Crown Prince's mouth twitched when he heard the venomous words of these two ancestors. He had just seen Qian Gui's figure flash past the duty room.","Then his imperial father must have heard the words of these two ancestors.","Who knows how angry he is right now! An enraged tiger cannot be approached!","The Crown Prince's eyes flickered. It was too dangerous to be around his imperial father at this moment; it would be better for him to go out and hide.","Therefore, using the excuse that the items were precious, the Crown Prince insisted on personally escorting Yue Fuguang back to her residence.","[Host, why didn't you mention what this guy did to the Eighth Princess?]","\"System, with all those previous crimes, this person is dead for sure. Why bother mentioning things that are destined not to happen?\"","When the nest falls, no egg remains intact. No matter how noble your previous status was, when the building collapses, you will fall into the mud and be trampled upon by others!","Meanwhile, Emperor Mingxi went straight back to his sleeping quarters and ordered someone to take the luminous pearl and give it to Qian Bao, who had already been locked up in prison.","He also ordered that Qian Bao must hold the luminous pearl day and night without stopping, not even letting go when eating or using the toilet.","On Yue Fuguang's side, upon returning home, she distributed the items she had obtained from today's taking down the local tyrant to each branch of the family.","As for the guards around her, she gave them each a small gold ingot. For them, money was the most practical thing.","The next day, after Yue Fuguang finished her studies and changed her clothes, a maid from the main courtyard came to invite her.","Today was only the thirtieth, and tomorrow was the first day of the month for the family banquet. She wondered what her grandfather and the others wanted to see her for.","Arriving at Shou'an Hall, as soon as she entered, she saw her second brother, Yu Boming, gesturing wildly as he talked about something.","Was this single-minded second brother of hers playing the fool to entertain their parents?","Walking into the main hall, everyone at home was present except for her. Yu the eldest and Yu the second were playing chess on one side, Yu the third was watching the game, and Yu Ningxuan and her sisters were playing Flying Chess.","\"Second Brother, when did you get back?\"","Ever since this guy was thrown into the military camp by their second uncle, he had grown quite a bit over the past few months and had gotten a shade darker.","He looked more robust, showing a trend of developing from a weak scholar into a rough military man.","No matter which era's military camp it was, good or bad, it was always a good place to temper a person!","Seeing Yue Fuguang enter, Yu Boming had a silly smile on his face, visibly a bit reserved, unlike his casual demeanor in front of their grandfather and grandmother.","\"I arrived at the end of the Wei hour.\"","Now, his Seventh Sister was his livelihood and future. When dealing with a golden rice bowl, even the usually careless Yu Boming couldn't help but be cautious.","Afraid that Yue Fuguang might have other thoughts, he quickly added, \"I got a leave of absence from General Wei today, and came back together with Baozi, Cai Bing, and Huo Shui. I'll be leaving the day after tomorrow.\"","Yue Fuguang naturally sat down in the special seat Old Madam Yu had reserved for her.","Seeing that Yu Boming was still standing, she motioned for him to sit down and talk.","Yu Boming carefully rested half of his buttocks on the chair, sitting properly like a primary schooler waiting for the teacher's spot check.","He was extremely nervous; this was the first time his Seventh Sister had shown concern for him since he went to the military camp a few months ago.","He had heard that his Seventh Sister summoned heavenly thunder the day before yesterday and struck the third courtyard of the Cao residence.","He and Huo Shui had specifically taken a detour to look at it before coming home. The houses were destroyed and collapsed, and the large pitch-black crater left on the ground still smelled of burning.","The unlucky Cai Bing even accidentally stepped on a half-charred piece of an arm, the arm attached to a pale palm, nearly scaring the young masters to death.","Yu Boming sighed in his heart. For the next few days, none of them would want to touch braised pig trotters or chicken claws!","After seeing the scene, they were both fearful and admiring of Yue Fuguang, who had caused all this. Thinking that they might be selected to join the army under her control in the future, they couldn't help but feel a burst of excitement.","However, the oldest, Bao Zihui, thought the most. He said, \"Among us, besides Boming, who can guarantee that they will definitely be chosen by that person?\"","As soon as these words were spoken, the dozen or so people who were extremely excited a second ago became like deflated pig bladders, drooping their heads.","To be honest, Bao Zihui's words made Yu Boming extremely proud at the time, if it weren't for the fear of being ganged up on.","He would have definitely laughed out loud three times in front of everyone and shouted, \"My sister is Fuguang. I have a backer, a huge backer!\"","The biggest backer in the Great Yan!","As for whether he would be called a nepotism hire, he didn't care at all, just looking at the jealous red eyes of those dozen or so animals staring at him.","Each of them wished they could replace him!","His sister even brought out the method to prevent smallpox just for him!","When the others heard this at the time, they were much gentler than usual towards him, who was moved to tears, and no one mocked him for crying like a girl.","Yue Fuguang: Second Brother is overthinking it. Bringing out the cowpox method was really just to complete the System's task!","Yu Boming was just a tool, her reasonable excuse for bringing out this method!","Yu Boming: I don't believe it, I don't care, I won't listen!","\"How is Second Brother doing in the military camp? Can you keep up with the training?\"","This ten-thousand-strong army used the training methods she provided, and even the ideological education was a redacted modern version.","To prevent this ten-thousand-strong force from being influenced by the old military veterans, they were nominally under the Right Martial Guard New Camp, and their station was transformed from an abandoned royal horse farm.","These ten thousand people were kept far away from the old army. Yue Fuguang absolutely would not allow those rat droppings to ruin the pot of soup she had personally brewed.","Even the generals inside were personally selected by Huo Ying and Wei Shouyi, with Yue Fuguang making the final decision.","\"Everything is fine. Do you see if your Second Brother is much stronger than before?\"","Yu Boming slapped his chest loudly, making Yue Fuguang feel the pain just watching him.","\"Second Brother does look much more solid now compared to before!\"","The whole family gathered around, smiling as they watched the siblings chat.","Yu Shuqin smiled and chimed in, \"Sending him to the military camp for tempering was the right choice. Otherwise, this boy would still be muddling through his days right now.\"","As he spoke, he glanced at Second Aunt Yu, nee Wang.","Seeing her husband like this, Second Aunt Yu suppressed the urge to roll her eyes. This guy was still holding a grudge from when they returned to their room and she pinched his soft flesh because he wanted to send their son to the military camp!","How could she have known back then that the family's precious lump of gold was the biggest Buddha in the whole Great Yan!","Look at her now that she knows the situation. Even though her son is setting off for the Three-Pronged Land in May, isn't she completely unworried?","Yu Zhongqin also said, \"Little Second has grown quite fast, which shows that he hasn't been lazy or slacking off during training.\"","\"Second Brother, how is the food in the military camp? Has anyone been embezzling or using inferior goods?\""]},{"number":257,"title":"Chapter 257: Capable of Transmitting Messages over Thousands of Miles","paragraphs":["She had contributed thirty percent of the military funds. If that money wasn't spent on the soldiers and instead was embezzled by certain people, she would truly unleash her \"thunderous wrath\"!","Yu Boming gave a sly smile, showing a rare flash of cleverness, and said, \"Don't worry, Sister. I listened to Grandfather and Father.","Besides our daily training, I've kept an eye on these matters at all times.","With your name backing us, no one dares to stretch their hands into this area.\"","The dozen or so sons of officials dined together with the regular soldiers, so no one dared to fool them with inferior food.","Not to mention that Minister Huo and General Wei frequently inspected the camp and ate with the soldiers, making it even less likely for anyone to dare try anything.","Seeing Yue Fuguang nod, he continued, \"Following the methods you taught us, we built pigsties next to the military camp and raised dozens of pigs separately.","General Wei also took us into the mountains, and we caught over a dozen litters of rabbits to raise. Now the rabbits have multiplied to over three hundred.","There are also chickens and ducks. The camp will soon be able to eat the meat we raised ourselves.\"","It was only after raising them that he understood why his sister had suggested raising rabbits—those things just reproduced so fast, they really could breed!","As for the pigs, what he didn't mention was that a few days ago, General Wei had taken them to his sister's estate to snatch grass.","Yes, snatch. For over two thousand acres of land and three hillocks, a thousand people had actually shown up.","Having never done farm work, they were assigned to pull weeds. The pulled grass had to be put into cloth bags to prevent others from snatching it away.","He still remembered General Wei urging them repeatedly, \"Move faster! We've agreed with the others: whoever pulls it, keeps it.","Brothers, whatever you pull is what you earn! But remember, it's better to be slow than to damage a single seedling, otherwise you'll face military law!\"","General Wei, who was initially excited, had said the last sentence very seriously, even wearing a chillingly intimidating smile.","It scared them into scurrying away like rats.","At the time, he was specifically stopped by him, \"Boming, you don't need to pull grass. You're responsible for patrolling around, not just on our side, but over by the others too.","If you find anyone destroying the seedlings, report to me immediately.\"","Later he found out that those weren't ordinary grasses; they were \"nutritious grasses\" that had absorbed the spiritual rainwater summoned by Seventh Sister and the others.","So when they went back that day, they had wild vegetable porridge, and the pigs, chickens, ducks, and rabbits also got a bonus meal of wild vegetables.","The way the animals fought over an extra bite of forage looked exactly like how the soldiers had fought over their porridge half an hour earlier.","Yu Boming couldn't help but smack his lips in nostalgia, then heard Yue Fuguang praise him, \"Second Brother, you've done very well.","It's just that when you go to Sancha Land in the future, the burden on your shoulders will be heavier, but you must not neglect the soldiers' diet and ideological education.\"","Both physical bodies and minds must be firmly grasped and strengthened.","Hearing that more responsibilities were being placed on his shoulders, Yu Boming's face flushed with excitement. His sister had not only praised him just now but also showed her trust in him; how could he not be thrilled?","He began thumping his chest loudly, promising, \"Don't worry, Sister. Second Brother guarantees to watch over Sancha Land for you.\"","Yue Fuguang also smiled and said, \"Naturally, I believe in Second Brother.\"","The others couldn't help but chime in, teaching Yu Boming management experience on the spot.","\"Little Zhu, do you still have any radio transceivers?\"","[Master wants to use that thing for communication?]","\"Yes, there is no spiritual energy here, so we can't use voice transmission talismans, and there is no signal, so we can't use cell phones.","If we want timely, fast, and long-distance communication, we can only use radio transceivers.\"","[Aren't there still Taxue and Wuhen? With their speed, a distance of a thousand miles would only take a day or two for a round trip.]","\"Even though they are animals, you can't really just use them like beasts of burden!","Besides, what your master wants is instantaneous transmission over a thousand miles, which they cannot do.\"","Hearing this, Yu Chongshan and the others couldn't help but tremble their hands holding their water cups. Instant communication over a thousand miles.","Did such a thing really exist in the world?","From Fuguang's words, she had more than one kind on hand, but it seemed the only one they could use was the one called a radio transceiver.","The father and sons couldn't help but glance at the goofily smiling Yu Boming.","They had to admit, this second son really had the dumb luck of a fool. He was just going to look at a piece of land, and his sister had already thought of everything for him.","\"After thinking it over, I still feel we need to equip that army with a radio transceiver so we can keep track of the situation there at all times.","Moreover, there is no other signal interference here, and no need to worry about being wiretapped, so I can even save the trouble of a codebook.","The two radios just need to send plain text. I remember the radios you have are solar-powered, so we even save on batteries.\"","The items she bought from the system mall, even if they were similar to modern items, were produced by the system kingdom.","Many drawbacks were optimized by the system, which possessed higher-dimensional technology. The quality was absolutely top-notch!","[Master, who do you plan to choose as the telegraph operator?]","\"The telegraph operator for Sancha Land will naturally be Yu Boming. Once someone learns to send telegrams, no matter who they are, they will possess a core competitiveness in this Great Yan Dynasty.","As for our side, I'll let Second Sister and Fourth Sister learn first. As for the others, we'll talk about it later.\"","The loyalty of these two could be trusted. When it came to her own people, she couldn't help but want to give them a bit more of a boost.","Moreover, with this skill, they would have more choices for their future.","Sitting together, Yu Ningxuan and Yu Ningxin held each other's hands tightly beneath their sleeves.","Seventh Sister truly treated the two of them best. In the entire Great Yan Dynasty, only the three of them had such a rare opportunity.","If it weren't for the inappropriate setting, the two sisters would have definitely hugged each other and cried.","They managed to hold back their tears, but Yu Boming couldn't. His eyes welled up, and tears were on the verge of falling.","Yu Shuchun glanced at his son, terrified he would give the game away. He glared at him and scolded, Did I say something wrong? How dare you cry!","Military training is important, but you cannot neglect your studies.","You must memorize the military strategy book your sister gave you backward and forward, and fully master it. If you dare to slack off...","Yu Shuchun raised his fist, which was as big as a sandbag, and waved it in front of his son.","Although he was a civil official, he had the best martial arts skills among his brothers.","Even his son and daughter, Yu Boming and Yu Ningxuan, were the most physically robust among all the cousins in the family!","Seeing her husband scold their son, Second Aunt Yu felt as sweet as honey in her heart. Although their branch of the family had the fewest children, they had all caught Fuguang's favorable eye. How could she not be happy?","Madam Zhang felt fine about it. Now that Yue Fuguang was her daughter, as long as the children were successful, they could help their Fuguang more in the future.","In her eyes, Fuguang was a natural-born noble who should only need to move her lips while others ran their legs off for her.","Meanwhile, Fourth Aunt Yu, Madam Bao, looked at the flushed faces of the sisters, Yu Ningxuan and Yu Ningxin, feeling a surge of envy.","The two were Fuguang's older sisters and also her study companions; their bond was naturally deeper than the rest of the family's.","Nowadays, even the three brothers from the first branch couldn't compare to the affection between these two sisters and Fuguang.","Looking at her own daughter, she could only sigh inwardly.","Seeing Yu Boming scolded by his father so harshly that he couldn't even lift his head, his tears naturally went patter-patter down his face.","Yue Fuguang found it highly amusing, though her second brother's crying face was indeed a bit ugly!","In a rare moment of kindness, she bailed him out, saying, Grandfather, Father, Uncles, Fuguang has an item here called a radio transmitter.","It has the ability to transmit messages across thousands of miles.","This book has been selected by the platform to be adapted into a short drama. Dear readers, please look forward to it!","Dear friends, please urge for updates, urge for updates, urge for updates! Important things must be said three times! Clasps hands in gratitude!"]},{"number":258,"title":"Chapter 258: Radio, Bridging Thousands of Miles","paragraphs":["\"Transmitting messages over thousands of miles... Fuguang, are you sure such a miraculous thing exists in this world?\"","Yu Zhongchun could finally express his astonishment openly and could not help but ask a few more questions. \"This thing...\"","\"Was this thing also given by Fuguang's maritime merchant friend?\"","Yu Chongshan pushed his eldest son aside and took over the conversation to cover for his granddaughter.","\"Grandfather guessed correctly. When my friend delivered the high-quality seeds last time, they also included some other items, among which was this radio station capable of transmitting messages over thousands of miles.\"","\"Fuguang, do you have enough silver with you?\"","Old Madam Yu's focus was clearly different from the men in the family.","\"Rest assured, Grandmother, I have plenty. If I ever run out, I will just take a stroll through His Majesty's private treasury,\" Yue Fuguang joked with the elderly woman.","Yesterday, she saw that the chests filled with gold cakes in the private treasury remained untouched, as she herself did not lack such things.","Although she had not yet received her salary as the Junior Preceptor, items were sent from the palace every few days, so she couldn't be bothered to worry about her wages.","Old Madam Yu smiled and said, \"Our family also has a storehouse. Someday, let your mother and the others take you to see it. There is also Grandmother's personal private vault; you can visit whenever you have free time.\"","Hearing his wife say this, Yu Chongshan could not hold back and blurted out, \"Grandfather has one too. When I have time, I'll take Fuguang to see it.\"","After speaking, he cautiously glanced at Old Madam Yu, but she did not even spare him a look.","The old fool actually thought she did not know he had a secret little treasury behind her back. In the past, she was just too lazy to manage it.","Now, she would interfere even less. The best things would always reach her granddaughter's hands first; only what her granddaughter did not want would fall to others.","Yue Fuguang smiled and replied, \"Then Fuguang will not stand on ceremony with you elders!\"","Seeing her agree so readily without any polite refusal, the crowd realized she did not treat them as outsiders, and they were all overjoyed.","Yu Chongshan waved his hand, interrupting the sons and daughters-in-law who wanted to join the fun.","\"Fuguang, let us grandfather and granddaughter return to the topic of this radio station. A device that can transmit messages over thousands of miles is a priceless treasure. How do you plan to use it?\"","\"Grandfather, I was thinking that since Second Brother is taking people to the Sancha region at the end of May, and the two places are separated by thousands of miles, communication will be inconvenient. So, I thought about letting him take one radio station, and we will keep one at our manor. This way, the two places can communicate constantly, and I can keep abreast of the situation over there in real time.\"","Yu Chongshan nodded heavily. \"That is excellent.\"","The whole family unanimously forgot to consider whether such an important instrument of the state should be reported to His Majesty first.","It had to be said that Yue Fuguang's strength gave the family courage and confidence. They never thought of usurping the throne.","However, when it came to items brought out by Yue Fuguang, the whole family tacitly agreed that their use and disposal were entirely up to her arrangements.","As for whether to inform His Majesty, they would certainly say they would, but that was merely lip service.","Yu Shuchun interjected and asked, \"Fuguang, what does this radio station look like, and how is it operated?\"","A father knows his own son best. Even with a father's biased filter, he had to admit that his son was indeed not as clever and dexterous as his niece.","It would be best to learn it in advance; otherwise, if that boy messed it up, he would be too ashamed to face his niece.","Little Zhu, place two radio stations on the bottom shelf of the bookcase in my study.","After instructing the system, Yue Fuguang turned to Cuizhu behind her and said, \"Cuizhu, go to my study and fetch the radio stations. They are on the bottom shelf of the bookcase. Bring both of the green iron boxes.\"","While waiting, Yue Fuguang pretended to reach into her wide sleeves, but in reality, she took out two small booklets from her storage ring.","She handed them to Yu Chongshan and said, \"Grandfather, these are the operation manuals for the radio station. I have never operated one either. Therefore, Second Brother and the others will need to memorize it themselves and practice sending messages daily. Transmitting messages with a radio station is not just a technical task; it is a craft. It requires the operator to have an extremely high level of proficiency to transmit and receive codes steadily, accurately, and quickly.\"","Yu Chongshan handed a copy to Yu Shuchun. \"Second Son Yu, you take a look first. Once you understand it, then teach it to Xiao Er.\"","Compared to his grandson, he trusted his son more. It was safer for the father to learn it first and then teach the son.","Yu Shuchun accepted it with both hands and began to study it seriously with a solemn expression.","Yue Fuguang glanced over and saw that the manual was written in great detail, even listing out radio maintenance and how to complete daily training.","The Radio Operation Manual could entirely be renamed Step-by-Step Guide to Telegraph Transmission, Reception, and Maintenance.","Seeing the Morse code inside, Yu Chongshan could not help but think a bit further. This thing could definitely be used elsewhere too.","Thus, he could not resist asking, \"Fuguang, the Morse code in here...\"","\"If Grandfather finds it useful, please feel free to take it.\"","In the future, she would also train an intelligence team that belonged entirely to her, so there was no harm in letting the Emperor and the others test the waters with this first.","Soon, Cuizhu and Shen Chunying came in, each carrying a box.","Placing the items on the desk, Yue Fuguang opened the lids of the iron boxes and took out the contents one by one.","She placed one in front of Yu Boming and the other in front of the sisters, Yu Ningxuan and Yu Ningxin.","\"Grandfather, a radio station requires both a sender and a receiver. The transmission at Sancha will be handled by Second Brother personally. As for the one here in our estate, we'll have my two older sisters operate it for now.\"","Yu Chongshan nodded. \"We will do as Fuguang says.\"","He then turned to his three grandchildren and said, \"Keep your younger sister's instructions in mind. Learn well and do your best.\"","\"Furthermore,\" he said with a stern expression, \"without Fuguang's permission, none of you are to speak a word about the radio's operation to outsiders. Not even to our own family members.\"","As for the gratitude owed for this guidance, he didn't need to say it. Looking at the children's expressions, he knew they understood how rare this opportunity was and would naturally keep it in their hearts.","Next, Yu Chongshan led Old Yu, Second Son Yu, Yu Boming, and the sisters, Yu Ningxuan and her sibling, to begin assembling and disassembling the equipment according to the instruction manual.","By dinnertime, Yue Fuguang, who had already taken a short nap, saw that although they were all covered in exhaustion, their eyes shone brightly.","Like children who had just found their favorite toy.","Over the next few days, Yu Boming, who was originally supposed to return to the military camp, specifically requested a leave of absence to stay at the estate and learn how to use the radio.","The news that the radio could transmit messages across thousands of miles quickly spread among the important ministers of the Great Yan court.","Huo Ying and Wei Shouyi rushed to the Yu estate right after the morning assembly the very next day.","When they saw the small radio and its seemingly precise components with their own eyes, they were all extremely envious.","Their eyes were practically glued to the radio. The sight of them rubbing their large, fan-like hands together, wanting to touch it but not daring to, was quite amusing.","In any case, the carefree Yu Boming couldn't hold back his laughter.","As a result, his head suffered the consequences. Minister Cai and General Wei didn't dare casually touch the precious radio.","But wouldn't they dare to touch this kid's head?","This kid's good fortune made their eyes red with envy and jealousy. By rubbing his head a few more times, perhaps they could really rub off some of his luck.","The Minister of Works, Lu Qi, who had also seen the radio, was currently standing in the Imperial Study feeling thoroughly uncomfortable.","When His Majesty asked if he could build one, he shook his head so hard he nearly made himself dizzy.","Lu Qi grumbled inwardly that if His Majesty wanted his head, he should just say so directly. Why use this to make things difficult for him!","Let alone not understanding the principles behind that thing, they didn't even know what materials many of the components were made of."]},{"number":259,"title":"Chapter 259: What do you think if I grant you the Yu family's second daughter as your side consort","paragraphs":["\"Your Majesty, some components on the radio are neither gold nor silver, neither stone nor wood. Frankly speaking, in my humble opinion, they are simply not items from our world.\"","Things of the immortals—you want to build them? You must be dreaming!","Emperor Mingxi held the Morse code that Yu Chongshan had copied for him, and then looked at Lu Qi's expression, which practically screamed that he couldn't replicate it even if his life depended on it.","Unwillingly, he waved his hand, dismissing him for now.","He then turned to the Crown Prince, who was standing to the side watching, and said, \"Crown Prince, what do you think if I take the second young lady of the Yu family as your side consort?","Fuguang has quite a good relationship with the Yu sisters, and this time she even chose her two older sisters to be those so-called telegraph operators.","With this exclusive technology...\"","Hearing his imperial father suggest he take Yu Ningxuan as a side consort, Xie Zhiyan felt his head was about to explode. He didn't hear a single word of what was said next.","With an incredibly strong desire to survive, he blurted out, \"Imperial Father, your son does not wish to.\"","If he didn't know his current imperial father reasonably well, Xie Zhiyan wouldn't be able to help but form a conspiracy theory: was his father trying to use the Junior Preceptor's hands to get him killed?!","Taking Yu Ningxuan as a side consort—even if he were to ascend the throne and become the emperor right now, without the Junior Preceptor giving the word, he wouldn't dare entertain the thought.","A Crown Prince's side consort, an Emperor's noble consort—aren't they still concubines in the end?","Making the Junior Preceptor, the Little Immortal Lord's sister a concubine... where did his imperial father get the audacity? If he wanted to recklessly court death, he didn't need to drag his own son down with him!","He was still young; he hadn't lived enough!","Could his imperial father's recent reckless, death-courting behavior be because the national treasury was full, making him overly arrogant?","Setting aside whether it would even succeed, once this idea reached the ears of the Junior Preceptor...","Xie Zhiyan felt even worse right now than Lu Qi, who had just left. He constantly felt that he might lose some vital body parts because of his father's bold idea.","He couldn't help but step closer, lowering his voice. \"Imperial Father, once this idea of yours is known by the Junior Preceptor, your son...\"","He looked at Emperor Mingxi with a bitter expression: I won't say it aloud, but you can imagine it yourself!","After Emperor Mingxi \"imagined\" it, a layer of cold sweat broke out over his body. Knowing he had misspoken, he let out a light cough.","Forcefully trying to save face, he said, \"Where is the Crown Prince's mind wandering to? What your father meant is, as long as you can make the Yu family's young lady develop feelings for you.","No matter who she is, I can make the decision to take her as your side consort.\"","He patted the Crown Prince's shoulder and added, \"My imperial son is as elegant as an orchid and a jade tree, handsome and dashing—exactly the type of appearance young ladies adore.","If you put your mind to charming a few young girls, it shouldn't be difficult.\"","Xie Zhiyan: You dare to say it, but your son dares not listen.","Asking me to seduce the Yu family's young lady... once the Junior Preceptor finds out, not only will my legs be broken, but it's hard to say if I'll even remain a man.","He hadn't forgotten the signature skills of those two ancestors. Their craftsmanship was much swifter and cleaner than Eunuch Qian's!","At this moment, Xie Zhiyan felt it was absolutely necessary to inform his imperial grandmother, so she could knock some sense into his imperial father's head and remind him who was truly in charge.","No one knows exactly what Xie Zhiyan told the Empress Dowager, but regardless, the emperor was summoned to her palace. When he emerged, even if he wasn't completely humiliated, his expression was utterly dejected.","The Crown Prince knew that by tattling, he had definitely earned his imperial father's grudge, so he simply avoided going anywhere near him.","He had had enough of reviewing memorials lately anyway, so he took the opportunity to slack off, bringing along The Eighth Sister, who had no classes, to visit the Yu mansion.","The siblings were both incredibly curious about what this radio, which could transmit messages over thousands of miles in real-time, actually looked like.","After the three Yu siblings secluded themselves for three days, they were already able to demonstrate simple messaging to the crowd, such as basic phrases like \"Have you eaten?\"","Witnessing firsthand that two people separated by dozens of miles could communicate flawlessly in real-time, the crowd was once again shocked speechless.","After all, hearing about something and seeing it with one's own eyes were two completely different things.","As they watched the seemingly random ticking sounds quickly convey clear meanings between the operators, they were astounded.","They didn't understand the underlying principles, but that didn't stop them from bestowing it with the title of \"Little Divine Artifact.\"","Following these demonstrations, the radio became the hottest topic among the upper echelons of the Great Yan at the start of the year.","Hearing the radio being crowned with the title of \"Little Divine Artifact,\" the true \"Divine Artifact,\" System 07, was extremely displeased.","[Master, a piece of trash like the radio is only something these ignorant mortals would value.","To actually dare call it a 'Little Divine Artifact'—where does that leave the dignity of a true divine artifact like me?","Isn't it just capable of transmitting messages over thousands of miles?","Can it, like this Realm-Breaking Pearl, cross world barriers to travel to any major or minor thousand worlds? Can it move mountains and drain seas, or summon wind and rain? Can it know everything in the world and remain indestructible for thousands and tens of thousands of years?","It's just the most ordinary mortal item in Little Zhu's natal space; it doesn't even qualify as a spirit artifact or a treasure artifact.","For these people to actually dare call it a 'Little Divine Artifact' is truly turning the world upside down. It's simply outrageous!]","The officials still attending the court session were so terrified by the wrath of the Lord Divine Artifact that they didn't dare lift their heads.","Emperor Mingxi and Eunuch Qian, the master and servant closest to Yue Fuguang, were even more extreme: one sat rigidly upright, while the other lowered his head, intensely focused on counting the floor tiles beneath his feet.","They desperately wanted to clear their names. They had never referred to the radio as a little divine artifact, so this little ancestor absolutely must not take its anger out on them.","Seeing that the system was furiously angry, Yue Fuguang quickly comforted it: \"Little Zhu, don't be angry. Isn't that just because mortals have shallow knowledge and haven't seen truly good things before!\"","\"If they knew we had walkie-talkies that allow instant communication within a hundred miles, or mobile phones that even mortals can use to see and talk to each other from ten thousand miles away, they naturally wouldn't call a mere radio a divine artifact. If they had seen Little Zhu, a true divine artifact, they would naturally understand that the difference between immortals and mortals is like an uncrossable chasm.\"","What walkie-talkies? Mobile phones? What were those? Being able to talk instantly was far more convenient than a radio.","After their initial shock, the crowd began exchanging meaningful glances with their Emperor. Their eyes clearly conveyed their thoughts: Want it! on one side, and Dare not! on the other.","[Hmph! These people really haven't seen anything good. This divine artifact despises them!]","The crowd was so frightened by that cold scoff that their minds instantly cleared. The entire imperial court plunged into an eerie silence. The time spent waiting for someone to step forward and present a memorial was actually no more than a dozen seconds.","But to everyone's senses, it felt as long as several hours.","The heavy breathing of the colleagues standing next to them could be heard with crystal clarity. If they hadn't gone through this, none of them would have known their hearing could be so sharp!","Some who couldn't bear the pressure exchanged glances with one another. 'I never called the radio a little divine artifact.'","'Me neither, at most I called it a big treasure.'","Even more people shrank their necks back; they had indeed been too presumptuous this time!","Seeing the heavy and oppressive atmosphere, Wei Ping closed his eyes, gritted his teeth, and stepped forward. \"Your Majesty, your subject Wei Ping has a memorial to present.\"","\"Beloved Subject Wei, please speak quickly!\" That plea to speak quickly was filled with the joy of immense relief.","To Emperor Mingxi, who was sitting on the dragon throne wanting to shift his posture but not quite daring to, Wei Ping's words were no different from the music of heaven.","It had to be his Beloved Subject Wei; his rescue was incredibly timely!","The crowd also secretly breathed a sigh of relief. The atmosphere just now was much more terrifying than when their Emperor lost his temper.","Even listening to royal scandals hadn't scared them this much.","\"Reporting to Your Majesty, as His Highness the Crown Prince's wedding approaches, thefts and murders have been occurring frequently in the capital. Last night, the City Patrol Department in charge of night patrols even captured three assassins near the Yu Manor.\"","Emperor Mingxi frowned and asked again uncertainly, \"Beloved Subject Wei, where did you just say the assassins were caught?\""]},{"number":260,"title":"Chapter 260: Is your monogamy literally one husband and one wife","paragraphs":["\"Your Majesty, what I'm referring to is the Yu Mansion, the residence of the Junior Grand Tutor!\"","Everyone gasped in shock. It seemed that the thieves were still determined to assassinate the Junior Grand Tutor!","\"Little Zhu, is this aimed at me?\"","[Master, the target is indeed you. You were sleeping soundly last night, so I didn't wake you up.","Anyway, there were just a dozen or so small fries. Without even the need for the City Patrol Department, as long as they got closer to our mansion, Chunying and the others, along with that new guy named Dai Yuxing, could capture them all!]","\"Who is behind this this time?\"","[They are enemy assassins. The night before last, they were from Xiqiang. Those captured last night were from Beili. There was also one from Nanyue hiding in the back. When they saw the Beili people being captured, they sneaked away.]","Shen Kang, who was standing in the crowd, suddenly relaxed his furrowed brows.","So those people he lost track of in Anmin Alley last night were Nanyue assassins. He seemed to know where to find them.","\"Do they want me alive or dead?\"","[The primary goal is, of course, to take you away alive. If they can't get you alive, they'll settle for dead.]","\"Humph, they really have audacious plans!\"","[Indeed, they do! This time, for the Crown Prince's wedding, among the leaders of the various country's missions, the one from Nanzhao is Princess Lan Xuan'er.","The representatives from the other countries have all changed. The one from Beili this time is Bei Yue's younger brother, Bei Ye. The one from Nanyue is the Second Princess, Gan Tang.","As for the one from Xiqiang, it's the newly - enfeoffed Prince Yi, Xi Yuanshan, who is the \"adopted son\" of Xi Yan.]","\"Among the Jiang, Tian, and Feng families, the power struggle is over? It seems that Feng Xu took on the other three families alone and won?\"","[That's right. In terms of intelligence and strategy, even if you combined the other three, they wouldn't be a match for Feng Xu.","However, in order to win over the Tian family, the three families conspired and changed their story. In the end, not only did Xi Yan recognize Jiang Yuanshan, but he also didn't suspect Xi Ling's identity.]","\"Why does Jiang Yuanshan still have the status of an adopted son after changing his surname to Xi?\"","[This is the result of the power struggle in Xiqiang. Although everyone knows that he is the lost son of Emperor Xi Yan in the folk.","But the royal family, especially the princes, don't want another brother competing with them for the throne. So, under pressure.","Xi Yan had no choice but to adopt Jiang Yuanshan as his adopted son and enfeoff him as Prince Yi. Now, his status is somewhat marginalized from the line of succession.","Moreover, he has another identity, that is, the husband of Princess Pingning, Xie Zhiyao, and the son - in - law of the royal family of the Xie clan in Dayan.]","\"Wasn't Xie Zhiyao's fiancé the Fourth Prince, Xi Xiang?\"","[At the recognition banquet, Prince Yi got drunk and \"accidentally\" went into the wrong room, where he happened to see Princess Pingning of Dayan changing clothes.","As a result, the groom was changed from the Fourth Prince to Prince Yi, Xi Yuanshan.]","\"Were these two people set up?\"","[They were indeed set up, but one of them took advantage of the situation and turned the tables. We'll talk about this juicy story another day.","Now, let's talk about yesterday's assassination attempt on you.]","Wei Ping, Cai Xian, and Feng Tang couldn't help but prick up their ears. They caught some people last night and each of them took one to interrogate separately.","Those three were very stubborn. Even after being tortured, they didn't say a single word.","The one Feng Tang interrogated was even more stubborn. He pretended to talk. After the soldier removed the wooden plug from his mouth, he bit his own tongue and almost died.","So, Feng Tang had been in a bad mood since last night, and his brows had never relaxed.","Bang! Emperor Mingxi slapped the imperial desk and angrily said, \"These scoundrels dare to have designs on our country's Junior Grand Tutor. They are simply audacious and unreasonable!\"","\"Wei Ping, have you found out who is behind this?\"","\"Your Majesty, I'm incompetent. I, along with Lord Cai and Lord Feng, interrogated those three villains all night, but they still haven't said a single word.\"","Cai Xian also stepped forward and bowed, saying, \"Your Majesty, I've sent people to intensify the search. We will definitely find the whereabouts of those dozen or so who escaped.\"","[Those people have already left the city and are now hiding in an abandoned temple in Lotus Mountain. These fools are searching in the city. How can they find anyone!]","\"Little Zhu, who ordered these people? Is it the Fifth Prince, Bei Ye?\"","[You guessed right, Master. It was indeed ordered by Bei Ye. Moreover, these people are not the same group as the Beili people who attempted to assassinate you last time.","The master of those previous ones was Emperor Bei Ji of Beili, while those last night were Bei Ye's private soldiers. Some of them had been lurking in Dayan for many years.","Some came to Dayan following the mission, pretending to be merchants.]","\"I've never met this Bei Ye, and we have no grudges. Why is he so eager to take my life?\"","[Of course, it's for the throne of Beili.","Master, you don't know, but you are an important bargaining chip in the eyes of the heirs of various countries.","Whether they capture or kill you, it's a great achievement.","Humph, daring to use you as a stepping - stone, I think they are looking for death!]","\"They really don't know what's good for them. Little Zhu, do you know anything about this Bei Ye?\"","[Master, there's a big juicy story about Bei Ye. Do you want to hear it? I think killing him is too easy on him.","Since he wants the throne, let's make it out of his reach.","Before killing him, we'll break his spirit and then destroy his body to vent my anger.]","\"What big juicy story? Tell me.\"","Everyone was scared by the master and the divine artifact's words about breaking the enemy's spirit before killing them, but they also felt speechless.","These two ancestors, when someone is trying to kill you, you still have the mood to hear juicy stories!","By the way, what juicy story does Bei Ye have that the divine artifact calls it a big one?","Is it more explosive than the story about his brother, Bei Yue?","I have to hear it!","At this time, the court of Dayan was divided into two factions. One faction was intimidated by the emperor's anger and looked dejected, while the other faction seemed dejected but actually had their ears pricked up.","[Master, I don't know if it's a genetic trait of the Beili royal family, but in matters of love, they are a bit indiscriminate.","Among the royal family members, there are those like Bei Yue who only love men, and there are also those like Bei Ye who like both men and women.]","\"What? You mean that Bei Yue's ancestors had this kind of preference? Is the current Emperor Bei Ji the same?\"","[Yes, there's also a juicy story about Bei Ji, but we won't talk about his today. Let's talk about the Fifth Prince, Bei Ye.]","\"Okay, go ahead!\"","Emperor Mingxi thought: Why are there such improper people among my fellow emperors?","It's one thing for the Nanzhao emperor to have different genders in his relationships, but why does the Beili emperor have such different preferences!","[This Bei Ye is not as single - minded as his brother, Bei Yue, who only loves men. He is a firm supporter of the one - husband - one - wife system.]","\"Little Zhu, do you mean the literal one - husband - one - wife?\"","[Master, that's exactly what it means. Bei Ye wants to have a family of three, with both a wife and a husband.","His current wife is Qi Xia, the daughter of the General of the Eastern Army of Beili. General Qi commands 100,000 troops of the Eastern Army of Beili.","His former boyfriend, Wei Qingyi, is the eldest son of Prime Minister Wei of Beili.","Their relationship broke up because Bei Ye wanted to marry the daughter of General Qi, who has military power.","This Wei Qingyi was so heartbroken that he fell seriously ill and was in a state of depression for a long time.]"]},{"number":261,"title":"Chapter 261: Beiye: The Other Woman Who Meddled in Others' Relationship","paragraphs":["\"So it seems Wei Qingyi is deeply in love with Bei Ye. For him to do that for military power is a bit underhanded!\"","[Master, if you think about it carefully, Bei Ye is actually the third party who intervened in someone else's relationship.]","\"How so? Did Wei Qingyi have another boyfriend before Bei Ye?\"","[Not exactly. Before meeting Bei Ye, Wei Qingyi was already married to Jiang Li, the daughter of Chancellor Wei's former classmate, to whom he was betrothed since childhood.","As the eldest son of Chancellor Wei, Wei Qingyi met the Fifth Prince, Bei Ye, during a royal autumn hunt.","At that time, Bei Ye was not yet sixteen, with red lips and white teeth. You could say Wei Qingyi fell in love at first sight and offered himself at the second.]","\"Uh... was he in that much of a rush? Isn't that developing a bit too fast?\"","[Fast? It's alright. At least compared to Xi Yuanshan's parents, it was a step slower.","This Bei Ye truly lives up to being born of the same father as Bei Yue; both brothers are experts at opening doors to new worlds for other men.","Before meeting Bei Ye, Wei Qingyi was known in Beili as a pure-hearted, modest gentleman with few desires.","He treated his wife with mutual respect and threw himself into his career, so much so that they had no children after three years of marriage.","He wasn't uninterested in women because he wasn't lustful; it was just that his lust was aimed at the wrong gender.","The moment he met Bei Ye, it was like dry wood meeting a blazing fire. Wei Qingyi, an old house that wasn't quite old yet, caught on fire.]","\"So Wei Qingyi likes men. Isn't his wife pitiful, then!\"","[It's more than that. Not only does Wei Qingyi like men, but he is also infertile, which is why they didn't have children after years of marriage.","The Wei family thought it was Jiang Li's fault, so she had to drink all sorts of bitter tonics every day.","Later, Bei Ye got drunk and slept with a palace maid, who gave birth to his son ten months later.","Wei Qingyi was furious when he found out. To appease him, Bei Ye gave the son to Wei Qingyi to raise.","They registered the child under the 'infertile' Jiang Li's name as the legitimate son.","And they falsely claimed the child was born to Wei Qingyi and another woman outside.]","\"What kind of logic is that? Wasn't Bei Ye afraid that Wei Qingyi would kill the child out of anger and humiliation?","Besides, the child looks nothing like Wei Qingyi. Wouldn't Chancellor Wei be suspicious?","Would Bei Ji not know his grandson was given away? Are those two blind?\"","[Bei Ye had already established his own estate outside. At that time, Bei Ji was lacking energy and paid little attention to this son, so he truly didn't know he had a grandson who was given away.","As for Chancellor Wei, that old fox naturally noticed the clues and investigated thoroughly. However, after investigating, he chose to tacitly accept it.]","\"Why? Was he afraid of the authority of the Beili royal family?\"","Hearing such explosive gossip, the monarch and officials of Dayan all wore expressions of eager curiosity, but they did not agree with the Junior Preceptor's words.","One's own bloodline could not be mixed up. If it were them, they would either tell the Emperor the truth or raise the child as a concubine's son.","They would never raise him as a future heir.","[That is because Chancellor Wei discovered that this child was actually of his Wei family's bloodline. Since the child carried his blood.","Returning to the Wei family in this capacity wasn't unacceptable.","Moreover, having guessed that the lack of children after years of marriage was not the daughter-in-law Jiang Li's fault, but rather his eldest son's infertility, Chancellor Wei was actually happy to see this happen.]","\"How does this involve the Wei family's bloodline again? Could it be that Bei Ye is Chancellor Wei's illegitimate son and Wei Qingyi's biological brother?","Little Zhu, is this gossip a forbidden one?\"","Everyone: Could you please not gloat so much? If you don't wipe that amused smile off your face.","Lord Liu, who is currently reporting, will think you are targeting him!","Yue Fuguang didn't care if others would overthink it. Right now, she just wanted to watch the drama unfold, no matter how chaotic it got.","In layman's terms, she was enjoying the gossip so much she didn't care about anyone else's misery.","Lord Liu, who couldn't hear any of this, was completely unable to ignore the smile hanging on the Junior Preceptor's face.","He wiped the sweat from his forehead and continued to report on the matters concerning the diplomatic missions from various countries.","His superior, Lord You Mingmin, seeing his subordinate sweating, felt helpless. What else could they do? Just endure it!","[Master, where is your mind going! Bei Ye is Bei Ji's biological son; he has absolutely nothing to do with Chancellor Wei.","The issue lies with the palace maid that Bei Ye slept with.","Why did a drunk Bei Ye sleep with that maid? Because her eyes and brows looked extremely similar to Wei Qingyi's, and she was considered quite a beauty among mortals.","And Wei Qingyi inherited his features from Chancellor Wei.]","\"So, this palace maid that Bei Ye favored is actually Chancellor Wei's daughter?\"","[Master guessed correctly. The palace maid's mother was the daughter of an offending official. As a young girl, she was sent to the Jiaofang Department and became a dancer.","When Chancellor Wei was young and not yet chancellor, he slept with that dancer during a palace night banquet. Actually, Chancellor Wei quite liked that dancer at the time.","He even tried to ask Bei Ji for her, but Bei Ji refused him with various excuses, and he failed to get her several times.","Later, he heard that the dancer had died, so he gave up on the idea.","Because of the affair between Bei Ye and Wei Qingyi, upon careful investigation, he discovered that the palace maid Bei Ye had casually favored was actually the daughter born to that dancer who died in childbirth—his own daughter.","Therefore, this child was his grandson. Naturally, he didn't mind raising the child under the name of his eldest son, who was suspected of being infertile, and bringing him up as the legitimate eldest grandson.]","\"Do Wei Qingyi and Bei Ye know all of this? A son turning into a nephew—he didn't lay a hand on that child, did he?\"","[At first, he indeed harbored ill intentions. But later, the father and son had a secret talk behind closed doors, and it is unknown what was said.","Wei Qingyi's attitude towards the child changed, and ever since Bei Ye sent the child away, he never asked about him again.","It was as if such a child had never existed.]","\"Then what happened to Chancellor Wei's daughter, the mother of the child?\"","[Chancellor Wei brought her out of the palace, and she entered the Wei family under the identity of the child's wet nurse.]","\"When all is said and done, the most pitiful ones in this whole mess are Jiang Li and Qi Xia, who are completely in the dark.\"","[The two of them are unfortunate, yet also fortunate. The misfortune is that they married these two bastards; the fortune is that neither of them currently has children.","Even if they divorce and return home, they won't have any burdens tying them down.","Master, this Wei Qingyi controls some of Bei Ye's hidden agents. He was the main mastermind behind last night's assassination.]","\"Are you saying that this Wei Qingyi has also come to Great Yan, and the two of them have hooked up again?\"","Yue Fuguang stroked her smooth, little chin. Bei Ye really managed to live this monogamous life!","That simply wouldn't do. Yue Fuguang considered herself to be a petty person; if someone wanted to capture and kill her, unless she had to temporarily endure it for a system quest, she wouldn't be able to swallow her anger without striking back.","However, if she killed the two of them right now, putting aside the diplomatic relations between the two countries, the loss of this competing faction in Northern Li would only benefit the Northern Li Emperor and those princes.","It would be best for her rivals to beat each other's brains out over the throne, constantly depleting their own strength. That would be the most advantageous outcome for her future unification of the lands."]},{"number":262,"title":"Chapter 262: Does the Master Want to Catch an Adulterer","paragraphs":["\"System, remember to leave a hidden mark on those two so we can claim their lives at any time.\"","\"Don't worry, Host. If you want them dead at the third watch, I definitely won't let them live to the fifth.\"","You Mingmin nodded to Emperor Mingxi.","In the Northern Li diplomatic delegation, there was indeed a young man named Wei Qingyi, the second-in-command of the envoy.","He had seen him more than once; this person had an extremely good relationship with the Fifth Prince, Bei Ye, perhaps even a bit too intimate, unlike what should exist between a lord and a subject.","Now, hearing what Lord Divine Artifact said, he suddenly realized that these two were actually a couple!","Is the bloodline of the Northern Li royal family poisoned? One after another, they bring their lovers when visiting foreign states. What do they take our Great Yan for?","Yue Fuguang: Naturally, as a part of their roleplay!","\"Yes, they even sleep together at night. As for their reconciliation, their old flames rekindled on the way to Great Yan.","Originally, the one sent as the envoy this time was Bei Yue. He also wanted to take the opportunity to search for Chonghua's whereabouts in Great Yan.","However, Bei Ye interfered and persuaded Bei Ji to temporarily replace him.","Chancellor Wei and his son Wei Qingyi were afraid that Bei Yue would make a move against Bei Ye on the road, so they sent Wei Qingyi along, firstly for protection, and secondly for Great Yan's potatoes and you.\"","\"Sleeping together is great! It makes it perfectly convenient for us to help these lovers tear off their fig leaf and let the whole world see!\"","\"Master, do you want to catch them in the act?\"","\"We definitely need to catch them in the act, but I won't be the one doing it. Among the over a hundred people in the Northern Li envoy delegation, there must be many hidden spies from various factions mixed in.","Moreover, the envoy delegations from several other countries are staying right next door. As long as we leak a little information, there will be plenty of people wanting to see the Northern Li royal family make a fool of themselves!\"","You Mingmin nodded; he understood the Junior Preceptor's plan. Borrowing a knife to kill someone, Great Yan would just stand on the shore and watch the show, remaining completely uninvolved.","\"Master, I'll go spread the news right away!\"","\"Little Zhu, remember to take pictures of their disgraceful state. When the time comes, expend a bit of your divine power to print out some extra copies of their photos.","It would be best if they could reach the Jiang and Xia families of Northern Li, and then we'll see how those two families choose to react.\"","Once again, she was thankful to her past self for even hoarding a color printer.","Everyone felt confused, wondering what a \"photo\" was, but judging by the tone of these two ancestors, they would probably find out very soon.","And indeed, it was very soon. Who knows whose efficiency was this high?","The system spread the news in the morning, the conspiracy was completed in the afternoon, and the two completely naked people engaged in intense combat were caught in bed by a crowd of people at night.","The system, having used some drugs and taken the photos, accomplished its task... but didn't retreat.","How could it miss out on eating melons in the front row? After reaching level four, the system even had a video live-streaming function.","Sitting at home, Yue Fuguang was also able to eat the hot melon broadcasted by the system.","One could only say the scene was quite stimulating. Fortunately, the system wouldn't ban the broadcast just because she was still technically a \"minor.\"","The most stimulating part was at the final climax, when the two were surrounded and watched by dozens of people who rushed in. Those who couldn't squeeze in even climbed onto the roof and removed the tiles.","Looking down from a high vantage point, with that angle and a sea of white flesh, Yue Fuguang actually saw someone getting a nosebleed. It was just absurd!","Being watched by so many people while doing the deed, Wei Qingyi lost his erection on the spot.","Pinned beneath him, Bei Ye was so ashamed that he covered his face with one hand and his round, perky buttocks with the other.","Yue Fuguang couldn't help but nod; those buttocks were indeed top-tier. No wonder someone got a nosebleed from looking.","However, Lan Xuan'er's personal \"maid,\" wasn't your nosebleed a bit too fierce?","Also blessed with eye candy were some people in the capital of Great Yan.","Early in the morning, people found a \"painting\" in various locations. Some smart ones guessed that this was the photo the Junior Preceptor had mentioned.","Many people were so startled when they first saw this painting that they almost dropped it. Wasn't this thing called a photo a bit too realistic?","The two people in the picture looked so real that they thought Bei Ye and Wei Qingyi had been trapped inside the painting.","Some people's attention was not on the image, but on the paper.","Yue Fuguang didn't use traditional photo paper, but high-quality A4 paper weighing over a hundred grams. The front was smooth, the back had a fine and dense texture, and the color was snow-white.","This was something Great Yan's current papermaking technology couldn't achieve at all.","Emperor Mingxi and several key ministers looked at the photo in front of them in silence.","Leaving aside this uncanny so-called \"photography,\" which looked exactly like real people.","Just this paper alone was something they could only look up to in despair.","Emperor Mingxi wrote some large characters on the back of a few sheets of paper. Whether it was ink absorption or ink retention, it was exceptionally good.","\"Your Majesty, from what this subject can see, this paper is very similar to the blueprint of the mountain villa that the Junior Preceptor brought out previously.\"","It was just that one was larger and the other smaller, but both were as white as snow. They now referred to this paper as snowflake paper.","Minister of Works Lu Qi was the first to break the silence. Papermaking was originally jointly managed by his Ministry of Works and the papermaking workshops.","\"My beloved ministers, do you still remember what those two said when the Junior Preceptor first enrolled and you accompanied me to the Hongwen Pavilion?\"","\"Is Your Majesty referring to the papermaking and printing techniques?\"","Chancellor of the National Academy Ling Yinghua was the first to point it out. He had always kept this matter in his heart.","He had thought the Emperor would keep it suppressed and unmentioned, never expecting that seeing this photo today would bring up the old matter.","\"Your Majesty, Fuguang has acted a few times and has already become a thorn in the side of certain factions. If those prominent aristocratic families find out that she holds the printing and papermaking techniques...\"","Yu Chongshan, who had guessed the Emperor's intentions, had to remind Emperor Mingxi. The internal affairs of the families had not been cleaned up yet; rashly bringing out this item would invite disaster for his granddaughter.","\"I am aware of all your concerns, Minister Yu.\"","He looked at the worried Yu Chongshan and said, \"I naturally would not put Fuguang in danger for the sake of those things.","In my heart, she is much more precious than those technologies.\"","Yu Chongshan quickly bowed and said, \"This subject thanks Your Majesty for your high regard.\"","Yu Chongshan's reply was very measured. He only expressed gratitude on his own behalf and absolutely would not represent Yue Fuguang, because that child owed nothing to Great Yan.","It was only right for the Emperor to consider things for her.","\"It's just that to hide Fuguang's contributions in this...\"","Feng Tang stepped forward and said, \"Your Majesty, the inventor of this technique can be left unmentioned for now. What we need right now is someone to present this technique.","The person who presents it is not necessarily the creator. We can just announce the Junior Preceptor's contributions when the time is right.\"","He absolutely would not allow anyone to steal the Junior Preceptor's credit.","Although Great Yan currently had papermaking and printing techniques, judging from what those two meant, the techniques in their hands were superior to Great Yan's current technology.","They could even bring down the exorbitant prices. This would undoubtedly be a massive contribution to scholars, especially those from poor families.","Its influence among scholars would be immense, so this merit had to fall on the Junior Preceptor.","Everyone understood; what they needed to do now was choose a suitable scapegoat.","Their status had to be high enough to continuously draw fire.","The crowd couldn't help but look at Emperor Mingxi, waiting for him to make a decision.","Emperor Mingxi coughed lightly, paused, and finally voiced the candidate he had decided on early on."]},{"number":263,"title":"Chapter 263: Papermaking and Movable Type Printing","paragraphs":["\"My beloved subjects, what do you think of the Ninth Prince?\"","Hearing that His Majesty had chosen this person, everyone was taken aback for a moment before quickly chiming in with their agreement.","\"Your Majesty, I believe the Ninth Prince is highly suitable.\"","\"I second that!\"","\"I second that!\"","Good heavens, a bunch of old officials instantly sold out the Ninth Prince without a second thought.","They had previously been speculating why, even though Zhou Yunxin and Chonghua were both dead, His Majesty had kept this formerly most favored prince around without punishing him.","They thought His Majesty still harbored some lingering father-son affection, never expecting that he had been kept all along to be the perfect scapegoat.","The Crown Prince's eyes flickered. His father intended to squeeze the last bit of value out of Little Nine before sending him to his death.","In that case, his own men could withdraw.","\"Father, how do you plan to have Ninth Brother reasonably present these things, and as for the Junior Preceptor...\"","No matter how well they planned, if Yue Fuguang did not hand over the technology, finding a few scapegoats would be useless.","\"As for Fuguang, I will have to trouble my beloved subject Yu...\"","Yu Chongshan bowed and said, \"I will do my best.\"","As to whether he would exert one ounce of effort or two, that would be left entirely to fate!","\"Once we obtain those two technologies, I believe the best opportunity will be your wedding. A younger brother presenting his elder brother with a wedding gift—it makes sense for it to be something precious.\"","If it could not be done in time for the Crown Prince's wedding, they would just have to wait for the Empress's birthday.","Everyone felt that aside from the timeline being a bit rushed, there was absolutely nothing wrong with the plan.","The Crown Prince said, \"Father, wouldn't it seem a bit thin if it's just Ninth Brother alone?\"","Emperor Mingxi paused, unable to help but ask, \"Do you have other ideas, Crown Prince?\"","\"Father, I believe it would be better for Fourth Brother and Ninth Brother to shoulder this together. When the news spreads outside, it can be kept somewhat vague.","This way, those noble families will naturally investigate, which can confuse the public for a while and buy us time to produce the finished products.","Because the specifics of who it was will be blurred, when we later announce the true inventor, the Junior Preceptor, we will have a plausible explanation.\"","As long as the royal family stepped forward to endorse it, they could simply overturn the previous 'rumors'.","The kind-hearted Junior Preceptor gifted this rare technology to the two princes who were searching everywhere for a fine item to present as a wedding gift to their elder brother.","This story made perfect sense.","As for the two younger brothers who had to bear the reputation, they only needed to learn to keep their mouths shut.","Suddenly hearing the Fourth Prince mentioned, everyone present was momentarily stunned, their hearts filled with the same complex emotions as when the Ninth Prince was brought up just moments ago.","Strictly speaking, although this man was His Majesty's own flesh and blood, he could also be considered an important chess piece placed in Great Yan by Gan Sheng.","This person was also grounded and had not appeared in public for a long time. They had almost forgotten about this individual, who had been deemed a menace by those two ancestors.","Ever since Emperor Mingxi learned about Concubine Wan and Yue Ying, he had merely surrounded them without taking action in order to placate Gan Sheng.","Using the excuse of Old Four, Xie Zhiwei, offending the Junior Preceptor, he grounded Concubine Wan and the entire Xinrong Palace.","Now that the Crown Prince suggested letting Old Four share this massive scapegoat duty, he merely glanced at his increasingly mature eldest son and nodded in agreement.","Using the hands of the noble families to probe exactly how many people Gan Sheng had left by Old Four's side was indeed a good opportunity.","Otherwise, with only Old Nine bearing the brunt alone, he might not truly be able to withstand the backlash from the noble families.","\"Grandfather seems to really like this kind of paper?\"","The photos in front of Yue Fuguang were not entirely inappropriate for children.","The whole family gathered in Old Madam Yu's courtyard to talk, and the topic quickly shifted to the mysterious drawings that had appeared everywhere that morning.","Because there were juniors present, especially the girls, the adults naturally would not discuss the illicit affair between Bei Ye and Wei Qingyi in too much detail.","So the conversation naturally turned to the painting techniques and the paper.","They guessed who possessed such superb painting skills and speed; the affair was discovered at night, and the drawings were found in the morning.","In Yu Boming's words, how many highly skilled painters would they have had to mobilize to draw so many copies in such a short amount of time?","Yu Chongshan and the others seemed more focused on the paper used for the drawings, which prompted Yue Fuguang's question.","Yu Chongshan smiled kindly, \"Grandfather just thinks this paper is different from the Xuan paper we usually use. Also, these drawings look like they were done by the same person.","It doesn't seem like what Boming and the others said, that many people were involved.\"","\"Grandfather, truthfully speaking, for writing purposes, this paper is still inferior to Xuan paper.","As for the drawings you mentioned, getting thousands of identical copies isn't very difficult; don't printing workshops have the means?\"","\"Although it's not as good for writing as Xuan paper, this paper is truly beautiful. It feels smooth and delicate to the touch; the name 'Snowflake' is well-deserved.\"","Yu Ningxuan and the other girls valued the paper's appearance more, loving all things beautiful.","\"If you want the paper to be whiter, just bleach it. You can also add talcum powder, chalk, or kaolin to the paper pulp, which also has a whitening effect.\"","\"Seventh Sister knows how to make paper too?\" Yu Ningxuan smiled. \"And what is bleaching?\"","\"I've never heard of talcum powder, chalk, or kaolin either,\" Yu Ningxin added.","The two of them asked very naturally; having attended school together, the three had long developed the habit of discussing problems.","Little did they know, their questions played right into the hands of the men in the family.","Yu Chongshan secretly breathed a sigh of relief. He hadn't known how to bring it up, but his three granddaughters had started discussing it on their own.","\"Papermaking isn't very complicated, and the materials are even more common. Can't broken fishing nets, straw, wheat stalks, reeds, bamboo, and tree bark all be used to make paper?","As for talcum powder and such, Grandfather, Father, and Uncles should know what they are.\"","\"So many things can be used to make paper?\"","The others also leaned in to ask. The paper mills in Great Yan used good materials, so the price of paper was relatively high, which was one of the reasons why the cost of studying was so expensive nowadays.","An ordinary family really couldn't afford for their children to use a large amount of paper every day.","\"Grandfather, aside from the books copied by scholars, how are the books in Great Yan printed nowadays?","Woodblock, movable type, or something else?\"","\"Great Yan primarily uses rubbing and woodblock printing. I've never heard of this movable type you mentioned, Fuguang.\"","Yu Zhongchun couldn't help but ask, \"Fuguang, can broken fishing nets, straw, wheat stalks, and reeds really make paper?","And is movable type a new kind of printing technique?\"","Yue Fuguang now wore a look of utter confusion. \"Does Great Yan really not have movable type printing? No wonder I heard the Eighth Princess and the others say paper is expensive; is it because they use precious materials?\"","Saying this, she took two sheets of paper from her sleeve. One recorded several methods of papermaking, detailing the pros and cons.","The other detailed movable type printing, including the production of the movable type and ink, with steps so detailed that even someone without relevant experience could produce something decent if they strictly followed the instructions.","\"Fuguang, this is...?\" Yu Chongshan couldn't help but blush, feeling as though they had schemed against a child.","Yue Fuguang: The Yu family was truly her divine assist. With one thing leading to another, she had reasonably presented these two technologies. The promotion of movable type printing and papermaking in her cultural promotion mission was finally about to begin.","This mission was phased; as long as Great Yan produced the first sheet of paper and printed the first book according to the methods she provided...","With that, the first phase of her mission was complete, and she effortlessly pocketed twenty thousand points."]},{"number":264,"title":"Chapter 264: Someone Takes the Blame, Mother and Daughter Reunite","paragraphs":["So, with her eyes sparkling, she looked at the conflicted Yu Chongshan and smiled playfully, saying, \"Grandfather, aren't you in the Ministry of Works? If I give this to you, can you get some benefits from His Majesty? Like getting a promotion for yourself or something?\"","Yu Chongshan felt a wave of emotion in his heart, but he couldn't help teasing her, \"If your grandfather gets promoted again, I'll have to take over Minister Lu's position.\"","He had just been promoted to Vice Minister before the new year. His sons at home had also been promoted by half a rank or a full rank over the past six months, all thanks to his granddaughter.","Minister Lu Qi, who had just returned to his manor and hadn't even had time to change his clothes, suddenly sneezed several times in a row, shaking his official hat askew. Why did he suddenly feel a chill down his spine!","Yue Fuguang thought for a moment. Granting titles to wives and bringing blessings to descendants—she had to secure at least one of these benefits.","\"Then can Grandmother's noble title be elevated? And as for the brothers and sisters in the family, some honorary official positions or titles—one is not too few, and two are not too many.\"","She knew her words would definitely reach the Emperor's ears, and she hoped he would be sensible!","Hearing that her granddaughter was still thinking of her at a time like this, Old Madam Yu felt incredibly warmed.","She held Yue Fuguang's chubby little hand and said, \"Grandmother doesn't need any noble titles. As long as our whole family is healthy and you younger ones are safe and happy, Grandmother is content.\"","\"That's easy. All of Grandmother's wishes can come true.\"","Yue Fuguang spoke with absolute certainty, and the Yu family believed her without a doubt.","Yu Chongshan said, \"Fuguang, the situation in Great Yan is still unclear. Even His Majesty has to be somewhat wary of the resources held by the great aristocratic families.\"","He shook the two pieces of paper in his hand and said, \"Grandfather has looked at this. The things you brought out today are cheap to produce and not difficult to use. If this can be popularized, the price of books and paper in Great Yan will drop by at least thirty to fifty percent. That's enough to shake the aristocratic families' control over literary inheritance.\"","Yu Ningxuan asked nervously, \"Grandfather, will Fuguang be in danger then?\"","The usually gentle and quiet Yu Ningxin even trotted over to close the doors of the main hall.","Seeing everyone looking at her, she blushed slightly and said, \"Only our family knows about today's matter. Grandfather, can we just not take that whatever-it-is technology out?\"","Yu Boming also agreed, \"Yes, Grandfather. Our family doesn't lack achievements right now. There's no need to put our sister at risk.\"","With the three brothers of the first branch studying away from home, he, as the eldest of the third generation present, naturally had to stand up to protect his younger siblings.","\"We can earn our own futures. Besides, Seventh Sister has already paved the way for us, so why make her take any more risks?\"","Great Yan had operated just fine for so many years without his sister's papermaking and printing techniques.","Moreover, it wasn't that they would never bring it out; they would just delay it until the situation in Great Yan stabilized and they themselves grew stronger.","The others all nodded in agreement.","Seeing the younger generation so united, willing to give up the benefits right in front of them for their sister, Yu Chongshan felt very gratified.","He smiled and said, \"Children, don't worry. Your grandfather and uncles know what to do. No matter what, this matter will not implicate Fuguang. It will also have absolutely nothing to do with our Yu family. Have you all memorized this? Don't let it slip when you go out!\"","\"Tongtong, are you saying that the Emperor plans to make the Fourth and Ninth Princes take the blame for me?\"","It wasn't until night when she was getting ready for bed that Yue Fuguang learned from the system about the scapegoat plan the Emperor and his ministers had hatched during the day.","\"Exactly! Anyway, rest assured, Host, this matter won't implicate you.\"","Although she had hinted early on for Emperor Mingxi to find someone to take the heat for her, she never expected him to choose his own sons.","She couldn't help but sigh sincerely, \"The Emperor is ruthless to other people's sons, but he's no less ruthless to his own!\" However, she liked this outcome! Time to sleep! Sleep!","After the morning court the next day, the Emperor and his ministers gathered again to study the two detailed records of papermaking and printing techniques brought by Yu Chongshan.","After reading the production lists, the way they looked at Yu Chongshan changed a bit.","Yu Chongshan: No, what do you old fellows mean by this? If you're jealous, go find Sun Huajing and Xuanmingzi. Why are you looking at me like that?","Emperor Mingxi said somewhat sourly, \"Fuguang truly shares a deep bond with you, my beloved Minister Yu. Since you personally stepped forward, Fuguang readily handed over such important technology.\"","Yu Chongshan: You guys really only look at the results and ignore the process!","Yue Fuguang: This is truly a beautiful misunderstanding.","Everyone: We can't look at the process; looking at the process is even more frustrating. Old man Yu didn't even mention it, and the Young Tutor brought out the very things they had been dreaming of day and night. Envy and jealousy—they were already numb from saying it! Who wouldn't want a granddaughter like that!","Emperor Mingxi couldn't help but think of Yue Fuguang's words from yesterday. His sons would take the title of the achievement, but the rewards could not be discounted in the slightest.","Since the Young Tutor wanted the credit to fall on someone else, he really had to think carefully about how to reward the Yu family to satisfy Fuguang.","And what was Yue Fuguang, who was on everyone's mind, doing?","She was receiving a guest!","\"Luo Xue of Luoxia Villa greets the Young Tutor!\"","Walking into the main hall of the Bright Moon Pavilion, Luo Xue saw an eight or nine-year-old girl sitting in the seat of honor. Without much hesitation, she bowed respectfully to Yue Fuguang.","\"Villa Master Luo, there's no need for such formality. Please sit down and speak.\"","Yue Fuguang couldn't help but observe Luo Xue. She was around forty years old, with a well-proportioned figure, neither tall nor short. She wore a dark red dress that exuded dignity and elegance.","She had fair skin and bright eyes. Even while sitting, her back was perfectly straight, like a sharp sword hidden in its sheath.","She perfectly fit the image of a female martial artist in her mind—beautiful yet heroic, her sharpness concealed but present, clearly not someone lacking in intelligence.","Yue Fuguang had a very good first impression of Luo Xue, which gave her more confidence in their future cooperation.","After the maidservants served the tea and pastries, she smiled and said, \"Villa Master Luo and Dongxue do indeed look very much alike. It seems I haven't found the wrong person.\"","Seeing Yue Fuguang get straight to the point upon meeting, Luo Xue, who had prepared herself to pay a heavy price, was taken aback!","She had made ample preparations on her way here, thinking that the other party would at least negotiate back and forth a few times to settle on terms before she could see the girl suspected to be her daughter.","She never expected that this highly respected Young Tutor, who looked so young, would be even more straightforward than people in the martial arts world.","Hearing that the girl looked like her, Luo Xue felt a surge of excitement. She couldn't help but stand up and say, \"Is what the Young Tutor says true? That child... that child...\"","Before she could finish her sentence, tears were already glistening in her eyes.","Seeing this, Yue Fuguang sighed inwardly and called out to the outside, \"Chunying, Dongxue.\"","As Yue Fuguang's words fell, Luo Xue saw two eighteen or nineteen-year-old girls slowly walk in from outside.","One of them was wearing a moon-white dress, her steps steady and her posture upright, and her face bore a fifty or sixty percent resemblance to her own.","She abruptly stood up and took two steps forward, unable to hold back her tears any longer as they fell silently.","Shen Dongxue's eyes also turned red. Her lips trembled as she tried to speak, but she couldn't utter a single word."]},{"number":265,"title":"Chapter 265: Scandal Exposed, Too Ashamed to Show Your Face","paragraphs":["Yue Fuguang looked at this family reunion scene, feeling a bit touched, and said, Let's all sit down and talk.","After everyone sat back down, Yue Fuguang finally said, I sent a letter to Villa Master Luo because I investigated some past events, which involved Dongxue being switched at birth eighteen years ago.","This is the information I found; Villa Master Luo, you might want to take a look first.","Cuizhu handed a letter from the table to Luo Xue.","She took it with trembling hands and read it carefully.","After half a cup of tea's time, Luo Xue suddenly stood up and was about to bow down to Yue Fuguang.","This time, she did not accept Luo Xue's grand gesture and said to the sisters Shen Chunying and Shen Dongxue, Quickly help Villa Master Luo up to speak.","The two acted as told and hurriedly helped up Luo Xue, who had already bent her knees.","With tearful eyes and a face full of gratitude, she looked at Yue Fuguang and said, That my daughter and I can reunite today is all thanks to Your Excellency's help. Luo Xue thanks Your Excellency for your kindness!","Holding Shen Dongxue's hand, she said to Yue Fuguang, Junior Preceptor, my Sunset Villa is somewhat respected in the martial arts world and holds some reputation.","In the future, if you ever need us, please do not hesitate to ask. The entire Sunset Villa is at the Junior Preceptor's disposal.","At her disposal? Was the pacing of this family reunion a bit off? She hadn't even said anything yet, and this person was already pledging loyalty with a massive villa?","In a rare display of conscience, Yue Fuguang couldn't help but remind her, Villa Master Luo, the matter of Dongxue being your daughter is currently just our side of the story. Shouldn't you confirm its truth first before discussing other things?","Luo Xue shook her head firmly. Junior Preceptor, there is no need. As soon as I saw Dongxue, I knew for certain she was the child I lost back then.","A mother and daughter's hearts are connected; I cannot be wrong!","Shen Dongxue also nodded. She also felt an inexplicable sense of familiarity when she saw Luo Xue.","Yue Fuguang nodded. Since they were certain, she wouldn't say more. She said, Then you guys chat.","She then said to Shen Dongxue, Dongxue, entertain Villa Master Luo well on my behalf.","After saying that, she stood up to leave. The mother and daughter had been separated for many years; now that they finally met, they definitely had a lot to talk about. She wouldn't stay and be a third wheel.","Besides, cooperating with Sunset Villa wasn't urgent. With Dongxue, the future young villa master around, she didn't even need to put much thought into it.","The people around Yue Fuguang were all very perceptive. They knew the official they served was a bit lazy and didn't like managing affairs.","Therefore, whenever there was an issue, they tried their best to solve it themselves. If they couldn't, they would go to Yu Chongshan through Yu Mochun.","In any case, they rarely bothered her with matters.","Even Dai Yuxing, who arrived the latest, was the same. The spies and assassins these two caught in the Yu Manor were, without exception, handed over to the Dali Court through Yu Chongshan. In the end, they only needed to report the results to Yue Fuguang.","Setting aside the fact that her status made her subordinates afraid to act out of line, with the system around, Yue Fuguang wasn't afraid of her subordinates daring to fool her anyway.","Junior Preceptor, shouldn't we first talk about the matters of Sunset Villa? She had such a large villa, so why did it seem like she couldn't even give it away when she wanted to!","Although Luo Xue also wanted to spend time alone with her daughter and talk about their experiences over the years.","However, she dared not neglect Yue Fuguang even more. Not to mention her current highly revered status in the Great Yan dynasty that was like the midday sun.","Just based on the kindness she showed to the mother and daughter, she couldn't just brush it off.","Yue Fuguang waved her hand nonchalantly and said, Villa Master Luo, you don't need to say more. Just go with Dongxue and relax. I lack nothing right now, and currently, there is nothing I need Sunset Villa for.","Seeing Yue Fuguang walk far away, Luo Xue was a bit dumbfounded.","Shen Chunying and Shen Dongxue, however, were full of smiles. With their master's current status and position, what did a single Sunset Villa amount to?","If it weren't for waiting for Villa Master Luo today, she would have gone back to her room to sleep long ago.","Did Yue Fuguang really go to sleep?","In the past, when she had nothing to do, she could only sleep to maintain her health.","Ever since the system upgraded to level four, it immediately awakened her dead memories. The internet-addicted girl was back online.","After the system upgraded, although she couldn't surf the internet, binge-watching movies and TV shows downloaded by the system was completely fine.","Not only did the person and the system watch together, but sometimes they could even discuss a single question with each other.","Just like that, time flew by, causing Yue Fuguang to constantly stay up very late these past two days to rush her homework.","It was only because of her esteemed status that the master teaching her could only sigh helplessly upon seeing her slightly sloppy handwriting over the past few days.","Let alone not daring to say a single harsh word, they even had to greet her with a smile when checking her homework.","Their Emperor had said that if anyone angered the Junior Preceptor to the point where she refused to attend class, then they wouldn't need to attend the morning court anymore!","Time quickly advanced to the ninth day of the fourth month in the fifth year of Yuankang, the wedding day of the Great Yan Crown Prince, Xie Zhiyan.","At the beginning of the Chen hour, Yue Fuguang, with her eyes closed, was dug out of her warm bed by Cuizhu and the others.","By the time she slowly woke up, she had already been washed, dressed, and styled.","Because it was a day of great rejoicing, Yue Fuguang wore a red dress embroidered with intricate patterns in gold thread today. Combined with a set of expensive accessories, she felt she looked more like a walking red envelope.","When she arrived at the main hall, the whole family was already there. Unsurprisingly, she was the last to arrive again.","The men wore official uniforms, while Old Madam Yu and the other ladies wore their full sets of noblewoman attire.","It looked very luxurious, but also very heavy!","At the beginning of the Si hour, Yue Fuguang was already in the Empress Dowager's Palace of Compassionate Tranquility.","Yue Fuguang was still a bit sleepy at this time, so she harbored deep resentment. The grand wedding ceremony wouldn't officially begin until the beginning of the Wei hour, so why did she have to come so early?","Seeing Yue Fuguang looking listless, the Empress Dowager knew she must not be fully awake yet, so she let her go to the side hall to rest.","However, once lying on the soft bed, Yue Fuguang couldn't fall asleep.","System, play two episodes of a TV drama to kill some time.","[Host, are you sure you only want to watch two episodes?]","How about three episodes?","As a result, by the beginning of the Wei hour, when the drums and music played in unison, Yue Fuguang had already binge-watched eight episodes.","Yue Fuguang followed by the Empress Dowager's side, looking down from the jade steps of the Taiji Hall.","At this time, the path from the palace gates to the main hall was covered with a red carpet.","Flagpoles stood on both sides of the path, hung full of red silk. The red silk fluttered gently in the spring evening breeze, like beauties dancing softly.","Red lanterns hung everywhere in the Taiji Hall. They weren't lit yet, but Yue Fuguang, whose mind was exceptionally active, couldn't help but imagine the scene after all the red lanterns were lit up at night.","It would illuminate the surroundings in a bright red, looking exactly like the scene in the horror movie she watched this morning.","Emperor Mingxi sat steadily on the high platform, while the civil and military officials of Great Yan lined up in order of their ranks, with civil officials on the left and military officials on the right.","In the middle of the Wei hour, the foreign diplomatic missions also arrived.","The Western Qiang mission had five people, led by Prince Yi, Xi Yuanshan.","The Northern Li mission only had three people, and the primary and secondary envoys, Bei Ye and Wei Qingyi, were nowhere to be seen.","The three people from Northern Li all wore expressions of embarrassment. When they said that their prince and vice envoy had caught a cold and couldn't come, they wished no one would notice them at all.","Little Zhu, are Bei Ye and Wei Qingyi really sick?","[Master, they are definitely not sick. They probably didn't come because their scandal was exposed, and they are too ashamed to face anyone?]","Has the capital of Northern Li already received the news about Bei Ye and Wei Qingyi having a secret affair?","Friends, please use your lucky hands to urge for more updates, thank you! Clasps hands in salute!"]},{"number":266,"title":"Chapter 266: Don't Look Down on the Poor Young Male Lead","paragraphs":["[Master, Little Zhu took action. The old emperor Bei Ji, the Qi family, and the Jiang family all received the news at the same time. They are making a scene right now!]","It’s good that they are making a scene. I was just afraid that these two families would swallow their pride and make peace for the sake of wealth and status, forcing their married daughters to endure the humiliation silently.","Emperor Mingxi’s lips curled up. According to the news sent back by the spies, it wasn't just the higher-ups of Beili who knew about this.","Thanks to the secret instigation of the royal family members, even the commoners in Beili now knew that their Fifth Prince and the eldest son of Prime Minister Wei’s family were having an affair.","Gossip about big shots had always been popular among the common people. This time, it was so explosive that its topic degree would definitely be the best conversation piece for the people of Beili and even several other countries after meals.","Then came the four members of the Nanzhao diplomatic mission. Lan Xuan'er walked at the very front. As soon as she entered, her gaze fell upon the pale-faced Prince Ming.","Prince Ming had a good appearance, and with the enhancement of his 'battle-damaged makeup', he looked even more graceful than before.","It had to be said that the Ministry of Rites, headed by Zhang Zhongping, understood the ways of the world.","They arranged for Nanzhao to stand next to Prince Ming, looking very much like the matchmaker Yue Lao.","It was just unknown what Emperor Mingxi and the others were planning. On the one hand, they acted like the Queen Mother who separated lovers, overtly and covertly preventing this marriage.","Seeing that the two were about to drift apart, they played the role of Yue Lao again to pull the strings.","Yue Fuguang couldn't help but take another look at Prince Ming's battle-damaged makeup. She didn't believe that he hadn't specially modified this appearance.","With this pitiful sickly beauty image, Lan Xuan'er's eyes were practically glued to him.","A blush appeared just right on Prince Ming's pale skin. Tsk tsk tsk, Prince Ming's master is very suspicious!","Just as Yue Fuguang was studying this pair of lovebirds, the 'Little Prince' of Dongyi, Matsuyama, had already walked into the team. If you didn't look carefully, you wouldn't even notice his overly short figure.","The last to enter was the Second Princess of Nanyue, Gan Tang, and her party of four.","Gan Tang, just like her name, was a beauty with strong features. Because she had dimples, when she smiled, Yue Fuguang actually felt that she was also a sweet girl.","[Master, this Second Princess Gan Tang has some gossip on her, do you want to hear it?]","\"Is it as sweet as Gan Tang's smile?\"","[Master, whatever a melodramatic romance novel is like, that's what this gossip tastes like today. Should I open it?]","Melodramatic romance novel? She read quite a few in her past life, but hadn't read any in this life. Of course, she had to open it!","\"Little Zhu, your Master is seated. Serve the melon!\"","Just as the person and the system were getting ready to eat the melon, the Crown Princess's dowry was carried in by the palace servants.","Every dowry box was tied with red silk, and the palace servants carrying the dowry wore red clothes. They entered from the palace gate and walked along the red carpet.","After circling around the people in the hall like flowing water, they continued towards the Taihe Palace Square where the evening banquet was held.","There was a place designated by the Ministry of Rites to place the dowry, commonly known as sunning the dowry.","The first box contained title deeds and house deeds, all placed in an open wooden box.","Starting from the second box were fabrics, including silk, brocade, fur, etc., in many colors. Following that were clothes for the four seasons, trunks, cabinets, and other daily necessities.","It seemed that the saying heard before, that when a noble family marries off a daughter, they prepare everything the daughter will need for the rest of her life in her husband's home, was not an empty phrase.","Seeing the beautiful clothing materials, Yue Fuguang suddenly thought of something and couldn't help asking, \"Little Zhu, the dyeing process for Dayan's clothing materials uses plant dyes, right?\"","[Is Master afraid they used toxic minerals?]","\"Exactly, like this red dress I'm wearing, it uses madder, safflower, and such, not cinnabar and the like, right?\"","[Master, rest assured, this outfit you're wearing only has the fragrance of plants, without the sour smell of minerals.]","The Emperor and officials of Dayan looked uniformly towards the Ministry of Works, especially the Minister Lu Qi. Although their official robes were made internally, the dyes really came from the Ministry of Works.","Lu Qi quickly shook his head subtly. Conscience dictated that their Ministry of Works wouldn't dare use toxic substances indiscriminately. After all, these things were used not only by colleagues but also by the royal family.","Who would dare mess around? Did they not want their nine generations?","But it seemed there were indeed quite a few folks using various minerals as dyes in the private sector. He really needed to investigate thoroughly!","Xue Ju: I dare! If I had known there was such a simple method, why would I have needed to rely on rebellion to take the whole family down? Poisoning the clothing materials would have been just as effective!","The Xue family: Shivering JPG","\"Then it's fine, Little Zhu, serve the melon!\"","[Alright!] The system's cheerful voice was highly penetrating as it finally reached its most beloved segment.","[Master, according to the plan, the Nanyue diplomatic mission will depart for their home country on the fifth day after attending the wedding. They will arrive at the border between the two countries on April 25th and stay overnight at the relay station in Lanshan, a border town of Dayan.","That night, the mission accidentally saves a critically injured Dayan man named Ling Yuanhang.","And his entanglement with the Second Princess Gan Tang begins there.]","\"Little Zhu, what's the background of this Ling Yuanhang?\"","[Master, this Ling Yuanhang is exactly like the male protagonist in mortal novels who says 'don't bully the young for being poor, thirty years east of the river, thirty years west of the river', a revenge-driven protagonist who had his engagement broken off.","Today you look down on me, but when I return in glory, I will exterminate your entire family!]","Yue Fuguang's heart skipped a beat. Could their world still be inside some Long Aotian novel?","If this Ling Yuanhang was really the 'male lead' or the darling of the Heavenly Dao, she wouldn't mind taking him out herself!","In this world, apart from her, no one was allowed to use cheats. The most awesome one could only be her. If others dared to have a halo, she wouldn't mind exterminating them as soon as she found one!","\"Little Zhu, this Ling Yuanhang doesn't have a halo, does he?\"","Having been together for so long, the system had some understanding of its host. Hearing the slight chill in her question, it guessed she had murderous intent.","So it quickly said, [Master, rest assured, this Ling Yuanhang doesn't have the kind of halo you imagine, nor is he the darling of the Heavenly Dao or the child of destiny.] Otherwise, his ending wouldn't have been so dramatic.","[Master, when Ling Yuanhang was critically injured and encountered Gan Tang's group, he had just been rejected by the Wei family's second branch, one of the prominent families in Lanshan.","Speaking of which, this Ling Yuanhang was also born into the Ling family, a family of officials for a century. Since childhood, he was betrothed to Wei Shumin, the eldest daughter of Wei Shoujun from the Wei family's second branch, who was a good friend of his father.","Who knew that after a few years, the Ling family started to have bad luck. First, the head of the family, Ling Lanshan, who was also the Ling family's biggest supporter in the court, suddenly died of illness.","Then, the elite youths of the family successively passed away for various reasons, some due to accidents, some due to illness, and even two young members committed suicide.]","Hearing this, the Emperor and officials of Dayan all nodded secretly. Most of them still remembered Lord Ling who passed away ten years ago.","His death was indeed sudden. At that time, Wei Ping and Cai Xian were still minor officials in the Dali Temple and the Ministry of Justice. The sudden death of a high-ranking official shocked the ruling and opposition parties.","Because the Emperor attached great importance to it, they inevitably followed their respective superiors to visit and investigate."]},{"number":267,"title":"Chapter 267: Ling Family","paragraphs":["After a preliminary examination by their two respective offices, it was found that Lord Ling had no external injuries or signs of poisoning on his body. On the surface, he indeed appeared to have died from some unknown 'illness'.","Emperor Mingxi and his ministers couldn't help but prick up their ears. Could it be that the question weighing on their minds for years was about to be unveiled today?","At this moment, the slightly hoarse voice of the eunuch reciting the dowry list became the most jarring noise in the entire grand hall.","Time flew by while enjoying the 'melon' (gossip). In what seemed like just a moment, the dowry procession had reached over forty loads. What was passing by now were jewelry—various gold bracelets, jade bracelets, gold necklaces, jade necklaces, earrings, rings, hairpins, and other exquisite pieces—neatly arranged in boxes adorned with the character for 'double happiness'.","Yue Fuguang stared blankly at these items, her mind racing. \"Is there someone behind the deaths of the Ling family members?\" Having read countless books, she smelled a conspiracy.","As the saying goes, too many coincidences are no coincidence.","[There is indeed another reason, Master, but this is a different 'melon'. Let's not dig into it today!] Yue Fuguang raised an eyebrow, seriously suspecting that her 'melon-eating' system hadn't yet uncovered the full picture of the event!","Meanwhile, the 'listeners' were nearly driven to frustration by the phrase, \"this is a different 'melon', let's not dig into it today!\" just as they were prepared to hear the rest.","With over a dozen members of the Ling family dying one after another over several years, even the most obtuse among the civil and military officials could see there was definitely a problem.","It even caused a wave of panic among the court officials for a time. Later, everyone gradually realized that this matter seemed to target only the Ling family.","It could be said that in the following years, every time a Ling family member died, Wei Ping and Cai Xian had attended the scene, yet after all this time, they had found nothing.","This became an unresolved knot in both their hearts.","[The Ling family members who died were all elite descendants and the heads of various household branches. The capital city of Shangjing became a place of sorrow for the Ling family.","The young clan leader at the time had no choice but to lead the entire clan back to their ancestral lands in Lanshan.]","\"Little Zhu, is this Ling family related to Ling Jijiu's family?\"","Ling Yinghua's eyelid twitched. Ten years ago, when Ling Langshan served as an official in court, his own father was still alive.","Because both families shared the surname Ling, they interacted more frequently than with others.","Being prominent clans, upon consulting their genealogies, they discovered their ancestors were indeed connected.","The two had even considered formally reconnecting their clan lineages, but the idea was abandoned following Ling Langshan's death.","Not long after that, his own father passed away, and the matter was never brought up again between the two families.","[Master, the two families were indeed once related, but that was before the Tong dynasty. By Ling Jijiu's generation, over ten generations had passed.","If the relationship weren't so distant, Ling Jijiu's family wouldn't have lost only his father!]","Ling Yinghua suddenly looked up, meeting Emperor Mingxi's stern face before realizing his own loss of composure.","He forced down his shock, but his trembling hands and the hidden crimson in his eyes as he lowered his head betrayed him.","Having always believed his father died of illness, upon first hearing that his father's death might have been caused by a villain, as a son, how could he not be shocked?","How could he not wish to immediately know who the murderer was and tear them to pieces with his own hands to vent the hatred in his heart!","[After returning to Lanshan, a starved camel is still bigger than a horse. The Ling family remained a wealthy and influential clan in Lanshan.]","\"Wealthy and influential? Wouldn't the Ling family's situation at that time be like a child holding gold in a bustling marketplace?\"","She seemed to somewhat understand why the Wei family had delayed breaking off the engagement with Ling Yuanhang until today.","[Correct. With all capable male members of the Ling family gone, a household of the elderly, weak, women, and children guarding a 'gold mountain' was indeed perilous.","Especially their in-laws and old acquaintances, who encroached upon the Ling family's assets under various pretexts.","By now, the Ling family has truly declined. The Wei family only broke off the engagement with Ling Yuanhang after seeing no more profit could be squeezed from them.]","\"Were the injuries on Ling Yuanhang's body inflicted by the Wei family?\"","[No, the Wei family was only greedy for wealth, not to the point of taking lives. But regardless of whether the Wei family did it or not, the seventeen-year-old, severely injured Ling Yuanhang blamed the Wei family for it all.","So when he 'returned reborn', the first target of his revenge was the entire Wei clan.]","\"Does this 'returned reborn' have something to do with Gan Tang?\"","[Yes. After the Nanyue envoy rescued Ling Yuanhang, Gan Tang, seeing his noble attire and demeanor, took him away from Danyan back to Nanyue.","Ling Yuanhang, who awoke after three days and nights of unconsciousness, saw Gan Tang as the first person upon waking.","From then on, his heart became devoted to the noble and beautiful Gan Tang. As for his devoted fiancée Wei Shumin, who was waiting for him and still wanted to marry him, she was long forgotten.]","Yue Fuguang nodded. Truly worthy of being the revenge-themed male protagonist Ling Yuanhang, as rated by the system. He might lack many things, but he would never lack the inherent attribute of being a scoundrel.","She just didn't know if this one was a harem-seeking type or a love-struck fool.","\"Hmph!\"","For some reason, just that single \"Hmph!\" from Yue Fuguang sent a shiver down the spines of Emperor Mingxi and his Danyan ministers.","Meanwhile, Crown Prince Xie Zhiyan, who had just walked outside the hall and was about to become a husband, involuntarily tightened his grip on the red silk in his hand.","Although the Junior Mentor hadn't said anything explicit, everyone knew she looked down upon the Danyan custom where men could have three wives and four concubines, while women were expected to follow the three obediences and four virtues.","Ever since guessing some of her taboos, those officials who could hear her thoughts, along with his Majesty the Emperor, had become extremely cautious about taking concubines.","Because the decreased demand from the upper echelons had even affected the related market economy!","Yue Fuguang: Are you sure it's out of wariness of me, and not because you're afraid after learning that Prince Qi, enemy state spies, and other factions like to plant their own people in your backyards? Disdainful JPG","The display of the Crown Princess's dowry finally neared its end after the last few chests of books were carried in and then away.","After viewing the dowry, the civil and military officials began their performance, whispering and discussing with colleagues in front, behind, left, and right.","Some said the Shen family was generous, others said it was only to be expected.","In short, they acted as if everything was normal, and they really hadn't been solely focused on eating 'melons'!","The sun gradually set, and dusk arrived.","A red-robed official from the Ministry of Rites stood on a high platform and shouted in a drawn-out yet penetrating voice, \"The auspicious hour has arrived. Please invite the Crown Prince and Crown Princess to enter the hall.\"","His voice carried clearly to Xie Zhiyan, who was hundreds of meters away, becoming a groom for the first time and feeling extremely nervous.","As his words fell, drums and music instantly sounded both inside and outside the grand hall. A melodious rendition of \"The Phoenix Seeks His Mate\" temporarily interrupted the 'melon-eating' duo.","Yue Fuguang looked towards the hall entrance. In the distance, she saw the handsome and dignified Xie Zhiyan with a solemn expression, wearing a red wedding robe embroidered with dragon patterns in gold thread and a purple-gold crown.","Beside him was the Crown Princess Shen Junshu in her magnificent phoenix crown and ceremonial robes. The long hem of her red wedding dress trailed on the ground like a blooming red flower.","The phoenixes and peonies embroidered on it refracted glints of golden light in the afterglow of the setting sun.","Golden threads and silver beads veiled her face, making it impossible to discern her expression."]},{"number":268,"title":"Chapter 268: Male Favorite","paragraphs":["Thanks to the Urge-to-Update Bot for the Great God certification, specially adding a bonus chapter, thanks buddy!","But from the original timeline, her unwavering loyalty to the Crown Prince and her resolute suicide after the fall of Great Yan show that she is a passionate, righteous, and fiercely decisive woman.","Accompanied by joyous music, the two walked step by step into the hall.","The civil and military officials who were whispering just a moment ago instantly fell silent.","The members of the foreign diplomatic missions also craned their necks to watch. The grand wedding ceremony of the Great Yan heir was clearly different from their own countries.","When the newlyweds entered the hall, they stopped about five meters away from the jade steps where Emperor Mingxi and the others were seated.","The Minister of Rites, Zhang Zhongping, stepped forward. Wearing his official uniform and holding the congratulatory address, he began to read aloud.","We subjects respectfully follow the rites of the Ministry, adhering to ancient systems and laws, to humbly congratulate His Royal Highness the Crown Prince on the joy of his grand wedding.","We humbly observe: Heaven and Earth unite in virtue, the sun and moon rise in eternal constancy. Starlight shines upon the Ziwei sector, and mythical birds sing in the vermilion halls.","Today's auspicious ceremony for the heir apparent is truly the weight of the ancestral temple and the foundation of the state.","The Crown Prince holds the virtues of benevolence and filial piety, carrying forward the order of heaven and earth.","The Crown Princess, nurtured from an illustrious family, possesses the gentle grace of the earth...","The speech was very long. Yue Fuguang only half-understood it, but it was all auspicious words of blessing anyway, wishing the Crown Prince and Crown Princess to grow old together, have a precious son soon, and bring fortune to the nation.","[Master, what is the use of Zhang Zhongping saying so much? His dozens of sentences are not as effective as one of yours.]","The Xie family, from the Emperor, Empress Dowager, and Empress, to Xie Zhiyan and his wife, were all thrilled. If they could get the blessing of the Junior Preceptor...","Hidden behind a veil of gold threads and silver beads, Shen Junshu could not help but purse her lips. She had long heard of the Little Immortal Lord's blessings.","In her heart, she had secretly hoped to receive his blessing when she and the Crown Prince got married.","Even before leaving her maiden home today, she had devoutly offered incense and prayed before the jade statue of the Little Immortal Lord.","\"The Crown Princess is a good person. When the couple toasts to this immortal, I will naturally offer my blessings.\"","Xie Zhiyan: Junior Preceptor, you said the Crown Princess is good, but what about me? Such a big person right in front of you, can't you see me?","Do I not deserve to be evaluated?","[Master seems to really like Shen Junshu? Little Zhu sees that among the wedding gifts Master gave the Crown Prince, there is a jade hairpin. Is it for the Crown Princess?]","\"Otherwise? Did you think it was for the Crown Prince to wear?\"","Because Yue Fuguang's gifts included the repeating crossbow the Crown Prince had long anticipated, the royal father and son had indeed paid special attention to Yue Fuguang's wedding presents.","Aside from the crossbow, there were several advanced technical blueprints, such as a method for refining fine salt, as well as a jade hairpin and a pair of jade pendants.","After his imperial father saw it, he laughed so hard his gums showed on the spot. Fortunately, only the two of them were present, sharing the same silly expression.","Neither father nor son judged the other.","Compared to these technologies, the green jade hairpin carved with a few vivid plum blossoms had nothing special about it other than being exceptionally beautiful.","Of course, the father and son simply did not see its specialness; they wouldn't look down on it. After all, it was a gift from the Junior Preceptor.","Everything came from Lord Divine Artifact's mysterious innate space, so not a single item was of poor quality.","Hearing it now, it was specially given to the Crown Princess by the Junior Preceptor. Could this jade hairpin have something special about it?","At this moment, Crown Princess Shen Junshu's hands, hidden in her sleeves, could not help but tremble.","She never expected that her simple wish for the Little Immortal Lord to give her a beautiful blessing would not only be realized so soon.","The Little Immortal Lord seemed to be giving her even more than she had hoped for.","Beneath the veil, the corners of Shen Junshu's mouth could not help but rise. Lord Divine Artifact said the Little Immortal Lord liked her.","The Little Immortal Lord did not deny it, so she would take it as his tacit admission!","The parents and siblings of the Shen family, standing aside to watch the ceremony, were all happy for the Crown Princess.","No matter what the Junior Preceptor gave her, even if it were just a blade of grass, this special sentiment and the comment \"the Crown Princess is a good person\" were enough for their Junshu to establish a firm foothold in the Eastern Palace before she even gave birth to an heir.","In this round, a world where only Crown Prince Xie Zhiyan was hurt had been achieved!","Uh... and a group of spectating officials who could hear the inner thoughts and whose eyes were red with envy.","Yue Fuguang held back a laugh. These people looked even more hurt than the Crown Prince!","Zhang Zhongping, who was judged by Lord Divine Artifact as useless no matter how many blessings he read, was also feeling very stifled at this moment.","His old face was redder than the groom Xie Zhiyan's. Finally, this congratulatory speech full of ancient charm concluded successfully with:","Teaching the Odes and delighting in the Rites, offering sacrifices at the ancestral temple; sharing one heart and bearing the yoke together, setting an example for the family and the nation.","We respectfully use the words of the classics to express our sincere congratulations. Respectfully congratulated.","Without catching his breath, he then cupped his hands to the Crown Prince and Crown Princess standing below.","And shouted loudly, \"First bow to Heaven and Earth!\"","The Crown Prince and Crown Princess turned, faced the sky outside the palace, and knelt to kowtow...","With the announcement, \"The ceremony is complete!\"","The senior maids helped the Crown Princess up, and a smile appeared on the Crown Prince's face.","Amidst the chiming of drums and music, the two were \"sent to the bridal chamber\"!","The newlyweds withdrew, and Emperor Mingxi said, \"Today is the Crown Prince's grand wedding, and My heart is very pleased. A banquet is bestowed in the Hall of Supreme Harmony, let all my lords celebrate together.\"","\"Thank you for Your Majesty's profound grace.\"","Yue Fuguang and the group then moved to the Hall of Supreme Harmony for the banquet.","The Hall of Supreme Harmony had a high platform where the Emperor, Empress Dowager, and Empress sat. Of course, Yue Fuguang was also mixed in among the Big Three.","The seat below the Emperor was empty, reserved for the Crown Prince.","The princes and princesses took their seats in order of age.","The civil and military officials sat below, one person per table. The foreign diplomatic missions sat in a specially designated area on the right; they used low tables and could sit cross-legged.","By now, the sky had turned completely dark, and the red lanterns were all lit. Just as Yue Fuguang had thought, the red lanterns cast a rosy glow over the people and objects around.","Even before the toasting began, everyone looked as if they were already drunk.","While watching the singing and dancing as an appetizer, Yue Fuguang continued to gossip with the system about the drama they had not finished earlier.","\"Little Zhu, continue telling me what happened after Ling Yuanhang followed Gan Tang to Nanyue?\"","[Master, this Ling Yuanhang later turned into a total simp, providing emotional value to Gan Tang every day.","Naturally, he also started living off a woman. After all, the Ling family had already declined, and being away from home, he did not have much money on him.","Gan Tang is generous, and Ling Yuanhang is handsome and can provide her with emotional value, so she naturally doesn't mind supporting one more person.]","\"Is Gan Tang keeping him as a male favorite?\"","[At first, she indeed kept him as a male favorite. Although Ling Yuanhang didn't think of himself as a male favorite, the fact is that he ate Gan Tang's food, lived in Gan Tang's place, and when he was harassed, it was Gan Tang's people who protected him.]","\"Harassed? Do you mean that kind of harassment?\"","[Yes, exactly the kind Master is thinking of.]","Everyone: What kind of harassment, make it clear! It's one thing for you two to secretly gossip, but why are you using secret codes?","[Relying on his handsome looks and sweet talk, Ling Yuanhang was quite favored by some noble ladies and young misses in Guangping, the capital of Nanyue.","At this time, he met a noble lady of the Jiang family, Gan Tang's cousin Jiang Yan.","Jiang Yan was obsessed with good looks and fell in love with Ling Yuanhang at first sight. She then pursued him relentlessly. Within a few months, Ling Yuanhang half-heartedly accepted Jiang Yan's declaration of love.]","\"Then what was Gan Tang's reaction at this time? Wasn't she keeping Ling Yuanhang as a male favorite?\"","Please drop a comment to urge for updates, add this to your library, and leave a five-star review! Thank you!"]},{"number":269,"title":"Chapter 269: She's All Too Familiar with This Trick","paragraphs":["[Master assumes the reason Ling Yuanhang would accept Jiang Yan is because his meal ticket, the Second Princess Gan Tang, is getting married.","Gan Tang's feelings for Ling Yuanhang are complicated. She was born into the royal family, and because Nanyue, like Nanzhao, has an open-minded culture, even as a woman, it's not impossible for her to fight for the throne.","So she married down to You Hong, the great general who held command over a hundred thousand troops in Nanyue.","At first, she treated Ling Yuanhang as a male pet, but later discovered he had quite a talent for military affairs, so she wanted to train him for her own use.","She used a little honey trap, never expecting that this sweet trap would not only ensnare Ling Yuanhang but also herself.","As for Ling Yuanhang and Jiang Yan, half of it was because he truly liked the pretty and cute Jiang Yan, and the other half was to spite Gan Tang.]","\"If you want to use someone, aren't there many ways? Why throw yourself into the mix?\"","[Master, for us, there are plenty of ways to control someone. But for mortals, especially young men and women, using love is a relatively fast way to achieve one's goal.","Furthermore, Ling Yuanhang has always had feelings for Gan Tang. She only needs to beckon with her finger, and he will obediently submit.]","[Since that's the case, why did he go and provoke Jiang Yan, and even provoke her with some genuine affection?]","\"This Ling Yuanhang is a bizarre scumbag. He indeed likes Gan Tang, but he also has feelings for Jiang Yan, and both are genuine.","So when Gan Tang proposed sending him to the army to gain experience, he agreed without much hesitation.","He still holds a grudge against the Wei family for breaking off the engagement, waiting to return home in glory and take revenge on them!\"","\"Little Zhu, does your 'return home in glory' mean Ling Yuanhang wipes out the Wei family? Or does he lead the Nanyue army to invade Dayan himself?\"","[He invades directly and bathes Lanshan in blood! From then on, he even earned the title of Ghost Hand General!]","The rulers and ministers of Dayan: !!!","These people, who considered themselves the most cultured group in Dayan, could no longer look straight at the phrase 'return home in glory'. They felt it was dripping with blood.","\"Another traitor leading the way! I just wonder what the Ling family will think when they see this version of Ling Yuanhang!\"","[Ling Yuanhang spent five years in the army and rose to the position of general, and he also married Jiang Yan.","Nine years from now, the twenty-six-year-old General Weinan, Ling Yuanhang, will lead the Nanyue army to invade Dayan and bathe Lanshan in blood.","Although he did not touch the Ling family, the entire Ling family was full of people with integrity.","The clan leader, Ling Yuandao, led fifty-six men, women, and children of the clan to open the ancestral hall and expel Ling Yuanhang from the clan.","The furious Ling Yuanhang killed the thirty-five-year-old clan leader on the spot and appointed himself as the new clan leader.","But the Ling family refused to acknowledge him. On that day, apart from a few young children, everyone else in the Ling family died. This included Wei Shumin, who had waited for him and never married her whole life.]","Hearing this, Yue Fuguang felt a sigh in her heart. The Ling clan members had integrity, yet Ling Yuanhang, this piece of rat feces, brought shame to his ancestors and disaster to his clan.","With Ling Yuanhang's actions, if Dayan hadn't fallen, the Ling family would have no place to stand in Dayan!","\"This Ling Yuanhang is truly a menace!\"","[Ling Yuanhang's title of Ghost Hand General was not for nothing. From then on, every time he conquered a city in Dayan, he allowed his soldiers to burn, kill, and loot.","This person could definitely be described as a great villain.","Although he married Jiang Yan, he didn't break things off with Gan Tang. Because he conquered Dayan, he made a great contribution, thus becoming an even more powerful general than You Hong.","After Dayan perished, not only did he force Gan Sheng to abdicate and help Gan Tang ascend to the throne, but he also schemed to kill You Hong, becoming the number one person by Gan Tang's side.]","The rulers and ministers of Dayan were grinding their teeth so hard they were about to shatter. Yue Fuguang slightly raised her eyes and saw the crowd gnawing on lamb legs without any regard for their image.","Were they treating the lamb legs as Ling Yuanhang?","The lamb leg: Bite lighter, my dead mouth! How innocent is my little leg!","\"And then what? I don't believe those two could live happily ever after.\"","The profession of an emperor has a kind of magic. No matter who sits on the throne, they will become a political creature, regardless of gender.","An emperor has three palaces and six courtyards. Didn't the only female emperor of Great Xia also keep a group of male pets?","They are all people of 'passion'!","She would bet a pack of spicy strips that Gan Tang, having sat on the throne, would absolutely not tolerate someone whose merits overshadowed the sovereign.","A mountain cannot abide two tigers, unless one is male and the other female, but that's in the animal kingdom.","When it comes to imperial power, even a male and a female won't work.","[Once Ling Yuanhang became the great general, naturally there were people who wanted to curry favor with him, sending him money and beautiful women.","The arrogant and confident Ling Yuanhang naturally refused no one.","He embraced women on his left and right, yet he couldn't stand Gan Tang taking in a large harem and dividing her affection.","The children Gan Tang had with You Hong, regardless of gender, were all placed under house arrest by him.","He wanted to have a child with Gan Tang, and then let this child inherit the throne in the future.","Little did he know, Gan Tang had been guarding against him all along. Before he invaded Dayan, she had secretly given him a sterilizing drug.","Master must remember the medicine seller. It was the same medicine seller who sold the drug to the Xue brothers, causing all four Xue brothers to lose their fertility.","After he went on the run, he ended up in Nanyue, and the sterilizing drug found its way into Ling Yuanhang's mouth.]","\"Could it be that Ling Yuanhang wanted to wait for Gan Tang to give birth to their child, then kill Gan Tang and assist the young child in succeeding the throne, while he acted as the regent?\"","She was way too familiar with this trope!","[Master guessed right, that's exactly what Ling Yuanhang was thinking. Although he had feelings for Gan Tang, he loved power more.","What he truly wanted was to lie drunk on the laps of beauties and awaken to grasp the power of the world, the kind of absolute power.","He planned to drag Gan Tang off the throne and make her the Supreme Emperor.","It was also because of this that he was a bit slower to make his move.","Unfortunately, he didn't expect Gan Tang to understand him too well. First, she chemically castrated him, and then she schemed to cripple him.","Once Gan Tang completely took control of the army in his hands, she killed him without mercy.]","Well done! If a woman isn't ruthless, her position isn't stable. Shouldn't someone like Ling Yuanhang be killed early as a sacrifice to the heavens, or were they supposed to keep him around for the New Year?","This man was promiscuous, lustful, and greedy for power. Not only did he live off a woman, but he also wanted to covertly steal her entire legacy and truly take control of Nanyue into his own hands.","What a pity he was one move short and eventually got counter-killed!","Hearing this, the rulers and ministers of Dayan, although dealing with an enemy country, had to praise Gan Tang for being decisive enough.","Just then, the Crown Prince had changed his attire and slowly walked over with the Crown Princess, Shen Junshu.","[Master, is the Crown Prince done with the wedding night? Isn't that a bit too fast?]","Hearing these words, the Crown Prince's footsteps visibly staggered, and his handsome face turned bright red, then black.","[Master, look, I was right. Just from this little bit, the Crown Prince's legs are already soft. Tsk, tsk, tsk, he's both fast and incapable!","Master, Little Zhu has some wine soaked with tiger bones here. You should have given him that as a wedding gift instead of useless things like the salt-making method.]","Hearing the system's teasing, Yue Fuguang couldn't help but want to roll her eyes. She really wanted to ask the system: do you still remember that you are a merit system, not a gossip system?","Moreover, she really didn't want to participate in complaints unrelated to the mission.","Was she exposing gossip every day? She was exposing points!"]},{"number":270,"title":"Chapter 270: Blessings from the Junior Mentor","paragraphs":["The originally dark-faced Crown Prince had now turned green with anger. What kind of decent person would go straight to the bridal chamber without even entertaining the wedding guests?","Wasn't that a reserved program for the dead of night?","The Crown Prince's cheeks puffed out in anger. He seriously suspected that Lord Artifact was deliberately smearing his name in front of the Lord Junior Preceptor.","It was rare for the Crown Prince to drop his poised facade and show his true temperament, which made the Crown Princess beside him find it quite amusing.","She gently squeezed his large hand, reminding him to mind his manners.","The Crown Prince took a deep breath, quickly adjusted his expression, and began to toast the guests with the Crown Princess.","He first toasted the Emperor, the Empress Dowager, and the Empress.","Next, it was Yue Fuguang's turn.","Yue Fuguang said, \"Then I, the Junior Preceptor, wish the Crown Prince and Crown Princess to be of one heart as a married couple, and never doubt each other.\"","As Yue Fuguang's words fell, the crowd saw a faint, pale golden light spreading from her body. It was so subtle that if one did not look closely, they would think their eyes were playing tricks on them.","It seemed to have a life of its own as it emerged from Yue Fuguang and directly submerged into the bodies of Xie Zhiyan and Shen Junshu.","Hearing her blessing, both of them were exceptionally overjoyed.","Being in the royal family, being of one heart and never doubting each other meant that they were destined to be not only each other's closest family but also each other's most trusted political allies.","Now, seeing the golden light envelop them, both felt their bodies become remarkably lighter.","Xie Zhiyan and Shen Junshu exchanged a glance, both seeing astonishment and joy in the other's eyes.","Naturally, their expressions did not escape the crowd who had been paying close attention to this side.","After all, the Lord Junior Preceptor's blessing tonight was also one of the programs they were looking forward to, much more captivating than the dances in the hall.","Everyone, including the royal family, was speculating whether the Lord Junior Preceptor's blessing had other effects.","Otherwise, why would the Crown Prince and Crown Princess, who originally had somewhat exhausted expressions, suddenly radiate energy and look so vibrant right after the Lord Junior Preceptor spoke?","\"Thank you for your auspicious words, Lord Junior Preceptor!\" The two respectfully bowed to Yue Fuguang.","Yue Fuguang did not dodge or avoid it; she accepted it calmly with a smile.","After the two stood up, they took the wine handed over by the attendants and drank it in one gulp.","Yue Fuguang also took a sip of the fruit juice in her cup and pursed her lips. It was not as good as the beverages from the System Shop.","[Master, why didn't you wish them a harmonious union for a hundred years and the early birth of a precious son?]","[Too cliché! Besides, if I wish them a harmonious union for a hundred years, wouldn't they have to live to be over a hundred years old?","If a reigning emperor lives to be over a hundred, it is not a good thing for either the country or the family!]","Great Xia had the most say in this point. In history, those emperors who lived a long time did no small amount of harm to the court and the world!","Emperor Mingxi and the Crown Prince, father and son, complained in their hearts. If they could live to be over a hundred, they would gladly abdicate the throne to their descendants when they reached the proper age. Being a Grand Emperor was also a good choice.","Emperor Mingxi: They say an elder in the family is like a treasure. Would the Lord Junior Preceptor really not consider adding some years to his lifespan?","[As for having children, the Crown Princess is not yet eighteen, so there is no rush to give birth.]","Shen Junshu's lips curled up, her heart full of gratitude. With the Lord Junior Preceptor's words, the burden on her to quickly bear children for the royal family would be lightened.","Hearing the Lord Junior Preceptor's words, the Empress, who was eager to hold a grandson, and the Empress Dowager, who wanted to hold a great-grandson, both dropped the idea.","How could they forget that this person advocated for that... oh right, late marriage and late childbearing.","If they rushed their daughter-in-law or granddaughter-in-law to give birth too early, would it incur her displeasure?","After accepting the congratulations from the princes and princesses below, the Crown Princess stayed by the side of the Empress and Empress Dowager, while the Crown Prince walked down the high platform to toast the civil and military officials and the foreign delegations.","As he walked to each table, the ministers stood up and offered their blessings one after another.","The Crown Prince was drinking wine, cup after cup. Yue Fuguang saw his face start to turn red, but he showed no signs of drunkenness. Was this the legendary thousand cups without getting drunk?","When toasting the foreign delegations, Xi Yuanshan said, \"This King congratulates His Royal Highness the Crown Prince.\"","He drank the wine in his cup in one gulp and continued, \"Western Qiang presents these congratulatory gifts: one treasured sword, ten fine steeds, a hundred pelts, and a thousand heads of cattle and sheep. May our two countries be on good terms forever.\"","An attendant brought forward a long box and opened it; inside was a sword.","The scabbard was decorated with precious stones. The Crown Prince picked up the sword, took a look, and handed it to the eunuch behind him.","He cupped his hands and said, \"Many thanks to His Majesty the Emperor of Western Qiang, and I ask Prince Yi to convey my gratitude on my behalf.\"","When it was Northern Li's turn, the gifts sent were also horses, cattle, sheep, and pelts.","However, the bow and arrows they gifted were quite exquisite. The Crown Prince tested the bowstring and praised, \"A fine bow.\"","Seeing this, the system could not help but complain again, [Master, the emperors of these countries are too stingy.","It is the grand wedding of a nation's Crown Prince, and they only send this little stuff?","Just one of Master's prescriptions could instantly crush them! Little Zhu seriously suspects that these people embezzled the gifts along the way!]","[Little Zhu, the items they brought have a gift list and a state letter. No one can forge that; it's just that their emperors are stingy!]","[And that nonsense about the two countries being on good terms forever, the monarch and officials of Great Yan actually believed it. Little do they know, the others have been preparing for years to annex Great Yan.","Only the emperors of Great Yan, generation after generation, just guard their own little patch of land and never think about expanding their territory and fighting outwards. What a bunch of losers!]","Emperor Mingxi, the good-for-nothing, and Xie Zhiyan, the future good-for-nothing, exchanged a glance from afar. Both caught a fleeting look of disgust in the other's eyes.","The fragile little boat of their father-son bond could capsize at any moment!","Hearing the Divine Artifact start cursing again, the civil and military officials ignored whether they were usually political rivals. They simply grabbed whoever was next to them and began offering toasts.","They looked like they were trying to get drunk as quickly as possible so they wouldn't have to hear a thing.","Shen Junshu, who was accompanying the Empress Dowager and the Empress, felt a little nervous. She looked worriedly toward the Junior Preceptor.","The Empress seemed to notice her concern and just smiled, patting her hand.","One couldn't tell at all that her own husband and son were currently being scolded.","Empress Xu thought: So what if they get scolded a bit? The Divine Artifact isn't wrong!","The Empress Dowager thought: The Divine Artifact's scolding is harsh, but its salvation of Dayan is just as real!","Although the Divine Artifact was a bit erratic, with the Junior Preceptor keeping it in check, nothing would go wrong.","\"Little Zhu, you are too caught up in appearances! As the saying goes, you reap what you sow. The monarch and officials of Dayan are addicted to comfort, so naturally, they will die in comfort.\"","Die in comfort! Die in comfort! These words struck the hearts of the Dayan monarch and officials like a warning bell.","It also shattered their recent restlessness and complacency. Especially after seeing the high-yield seeds growing so well across tens of thousands of acres of fertile land, it had been inevitable for them to become a bit smug and inflated.","Some had even grown slack, forgetting that the sharp blade of national subjugation still hung over their heads.","Surrounded by four other nations, Dayan was nothing but a piece of fat meat. The other nations' desire to destroy Dayan had never wavered.","How was the struggle between nations any different from the struggle for power and interests between people?","Looking at the diplomatic missions from the other countries, they appeared respectful on the surface but were actually arrogant.","In the hearts of the Dayan monarch and officials, the seed of fighting back and expanding their territory suddenly burst with vitality. A great tree named Unification began to take root and sprout in their minds.","\"Huh, System, why did I suddenly get twenty thousand more points?\""]},{"number":271,"title":"Chapter 271: Do you know which royal family is the most peculiar among the six nations","paragraphs":["Ling Yuanhang was far away in Lanshan. Great Yan had only just heard their revelations; even if they flew, they wouldn't have dealt with this person so quickly!","However, his little life was indeed worth a whopping twenty thousand points, second only to Sima Jing.","[Let me take a look!]","In the system space, it ran a data retrieval. Amidst the flickering of massive amounts of data, the system saw the mission line, which looked like a large tree with a straight trunk and countless large and small branches branching out.","Some branches of the entire tree had already been lit up, while others remained dull and unlit.","The system ignored the branches and only looked towards the main trunk.","[Host! The main quest suddenly advanced by five percentage points, so the system gave a reward of twenty thousand points.]","The system looked at the progress bar that had suddenly advanced by five percent, feeling extremely excited.","\"The main quest advanced by five percentage points? What did we do to advance it so much all at once? Didn't it always advance at a speed of fractions of a percent before?\"","Yue Fuguang really wanted to find the reason and replicate it!","After all, the two of them had exposed so much dirt and sent hundreds, if not thousands, of people down, yet the completion progress was still in the single digits.","With a sudden increase of five points, how could she not want to know the reason behind it?","[It seems we only exposed Ling Yuanhang's dark secrets, and you gave a blessing to the future heir of this dynasty.","It doesn't seem like we did anything extra today!]","The system scratched its smooth, round head, unable to figure out the reason.","[How about I ask the main system?] 07 had already lain flat like a system pancake at this point.","Unable to come up with a result, it wanted to find a parent to seek the answer.","Anyway, it didn't think there was any problem with this. It was still a novice system doing a task for the first time. If it didn't look for a parent, it would look for a senior.","However, System 07 always felt that its seniors seemed to be intentionally or unintentionally avoiding it, as if they didn't really want to chat with it much.","Yue Fuguang didn't want to give up easily. Besides, she felt that asking the main system might not necessarily yield an answer.","\"Ling Yuanhang is at best a formidable warlord. Exposing his dirt, or even his death, couldn't possibly advance it by five points.","As for blessing the Crown Prince and the others, that's even more irrelevant. It doesn't even count as a task, and the blessing talismans used were paid for out of my own pocket!\"","Yue Fuguang analyzed it point by point, carefully thinking over everything she and the system had said and done tonight.","It couldn't be that the Emperor was scolded as useless by the system and had his fighting spirit roused, right?","The two of them had done their fair share of scolding. If scolding were useful, they wouldn't have had to wait until today.","While Yue Fuguang was brainstorming, Xie Zhiyan's toast had already reached Dongyi.","The little prince of Dongyi, Matsuyama, cupped his hands and said, \"Your Highness, Crown Prince of Great Yan, my great Dongyi presents our congratulatory gifts: a hundred pearls, a coral tree, and ten boxes of specialty fruits from Dongyi. We also wish for generations of friendship between our two nations, never to invade each other.\"","The pearls were very round, the coral was very red, and some of the fruits Yue Fuguang had never seen before; they were small, just like the stature of the Dongyi people, who could never grow tall unless they resorted to crooked methods.","Unable to find the reason for the sudden increase in the task progress bar, Yue Fuguang inevitably felt a bit annoyed.","When she was annoyed, she needed to find someone to vent it on; she wouldn't hold it in and consume herself internally.","Unfortunately for him, the moment Yue Fuguang looked up, she saw Matsuyama, who was holding his head high and puffing out his chest, trying to make his height of less than 1.6 meters look like 1.9 meters.","You're the one!","It had been a long time, and they hadn't really exposed any dark secrets about Dongyi yet.","Yue Fuguang picked and chose on the task panel and finally selected one.","The system received the signal and immediately entered a gossip-consuming state.","After several rounds of drinks and dishes, the crowd, who were already somewhat drunk, mostly leaned halfway back in their chairs.","They were very relaxed, squinting their drunken eyes at the beautiful dancers twirling in the center of the hall.","Yue Fuguang felt that these people needed a beating, so she said, \"Little Zhu, look at these lords staring lecherously at the dancers in the hall.","Those who don't know might think they're looking at Tang Monk's flesh.\"","[Master, eating Tang Monk's flesh can grant immortality, but these dancers can't do that. If they don't exercise some restraint, they will only deplete their bodies and die early.]","As soon as these two ancestors spoke, the alcohol buzz of everyone who heard them instantly sobered up! Not having time to wonder where to find immortality-granting Tang Monk's flesh, they all first drank a cup of cold tea to calm their nerves!","Once they recovered slightly, they no longer leaned back in their chairs to look at the beauties, but instantly got busy.","They either lowered their heads to drink wine... drink tea and eat meat—they didn't dare drink wine anymore, afraid that if it went to their heads, they might do something they would regret for the rest of their lives.","Or they found colleagues to chat and compete in drinking... tea!","No matter how beautifully the dancers in the hall danced, they didn't dare take another look.","If it had been in previous years, if the Emperor saw that one of his trusted ministers liked them, he really might have given a few away. That was how some of the concubines and bedmaids in the backyards of certain ministers' homes came to be.","This year, it seemed impossible. Emperor Mingxi dared to bet that if he dared to give them away, these two ancestors would gossip and scold him right to his face until he was dripping with dog's blood.","A certain divine artifact might even take revenge against him!","Shen Junshu, who had been constantly observing the changes in the hall, saw the reactions of everyone, including her Crown Prince and her father-in-law, Emperor Mingxi.","It once again refreshed her understanding of the Junior Preceptor.","This immortal lord's influence in the court of Great Yan was even greater than what her father and brothers had told her.","At this moment, Shen Junshu's half-suspended heart finally settled completely.","She carefully replaced the cold food on Yue Fuguang's table with hot dishes, and silently added a few pretty pastries.","All of this was seen by the Empress Dowager and the Empress. The two exchanged a smile, both feeling that this granddaughter-in-law/daughter-in-law was very perceptive. No wonder the Junior Preceptor treated her with special regard.","The Empress thought a bit further. In a few days, she planned to take her daughter-in-law to properly familiarize herself with the palace rules and delegate some of the power of managing the inner palace to her.","After all, she was the future Empress. It would be good for her to get the hang of it early while she was still around to guide her.","Since the Junior Preceptor had blessed her daughter-in-law and son to be of one heart as a married couple, never doubting each other, it meant that this daughter-in-law was a trustworthy person.","The Empress didn't mind slowly delegating power to her.","At this moment, Shen Junshu still didn't know that her subconscious little act of goodwill towards the Junior Preceptor would bring about such a huge unexpected joy.","After gossiping about the crowd who had almost made a fool of themselves, the system continued, [Master, did you see that short winter melon?]","What kind of melon was a short winter melon?","The farming expert, old Lord Wang Shouchen, silently searched the hall with his eyes. Finding nothing, he craned his neck to look outside the hall at the low-ranking officials who were bustling about drinking and joking.","Let alone something called a short winter melon, there wasn't even a single watermelon or pumpkin like the ones he had seen.","\"Little Zhu, are you talking about Matsuyama?\"","Wang Shouchen: So the short winter melon was referring to him! The little immortal lord and the divine artifact were indeed worthy of being master and servant; they had such a tacit understanding. They couldn't compare, they just couldn't compare!","[Yes, that's him! Master, do you know which royal family is the most bizarre among the six nations?]","\"Since you're asking like that, it must be Dongyi! What's wrong with the Dongyi royal family?\""]},{"number":272,"title":"Chapter 272: Has anyone among all the court officials fallen victim to this","paragraphs":["[Master knows that marrying cousins within three generations is considered inbreeding. But you don't know that in Dongyi, marriages between brothers and sisters are common occurrences.]","\"Are their tastes that heavy? Is it because there are no attractive men and women in other Dongyi families, or does the Dongyi royal family just prefer this and insist on keeping it all within the family?\"","[Because the Dongyi royal family wants to maintain the purity of their bloodline, they generally do not marry outsiders.","Matsuyama's father is also his uncle, and his mother is also his aunt.","Among his siblings, some are his paternal cousins, and some are his maternal cousins.","Half the reason Matsuyama was able to represent Dongyi as an envoy to Dayan this time is that he is among the taller ones of his brothers.]","Not even 1.6 meters tall is considered tall? Then wouldn't the short ones be dwarf-sized!","Yue Fuguang silently counted on her fingers, and the others, one by one, silently tried to sort out the complicated family tree.","Hiss!","Yue Fuguang suppressed the urge to click her tongue and spoke to the system, \"Little Zhu, are they trying to keep their short-melon genes from spreading?","How awfully kind of them!\"","Let alone the others, even the system could hear the thick sarcasm in her voice.","The crowd nodded silently. Speaking of nobility, across the six nations, who could compare to the Junior Preceptor, who was like an immortal descending to earth?","Even their Dayan royal family would have to step back a bowshot's distance in comparison.","[That's not it. After all, Dongyi is a small country, and you can hardly find anyone tall on the island. It's been better these past few years, but twenty years ago, Dongyi was full of short melons under 1.5 meters rolling all over the place.]","\"Why has it gotten better these years? Did they eat swelling agents and undergo genetic mutation?\"","This was the second time tonight the crowd heard the Junior Preceptor mention the word 'gene.' Although they didn't understand what it meant, they felt it was something extremely important.","[It's not a genetic mutation, but genetic improvement by bringing in excellent breeds!]","\"Little Zhu, elaborate on how they brought in breeds for improvement?\"","[Master, twenty years ago, when Emperor Mingxi's father, the old Emperor, was still on the throne, the new Emperor of Dongyi, Emon, carefully selected among the five nations and ultimately chose Dayan, which had excellent conditions in all aspects, as their breeding... seed-borrowing base!]","Yue Fuguang didn't react much, but upon hearing the words 'seed-borrowing,' many of the Dayan ministers in the hall dropped their teacups to the ground with a clatter.","The sound of each was small, but there were so many of them!","Emperor Mingxi frowned. Weren't his trusted ministers being a bit too unsteady? It was just seed-borrowing; was there a need for such a huge reaction?","It wasn't as if they were borrowing their seed, so why get so worked up?","Even though he was displeased, in order not to expose anything, he still had to cover for them!","Emperor Mingxi, full of smiles, said to the Empress beside him, \"It seems our beloved ministers have had quite a bit to drink tonight; they can't even hold their teacups steady.\"","The Empress also smiled and said, \"Today is our Imperial Son's big wedding day. The lords are happy, so it is inevitable they drank a little too much. I have already ordered the attendants to brew hangover soup.","I will have someone deliver it to the gentlemen right away.\"","Emperor Mingxi nodded in appreciation and said, \"My beloved Empress is very thoughtful!\"","As he spoke, he even took the Empress's hand, looking like a deeply affectionate couple.","Yue Fuguang said, \"I hope the Emperor can consistently maintain his respect for the Empress, and not spoil another one like Zhou Yunxin and the Ninth Prince in a few days.","He's already in his early forties; wouldn't it be better to just focus on his career?\"","\"With the current development of Great Yan, Emperor Mingxi's posthumous title might not be Emperor Yanmin as it was in the original timeline.\"","Emperor Yanmin!","Emperor Yanmin!","Min means pity and sympathy! Min means compassion and sorrow!","Emperor Mingxi's happiness lasted less than three seconds before he was utterly stunned by the posthumous title of Emperor Yanmin!","Although he was prepared for the fact that, while he wasn't the ruler who lost the nation, the blame for Great Yan's ultimate downfall would still be pinned on him by future scholars.","Not to mention he was poisoned by his own son; getting even an average posthumous title would be a blessing.","But he never expected that his posthumous title would contain so much pity!","For an emperor to be pitied by his own ministers and future generations, Emperor Mingxi felt his old face burning with shame!","Everyone in the hall silently lowered their heads. They didn't know if they would still be around when His Majesty passed away.","Or if they would have a hand in drafting this posthumous title...","Emperor Mingxi, who was almost fainting from anger, hadn't thought of this yet. He secretly clenched his fists. The Junior Preceptor was right; he needed to focus on his career. He refused to believe that if he expanded the territories and vigorously developed civil administration,","he couldn't earn a posthumous title related to civil or martial greatness after his death!","While the infuriated Emperor Mingxi secretly cheered himself on, the two ancestors over there, having lit the fire, had already shifted the topic back.","\"Little Zhu, who in the Great Yan capital has been... you know?\"","Her bright eyes swept over the officials in the hall. Those caught in her gaze inexplicably felt a bad premonition. Were they going to lose their reputations in their old age?!","All the men present, except for Emperor Mingxi, silently prayed to all the gods and Buddhas for protection. They shrank their bodies to minimize their presence, wishing they could be as petite and exquisite as Matsuyama right now.","They forgot, however, that the current topic was sparked precisely by the petite and exquisite Matsuyama.","Unfortunately, running into Yue Fuguang meant even the gods and Buddhas couldn't save them.","Ask and you shall receive. Just as everyone feared, the Junior Preceptor had no intention of letting them off. Yue Fuguang's teasing and curious voice reached their ears: \"Has anyone among the civil and military officials fallen for it?\"","Compared to the Junior Preceptor's teasing curiosity, the Divine Artifact's voice was even more cheerful and gloating: \"Master, of course there are, and more than one!\"","Not only were there some, but more than one!","The sovereign and ministers of Great Yan collectively gasped, the hairs on their bodies standing on end!","They looked at each other, their eyes revealing only one question: Is it you?","Everyone shook their heads in unison, like they were performing a pantomime. If it weren't for the prop wine cups in their hands, onlookers would have thought they were possessed or having a seizure!","Not me!","It is you!","The crowd remained silent but locked in a stalemate. People who were just acting like best brothers and chatting merrily over tea now wanted to throw the blame onto each other. The little boat of friendship capsized just like that!","\"Then tell me, who exactly is it?\"","Who was it? Before the Divine Artifact could start its socially fatal roll call, some of the guilty ones were already on the verge of a heart attack!","On such a joyous day, did they really have to discuss such a cursed topic?","The crowd looked toward their Emperor, but Emperor Mingxi turned his head to bond with the Empress.","They then looked at the protagonist of this wedding banquet, His Royal Highness the Crown Prince. If His Majesty will not intervene, will you not step up and do something, Your Highness?","The Crown Prince copied his father and silently lowered his head. Intervene?","How could he intervene? With what?","And who would dare to intervene?","If they didn't let these two ancestors enjoy their gossip to the fullest, they would become the gossip themselves! They would be stripped down until not even their underwear was left!","Although they had pretty much already been stripped to the point of losing their underwear long ago, being repeatedly dragged out and beaten like dead horses was still unacceptable!","Anyone with a shred of self-respect wouldn't be able to stand this for a second.","Shen Junshu silently watched the subtle exchanges of glances among the people in the room. For some reason, she felt an inexplicable surge of excitement.","Her pretty face flushed a rosy pink from the thrill.","Seeing this, Xie Zhiyan assumed she had simply had too much to drink and quietly handed her a cup of sobering broth.","Shen Junshu cupped the broth in her hands, staring blankly ahead, just as the high-pitched voice of Lord Artifact rang out in her ears."]},{"number":273,"title":"Chapter 273: Are you discriminating against fat people","paragraphs":["\"Master, every time the Eastern Yi delegation visits Great Yan, they always have the largest number of people among the various nations. And by 'largest', I mean the most women.","Out of the hundreds in the Eastern Yi delegation, half are beautiful women.","More than half of these women are married women from Eastern Yi. After all, childbirth for a woman is like walking through the gates of hell.","Women with prior childbirth experience have a higher chance of a smooth delivery.","As for the other young maidens, they are prepared for the high-ranking officials of Great Yan, because these lords just love that fresh and tender taste.\"","The crowd's faces flushed bright red at Lord Artifact's remark about 'loving that fresh and tender taste'. In their embarrassment, they resorted to tactical water-drinking or coughing!","No one dared to look up.","\"I have to say, they really thought it through. They took care of every aspect, no wonder they succeed!\"","\"Isn't that right! Those married women specifically target the tall and sturdy men of the Capital, especially the men in the military; they are the most popular.","As for the beautiful Eastern Yi maidens, they set their sights on the important court officials and the young men of their families, who are most fond of petite and exquisite beauties.","The people of Eastern Yi believe that the nobles in the Capital not only have noble bloodlines but are also universally smart and good-looking. By uniting with them, they will definitely produce outstanding offspring!\"","\"So, among these lords present, do some of them have children or grandchildren left behind in Eastern Yi?\"","\"Yes! He Hongguang's grandson, Liu Mingqi's granddaughter, the daughter of that Xu Qian who got struck by lightning, Zhang Tingji's son, and Wei Ping...\"","As Lord Artifact called out the names, those who couldn't hear it were fine, but those who could hear were all ashen-faced!","Cai Xian, Wei Ping, Huo Ying, and Wei Shouyi had been silently grinding their teeth since hearing their names. They wished they could drag their little brats over from the military camp right now and give them a severe beating.","That was too close!","If their little brats hadn't followed Yu Boming into the military camp, they really would have ended up with descendants in Eastern Yi this time!","Sure enough, clinging to the Junior Preceptor's golden thigh not only saved lives but also preserved their dignity in their later years.","\"According to what you're saying, Cai Bing, Huo Shui, and Wei Ping's kid—Wei Yan, right? Because they went to the military camp, won't they miss out?\"","\"They certainly will miss out! Master, you don't know this, but those three boys are quite lucky in love. Hidden among the maidens of this delegation are three individuals of extraordinary status.","They are the Imperial Princesses of Eastern Yi, Yōko, Matsuka, and Koba. These three respectively set their sights on Wei Yan, Huo Sui, and Cai Bing.","They fooled around with those playboys in the Capital for over half a month and successfully ran away pregnant.","It's a pity those three idiots didn't even know they were being played, and there was no drama of 'she flees, he pursues, and she has nowhere to hide.'","It really takes away a lot of the fun.\"","The faces of Wei Ping, Cai Xian, and Huo Ying grew even darker. They turned a blind eye to the teasing glances their colleagues cast their way, intentionally or otherwise.","They were too busy thinking about all the creative ways to beat their sons once they got home. They had no time to pay attention to those colleagues who were just enjoying the spectacle.","Far away in the military camp, the three boys simultaneously shuddered. Why did they suddenly feel a sense of impending doom?","The three looked at each other, and that ominous premonition grew even stronger!","They couldn't help but seriously recall the outrageous things they had done recently!...","General Wei was temporarily away from the camp due to the Crown Prince's grand wedding.","The day before yesterday, they secretly ate three chickens. Yesterday, they secretly roasted two rabbits. Today... looking at the knife in their hands and the tied-up little fat pig...","Could it be that today was not a good day to eat pork?","But thinking about the crime-inducing, tantalizing aroma of those young chickens and rabbits that grew up eating the grass in the Junior Preceptor's fields...","Cai Bing was the first to give in. He swallowed hard; he simply couldn't bring himself to say they should let the pig go.","Huo Sui said, \"How about we eat it first and worry later?\"","Wei Yan nodded, \"Eat it first! Besides, Baozi has already boiled the water.\"","They were just waiting for the pig to go into the pot!","To strengthen their resolve, Cai Bing added, \"Boming is still waiting! If we don't feed him well, our chances of following him to the Three Forks might fall through!\"","On this matter, without the Junior Preceptor's nod, even their high-ranking official fathers couldn't help them!","Huo Sui gritted his teeth and raised the sharp knife in his hand again, \"Whatever, let's just eat it first!\"","\"Sigh! History has slightly deviated again! Little Zhu, do you think we should call the three of them back?","After all, it's not great that they missed out on the romantic luck they were supposed to have because of me!\"","The biological fathers of the three boys silently shook their heads. There was absolutely no need for such romantic luck!","Calling them back was out of the question. The three fathers couldn't help but reach for the jade belts fastened around their waists.","They decided to personally make a trip to the military camp tomorrow. They wondered what the difference was between hitting someone with a jade belt versus whipping them with a leather belt.","The system felt that the pit it dug for the three wasn't deep enough, so it continued to fan the flames: \"If they really could be called back, then Minister Cai and the others would become relatives with the Emperor's favored official, Sima Jing, through the next generation!\"","Cough, cough, cough!","Wei Ping and the other two, who were trying to drink water to calm their nerves, nearly choked to death on a mouthful of tea!","The tea sprayed out from their noses, scattering unevenly over the food in front of them.","Great, a table full of good food was ruined.","But even if it wasn't ruined, they couldn't eat another bite anyway.","Who was Sima Jing? Just three months ago, he was still the reigning Emperor's favorite.","Now, he was a thorn in His Majesty's side. For various reasons, if the Emperor wanted to uproot this thorn completely, he couldn't act rashly just yet.","Just like now, he still had to deal courteously but insincerely with the Sima family, pretending to be close and affectionate.","The three men coincidentally looked over at Sima Jing's second son, Sima Xiong. This second young master was attending the Crown Prince's grand wedding on behalf of the Sima family.","The Emperor had arranged his seat just below the princes, and from time to time, he had to grit his teeth and reward him with a pot of wine or a plate of food to show favor.","If the three of them became relatives with the Sima family, their political careers would become increasingly narrow!","The three of them simultaneously cried out in their hearts... Junior Preceptor, save us!","\"What's going on, the Sima family also left a child in Eastern Yi? Whose is it, Sima Jing's, Sima Ying's, or that fat guy down there, Sima Xiong's?","The timing is just right, could it really be this fat guy?\"","\"Master, are you discriminating against fat people?\"","While others didn't feel much about the system's question, the first one to feel bad was Wu Yong.","He silently squeezed the soft, undulating waves of flesh on his belly—he had earned all of it through his own eating abilities, and now it was too late to lose weight!","\"Little Zhu, I'm not discriminating against fat people, I just don't like the people from the Sima family.","Speaking of fat people, look at Wu Yong, he's very fat, but he's not as greasy as a pig like this Sima Xiong.","No wonder he died of obesity just a few years after the founding of Great Wei!\"","\"Master, this person didn't die of obesity, he died from a disease caused by eating people! Though obesity does sometimes affect one's lifespan.","That little fatty Wu Yong, does Master want to help him lose some weight?\""]},{"number":274,"title":"Chapter 274: There Are Mines in the Eastern Yi Region","paragraphs":["Eaten after dying of illness? Those who had just eaten meat felt waves of nausea rising in their stomachs. Looking at the meat dishes in front of them that were perfect in color, aroma, and taste, they couldn't help but close their eyes. It seemed they would only be keeping company with vegetarian food for the next few days!","Yue Fuguang stroked her small chin, thought for a moment, and said, \"Wu Yong's figure is just a matter of one or two weight-loss pills. However...\"","Hearing the \"however,\" Wu Yong couldn't help but clutch the flesh on his body, while his father, Wu Yuanjing, gripped the chopsticks in his hand even tighter.","Snap, the chopsticks broke!","He also successfully heard Yue Fuguang's following words, \"However, I'm afraid Wu Yong might be reluctant to lose it. After all, it's meat gained through his own eating abilities, so why should he lose it?\"","[To stay alive, of course! How does Master think Wu Chengye got rid of Wu Yong back then? He fattened him up and slaughtered him like a pig!]","Fattened up and slaughtered like a pig!","Wu Yong merely trembled in fear, but the old father, Wu Yuanjing, was already shaking like he had Parkinson's. With hot tears in his eyes, he was ready to cry!","Yue Fuguang considered herself to have a heart of stone, but she just couldn't stand seeing people cry. The reason she had lost her head and jumped into the water to save someone back then was all because of tears!","Seeing the elderly Wu Yuanjing about to cry, she hurriedly said, \"That is all in the past. Now that I am here, it's impossible for him to die from being fat even if he wanted to.","I remember Wu Yong's birthday is at the end of the month? I'll just give him a few weight-loss pills then. Such a trivial matter is not worth mentioning.","Little Zhu, you've digressed again. Let's get back to the Sima family.\"","The system, accused of digressing, felt extremely wronged and crumpled up. It was aggrieved, but it endured it!","[Actually, it's Sima Jing. Eighteen years ago, the Dongyi Imperial Princess Meizi, as part of the second batch of royal family members executing their king's plan, arrived in the capital city of Shangjing with the envoy delegation.","Meizi lived up to her name. Aside from being a bit short, because her parents were not close relatives when they married, she was born exceptionally charming and moving.","In truth, the first person Meizi set her sights on was Emperor Mingxi, who was still the Crown Prince at the time.]","Emperor Mingxi: I was perfectly fine just watching the drama, why must I be dragged into this?","Am I some sort of cheap person?","The Emperor puffed up with anger. I do not discriminate against women, but Dongyi women are a no-go!","Emperor Mingxi felt Dongyi women were a no-go, but evidently, Yue Fuguang did not think so. She continued to disgust him by saying, \"So our Emperor became the secret lover of Princess Meizi?\"","Emperor Mingxi tightly gripped the Empress's hand, his eyes unconsciously glancing toward Yue Fuguang. His entire body screamed rejection: I am not, I did not, don't ruin my innocence! Stop spouting nonsense JPG.","[That didn't happen. He was intercepted halfway by Sima Jing. Sima Jing was tall and sturdy, but he had a preference for petite and exquisite women.","Princess Meizi hit exactly on his aesthetic preferences, so he snatched her right out from under his good brother.]","\"So, it turns out that from so early on, this cousin and study companion who claimed to share joys and sorrows with the Emperor had already started stealing things from him?","First stealing his brother's woman, then stealing his brother's empire. What a great scheme!\"","A faint smile curled the corners of Yue Fuguang's mouth as she desperately plunged knives into Emperor Mingxi's heart on this highly joyous day.","The actions of the ruler and ministers of the Great Yan Dynasty were a bit too slow. If they didn't hurry up and close the net on the Sima family, it would affect her subsequent missions!","[Later, after Meizi returned to her country, she gave birth to a healthy boy for Sima Jing, named Oshima, and this boy is the older brother of these three princesses.","They are all Meizi's daughters.]","\"Calculating it this way, Wei Ping and the others really are related to Sima Jing. Did Sima Jing know he had a son wandering outside?\"","Wei Ping: Junior Preceptor, could you please not only call my name at a time like this?","Do Cai Xian and Huo Ying not deserve to have their names mentioned here?","Yue Fuguang: Their names burn the mouth!","[Of course he knew. His deep cooperation with Dongyi was also because that mother and son acted as intermediaries.","This Oshima and Matsuyama are cousins. Oshima later also inherited the throne five years after the founding of the Great Wei.]","\"His father Sima Jing and his brother Sima Ying supported him to take the throne? Then how did the original king of Dongyi die?\"","[Naturally, it was the Sima family joining hands with Meizi's faction to make the move. Oh right, Xu Qian's daughter in Dongyi is also one of Oshima's many concubines.","And that son of Zhang Tingji, Gongchang, will become a famous pirate leader along the coast a few years later, nicknamed 'Sea King'.","He is also the Sima family's most important overseas partner. In the final years of the Great Yan, the Sima family allied with Gongchang to rob merchant ships in the waters near Great Yan.","While making a fortune themselves, they also dealt a massive blow to Great Yan's maritime trade and overland commerce, directly leading to a decline in the imperial court's tax revenue.]","\"The Sima family shows no mercy at all when undermining the foundations of Great Yan! Being an emperor is also a high-risk profession. One after another, they are either poisoned to death or killed by others.","Tell me, out of the emperors of these six nations, did a single one die of natural causes?\"","Emperor Mingxi: That pierced my heart, Junior Preceptor! Clutching chest and vomiting blood JPG.","However, knowing that his peers also didn't meet a good end, he felt relieved!","[Uh... this... how about we talk about it later?]","Wait for my data to recover a bit more!","The system quickly changed the subject and dropped a bombshell, [Master, Little Zhu forgot to tell you. The reason the Sima family wanted to support Oshima to take the throne.","It was also because their family and Gongchang together discovered a mountain of gold and silver mines on the reefs near Dongyi.","The Sima family first used the Dongyi people to completely wipe out Gongchang, and then stirred up internal strife within Dongyi, resulting in the king dying under a hail of stray arrows.","Oshima took the throne, and the silver mine began to be excavated.]","A silver mine? The eyes of the Great Yan ruler and ministers suddenly lit up frighteningly, sparkling with golden light and silver stars.","If it weren't for the teacups blocking their faces, their drool would probably be dripping onto the floor.","However, after their excitement, everyone quickly calmed down again. They had a fair understanding of Dongyi, and it seemed they had never heard of any reef in Dongyi called Gold Mountain!","Could it be an unnamed reef that was only given a name after the Sima family discovered the silver mine?","Emperor Mingxi and his ministers couldn't help but steal glances at Yue Fuguang, praying in their hearts that it would be great if these two ancestors could say a little more.","Would Yue Fuguang grant their wish? That was obviously impossible.","Great Yan currently lacked the ability to mine it. Knowing too much and aiming too high was meaningless. It was better to properly save up resources and strengthen themselves, then take down Dongyi early on.","The mountain of gold and silver mine was the carrot she dangled in front of the donkey that was Great Yan.","She believed that for the sky-high wealth of the gold and silver mine, they would exert their subjective initiative!","To increase the weight of the carrot, Yue Fuguang continued to ask, \"The Sima family had a silver mine, yet their nation perished so quickly? Was the silver mine's reserve insufficient?\"","[With current technology, the silver mine's reserves are enough to be mined for one or two hundred years. The Sima family's nation didn't perish because they lacked money, but because they were too wealthy.","Their family had only mined it for a dozen years before this silver mine changed owners.","However, because the Shen family replaced the Sima family, the Shen family's dynasty had the worst relationship with the Dongyi nation during the three hundred years of chaotic times.","They got no share of the silver mine, while Dongyi used it to develop and grow.","With strong soldiers and sturdy horses, Dongyi leapt to become a powerful nation, turning into a major threat to the subsequent dynasties of the Tong family, the Murong family, and others.]","After the Crown Prince's grand wedding, as the envoy delegations from various countries successively left the capital city of Shangjing, the fact that Dongyi had a mine was still sending shockwaves through the imperial court."]},{"number":275,"title":"Chapter 275: The Playboys Were Called in for a Parent-Teacher Meeting","paragraphs":["Knowing that their neighbor Nanzhao possessed large reserves of high-quality iron ore, Huo Ying dispatched men disguised as bandits. Not only did they find iron ore on the side close to Nanzhao, but they also discovered a copper mine in the no man's land near Xiqiang!","Now, knowing that their neighbor across the sea, Dongyi, had a large silver mine, the entire Dayan dynasty, from the emperor to the officials, from civil servants to military generals, grew restless.","The originally vague idea of expanding their territory now began to surface uncontrollably.","Especially after the emperor and his officials saw the unprecedentedly excellent growth of crops on the imperial estate, this thought could not be suppressed at all.","If it weren't for the memory of a severe drought that swept the entire region in the eighth year of Yuankang, Emperor Mingxi might have truly let the silver mine go to his head.","Even so, Emperor Mingxi couldn't help but drink a few extra cups upon returning to the palace.","The next day, Yue Fuguang returned to her estate completely baffled, bringing with her two carriages full of palace specialties.","Emperor Mingxi was now very accustomed to throwing money at her!","Therefore, she didn't care about the reason. Since it was given, she accepted it; after all, gold, silver, and jewels wouldn't bite.","The restlessness in the imperial court was quickly noticed by sensitive officials, but tracing the root cause proved impossible.","Even Zhang Tingji, who had just started attending court after recovering from illness, noticed something was amiss.","Especially the way some colleagues looked at him; whenever he thought about it, he felt a bit creeped out.","Even Huang Shouping, who had once fought alongside him, was clearly distancing himself, looking as if he didn't want to speak much, leaving Zhang Tingji feeling even more uncertain.","Just as his multiple attempts to investigate yielded no results, a piece of news circulated throughout the Dayan court, from top to bottom.","The Fourth Prince and the Ninth Prince had gifted the Crown Prince a wondrous book as a wedding present.","This book recorded many extraordinary techniques, among which were papermaking and a technique called movable type printing.","Because the Six Kingdoms had possessed paper for a long time, albeit at a higher price, no one paid attention to the papermaking technique yet. Instead, all focus was placed on the new, more efficient, and cheaper printing technology.","It wouldn't be until a few months later, when large quantities of cheap paper flooded the market, that certain people would truly start to panic.","Of course, right now, faced with the more efficient and cheaper movable type printing technology, those who should panic were already panicking!","While others were either panicking or excitedly anticipating, Yue Fuguang noticed another minor incident.","A theft occurred in the military camp. The stolen items weren't valuables; they were just a few chickens, a few rabbits, and two pigs.","A group of young masters, including Yu Boming, collectively had their parents called in.","Yue Fuguang, accompanying her grandfather and second uncle as Yu Boming's guardians, went to the new recruit camp on the outskirts of the city.","On the way, they coincidentally ran into Wei Ping, Huo Ying, Cai Xian, Bao Yuanjun and his son, along with several other parents.","When everyone met and greeted each other, the atmosphere was inevitably awkward.","This was the first time Yue Fuguang had visited a military camp in both her lifetimes combined.","From a distance, she saw a plaque above the camp gates, with a few vigorous and powerful characters written in red paint: Right Martial Guard New Army Camp.","Yue Fuguang recognized this handwriting; it was Emperor Mingxi's.","Standing at the gate, Wei Shouyi and the others saw the leading carriage, and a flash of surprise crossed their bronzed faces.","This was followed by immense joy. From his grinning teeth to his quivering beard, from the crinkled lines on his face to his sparkling eyes, everything indicated his delighted mood.","The lieutenants and captains were surprised to see their general suddenly dash out, but they quickly followed, only half a step behind.","Was their general a bit too happy today?","Was it because high-ranking officials were visiting today?","They first saw Minister Huo, but their general didn't even glance at the Minister, making a beeline for the most beautiful carriage.","From its exterior, the carriage looked exquisite and beautiful, very much like a lady's conveyance.","Before they could think further, a beautiful and delicate little girl stepped out from inside.","Seeing her face and the iconic lotus mark on her forehead, they instantly understood her identity.","They also instantly understood why their general was so unusually happy.","Genuine smiles unconsciously appeared on their faces as well.","Yue Fuguang: This is the look of seeing a generous and easygoing financial backer!","The group was led inside by Wei Shouyi. At every stop, he enthusiastically and carefully introduced the area.","It could be said that he was extremely respectful to Yue Fuguang, his half financial backer!","Junior Preceptor, those little rascals who caused trouble are waiting on the drill ground.","Wei Shouyi led the crowd toward the drill ground.","Initially, Yu Boming and the others had acted like dead pigs unafraid of boiling water, just waiting for General Wei's judgment.","Later, upon hearing that General Wei had summoned their parents, they began to feel anxious, readying themselves to be beaten and scolded.","Now, baking under the sun, they all hung their heads, devoid of energy.","Just as the three boys with sore butts leaned against each other, almost falling asleep, they saw a group of people approaching from the entrance of the training ground in the distance.","Looking over, before the group even got close, they spotted a tiny yet impossible-to-ignore beautiful figure mixed among the elders.","Junior Preceptor!","Sister!","The group, already anxious and prepared for the worst, instantly changed expressions. It could only be said that there was no worst, only worse!","Exchanging a tacit glance, they all revealed expressions uglier than crying. The still-injured trio of Cai Bing, Huo Shui, and Wei Yan looked toward Yu Boming for help.","Yu Boming: Who can I save? I am a mud idol crossing the river myself! Groundhog scream JPG.","As the crowd approached and that tiny figure became clearer, those with slightly thinner skin had already covered their faces with their hands.","They were truly wronged. They had just helped tend the fire and ended up getting a sip of soup, yet their parents were called in too.","They accepted having their parents called; after all, they were brothers!","But losing face in front of the Junior Preceptor today made them really want to find a hole to crawl into!","Lin Huaijing, the youngest son of Deputy Supervisor of the Household Lin Congxue, peeked through his fingers at his father.","Huh, his father didn't seem as angry as he had imagined. In fact, when looking at him, there was a rare hint of approval!","Did he actually do the right thing this time?","Lin Huaijing silently smacked his lips. Even though he only got a little soup, it was still soup, and soaking steamed buns and flatbreads in it was truly delicious!","He could eat eight, nine, or ten of them in one meal. That amount of food would be enough for him to eat for two days at home!","Yue Fuguang didn't look at her second brother, Yu Boming, who was already awkwardly drawing circles on the ground with his foot.","The first ones she noticed were Cai Bing, Huo Shui, and Wei Yan, who were grimacing and trying hard to stand straight, but had to stick their butts out.","If their parents hadn't been called, these three wouldn't have been able to get out of bed today.","Yue Fuguang's visibly curious expression caused Wei Ping, Huo Ying, and Cai Xian a wave of awkward guilt.","A few days ago, they had indeed been a bit heavy-handed with the brats because of the seed-borrowing incident. But today, upon learning that the boys had also stolen and eaten livestock from the military camp's farm.","They suddenly felt that they had been too light-handed back then!","However, faced with the Junior Preceptor's puzzled expression, they silently turned their heads away. The brats had thick skin and flesh; they would recover in ten days or half a month, no big deal!"]},{"number":276,"title":"Chapter 276: Junior Preceptor","paragraphs":["[Master, the injuries on Cai Bing, Huo Shui, and Wei Yan's butts and backs are all from a father's love!]","The three of them blushed. Couldn't the Divine Artifact keep its mouth shut? Why would it tell the Lord Junior Preceptor such things!","\"A father's love\" indeed! This love was too heavy; they didn't want it! (Disgusted face JPG)","Meanwhile, the three old fathers silently nodded. Yes, yes, yes, sparing the rod spoils the child; the harder the beating, the deeper the love!","\"Greetings, Lord Junior Preceptor!\"","\"Grandfather!\"","\"Father!\"","\"Greetings, my lords!\"","Though they were dandies, their manners were impeccable. Upon seeing the crowd, regardless of whether they were about to be beaten, they made sure to pay their respects first.","Wei Ping spoke first, \"I heard that you boys used items in the camp without your superiors' permission. Is this true?\"","Although Wei Ping questioned them with a stern face, he mentioned neither stealing nor theft, and he used the word items instead of property.","It was a well-intentioned effort, secretly protecting the reputations of these dandies!","After all, the military camp was a restricted area. Even if they had merely eaten a few chickens, rabbits, and pigs, if taken seriously, it was a crime punishable by military law.","Taking a beating was a small matter, but ruining their reputations, being kicked out of the camp, or leaving a bad impression on the Lord Junior Preceptor would be a huge deal!","Wei Yan had secretly mentioned to him that he wanted to go to the Sancha region, and he naturally highly approved of his second son's choice.","As long as this boy successfully got on the Lord Junior Preceptor's good side, his future would be secure!","Wei Shouyi naturally understood the underlying meaning in Wei Ping's words.","He had only called their parents over to put on a show for outsiders and had never intended to punish the boys severely.","Now that the Lord Junior Preceptor had been drawn here, it was truly an unexpected pleasant surprise.","Huo Ying also chimed in, \"These boys just lack discipline.\"","He circled around Huo Shui, and just as he was about to kick out his foot, he noticed Yue Fuguang staring at him with burning eyes.","Ahem!","\"Nurture your body well and recover!\" Huo Ying coughed lightly, silently retracting his foot when it was only a centimeter away from Huo Shui's injured butt.","Changing his kick to a pat, he slapped his large hand heavily on his son's shoulder, making Huo Sui's body bob up and down with each strike.","Cai Xian also nodded. They indeed needed to recover quickly, otherwise, they might really miss the opportunity to go to the Sancha region.","Yu Shuchun also said, \"Yu Boming, in front of your grandfather and sister, what do you have to say for yourself?\"","Yu Boming's toes had already awkwardly dug out the layout of a two-courtyard estate on the ground. If Yu Shuchun had asked him any later, he probably would have dug out a three-courtyard mansion.","Now hearing his father's question, Yu Boming stood up straight, his face flushed red.","With his head initially lowered, he quickly glanced up at Yue Fuguang and Yu Chongshan, stammering, \"I... I was wrong. I let down my family's trust and my sister's cultivation!\"","By the end of his sentence, tears were about to fall.","Yu Shuchun clicked his tongue. If Fuguang wasn't here today, he would definitely have taught this boy a lesson.","He hadn't even raised a hand yet, and the boy was already acting aggrieved!","Seeing Yu Boming's red face and red-rimmed eyes, Yue Fuguang's tone suddenly shifted as she smiled and asked, \"Second Brother, was the food tasty?\"","Gulp, gulp!","It would have been fine if she hadn't asked, but the moment she did, the whole group couldn't help but swallow their saliva.","[Master, what they secretly ate were chickens and rabbits that grew up eating grass watered by spiritual rain. The taste is naturally more delicious than ordinary ones.]","It would have been fine if the system hadn't spoken, but the moment it did, this group of parents all silently looked at Wei Shouyi.","We are your superiors and colleagues after all. We came all this way, shouldn't you host us properly?","At this point, the situation was successfully derailed by a single sentence from Yue Fuguang.","The original trial assembly suddenly changed its tune, turning into a military camp inspection.","Wei Shouyi thought: Don't you guys just want to check out the livestock farm and grab a bite before leaving? As if no one could tell!","As for the erring dandies, Wei Shouyi asked Yue Fuguang, their half-sugar-daddy of a sponsor, how to handle them.","Technically, she did have the actual authority to deal with them. Since the camp's establishment, Emperor Mingxi had granted her full administrative power over the entire military camp. She was arguably the superior of all the officers and soldiers.","It was just that her personality—put politely, she didn't covet power; put bluntly, she was a slacker who hated managing things—meant that Wei Shouyi had always been fully in charge.","Since she was present today, Wei Shouyi naturally wouldn't overstep his bounds.","Yue Fuguang looked at the boys and said, \"Although the matter isn't big, we cannot let it go lightly.\"","Hearing her words, their faces turned pale. It wasn't that they feared military punishment, but rather they worried that because of this incident, the Lord Junior Preceptor would view them in a bad light.","Did that mean all of them, except Yu Boming, had lost their chance to go to the Sancha region to gild their resumes?","\"However,\" seeing their drastically changed expressions, Yue Fuguang curled her lips into a smile and continued, \"However, considering it is their first offense, they will be punished by cleaning the pigpens and teaching the soldiers how to read and write for half an hour every day.\"","\"Do any of you have objections?\" She dropped her smile, her face filled with the majesty of a superior. The boys even felt a pressure from her that surpassed their Emperor's.","Led by Bao Zihui and Yu Boming, the group quickly knelt on one knee, cupped their fists, and said, \"We obey the Lord Junior Preceptor's command!\"","\"We obey the Lord Junior Preceptor's command!\"","The dozen or so people shouted with the momentum of dozens, causing the soldiers training in the distance to turn their heads.","Lord Junior Preceptor?","The Lord Junior Preceptor had come to their military camp?","Because Yue Fuguang was young and short, she and the two behind her, Shen Chunying and Liu Wei, were surrounded in the circle, so the people training in the distance didn't see her.","Who knew that Yu Boming and the others' shouts would expose her whereabouts.","The soldiers training on the martial arts field slowly gravitated toward their group as they practiced.","The Lord Junior Preceptor—leaving aside the fame of the potatoes, just the fact that a part of their three daily meals came from her was enough to fill their hearts with gratitude.","Regarding their diet, although it was everyone's first time serving as soldiers and eating military rations, whose village or town didn't have a few grunts eating military grain?","Even if they hadn't seen the food firsthand, they had heard plenty about it.","Not to mention, their superiors were elites transferred from other military camps. Whenever mealtime arrived, they would talk about their past lives in other camps.","They all sighed with emotion that life in the new recruit camp was much better!","They didn't even compare it to other armies; they just compared it to their own family's meals. During busy seasons, they ate solid food; during idle seasons, they ate watery porridge, let alone having three full meals a day.","That was a treatment reserved only for when doing heavy physical labor.","As for meat, they used to eat it only two or three times a year at home. They might have it a few more times in a good harvest year, but in a bad year, surviving without starving or freezing to death was already a blessing, let alone eating meat.","But now, they could eat it once every two or three days, and it was always big chunks of fatty meat.","They had also heard General Wei say that once the adjacent livestock farm reached a proper scale, they would be able to eat meat every day.","They walked past there every day, eagerly awaiting that day.","However, some people clearly thought more and further ahead. Unlike those who only waited to eat meat every day, they thought more about how to be selected to go to the Sancha region.","The General had also said that for their ten thousand men, apart from the food, everything else—whether it was training, armor, weapons, or military pay and other treatments—was incomparable to anywhere else.","And all of this was connected to only one person: Junior Preceptor Yue!","Although they all appeared to be on equal footing right now, the clever ones among them knew perfectly well that only those heading to Sancha could truly be considered Junior Preceptor Yue's inner circle—her own people!","And they wanted nothing more than to become the Junior Preceptor's own people."]},{"number":277,"title":"Chapter 277: Strengthen the body and cultivate the mind.","paragraphs":["To become one of the Junior Preceptor's own people, one had to stand out from ten thousand others.","Selecting five thousand out of ten thousand—a one-in-two chance seemed high, but who could guarantee they wouldn't be among the five thousand left behind?","General Wei had said they would depart in late May. It was already mid-April; little time remained for the selection, yet the criteria had still not been finalized.","Those who had ambitions couldn't help but feel uncertain.","With the Junior Preceptor visiting the military camp today, it would be wonderful if they could take the opportunity to ask!","Yue Fuguang was still unaware of the little schemes of the soldiers slowly approaching from a distance.","She followed the crowd toward the armory.","Master, Wei Shouyi and the others are already giving these men ideological education classes according to your requirements. Why did you also punish Yu Boming and his group by making them teach the ordinary soldiers how to read and write? Do you actually expect them to take the imperial examinations?","The crowd secretly nodded in agreement; their hearts were also full of doubts.","The ideological education classes were showing initial results. Given their current treatment, these men were destined to be slaughtering brutes on the battlefield. If their martial skills weren't perfected, a single battle could wipe them out.","Was it really necessary for the Junior Preceptor to pour so much effort into teaching them to read and write?","The crowd hadn't realized it yet, but they subconsciously viewed these men as expendable supplies and slightly capable cannon fodder.","Yu Boming and the others had agreed readily and would execute the order without compromise, but their thoughts were similar to their fathers': was it necessary to make these killing machines literate?","Little Zhu, since we plan to train a formidable army for fun, we can't end up making them just like the rest of Great Yan's troops.","At the very least, ideologically, they must know that being a soldier isn't just about getting fed.","They must at least know who they are and where they come from.","Even when they step onto the battlefield in the future, they must be clear about what and who they are fighting for!","Even if death is inevitable, they shouldn't die in ignorant obscurity.","This is the original intention of the ideological education.","Wei Shouyi and Huo Ying's hearts skipped a beat. So the Junior Preceptor's ideological education for the grunts had such profound meaning!","Great Yan should have more heroic and passionate warriors, rather than ignorant fools or those who only seek to protect themselves, soft and overly sentimental.","Master, even if you give these people ideological education, they won't become an army like Great Xia's. Serving the country and the people, generous and unyielding, strictly disciplined, not taking a single needle or thread from the commoners—do you think that's possible?","Wei Shouyi thought to himself that strict discipline could probably be achieved, but not taking a single needle or thread from the commoners? That was truly too difficult.","After breaching a city, looting the commoners was almost an unspoken rule; the only difference was the extent, which depended on the commander.","As for serving the country and the people? Who became a soldier if not for the food and pay?","It is indeed difficult to make them do that, which is also why I am reluctant to interact with them too much.","However, none of this affects my original intention to civilize their minds while toughening their bodies.","Perhaps after some of them learn to read and write, their sense of honor and their moral bottom line will be higher, making the education worthwhile.","Master, when it comes to reading a lot, who can compare to the various lords in the imperial court? And when it comes to propriety, justice, integrity, honor, and racing to the bottom of morality, who can match them?","The system's words made the faces of everyone behind her turn bright red, without exception.","Wei Shouyi, who was still explaining the uses of the various barracks, subconsciously lowered his voice.","He was just a boorish fellow who knew a few more words than most. His current achievements, aside from his father's struggles, were earned through his own fighting, spear and sword.","He felt the Divine Artifact's words were flawless!","Meanwhile, Yu Boming and Cai Bing, hearing their fathers' generation being scolded, consciously and silently distanced themselves from the crowd. Today they dared to watch their own fathers become a joke.","Their fathers couldn't do anything about his sister or the Junior Preceptor, but they could absolutely guarantee to turn them into jokes tomorrow!","That's different. Those people have read too many books and read away their conscience.","Besides, when I told Second Brother and the others to teach the soldiers how to read and write, I also insisted on the principle of voluntariness.","I don't require everyone to go, but my five thousand men must all know the most basic characters. If one year isn't enough, then two.","Sancha Land does not want trash, nor does it raise illiterates!","Yue Fuguang wept silently in her heart. What could she do? The system's tasks were too tricky; for the sake of points, she had no choice but to do it!","System, we can set the definition of an illiterate ourselves, right?","Host, to what extent do you think cultured should be when building a ten-thousand-strong army with thoughts and culture?","Being able to simply read and write should be enough, right? Yue Fuguang answered with a guilty conscience. Equating basic literacy with being cultured was a forced move on her part.","A ten-thousand-strong army—even if her forces continued to grow in the future, gathering the best of the best into one army, having them be both ideological and cultured would be quite difficult to achieve without lowering the standards.","System: The host is bullying me for reading too little again!","Hearing Yue Fuguang mention Sancha Land and realizing they would set off next month, the crowd couldn't help but feel a stir in their hearts.","Wei Shouyi couldn't help but change the subject, saying, By the way, Junior Preceptor, there are only a few days left until the selection of personnel to be stationed at Sancha Land. I wonder if you have any selection criteria?","Wei Yan, Huo Sui, and the others who had originally been trailing behind silently inched closer to the front, their ears perked up high.","Yue Fuguang thought for a moment and said, \"Based on all the assessments, including the ideological education test, I will take the top seven thousand people. From those seven thousand, I will then select five thousand.\"","[Master, me, me, me! Little Zhu can distinguish the loyal from the treacherous with just a glance. No matter how outstanding they are, we cannot accept anyone whose heart is not with you, Master!]","\"Alright, I will listen to you!\"","\"Lord Junior Preceptor, do you think we can go?\" The one who spoke up was the youngest, Lin Huaijing.","Wei Yan and the others looked in astonishment at this usually meek kid. To think that this guy, who usually only got to drink the broth while others ate the meat, would be so bold today!","Good lad, even with the courage of a mouse, he dared to step up and ask a question before his older brothers. They had truly underestimated him!","Seeing Yue Fuguang look his way, Lin Huaijing immediately introduced himself, \"Lin Huaijing greets the Lord Junior Preceptor.\"","His eyes were full of stars as he looked at Yue Fuguang. She could read the meaning behind his gaze: pure admiration for the strong!","Lin Congxue shot his youngest son another appreciative glance and said, \"Lord Junior Preceptor, this is my unworthy youngest son. Please excuse his impudence!\"","Lin Huaijing?","On the virtual panel in front of Yue Fuguang, his favorability score of seventy-eight and his life story were displayed...","\"Whether it is food or entertainment, the Sancha region cannot even compare to a ten-thousandth of the capital. Besides you all, there probably will not be many people there. The environment is harsh, and the climate is brutal. Lin Huaijing, are you sure you want to go?\"","Lin Huaijing's gaze was resolute. \"Lord Junior Preceptor, Huaijing wants to go! I am not afraid of hardship!\"","Fifteen years old, right at the rebellious age. But this kid was a talent. Since he had delivered himself to her doorstep, there was no reason to turn him away.","Thus, a gentle smile graced her lips. \"Whether the others can go is still uncertain, but if you truly want to go, it is naturally not a problem.\"","She then turned to Yu Boming and said, \"Second Brother, please guide him and take him under your wing from now on.\"","Having Yu Boming look after him meant that she was officially drawing him into their inner circle."]},{"number":278,"title":"Chapter 278: Don't I Have Any Pride","paragraphs":["Clang! Clang!","Lin Huaijing, caught completely off guard, was left dizzy by the two massive surprises Yue Fuguang had just dropped on him. He stood frozen on the spot, eyes wide, momentarily speechless.","It was his father, Lin Congxue, who couldn't bear to watch anymore. Both amused and exasperated, he gave his son a light kick on the backside and reminded him, \"You silly boy, aren't you going to thank the Young Tutor?\"","Prompted by his father, Lin Huaijing quickly snapped back to his senses and immediately bowed. \"Huaijing... thanks... thanks the Young Tutor!\"","His face flushed red with excitement, his eyes crinkled into crescent moons from smiling so hard, and his grin was so wide it showed his pink gums.","Ignoring Lin Huaijing, who was grinning like a total fool, Yu Boming only spoke to Yue Fuguang, \"Don't worry, little sister, your second brother will definitely take good care of this kid!\"","Yue Fuguang nodded and said with the serious air of a little adult, \"I'll give Second Brother an extra chicken drumstick later.\"","When it came to giving extra chicken drumsticks, Yue Fuguang was a girl of her word. Once all the dishes were served, she picked up the untouched drumstick from her own bowl and placed it into Yu Boming's.","\"Smells amazing!\" Cai Xian and the others swallowed hard as they took in the mouthwatering aromas of the whole roasted rabbit, braised chicken, and braised pork. Although the preparation was not as refined as what they usually ate, the rich, tantalizing scents were simply irresistible.","The parents finally understood why these little brats, who were usually so picky about their finely cooked meals at home, would sneak off to steal live poultry from the pastures.","These kids, who normally wouldn't lift a finger to do any chores, actually rolled up their sleeves to cook for themselves just to get a bite of this food.","Lin Congxue had heard his younger son mention that he had only managed to get a little bit of soup at the time.","However, if they were back in their youth facing such delicacies, they would have acted even worse than the kids did. Even just drinking the soup would be worth it!","The little brats had only stolen a few birds to eat. This showed that the military camp's training, especially the ideological education, was already starting to show results on these playboy sons.","Wei Shouyi laughed and said, \"This is also my, Lao Wei's, first time eating these. It's not like they raised these poultry and livestock, so how did those little brats know they tasted so good?\"","Huo Sui and the others silently looked toward Yu Boming.","Yu Boming's face turned red. He nearly buried his head in his bowl, almost making intimate contact with the chicken drumstick Yue Fuguang had given him.","Just as everyone was about to start eating, the voice of the Divine Artifact rang out in their ears.","[Master, the wild herb and vegetable soup is poisoned.]","Yue Fuguang's hand, reaching for the soup bowl, only paused for a brief second before she continued serving herself soup, asking in her mind, \"Little Zhu, aside from the soup, are any of the other dishes poisoned?\"","[No, only the soup has been laced with a deadly poison called Morning Fragrance Powder.]","The people at the two tables felt their hearts sink upon hearing that the soup was poisoned, especially with an incurable, deadly poison like Morning Fragrance Powder. The chopsticks in their hands almost dropped to the floor.","Wei Shouyi, in particular, had his head bowed, his face full of gloom.","Poisoning the food at his banquet, and targeting the Young Tutor no less! This was basically someone thinking his Lao Wei family and all nine generations of his kin were living too comfortably!","If you asked him how he knew the poison was aimed at Yue Fuguang, it was because he had specifically ordered the kitchen to make this bowl of soup for the Young Tutor.","Precisely because he knew she usually liked eating these fresh wild herbs and seasonal vegetables, this bowl of soup was prepared today.","Wei Shouyi's fists cracked as he clenched them tightly. In his mind, he carefully went over all the kitchen staff, from the head chef to the helpers, their information flashing through his head one by one.","Thinking about it now, everyone seemed like a suspect.","Seeing Yue Fuguang casually serving herself soup as if nothing was wrong, the crowd couldn't help but feel nervous, even though they knew the Divine Artifact had an antidote pill.","Yu Chongshan steadied his nerves and said with a smile, \"Fuguang, Grandfather also wants some soup. Could you give Grandfather the soup in your bowl?\"","Yue Fuguang paused for a moment, quickly realizing the reason behind his request. She smiled and handed the bowl to Yu Chongshan, saying, \"Here you go, Grandfather. This soup was flavored with chicken broth, so it must be absolutely delicious.\"","Yu Chongshan smiled back. \"Since Fuguang says it's good, Grandfather will have to drink a couple more bowls.\"","Seeing that the soup was already in Yu Chongshan's hands, Cai Bing and the others, who had originally wanted to seize the chance to show off their loyalty, instantly gave up.","Even his own biological son didn't get a turn, so how could it be their turn to show off?","\"Little Zhu, drop half an antidote pill into the soup.\"","[Master, the poison has been neutralized. However, the poisoner is about to run away.]","Still gnawing on a chicken wing, Wei Shouyi slapped his thigh and said, \"Oh my, there's still one dish that hasn't been served. I'll go hurry them up.\"","Huo Ying made a symbolic gesture to stop him and asked, \"What dish is taking so long that you need to go hurry them up yourself? Can't you just send a personal guard?\"","Wei Ping also chimed in, \"Exactly, Lao Wei. The head chef in your camp is slacking!\"","Wei Shouyi smiled and replied, \"It's the spring bamboo shoots we dug up near the mountain yesterday. The head chef is stewing them with old duck to make a soup. I'll go urge them along. You guys eat first, I'll be right back.\"","[Master, do you think Lao Wei will be able to figure out that the old woman working as a kitchen helper is a spy?]","\"Not necessarily. If he was going to notice, he would have noticed long ago.\"","[True. That old woman is actually a man in disguise. Even though his disguise skills are top-notch, the fact that Lao Wei and the others haven't noticed anything unusual after all these days means their vigilance is really quite poor!]","Wei Shouyi, who hadn't gone far, suddenly looked a bit sheepish upon hearing the Divine Artifact's critique.","Leaving the dining hall, he sprinted toward the kitchen. The images of the few old women working as kitchen helpers flashed through his mind, and he quickly figured out who the biggest suspect was.","This person lived in a nearby village, had a family with sons and daughters. If it weren't for the two ancestors bringing it up, he truly never would have suspected this kind of peasant woman who so obviously had vulnerabilities!","\"A military camp is a crucial area; using outsiders is indeed prone to causing problems. If we employ the family members of trusted soldiers and have them all live together in a centralized area to prevent them from being coerced, it should be much safer.\"","Everyone nodded in agreement in their hearts upon hearing this. The Young Tutor's idea was excellent.","Having the whole family in the military camp served as both a hostage situation and a form of protection. Moreover, the pastures wouldn't need to be entirely managed and fed by soldiers anymore; they could easily hire these family members.","Finding a livelihood for their families would only make the soldiers more loyal, and they would hope for the military camp's success even more than outsiders, ensuring they could sustain themselves for a long time.","\"Little Zhu, do you know who is trying to make a move on me this time? Also, that old woman who is actually a man in disguise—hiding in the military camp for so long couldn't have been just to wait for me, right?\"","[Master, you were just a target of opportunity. His original purpose for sneaking in was to gather intelligence on the new military camp and its daily training routines.","However, Lao Wei is quite strict with the management of non-military personnel. Separated by high walls, they couldn't see what was going on inside at all.","This guy has been here for months and hasn't obtained a single piece of useful information. He was almost in despair, but then he finally waited until a big fish worth a thousand pieces of gold like you came along!]","\"My life is only worth a thousand gold pieces? Who are they looking down on?\"","Yue Fuguang was very angry, while the people around her were quite flustered. Ancestor, is this really the time to focus on how much your life is worth?","However, a small voice in their hearts quietly agreed that it was indeed too low an offer. In their eyes, a thousand pieces of gold couldn't even buy a single strand of the Young Tutor's hair.","[Exactly! By that calculation, Master's life isn't even as valuable as the half an antidote pill Little Zhu just dropped into the bowl. It's simply outrageous!]","The system flattered her sycophantically, but its bootlicking clearly hit a sore spot.","Yue Fuguang: There's really no need for such a comparison! Don't I need to save face?","Happy New Year's Day, everyone!","May your 2026 be filled with happiness, health, prosperity, good luck, peace, and joy...","May everything go your way, and may your years be forever free of worry!"]},{"number":279,"title":"Chapter 279: In the end, it's just about stepping on my life to boost his reputation, isn't it","paragraphs":["[Master, Little Zhu is telling you, this person is a fish that slipped through the net of the Wind and Rain Pavilion, because he came in when you struck the Cao family with lightning. As a result, he actually managed to avoid the imperial court's hunt for the pavilion's remnants.","This person is named Wu Lao'er, a trusted aide of the old pavilion master, Feng Yang.","His mission to infiltrate the recruit camp is only known to the current pavilion master, Luo Feng, and the old master, Feng Yang.","That Luo Feng is tight-lipped; even under severe torture, he didn't give him up. It shows he's a die-hard villain.","Today, because of a bowl of soup, this Wu Lao'er unexpectedly learned that you came to the military camp and are staying for lunch. Naturally, he felt his chance to kill you had arrived.","Although poisoning you is a bit risky, the rewards are equally great. His eagerness to make a major contribution drove him to take the desperate risk of poisoning you.]","\"Little Zhu, doesn't Wu Lao'er know that the Wind and Rain Pavilion has already been destroyed? Their pavilion master, vice pavilion master, and all the assassins, except for the 'temps', have all been either captured or killed.","Even if he succeeds, who is he going to claim his reward from?\"","[Master, the news of the Great Yan's Wind and Rain Pavilion being uprooted has not only spread through every street and alley of Shangjing City, but the other five nations know about it too.","They have also begun to encircle and intercept the Wind and Rain Pavilions within their own borders.","It can be said that except for the headquarters in Western Qiang, the pavilions in the other four nations are truly tottering in the wind and rain.","However, it is only tottering; the foundation of the Wind and Rain Pavilion hasn't been harmed.","Therefore, Wu Lao'er, who knows the inside story of the pavilion very well, is clear that as long as he can successfully escape, find the contact person outside, travel west, and safely reach Western Qiang, he will be the number one hero.","His name will become famous not only in the Wind and Rain Pavilion but also in Youtan and the Tianxing Pavilion after a single battle.]","\"In the end, he just wants to step on my life to make a name for himself!\"","Uh, there is nothing wrong with this summary!","The system laughed and immediately said, [But Master, with me, the Realm-Breaking Bead, by your side, even if you make enemies of the whole world, you will remain completely unharmed and retreat safely.]","\"Why should I retreat? Even if my divine power is gone, I still have my godhood. This mortal flesh and blood is nothing but a shackle confining me now.","Once I break free from this shackle, could this tiny mortal realm withstand even a single strike from me?","Besides, why would I make enemies of the whole world for no reason? Do I have too much free time?\"","[Hehehe, Master, it's just a figure of speech!","Besides, with Little Zhu here, why would a tiny mortal realm require you to personally take action?","Wouldn't that be a slap to Little Zhu's face?]","The crowd was already listening with trepidation, especially the three generations of the Yu family: Yu Chongshan, Yu Shuchun, and Yu Boming.","They were terrified that if Yue Fuguang got unhappy and really broke free from her 'shackles', wouldn't their big granddaughter, niece, or sister be shattered into pieces?","Several people glared at Wei Ping and Cai Xian with condemnation. The Wind and Rain Pavilion was the responsibility of these two guys.","They couldn't even interrogate a single Luo Feng properly, allowing the Junior Preceptor to fall into 'danger'. Truly incompetent!","Wei Ping and Cai Xian also looked embarrassed, and even the young brothers Wei Yan and Cai Bing suddenly felt they couldn't lift their heads in front of their brothers.","It was bad enough that their fathers were unhelpful, but they were holding everyone back. They suddenly felt their chances of going to the Three Forks were even slimmer.","Looking at Lin Huaijing, who was sitting next to Yu Boming eating and drinking well, the brothers in distress got even redder eyes!","Meanwhile, Shen Chunying and Liu Wei, the two personal guards, had strikingly bright eyes. Their Junior Preceptor was simply too domineering.","Even if she made enemies of the people of the world, she wouldn't care at all. Was this the true portrayal of what Yu Huaixian said about immortals viewing mortals as ants?","Sitting opposite them, Yu Huaixian saw their expressions and almost couldn't resist rolling his eyes.","These people's understanding of his little cousin was still too superficial.","The name of an immortal brooks no blasphemy, mortals must maintain reverence, and those who act recklessly will surely be condemned. This was what they should do as guards.","He gave the two a meaningful look, silently retreated from the dining room, and headed toward the kitchen.","As for the people still worrying beside Yue Fuguang, hearing the divine artifact speaking with the sycophantic tone of Eunuch Qian, they almost couldn't help but laugh out loud.","[But Master is right.] The system continued to flatter, [We, master and servant, will live a low-profile life in this incarnation and safely complete this tribulation.","When Master successfully returns to Mount Lingxu, it will be the time for your promotion to High God.]","Yue Fuguang gave a reserved sound of agreement, feeling that enough groundwork had been laid, and said, \"Little Zhu, I'll leave that person to you. I permit you to search his soul.","When the time comes, send the information you get anonymously to Wei Ping and Cai Xian, one copy each.\"","[Rest assured, Master. If these two guys still can't get it right this time, watch how I deal with them, hmph!]","Wei Ping and Cai Xian couldn't help shrinking their necks, instantly feeling a chill from head to toe. It was only mid-spring, but they broke out in a cold sweat!","They weren't afraid that the two ancestors would actually take their lives, but the methods of the divine artifact...","It didn't take lives, it took face!","Thinking of the fates of Wu Shouping and Zhang Tingji, as well as Xu Qian who was lying in bed ruined and waiting to die, the two men could hardly sit still.","Before the two could take any action, Wei Shouyi walked in carrying a clay pot.","He looked embarrassed and said, \"Junior Preceptor, my lords, sorry for the wait.\"","He placed the fresh bamboo shoot and old duck stew in front of Yue Fuguang and said, \"Something happened to a kitchen helper, which is why the food was served a bit slow.\"","The crowd, already curious about the outcome, immediately asked, \"General Wei, what happened in the kitchen? Is it serious?\"","\"Yes, the military camp is a vital area and cannot be neglected. Small matters are also big matters. Lao Wei, quickly tell us!\" Their faces full of eager gossip were fully revealed.","Wei Shouyi thought to himself: If you guys reigned in those eager expressions of wanting to watch a show, I, Lao Wei, might actually believe you!","However, the complexions of Minister Cai and Deputy Minister Wei didn't look good. Could the incident in the kitchen be related to them?","Wei Shouyi looked like a rough man, but he was actually very meticulous. With just a glance, he noticed something was off with these two.","Though his mind raced with thoughts, he smiled and replied, \"Just now, an old woman working as a kitchen helper suddenly went crazy.","She was crying and laughing. I ordered the guards to hold her down, but as soon as they laid hands on her, we realized this wasn't an old woman at all.","It was clearly a man.\"","\"Lao Wei, this person dressed as a woman to infiltrate the military camp. His purpose must be impure. You must investigate this thoroughly.\"","As the Minister of War, Huo Ying showed his attitude of taking this matter very seriously.","\"Lao Wei, how did he get in? Does he have family? Where does he live when he is off duty?\"","Wei Ping and Cai Xian finally found a place to be useful, throwing out a series of questions just to get involved.","\"His family lives in a nearby village. He has a wife and children, but we don't know if they are his real relatives.\"","Wei Shouyi cupped his hands toward Yue Fuguang and the crowd, saying, \"I am going to the village to apprehend people right now, so I cannot accompany you. Please forgive me, Junior Preceptor and my lords.\"","The crowd said dismissively, \"General Wei, official duties come first.\"","\"Go quickly, General Wei. We will help ourselves, no need to worry.\"","\"Please enjoy your meal, everyone. I will take my leave first!\""]},{"number":280,"title":"Chapter 280: Bringing Rain and Clouds Along the Journey","paragraphs":["[Master, mortals' souls are just too weak. I was already very careful when searching his soul, but in the end, this Wu Lao'er still couldn't handle it and was turned into an idiot.]","The system's voice sounded a bit downcast. Its data had only connected to Wu Lao'er's brain for half a minute before his cranial nerves couldn't take it and collapsed.","\"Little Zhu, mortals are fragile, you can't be blamed for this. Did you get the information?\"","[I got it, I got it. This guy truly is Feng Yang's trusted aide, he knows quite a lot. I've compiled it all into a document and placed it on Wei Ping and Cai Xian's desks.]","Hearing this, Wei Ping and Cai Xian felt greatly reassured, but thinking about the Divine Artifact's miraculously skillful so-called soul searching, their hearts were filled with shock and dread.","People like them had quite a few secrets, many of which could not be exposed to the light of day.","If one day they accidentally angered these two ancestors, and the Young Master gave an order for the Divine Artifact to search their souls!","Then what face would they have left to live in this world? Even if they became idiots...","Yue Fuguang: That's called social death. It's equivalent to someone dying before they could delete the study materials on their computer, and having their acquaintances find out about it!","Everyone was trembling with fear, yet they could hardly conceal their curiosity.","What useful information could the Divine Artifact actually obtain from Wu Lao'er through this so-called soul searching?","At the table for the younger generation, they were scratching their heads in anxiety, pushing and poking each other. Wei Yan and Huo Sui were unanimously pushed forward by their brothers.","Who asked their fathers to be the only ones from whom they could fish out a little information!","As a result, a few tails were added behind the carriage on the journey back.","Yue Fuguang didn't care what her second brother and his playboy friends wanted to do. Since she was out of the city, she wanted to take care of another matter along the way.","So she deliberately asked, \"Little Zhu, if we go a few more miles ahead, can we reach the Imperial Manor by turning a corner?\"","When Emperor Mingxi, Huo Ying, and the others chose the location of the new recruit camp near the Imperial Manor, they had indeed harbored the intention that having a garrison nearby would allow the military to promptly come to the rescue if anything happened to the manor.","[Master, go three more miles ahead, turn the corner, and walk another mile. There is a fork in the road there, and turning into it leads to the Imperial Manor. Why do you ask this, Master? Do you want to go see how the new crops are growing?]","\"Since we're already out, should we drop by and cast a spirit rain on the Imperial Manor to boost their yield?\"","[Then let's do it, it's not a big deal anyway.]","One spoke lightly and the other answered casually, completely unaware of how excited the people following behind them were at this moment.","Everyone: Blessed by the Immortal Lord and the Divine Artifact, we actually managed to run into such a good thing!","Wei Ping and the others rolled their eyes, wondering what their Emperor would think if he knew.","Since it happened so suddenly, they didn't have any suitable tools to catch the rainwater.","Though they thought this, everyone still couldn't help but look at the small teacups and teapot on the low table in the carriage.","Holding this delicate tea set, for the first time, they felt that sometimes things that were too exquisite were truly impractical!","Following behind the carriage, Yu Boming and the others, who were originally swaying on their horses, suddenly sat up straight.","The slight guilt they had for tagging along vanished in an instant.","If they could get drenched in this rain, even if they had to turn around and head back to camp right after, this trip out would be worth it!","Thus, after Yue Fuguang proposed taking a different route back, it was passed unanimously, and the convoy smoothly turned into the fork leading to the Imperial Manor.","[Master, are you going to get out of the carriage and enter the Imperial Manor later?]","\"No need for such trouble. We can just spread the clouds and bring the rain as we travel.\"","At this time, they were less than a mile away from the Imperial Manor. As Yue Fuguang's words fell, the originally bright sunlight was suddenly covered by patches of shadows.","The previously bright sky suddenly grew dim.","The gentle breeze that had been blowing softly against them suddenly intensified without warning, as if coming from all directions.","The people who had long since climbed out of the carriage and were sitting on the shafts, ready to be rained on, had their robes blown up like balloons by the wind.","They all looked up at the sky in unison. At this moment, the dark clouds hung so low that it seemed they could be touched just by reaching out a hand.","The wind grew stronger, and the dark clouds accumulated more and more, slowly turning from gray to black.","[Look, Master, doesn't this scene look like the weather is suddenly changing and it's about to rain?]","Yue Fuguang praised generously, \"Little Zhu did a great job. This way, no one will suspect that this rain came about strangely!\"","Hearing the conversation between these two ancestors, the corners of everyone's mouths couldn't help but twitch.","No wonder this time the rain, compared to the last time, had such a long and dramatic build-up. It turned out they were guarding against them!","Meanwhile, Yu Chongshan stroked his slowly darkening beard, laughing heartily. Sitting opposite him, Yu Shuchun saw his old man's smug expression and also smiled silently.","Turning around to look back, although there were rows of carriages blocking the view and he couldn't see anything, it didn't stop him from knowing that those few brats were still following behind.","Yu Shuchun couldn't help but laugh softly and scold, \"Those stinky brats actually have pretty good luck!\"","Wei Ping, Huo Ying, and Cai Xian shared the same thought. They were very curious about how the injuries on those three boys would fare after being drenched in the rainwater.","Why were they looking forward to the arrival of this rain more and more!","Perhaps those two ancestors felt that it had brewed long enough and the time was ripe. When they passed by the Imperial Manor, barely half a mile away, the wind finally brought threads of rain.","At first, it was just sporadic, tentative drops, leaving dark marks the size of copper coins on the dusty road.","In just a few breaths, those marks connected into patches.","The wispy rain mist slowly turned into long, slanted silver threads. Finally, billions of silver threads intertwined, becoming transparent raindrops of various sizes.","The rustling sound rapidly swelled into a crashing roar, and a vast white curtain of rain was erected between heaven and earth, blurring the outlines of the surrounding people, carriages, horses, and roadside trees.","The increase in the rain's intensity didn't seem gradual; it was more like a dam bursting after accumulation. One could only say that this rain very much suited the style of the Divine Artifact!","In the entire convoy, aside from Yue Fuguang, who was still resting comfortably in the carriage, leisurely watching the swaying scenery in the wind and rain, everyone else was thoroughly drenched, turning into happy drowned rats.","At first, everyone only felt a few traces of coolness brushing against their faces, carrying a fresh, earthy scent.","Soon, the coolness turned into a heavy pounding. The wind swept in the raindrops, and the air suddenly grew cold. Yet, the cold rain that should have been hitting their bodies inexplicably gave them a strange sensation of being enveloped in a hot spring.","This feeling was especially pronounced for people like Huo Ying, who had hidden injuries, and the three partners in crime trailing behind.","They couldn't help but twist their waists. Waves of itchiness spread from their backs to their bottoms. Yu Boming and the others, who didn't look particularly bright, couldn't help but scratch their heads, were they about to grow some brains?!","\"Chunying, Liu Wei, do you want to come into the carriage to hide from the rain?\"","Yue Fuguang put on a full show, pretending to politely ask the two girls among the guards. As for her cousin and the others, she didn't even bother to pretend.","Shen Chunying wiped the rainwater from her face and smiled, \"My Lord, we're fine, you don't need to worry about us.\"","Liu Wei also looked at her with starry eyes and said, \"My Lord, it feels so comfortable to be drenched in this rain! Spring rain is as precious as oil, we wouldn't want to miss out on such rare, wonderful rain.\"","Yue Fuguang nodded and didn't try to persuade them further. After all, she was just putting on an act."]},{"number":281,"title":"Chapter 281: What could be better than staying close to adults","paragraphs":["[Master, if those two passersby really listened to you and came in to take shelter from the rain, what would you do?]","\"Guess!\"","These people were all professionals; there was absolutely no way they would come in to seek shelter from the rain, especially when they were already completely soaked.","Ordinary people might not notice it right away, but people like Shen Chunying and the others must have already felt the benefits of the rain on their bodies.","In today's escort team, apart from Shen Chunying and Yu Huaixian who had followed her to the manor last time, it was everyone else's first time being drenched in the spiritual rain.","But that didn't stop them from quickly discovering the difference.","Just as Liu Wei had said, this rain felt incredibly comfortable on the body, and hidden injuries and latent ailments felt significantly alleviated.","Thinking that this rain was brought down by their Lord and the Divine Artifact, the crowd, who had already accepted that the person they were protecting was a true immortal descended to the mortal realm, once again refreshed their understanding of what an 'immortal' truly was.","The crowd couldn't help but look at Yue Fuguang's carriage with even more fervent gazes. They unilaterally declared that unless the Lord killed them, no one could make them leave her side.","Just like their colleague Shen Chunxue, who had a biological mother as a manor lord. As the sole heir to the mountain manor, she chose not to return and be a young miss, willingly staying by the Lord's side instead. At this moment, they could understand her better than anyone else.","So what if it was the Luoxia Mountain Manor of the Five Mountains and Six Manors?","Was it as appealing as staying by the Lord's side?","The crowd, whose thoughts were racing wildly due to excitement, quickly noticed something amiss with that kid Yu Huaixian.","At first, when they saw him opening his mouth wide to catch the rainwater to drink, they thought the kid was just thirsty.","But the fact that he was still drinking after a while was highly suspicious!","None of them were fools. The moment they thought of his identity as the cousin of the Junior Preceptor, they all silently raised their heads and opened their mouths wide.","It didn't matter if one wasn't smart, but one had to be perceptive and know to follow the smart people closely.","Fortunately, everyone was riding horses, so they didn't have to worry about tripping over their own feet while walking with their heads tilted back.","The only downside was that lunch had been so delicious that none of them had eaten sparingly. On the other hand, Shen Chunying, Liu Wei, and Yu Huaixian had stepped out halfway through, so they had eaten a bit less than the rest.","The advantage of this became apparent right then.","Liu Wei and Shen Chunying weren't as boorish as the men; they merely caught the rainwater secretly with their hands to drink. Because the rain was heavier this time compared to the incident at the alternate estate, it only took a short while for the two of them to fill their stomachs. They felt a faint sense of regret that their appetites were small and their stomachs couldn't hold more.","Wei Ping and his group shared the same regret.","The kettles and small teacups on the carriage were already filled. Just as they were fretting over what to do next, they saw the Junior Preceptor's escort team, led by Yu Huaixian, all craning their necks toward the sky with their mouths wide open...","First it was Cai Xian and Huo Ying at the front, followed by Wei Ping and the others, who all began to imitate them.","Even Lin Congxue, who had the strongest scholarly air, temporarily set aside his reserve.","Compared to a bit of modesty, a healthy body seemed far more important.","Especially when everyone around him was doing it, joining in was called being sociable and fitting into the circle!","Senior officials like Yu Chongshan and Bao Yuanjun watched all this with chuckles, then turned their gazes toward the endless expanse of the imperial manor's lands in the distance.","They could almost imagine the seeds here, having drank their fill of the spiritual rainwater, desperately sprouting and growing.","Around the fields, there seemed to be faint silhouettes of people moving about; those were the guards protecting the fine seeds.","From the moment these guards saw their carriage procession approaching the imperial manor, they had been silently tailing them. Even without seeing their expressions, one would know that these people had already quietly heightened their vigilance.","Yu Chongshan stroked his beard. The boys on duty today were lucky to catch his granddaughter bringing down the spiritual rain.","They weren't the only lucky ones; there was also Wei Shouyi and his men, who had led a group to capture Wu Lao'er's accomplices.","They had already captured Wu Lao'er's parents, wife, children, and elders. While returning to the military camp, they suddenly noticed that the previously clear sky to their rear flank had abruptly become heavily overcast.","Wei Shouyi, who was particularly sensitive to geographical locations due to years of warfare, immediately pinpointed that it was the direction of the imperial manor.","Normally, seeing that it was about to rain wouldn't be strange, but the area covered by the dark clouds wasn't far from them. The sun was shining brightly right above their heads, yet heavy rain was about to fall over there.","Wei Shouyi's eyes flickered. If he wasn't mistaken, didn't the shape of those dark clouds perfectly cover the territory of the ten-thousand-acre imperial manor?","He quickly thought of the Junior Preceptor who happened to be there today, and the spiritual rain she once summoned that only fell on her own fields, without a single drop landing next door.","\"Giddy up! Giddy up! Giddy up!\"","Having figured this out, regardless of whether it was true or not, Wei Shouyi decided to head over and freeload on the rain first.","At worst, he'd be wrong and just take a cold rain bath. With his thick skin and sturdy build, he wouldn't even catch a cold!","It could be said that Wei Shouyi's benefit from this wave was entirely due to luck and his own decisiveness.","The group followed behind Yue Fuguang's carriage along the rainy road. As they slowly left the boundaries of the imperial manor, the originally continuous curtain of rain first splintered into threads, then scattered into an invisible floating mist that slowly dissipated into the world.","The trees along the road were washed bright and clear, every leaf looking like fine jasper.","Faint light pierced through the clouds on the horizon, rapidly illuminating the earth.","The imperial manor guards, who had been following the convoy all along, looked at the sky where the clouds had parted and the rain had stopped, and then at the convoy that was about to disappear from sight...","\"General!\"","A soldier uncertainly called out to their leader, who had an indescribably complex expression on his face—their general, Shen Jian.","At the same time, he was the Emperor's nephew, the Grand Princess's eldest son, and Shen Kang's older brother.","\"Fall back!\" he commanded with a wave of his hand.","He had heard about that miraculous Junior Preceptor many times, but due to various reasons, he had never had the chance to meet her.","Meeting in such a manner today had to be considered luck for him and his brothers-in-arms.","\"Fang Cheng, pass down the order. Today's events are not to be spread outside. Violators will be dealt with by military law!\"","\"Yes, General!\"","...","Smack! After listening to Eunuch Qian's report, Emperor Mingxi frustratingly slammed the memorial in his hand onto the desk!","He couldn't help but secretly regret it; his trip to the imperial manor a couple of days ago was simply too early!","If he had gone today, wouldn't he have had a chance encounter with Fuguang, and had the opportunity to be like Wei Ping and the others!","If nothing else, his son could have joined those silk-pants in stealing a chicken or grabbing a pig, right?","Sitting at the lower desk, Xie Zhiyan, who was working hard at reviewing memorials, didn't even need to think to know what his imperial father was pondering.","He covertly rolled his eyes, really wanting to tell his imperial father that this sort of thing depended on fate.","Emperor Mingxi didn't know his good eldest son was secretly criticizing him. He turned to ask Eunuch Qian, \"Old Qian, where are Wei Ping's carriages now?\"","Qian Gui: Your Majesty, just say you want to know if those officials are heading to the palace!","Qian Gui bowed and said, \"Reporting to Your Majesty, Ping San reported that Lord Wei and the others have already returned to their respective estates.\"","Qian Gui quickly raised his eyes to glance at the Emperor and added, \"According to Ping San, the rain was very heavy. All the lords, except for the Junior Preceptor, were drenched in the rain.\"","Emperor Mingxi nodded. \"Send a message to Shen Jian. Have him keep an eye on the growth of the crops over the next few days.\"","Thinking that besides the grain seedlings, there were also wild vegetables and weeds in the fields, he said, \"Crown Prince, tomorrow or the day after, take some people to pull the weeds, and remember to sort and store them all properly.\""]},{"number":282,"title":"Chapter 282: Secret Talk","paragraphs":["The reason those boys secretly ate the livestock in the military camp was simply that the animals had been grazing on the grass from Fuguang Farm for a while.","It was a pity that the royal family's grass was all used to feed horses. This time, he had to make the Court of the Imperial Stud use this grass to raise some chickens, ducks, pigs, and sheep.","Yue Fuguang didn't bother to care whether Emperor Mingxi eventually received the spiritual rainwater brought by his trusted ministers.","Instead, she turned her attention to another matter.","\"System, are you saying that Matsuyama hasn't left the capital city of Shangjing? Are you sure?\"","[Host, the system has never made a mistake. He is indeed still in Shangjing.]","\"According to their itinerary, the Dongyi delegation should be almost out of Great Yan's borders by now. Why would he return?\"","[Host, Matsuyama's sneaky return definitely means he is up to no good.] It was a pity that it couldn't foresee the future; it could only predict the course of events based on the system's precise calculations.","Yue Fuguang nodded. She didn't need the system to tell her to know that this Matsuyama definitely had an ulterior motive.","The first time she saw the Dongyi people, it had stirred up bad memories for Yue Fuguang.","Therefore, out of the other five nations, if asked which one she hated the most, Dongyi would definitely rank ahead of the other four nations that had once organized her assassination.","Simply because they were too similar to the people from her old home, making it impossible for her to feel the slightest bit of goodwill towards them.","\"System, can you find out where he ended up staying?\"","Just as Yue Fuguang ordered the system to track down Matsuyama's whereabouts, two groups of people were also secretly discussing her.","In a secret room within an ordinary courtyard somewhere on South Street, a bean-sized oil lamp could only illuminate a palm-sized area in the dark, cramped space. Four people, three men and one woman, sat around a small square table in the center.","One of them, a middle-aged man with an honest-looking face, said, \"Leader, Mao Wu sent word that today Yue Fuguang did nothing special other than visiting the new recruit camp with Yu Chongshan and the others.\"","The old man addressed as the leader had his eyes slightly lowered. His deeply wrinkled face was etched with the vicissitudes of a lifetime of toil for a livelihood, a look typical only of the common people at the bottom of society.","\"Have you found out why they went to the military camp and what they did inside?\"","The middle-aged man opposite him shook his head. \"Their group was escorted by twenty or thirty guards. Our people didn't dare to get close. We only watched from a distance as they entered the camp and stayed inside for nearly two hours before coming out.\"","\"Who accompanied them?\"","\"The Yu father and son, Wei Ping, Cai Xian, the Bao father and son, Huo Ying, Lin Congxue, Ji Hongming, Zhang Zhongping...\"","He rattled off more than a dozen names in one breath. The group consisted of both civil and military officials, and prominent figures like the Ministers of the Six Ministries were all present without exception.","It looked exactly like the entourage of an emperor's excursion, which momentarily confused these people as to what they were actually doing. After all, the spies they had planted in the imperial court hadn't received any related official news either.","Thinking of something, he hesitated for a moment and said slowly, \"There is one more thing...\"","The old man lifted his eyelids and glanced at him. \"What is it that makes you stammer so?\"","He wrapped his coarse cloth gown tighter around himself. \"Chou Yi, just say it.\"","\"Mao Wu said he noticed that more than an hour after the group entered, Wei Shouyi led a squad of men towards the West Mountain.","Fearing exposure and also worried that Yue Fuguang and the others might come out, he and Mao Nine didn't follow them.\"","\"Towards the West Mountain? Is there anything special there?\"","\"Other than mountains, there are just a few villages over there, and further past that is Pingling Town.\"","He frowned, shook his head, and said, \"Your subordinate really can't think of anything special about that place. Perhaps it's not a matter of importance?\"","The leader shook his head. \"Given Yue Fuguang's current status as the most favored person right under the emperor, with her present, for Wei Shouyi not to accompany her but instead take men outside, something we don't know about must have happened.\"","He suddenly raised his head, a sharp gleam flashing in his eyes. Beneath his hooked nose was a pair of thin lips. At this moment, he didn't look the least bit like an ordinary commoner.","He looked exactly like a scheming, shrewd old fox.","\"Furthermore, if something really did happen, it definitely wouldn't be a small matter.\"","The young man sitting next to the middle-aged man asked, \"Leader, should we intervene?\"","The implication was that this was not within the scope of their mission.","The middle-aged man chimed in, \"Yes, Leader, our top priority right now should be to first find out the origins of movable type printing and snow-flake salt.","We've been following Yue Fuguang for a while. Her life is very regular. Other than leaving the city today to go to the new recruit camp, she hasn't been anywhere else besides the Yu Residence and the Imperial Palace.\"","The young man added, \"Exactly, we've been watching her the whole time, and she hasn't visited those two workshops at all. Your subordinate believes these things probably have nothing to do with that little girl.\"","Otherwise, with such a massive achievement that could merit being enfeoffed as a noble or appointed as a prime minister, she couldn't possibly not have a hand in it. If it were any of them, they wouldn't bear to truly wash their hands of it, unless it really had nothing to do with her.","Little did these people know that Yue Fuguang now treated wealth and fame like dirt... well, she still cared a bit about her reputation!","These rats hiding in the dark judged others by their own standards, committing the error of empiricism, and thus completely missed the correct answer.","\"Leader, there's one more thing,\" the middle-aged man continued to report. \"Mao Wu said they followed those people's convoy from a distance back to the city today.","On the way, the convoy suddenly turned towards the imperial estate, but they didn't go inside.\"","The old man nodded, not finding any issue with that, and signaled him to continue.","\"He said that just as the convoy turned onto the small path next to the imperial estate, the previously clear sky suddenly broke into a heavy storm.","Mao Wu originally wanted to follow them in, but right then, a group of men dressed as guards rushed out of the imperial estate. Therefore, he didn't follow but took another route around.","After waiting for almost half an hour, he finally saw the convoy coming out from the path by the imperial estate.","He said he saw it as clear as day, that rain seemed to have fallen entirely on the land near the imperial estate!\"","\"Is this true?\" Hearing the latter part, the leader's initially nonchalant expression instantly vanished. His half-closed eyes suddenly snapped open, shooting a sharp gaze straight at him. \"Where is Mao Wu? Have him come report in person.\"","\"Your subordinate has already sent Xin One to relieve him; he should be arriving any moment.\" Just as he spoke, there was a knock on the secret room's door, three long and two short taps.","\"Enter.\" Following the leader's aged voice, a young man with an ordinary face, dressed like a small peddler, walked in.","\"Mao Wu of the Earth Camp greets the Right Leader of the Earth Branch.\"","Not only did this person have a completely average appearance, but even his voice was devoid of any distinct characteristics, and his accent was an authentic Shangjing local accent.","The Right Leader of the Earth Branch pointed to a stool lower down. \"Mao Wu, sit down and give your report.\"","\"Thank you, Leader.\" Mao Wu sat down, perching only half of his body on the stool.","\"Tell me again in detail everything you saw and heard today.\"","\"Yes, today your subordinate...\"","The leader nodded. \"Are you certain there are no omissions?\"","\"Yes. Your subordinate dares not conceal anything. Mao Nine and I followed them all the way, and everything we saw and heard was exactly as described.\"","The old leader asked a few more questions. Finding no omissions, he waved his hand at him. \"You may step down for now.\"","He turned his head and said to the middle-aged man, \"Chou Yi, get him twenty taels of silver.\"","\"Mao Wu thanks the Leader for the reward!\""]},{"number":283,"title":"Chapter 283: The Most Feudalistic and Superstitious Pair in the Entire Great Yan Is Us Two","paragraphs":["After Mao Wu expressed his thanks and left, the middle-aged man named Chou Yi said, \"Leader, the situation is obvious now. Those newly emerged technologies must be the contents of the book that the Fourth Prince and the Ninth Prince gave to the Crown Prince. Since we cannot touch the Crown Prince, we can still figure out a way to deal with the Fourth Prince and the Ninth Prince.\"","The fourth person, who had been silent all along—a plainly dressed, ordinary-looking middle-aged woman—spoke up, \"Leader, you must make a decision soon. Yesterday, your subordinate saw people from Nanyue by the Fourth Prince's side...\"","Hearing that Nanyue people had already appeared beside the Fourth Prince, the leader couldn't help but feel a surge of urgency and ordered, \"Contact the people from those aristocratic families. Tell them we have accepted their commissions.\"","The middle-aged woman said, \"Leader, do you mean...\"","The leader gave her an appreciative look and nodded, \"Exactly, it is just as you think.\"","After saying that, he waved his hand, \"Alright, all of you, head upstairs.\"","\"Yes, Father.\"","\"Yes, Father.\"","\"Yes, Grandfather.\"","In an instant, the superior-subordinate dynamic transformed into that of an utterly ordinary four-person household spanning three generations, just like millions of others in the capital city of Shangjing.","In the backyard of an ordinary grocery store somewhere in the East Market, inside a small room against the wall, five people were currently sitting around a wooden table lit by an oil lamp with a flame the size of a bean.","Spread impressively across the table was a map detailing the route from the new military camp to the imperial estate, the very path Yue Fuguang had traveled just today.","And sitting at the head of the table, a heavily bearded man who looked quite aged, was none other than the Dongyi Prince, Matsuyama, whose whereabouts Yue Fuguang had asked the system to track down.","Sitting to Matsuyama's left was his sister, the Dongyi Royal Princess Yōko, who in the future would have a son with Cai Bing.","She asked, \"Brother, can we be certain that this thing called a potato is truly planted in the Great Yan Emperor's private fields?\"","The previous intelligence they received stated that the potatoes were planted in the Xuanwei Manor. They had sent people to sneak in and probe a few times, but none succeeded.","Just as they were about to give up, their old friend from Dongyi, their mother's lover, sent someone with news, claiming they could find a person to buy reliable information about the potatoes.","Unexpectedly, they spent a mere few hundred taels of silver to obtain the information on the potato planting.","Although it was different from the Xuanwei Manor they initially believed, after making various inquiries, the news that the potatoes were in the imperial estate was ninety percent true.","\"Yōko, that person's information is still trustworthy; otherwise, why would we siblings risk returning to this perilous capital city of Shangjing?\"","What he didn't say was that the esteemed lord seemed to have sensed danger and urgently needed the support of their Dongyi royal family, which was why he went through so much trouble to deliver such vital information into their hands.","Therefore, the information he provided wouldn't be fake.","That person also knew that their Dongyi had little and barren land, making high-yield potatoes far more attractive to them than to the other nations.","As long as he, Matsuyama, successfully obtained the potatoes, he would become the descendant most favored by the Sun God in the entire Dongyi royal family.","The succession to the Dongyi throne would undoubtedly be his.","As for that lord's biological son, Oshima, a non-pureblood Dongyi person, he had plenty of ways to kill him!","He then turned to a man sitting opposite him, who looked to be in his early twenties and was dressed as an ordinary shop assistant, and said, \"Goro, tell us about the situation.\"","\"Yes, Lord Matsuyama. Following your orders, this humble one has investigated thoroughly. There are indeed stationed troops inside the imperial estate, not just the guards we initially thought.\"","Hearing the confirmation of stationed troops, Matsuyama's expression instantly turned very ugly. \"Goro, can you confirm how many troops are stationed there? Who is the commanding general? How is their combat strength?\"","The young man named Goro shook his head. \"Please forgive me, Your Excellency. This humble one is incompetent. The imperial estate is heavily guarded, and unauthorized personnel are strictly forbidden from approaching within two miles.","I led men to keep watch for half a month, but we only saw a few carriages belonging to nobles going in and out.","We tried to approach multiple times without success and even alerted the guards inside.","So... so, their defenses are even tighter now!\"","As Goro spoke, he couldn't help but lower his head. Suddenly, as if remembering something, he looked up and said, \"Oh, right! Today, that Junior Preceptor of Great Yan and a group of nobles passed by the imperial estate and were not stopped.\"","As for the localized rain that fell over the imperial estate, although Goro found it faintly strange, he quickly dismissed it and did not mention the matter to Matsuyama.","Sitting next to Goro was a petite woman of a similar age. She added, \"Your Excellency, while we were keeping watch, we also unexpectedly saw two Great Yan people stealthily tailing the convoy.\"","Matsuyama became interested, immediately sitting up straight. \"Oh, Kohana, do you know who they are? Were you discovered by those two?\"","The woman named Kohana shook her head. \"Your Excellency, we were well hidden, so they didn't spot us. Because we had a mission and were afraid of being discovered by them, we didn't follow them to investigate their background.","However, those two had ordinary features, and we couldn't tell their origins just from their clothing.\"","\"Brother, are you thinking of finding those people to cooperate with?\"","Those tailing the highly esteemed Junior Preceptor were likely not officials of Great Yan. As long as enough benefits were offered, those people could indeed be used by them. Perhaps both sides even shared the same goal.","Matsuyama nodded with an air of self-importance and said, \"Exactly. This prince has exactly that intention. Goro, find a way to locate them.\"","\"Yes, Your Excellency!\"","Suddenly, the smile on Matsuyama's face faded, and he sighed slightly. \"That lord is terrified of their Emperor catching something to use against him, so his help to us is limited. Even for the information, we had to step forward and make the trade ourselves.","Yōko, we siblings are strangers in a strange land here. If we can find a local faction to help us, it would be the best choice.\"","\"Is that why you spent a fortune to have Takeo contact the Heavenly Star Pavilion, the Nether Blue Lotus, and the Wind and Rain Pavilion?\"","Matsuyama nodded. \"Unfortunately, I don't know why, but the two major organizations, Nether Blue Lotus and Heavenly Star Pavilion, have been extremely cautious lately. They have consistently refused contact, and Takeo is still waiting for news.","And as for the Wind and Rain Pavilion, we can't even find anyone from there!\"","Matsuyama didn't know why the assassins from Nether Blue Lotus and Heavenly Star Pavilion were hiding like turtles. It was because he hadn't connected the lightning strike incident in the capital of Shangjing with the other assassin organization he wanted to hire, the Wind and Rain Pavilion.","Nor did he know that their Young Pavilion Master and all his subordinates had been captured. From this, it was clear that what he said was true—they were indeed strangers in a strange land!","Speaking of the Wind and Rain Pavilion, System 07 indicated it had something to say.","[Host, Luo Feng and Luo Yu are both dead!]","Early in the morning, Yue Fuguang, who was attending class at the Hongwen Academy, was enjoying a perfectly good nap. Because she was dozing off, the teacher had lowered his voice by a couple of notches, making it the perfect background noise for sleeping.","Unfortunately, her sweet dreams were rudely awakened by the system's death announcement.","\"System, aren't you getting a little too skilled at this job of announcing deaths?\"","Since they were already dead, couldn't it have waited until she woke up to tell her?","\"If you keep this up, you're going to turn into a jinxed system!\" Let's see who would dare bind with it in the future.","The system cheerfully replied without a care, [Host, you need to believe in science!]","Yue Fuguang was speechless for a moment. \"The two most superstitious entities in all of Great Yan are us, and you're telling me to believe in science!\"","Was it trying to be funny or what!","The system appeared to be an ultra-high-tech product from a higher dimension, but Yue Fuguang simply felt that the system itself was the most unscientific existence of all!"]},{"number":284,"title":"Chapter 284: Someone Broke into the Prison Last Night","paragraphs":["[Oh my, didn't you say before that when you're away from home, you give yourself your own identity. Who can blame the people here for believing in ghosts and gods!]","Yue Fuguang shook her head, not arguing with it about what was more scientific, but asked, \"How did Luo Feng and Luo Yu die?\"","The two were the Pavilion Master and Vice Pavilion Master after all, how could they lose their value so quickly?","[Last night someone broke into the prison. After failing, they conveniently slaughtered the two brothers. The prison breakers also all committed suicide, leaving no survivors.]","The Wind and Rain Pavilion not only had assassins, but also death warriors?","\"System, do you know who the mastermind behind this is?\" Although she asked this, Yue Fuguang actually already had a guess in her heart.","[Host, the mastermind behind yesterday's action is...]","\"Little Bead, who masterminded the prison break last night?\"","The system was stunned by her call for a moment before reacting, immediately saying, [Master, the mastermind behind the prison break is the old Pavilion Master, Feng Yang.]","\"Feng Yang? Last time I heard Wei Ping and Cai Xian say he escaped. This person didn't return to Xiqiang to take refuge, but dared to come back to the capital to stir up trouble?\"","[Master, Feng Yang sneaked into the capital in disguise three days ago. He had only been here for a day when he heard that Wu Lao'er, who had infiltrated the Right Guard New Army Camp from the Wind and Rain Pavilion, and his 'family' in Xiashan Village had all been arrested.","Because of Wu Lao'er's identity and mission, only he and Luo Feng knew.","Therefore, Feng Yang immediately suspected that Luo Feng had mutinied. But due to his daughter's pleas and the sake of his two grandchildren, he sent people to risk a prison break the following night.","Seeing the prison break fail, the assassins killed Luo Feng and Luo Yu before committing suicide.]","\"So this prison break is still a continuation of the incident caused by calling the parents the other day? Feng Yang's people didn't know that Wu Lao'er was caught because his attempt to poison me was exposed?\"","Looking at it this way, although this Luo Feng deserved to die, dying in such a way was indeed a bit wrongful!","Hearing that Yue Fuguang had accompanied her grandfather and second uncle to the military camp to see her second brother the day before yesterday and was actually subjected to a poisoning attempt, Yu Ningxuan and Yu Ningxin both turned pale.","Although Yue Fuguang was now sitting safe and sound in front of them, the fear in the little sisters' hearts could not be calmed no matter what.","The Seventh Prince and Eighth Princess, Yue Fuguang's two little companions, were also full of shock.","Because the Junior Preceptor had helped the imperial court, she had narrowly escaped assassination many times, and this time she was almost poisoned. The brother and sister both felt terrible.","The Junior Preceptor's kindness to Great Yan was as heavy as a mountain. Her repeated encounters made the pure-hearted young brother and sister feel that their Xie family had greatly wronged the Junior Preceptor.","A perfectly good immortal, dragged into this mortal power struggle, it was truly their Xie family who had let her down.","Yue Fuguang: The conscience of the Xie family is probably all grown on these two little ones!","However, this was truly a beautiful misunderstanding!","She, Yue Fuguang, a cheat-like existence from another world, was not some innocent chess piece dragged onto the board.","She was the true chess player standing behind the players, actually playing the game.","She took the world as her chessboard, saving the common people, and even more so, achieving her own goals.","Those who heard her inner voice were momentarily speechless, while the conversation between Yue Fuguang and the system continued.","[Master, because the New Army Camp is strictly controlled, the sand mixed in is only a few stray cats.","These people are all ordinary soldiers. The incident happened suddenly that day, Wei Shouyi dealt with it quickly, and later blocked the news. The camp was only allowed to enter and not exit.","So up to now, not a single bit of information has leaked.]","Although their group appeared at the training ground, because both sides had a gentle attitude, those who saw them only thought that the big shots had come to the military camp on official business and dropped by to visit the younger generation of their families.","After all, stealing chickens and touching pigs was not glorious. To cover up for the respected, considering the face of the elders in the family, Wei Shouyi would not ruin the reputation of the playboys, although they had no reputation to speak of.","What's more, there was Yu Boming inside, who couldn't be touched.","This single sentence from the system, however, made Yun Tianxing, who was teaching, unable to remain calm.","The Director of the Imperial Astronomy Bureau, who was just passionately speaking and talking eloquently about the stars and the moon, suddenly slowed down his speech.","Although he did not participate in the entire process of training the New Army Camp, he was indeed an onlooker.","Naturally, he knew how much hope and effort everyone, from His Majesty down to his colleagues, had placed in it.","The ten thousand people in the Right Guard New Army Camp were the testing ground for Great Yan's brand-new military management and training model.","Once successful, countless new recruit camps would be established all over Great Yan, and these people would also be one of the main forces for Great Yan to expand its territory in the future.","Now he was told that despite their thousand and ten thousand precautions, someone had actually mixed sand into them!","It was not hard to imagine how furious His Majesty would be upon learning of this!","Swish! Bang! Soon Yun Tianxing witnessed with his own eyes their furious Emperor, like a tiger whose lifeblood had been injured.","Wishing he could catch anyone and take a bite out of them to vent the hatred in his heart!","\"Qian Gui, tell Huo Ying and Wei Shouyi to roll over and see Zhen!\" Emperor Mingxi roared at Eunuch Qian below, holding the Son of Heaven's sword in his hand.","\"Summon Wei Ping, Cai Xian, Feng Tang... and Elder Yu into the palace!\"","Regardless of how angry Emperor Mingxi was at this time due to the chain reaction caused by an assassination and a prison break, Yue Fuguang was also dealing with the aftermath brought about by the prison break.","\"Villa Master Luo, my condolences!\"","For a moment, Yue Fuguang could not find more comforting words for Luo Xue, whose only son had died.","In the eyes of outsiders, no matter how much Luo Feng deserved to die, as a mother, Luo Xue inevitably had to bear the piercing pain of losing her son.","Luo Xue, whose face was visibly more weathered than when they first met, shook her head and said, \"To be honest with Your Excellency, ever since I knew what he had done, I had long prepared for this day.\"","Only, she never expected this day to come so quickly. From his capture to his death, it had only been a month.","Yue Fuguang nodded. She really could not bring herself to say against her conscience that Luo Feng's crimes did not warrant death.","Luo Xue continued, \"Not to mention the human life trade done by the Wind and Rain Pavilion, just the intention to assassinate Your Excellency is an unforgivable crime. He chose this path back then, and he can't blame anyone for this outcome.\"","If you ask who Luo Xue hated the most for Luo Feng's death? Besides hating herself for not teaching her son well, she only hated one person the most, and that was Feng Yang.","Feng Yang led her perfectly good son onto this path, and the person ultimately died at his hands.","Whether for the dead Luo Feng or for her Dongxue, Feng Yang had to die!","\"What are Villa Master Luo's plans next?\"","\"I came to see Your Excellency this time to bid you farewell. Tomorrow I will send Luo Feng back to our hometown for burial.\"","Yue Fuguang nodded, \"As you should. Then Dongxue...\"","Hearing herself mentioned, Shen Dongxue, oh, Dongxue who would soon change her name to Luo Shendong, immediately stepped forward and said, \"Your Excellency, your subordinate requests half a month's leave from you. After safely escorting my mother back to the Sunset Villa, your subordinate will rush back as soon as possible.\"","Yue Fuguang smiled and shook her head, saying, \"Dongxue, there's no need to rush back. When you get to the Sunset Villa, spend some good time with Villa Master Luo. I will be fine here.\"","Shen Dongxue did not dare to leave Her Excellency's side for too long.","Every position by Her Excellency's side was highly sought after. Not to mention those far away, just those old acquaintances from the Guest Courtyard, who wasn't jealous of their current lives?","My lovely readers, please use your lucky hands to hit that 'urge update' button! Thanks a million!"]},{"number":285,"title":"Chapter 285: The wind sweeping through the tower heralds a rising storm in the mountains.","paragraphs":["Hearing from Zhang Fang and Dai Yuxing, the higher-ups were looking for new guards for Her Grace. The team was expanding, but only a few could actually get close to her.","Even Dai Yuxing, the Vice Protector, had fewer opportunities to serve closely by Her Grace's side because she had joined later than them.","Shen Dongxue was afraid that if she left for too long, Her Grace would forget her and turn to like someone else!","Yue Fuguang thought to herself: Do I look like such a fickle person?","Shen Dongxue smiled playfully and said, \"This subordinate cannot bear to leave you for too long, Your Grace!\"","Yue Fuguang thought: Hmm, that was sweet!","Little Zhu, give me a Detoxification Pill and a Rejuvenation Pill.","Master, what do you need the pills for?","Feng Yang and the Wind and Rain Pavilion of Western Qiang want Luo Feng's child to inherit the Sunset Villa, and Luo Xue and Dongxue are his biggest obstacles. With Dongxue by my side, I don't need to worry, but I'm afraid he might make a secret move against Luo Xue. Don't forget, in the original timeline, Luo Xue did not meet a good end.","Giving her immortal pills is equivalent to giving her two extra lives, Master. How is this Luo Xue worth you caring so much?","It is all for Dongxue's sake. Besides, Luo Xue has a great reputation; she is an open and upright person who shouldn't die at the hands of a villain.","As the person and the system were still conversing in their minds, Luo Xue, who was sitting below, had already widened her eyes, tightly gripping her daughter's hand.","Shen Chunying, standing on her other side, took the opportunity of pouring her tea to secretly signal her not to make a sound.","Luo Xue gave a subtle nod, trying hard to calm her heart that was pounding wildly in her throat.","Was this what her daughter had obscurely hinted at multiple times after asking her true opinion of the Junior Preceptor and confirming her genuine gratitude—that the Junior Preceptor had an extraordinary identity and possessed miraculous abilities?","Master, one pill is too much. As a mortal, she cannot withstand the potency of an immortal pill; the energy would make her explode.","Then make them into smaller pellets suitable for mortal martial artists, and pack two of each for me.","The system divided one pill into five portions. This was only because Luo Xue's martial arts cultivation was superb; if it were an ordinary person, the medicine would still be too strong.","At this moment, Luo Xue gripped Dongxue's hand even tighter.","She had previously thought that she didn't need her daughter's reminder to understand the Junior Preceptor's esteemed status in Great Yan. However, she never expected that the extraordinary identity her daughter mentioned had nothing to do with the title of Junior Preceptor!","Immortal pills? Mortals!","The true identity of the person in front of her was glaringly obvious.","It could be said that Luo Xue truly lived up to her reputation as a seasoned veteran of the martial world; she quickly figured out the crucial points.","She was not like Shen Chunying and the others, who had taken a long time back then to figure out Yue Fuguang's true identity.","Realizing what a massive pillar of support sat before her, she wouldn't have even wanted her daughter to return with her if it weren't for the fact that she needed to finalize Dongxue's status as the future heir of the Sunset Villa, which required Dongxue to meet with various parties.","Thus, after forcefully calming her emotions, Luo Xue followed up on Shen Dongxue's words and said, \"Yes, Your Grace, Dongxue has always told me that she cannot bear to leave you.","That is why she is only willing to stay for a few days when returning with me this time!\"","She smiled with a face full of maternal love, showing that she truly cherished Dongxue as her daughter.","Yue Fuguang also smiled and said, \"Since Villa Master Luo is in a hurry to return, I will not keep you.\"","Saying this, she took out two exquisite small jade bottles from her sleeve. \"This is my return gift to Villa Master Luo. The white bottle contains Detoxification Pills, which can cure a hundred poisons.","The cyan bottle contains Rejuvenation Pills; you can use them when heavily injured.\"","To thank Yue Fuguang for helping to find her daughter, Luo Xue had sent several carriages full of gifts, so it made perfect sense for Yue Fuguang to call this a return gift.","Master, our Detoxification Pills can cure all the poisons in this world, not just a hundred. As for the dosage of the Rejuvenation Pill I left for her, as long as she still has a single breath left, it can save her life and prevent any hidden injuries later on.","Hearing the explanation of that mysterious childlike voice, and seeing the genuine immortal pills placed right on the table before her,","Luo Xue could hardly sit still. She hurriedly stood up, waving her hands frantically as she said, \"No, no, no, Junior Preceptor, I cannot accept this, I simply cannot! This... this is far too precious! I am unworthy of such a gift.\"","She really wanted to say that the few carriages of gifts she brought were nowhere near the value of two bottles of immortal pills. The Junior Preceptor was far too generous to her own people!","Such pills were the kind of existence that auction houses would charge ten thousand pieces of gold just to let you catch a glimpse of.","Yue Fuguang pressed her hands down gently and said, \"Please sit down, Villa Master Luo. You can accept these two bottles of pills with peace of mind. Only when your safety is guaranteed can Dongxue feel at ease serving by my side, rather than worrying about your well-being every single day.\"","After thinking for a moment, she still reminded her, \"Villa Master Luo, the Feng family of Western Qiang will not give up on annexing the Sunset Villa, so you must be mentally prepared.","You should be more vigilant in your daily life, and keep an eye out even when it comes to the people you trust the most.\"","Master, in the original timeline, Luo Xue passed away two years later precisely because Feng Yang and his people bribed someone close to her. And they used poison.","Hearing this, Shen Dongxue could not help but look at her mother with worry. Luo Xue gently patted her hand to reassure her.","Luo Xue had already made up her mind that Luo Feng's corpse would not be buried in the Luo family's ancestral graveyard. This would indirectly tell outsiders that Luo Feng's branch of the family had no right to inherit the villa.","No matter what, she would first legally sever the inheritance rights of his branch.","Shen Dongxue gritted her teeth, suddenly dropped to one knee before Yue Fuguang, and said, \"Dongxue thanks the Young Preceptor on behalf of my mother for bestowing the medicine. From now on, Dongxue's life belongs to you, My Lord. I will strike wherever you point!\"","Yue Fuguang believed these words. After all, in just this short while, Shen Dongxue's affection level for her had surged from over eighty into the nineties, stopping at exactly ninety-eight points.","This was one of her own people whom she could absolutely trust right now.","Naturally, she had to be generous to her own people. She smiled and said, \"Hurry and get up. What would I want your life for! However, I do quite like the part about striking wherever I point!\"","[Exactly, with Master and Little Zhu here, as long as these people do not actively seek death, they will not die. Serving the Master means having absolute loyalty and obedience.]","She then turned to Luo Xue and said, \"Manor Lord Luo, your daughter has already thanked me, so please accept it with peace of mind!\"","Luo Xue no longer declined. She stood up, bowed deeply, and said, \"Luo Xue thanks My Lord for the medicine. From now on, Luo Xue and the Sunset Glow Villa will follow your lead alone!\"","Yue Fuguang nodded. That was exactly what she had been waiting to hear; today's efforts had not been in vain after all.","After sending off the Luo mother and daughter, Yue Fuguang returned to her routine of attending court and school.","Meanwhile, the news of the death of the Pavilion Master of the Great Yan's Wind and Rain Pavilion spread like wildfire.","At this time, the capital city of Shangjing appeared peaceful and serene, but beneath the surface, dark currents surged because Feng Yang, the old Pavilion Master of the Wind and Rain Pavilion, and the Eastern Yi Prince Matsuyama remained hidden in the shadows, delaying their appearance.","Emperor Mingxi, however, did not know that aside from these two forces, even more hands had already reached in, intertwining with the dark factions already lurking within Shangjing.","The coming period of time was destined to be anything but peaceful.","Standing in the pavilion and gazing into the distance, Yue Fuguang could not help but sigh, \"The wind sweeping through the tower heralds a rising storm in the mountains!\"","Cuizhu glanced at the clear sky outside the window and said, \"Miss, will it really rain in such fine weather?\"","Before Yue Fuguang could witness the wind and rain, she was first met by her study companions.","Why use the plural for 'companions'?"]},{"number":286,"title":"Chapter 286: The Father of the Future Emperor Liang Shizong, Posthumously Honored as Emperor Liang Shizu","paragraphs":["[Master, how come you chose three more study companions in one breath this time? Didn't the emperor say four study companions per person?]","Her host now had five tails of varying sizes following behind her. With her entourage expanding, she walked with an undeniable swagger.","The system believed that if it weren't for her status and her slight concern for her public image, her host would be strutting with absolute arrogance right now.","Not to mention the system, even the five study companions behind her couldn't help but worry when they heard the divine artifact's question.","The Young Preceptor's entourage of study companions had exceeded the quota. Could it be that one of the five of them would be eliminated?!","Especially the three who had just joined the crew today; they looked at each other, their faces flushing slightly, but none of them wanted to be the one told to leave.","After a few awkward glances at one another, they all turned their eyes toward Yue Fuguang, who was walking at the very front.","With six pairs of eyes as bright as stars looking at her, the highly perceptive Yue Fuguang sensed it.","She said nonchalantly, \"You said it yourself, that's the emperor's rule. I can choose to listen to it or ignore it. I am the dignified Young Preceptor of a nation, so what if I have one extra study companion? Does anyone dare to jump out and object?\"","Yue Fuguang spoke casually, but in the eyes of the little companions behind her, it was incredibly domineering.","Yue Fuguang's tall and mighty image in their hearts instantly surpassed that of their fathers.","Pairs of adoring eyes gazed at her fervently. If Yue Fuguang's skin weren't thick enough, she would have been burned right through.","The system seemed to just realize this and said loudly, [That's right! With Master's status, having a few more study companions is perfectly fine. Back at Mount Lingxu, in Master's palace, not counting the ones in the outer halls, there were thirty-three little immortal attendants in the inner halls alone. If you pulled out any random one of them, they could flatten the Six Nations within a single day.]","The older and younger study companions thought: Does that mean we are also the Little Immortal Lord's immortal attendants in the mortal realm?!","Whether they were or not, the few of them instantly straightened their backs. The five of them were now among the people closest to the Little Immortal Lord.","As the people closest to the Little Immortal Lord, they absolutely could not bring disgrace to her.","Especially the newcomers; the three of them had fought their way out from over a hundred qualified candidates.","They were able to be selected because the Immortal Lord was giving face to their fathers.","From now on, the prestige they held in front of the Little Immortal Lord would have to be earned by themselves!","\"I originally did want to choose two girls to be study companions, but who asked Feng Tang's family to only have sons of the right age?\"","Speaking of this, the new study companion behind Yue Fuguang, the only boy among the five, Feng Tang's second son, nine-year-old Feng Xiu, had a lot to say.","His mother had given birth to the three brothers in quick succession, and only a few years later did she give birth to his little sister, Feng Yu, who was only three years old this year.","If it weren't for the fact that his sister was simply too young, and sending her to the Young Preceptor would mean making the Young Preceptor babysit rather than having a study companion, such a great opportunity would never have fallen to him.","His father said that luck is also a part of strength.","His older brother, Feng You, was thirteen and studying at the Imperial College, preparing to take the imperial examination for the scholar degree this year. Therefore, the opportunity to be a study companion to the Little Immortal Lord fell upon him and his third brother, Feng Liang.","Compared to his third brother, who was only seven this year, he, who was about to turn ten, was obviously of a more suitable age.","[Master, why did you insist on choosing the little brat from Feng Tang's family as a study companion?]","\"Who told your Master to find Feng Tang pleasing to the eye? Little Zhu, didn't you also say that Feng Tang is a pretty good guy?\"","[Master, Little Zhu thinks he is pretty good because I can sense he harbors great goodwill towards you, Master.","Master, the other two study companions, did you also choose them just because you found their fathers agreeable?]","\"It was because of their fathers, but also because they themselves are very fine young girls.","Wu Yong's younger sister, Wu Yunmiao, is the same age as my second sister. Both are nearing the age for marriage prospects. Staying by my side for a year or two will be better for their futures.","At the very least, they will have more choices, and in the future, no one in their in-laws' families will dare to bully them.","As for Bao Qianjun's daughter, Bao Zihui's younger sister Bao Zilan, although I have only met Bao Qianjun once and don't know him well, I deeply respect his loyalty to the sovereign and love for the people.","Bao Zilan is very smart and has great potential. The father and daughter are worth me giving their family a chance.\"","The system seemed to agree completely. [Master, if you want to accomplish things in the future, you indeed need to cultivate some of your own people.","Even if we do nothing, when Great Yan falls in the future and we migrate to an island, we will still need to bring some people with us.","Your little study companions are excellent candidates.]","Hearing the young immortal lord's words and the divine artifact's talk of their own people, the worries in the hearts of the few people finally settled completely.","A boundless sense of lofty ambition surged within them. The meaning of their studies seemed to change from this day forward.","To transform themselves into useful people, people useful to the young immortal lord, became their greatest motivation and goal for learning at this moment.","The person teaching Yue Fuguang and the others in the morning was Feng Tang. The lesson covered the local customs, regional powers, and military and political situations across Great Yan.","Yue Fuguang did not know what the Seventh Prince and the Eighth Princess had been learning before she arrived.","But ever since she started attending classes, she slowly began to sense that something was off.","It was normal for the master to teach the Confucian classics, history, philosophy, and literature, as well as the Six Arts. After all, Great Yan also aimed to cultivate talents in a well-rounded manner, encompassing morality, intellect, physical fitness, aesthetics, and labor.","They were not trying to raise frail scholars who couldn't tell the five grains apart or lacked the strength to truss a chicken.","But it was one thing to include various crime-solving details when teaching the law; it was another when the astronomy and geography teacher used the map of Great Yan to teach them.","They even gave brief introductions to the minerals currently discovered in various regions.","When Feng Tang talked about local customs today, he was also constantly slipping in his own agenda.","He explained the main cash crops of the local areas, the yield per acre, the tax situation, the living conditions of the commoners, and exactly whose hands the land was primarily concentrated in with absolute clarity.","He even casually mentioned the deities worshipped by the local people.","The background information of key officials in regional factions and the military and political spheres was detailed extensively. Feng Tang even analyzed the personalities and moral characters of several important figures.","While Yue Fuguang listened with great interest, her head was full of question marks. Were these things really meant to be spoken out loud?","Yue Fuguang couldn't help but mutter in her heart. Right now, they were talking about the domestic affairs of Great Yan. In a few days, would they start teaching her about the other five nations?","Was this to give her a comprehensive understanding of Great Yan before she even started expanding territories?","[Master, did Feng Tang just say that the border army general of Xinzhou, Murong Liang, has a son named Murong Qian?]","\"It seems so. Little Zhu, what is it? Is there a problem with this Murong Qian?\"","At the entrance of the Hongwen Pavilion, because of this brief exchange, a large golden foot was withdrawn.","[The problem is huge. Master, let me tell you, this Murong Qian is the father of the future Emperor Shizong of Liang, the one who was posthumously honored as Emperor Shizu of Liang.]","[So it was his family that founded the nation after succeeding the Tong family's throne!]","[Master, this Murong Qian is actually Hong Yueling's husband. Do you still remember Hong Yueling, Master?]","Yue Fuguang thought for a brief moment before recalling who she was. \"She is the one who wanted to marry the Crown Prince, and even almost became my sister-in-law. Why didn't she marry the Crown Prince, and instead married into the Murong family stationed at the border?\""]},{"number":287,"title":"Chapter 287: Nurturing bandits to boost one's own importance Killing innocent civilians to claim false merits","paragraphs":["\"Since Murong Qian is her husband, then Emperor Shizong of Liang couldn't be her son, right?\"","[Master, this matter is a bit complicated. It's a long story.]","\"It's fine, we have plenty of time. Take your time and tell it slowly, I'll just treat it as listening to a story.\"","The few people sitting behind Yue Fuguang were nodding madly in their hearts. The Junior Preceptor was right, the Divine Artifact must absolutely not make a long story short.","Tell it slowly, they also loved listening to stories!","[Let's address the first question. The reason Hong Yueling wanted to marry the Crown Prince wasn't because she wanted to cling to the powerful and enjoy wealth and glory.","It was entirely because her mother, Madam Fang, had only given birth to her, a single daughter. Without a son, she was constantly looked down upon by her mother-in-law and sisters-in-law in her husband's family.","Even her husband, Hong Yueling's father, Hanlin Academy Reader-in-Waiting Hong Feng, lost respect for Madam Fang due to her lack of a male heir to carry on the family line.","Hong Yueling wanted to marry well just to win some face for her mother in the Hong family. Even after she married, she would be able to protect the only person who truly loved her.]","\"This Hong Feng, as a Hanlin Reader-in-Waiting, although his status isn't high, is at least considered a courtier relatively close to the Emperor.","Disrespecting his legitimate wife... he couldn't be favoring a concubine and destroying his wife, could he?\"","Thud!","As Yue Fuguang's words fell, in front of the Hongwen Pavilion, among the officials who were intending to welcome the Emperor and his entourage, a person suddenly dropped to his knees with a thud right in front of Emperor Mingxi's golden boots.","Ever since Yue Fuguang started giving lessons, much of the teaching at the Hanlin Academy had been taken over by various well-connected lords, but the daily work and the lessons for the princes next door were still primarily taught by them.","Therefore, Reader-in-Waiting Hong was exceptionally lucky to be present today, and just so happened to hear the gossip about his own family along with everyone else!","With the Junior Preceptor pinning the label of 'favoring a concubine and destroying a wife' on him, regardless of whether it was true or not, he had to kneel first.","[In Hong Feng's backyard, there is one wife and four concubines. Aside from the legitimate wife Madam Fang, the other concubines all have sons and daughters. It is hard to tell which concubine he favors most.","However, he truly favors the eldest concubine-born son and the third concubine-born daughter born to Concubine Mu. He treats her better than all the other wives and concubines, including the legitimate wife Madam Fang, and her pillow talk is the most effective.","Even Hong Yueling's marriage to Murong Qian was orchestrated by Concubine Mu, who hails from a branch family of the Mu clan in Xinzhou!]","\"Are you saying Hong Feng let a concubine interfere with the marriage of his legitimate daughter? This legitimate daughter's birth mother is still alive, and the girl was neither born nor raised by the concubine. Is it any of her business?","Does this not count as favoring a concubine and destroying a wife?\"","Thump thump thump!","Along with Yue Fuguang's words, the sound of Hong Feng kowtowing became the perfect background music.","A few days ago, Concubine Mu had indeed mentioned his eldest daughter's marriage to him, saying there was a fine young man on her maiden family's side who was very suitable for Yueling.","At first, when he heard it was a family of military generals, he had refused.","But Concubine Mu said that a great scholar had emerged from a branch of the Murong family. If the marriage between the two families was successful, perhaps their eldest son, Hong Yulin, could become a disciple under that great scholar.","Hong Feng admitted he was tempted. He had even planned to bring the matter up with Madam Fang in a few days.","As if thinking of something, Yue Fuguang continued to ask, \"How old is Hong Feng's third concubine-born daughter this year?\"","[Hong Yufei is fifteen, two years younger than Hong Yueling.]","\"Why didn't Concubine Mu betroth her own daughter to Murong Qian? Is there something wrong with him, or is there another reason?\"","[Master has seen Hong Yueling's portrait; in the eyes of mortals, she is a rare beauty. This Murong Qian is someone who values a woman's looks.","When Concubine Mu wanted her son to take Murong Wen as his teacher and was rejected, she heard that the Murong family in Lancheng was looking for a wife for their youngest son, so she thought of the beautiful Hong Yueling.]","\"So this Hong Feng wants to sell his daughter to seek glory for his son? What a calculating move!\"","Hong Feng had kowtowed until he was almost dizzy, praying madly in his heart: Oh ancestors, please stop talking, he truly knew he was wrong!","Hong Feng really couldn't figure out how he had offended these two ancestors. As things stood, everything seemed to have been done by Concubine Mu.","Why was every word from the Junior Preceptor targeted at him?","Yue Fuguang: Because the root of the problem is you! No matter how high Concubine Mu jumps, without your nod of approval, all her schemes are just empty talk.","At this moment, Hong Feng blamed heaven and earth, but he did not dare harbor the slightest resentment toward those two ancestors.","He knew clearly that since he could hear the inner voices now, as long as he had a good attitude in admitting his mistakes, he could still be saved. If he ever harbored resentment toward those two, he might end up like a certain unlucky fool, losing the light and returning to darkness, unable to hear the inner voices anymore—then he'd truly be finished!","\"Little Zhu, what kind of person is Murong Qian, and how was Hong Yueling's life after marrying him?\"","[Master, Murong Qian is the exact opposite of his name. He is arrogant, conceited, and obstinate. He clearly only has half a bucket of knowledge, yet he is haughty and considers himself extraordinary.","He compares himself to talented scholars and banished immortals, yet he lives a dissolute life, sleeping among flowers and willows. In the border city of Lancheng, he is a notorious playboy. Compared to him, Wei Yan and Cai Bing could be considered good boys.","When it came to finding him a wife, the families the Murong family took a fancy to were unwilling to marry their daughters to him. As for those who wanted to cling to them, either the Murong family disdained their low status, or Murong Qian thought the girls weren't pretty enough.","The Mu family wanted to cling to the Murong family. When Concubine Mu learned of this news, it led to the ill-fated karma between Murong Qian and Hong Yueling.]","\"Ill-fated karma? Did they not have a good life after getting married?\"","[Hong Yueling was forced to marry for the sake of her birth mother, Madam Fang. For the first two years of their marriage, because Murong Qian was captivated by Hong Yueling's fresh beauty, he restrained himself somewhat. Although he still went out to fool around and live a dissolute life, at least he didn't bring his messes in front of Hong Yueling, so she just pretended not to know.","However, as she gradually became more familiar with the Murong family, she slowly discovered Murong Liang's secret, which could also be called the history of his rise to power.","The secret of how he climbed from a low-level military officer to one of the five great defending generals of the border army without relying on his family.]","Outside the courtyard, Emperor Mingxi signaled the imperial guards to drag Hong Feng to the side, deciding to deal with him later.","Stroking his beard, he fell into deep thought. Since Murong Liang was one of the five great defending generals stationed at the southernmost border of Great Yan, he was naturally very familiar with his life history.","Murong Liang was forty-three years old. Before the age of thirty, he was merely a low-ranking officer leading only a few hundred men.","From the age of thirty onward, relying on his personal bravery and multiple successes in repelling bandits outside the borders, he climbed step by step to his current position.","Could there be a problem with his promotions? Did he falsely report his battle results or falsely claim the achievements of others?","Emperor Mingxi couldn't help but think of Zheng Feng, who was still in the Right Martial Guard's new recruit camp. Wasn't his experience exactly that of having his military merits falsely claimed by a superior!","\"What secret? Little Zhu, don't keep me in suspense, make a long story short.\"","[Master, to make a long story short, Hong Yueling discovered that Murong Liang was raising bandits to elevate his own importance, killing innocent civilians to claim military merit, and even raising mountain bandits to plunder passing merchants.","The initial funds for the Murong family's rise were accumulated bit by bit starting from that time.]","\"Raising bandits to elevate his own importance! Killing civilians for merit? If Hong Yueling could discover this, did the rest of the Murong family know? What happened to Hong Yueling later?\"","[When Hong Yueling discovered this, she had already been married to Murong Qian for over two years. Because Murong Qian had indulged in matters of men and women too early,","he had ruined his body. As a result, the two of them didn't have a child even after over two years of marriage. As time passed, Murong Qian's feelings for her faded, and he often did not return home.","Using this as an excuse, Hong Yueling wanted to take the opportunity of returning to the capital for medical treatment to report this matter to the imperial court.]"]},{"number":288,"title":"Chapter 288: He felt like he was going to shatter too","paragraphs":["\"Murong Qian's body is already ruined, yet he still visits brothels? Isn't he afraid those women will despise him for being impotent?\"","Everyone who heard her question had dark lines on their faces. Lord Junior Preceptor, aren't you focusing on the wrong point?","At such a critical moment, shouldn't you be asking the Divine Artifact if Miss Hong successfully left the Murong family?","[Doesn't he have medicine for that! Master, Murong Liang nurtures the enemy to elevate his own status. Not only does he merely repel the enemy's harassment during wartime without destroying their core strength,","he deliberately slows down his offensive when the enemy is weak, even tacitly allowing them to recover.","He also murders innocent civilians under his rule, claiming their heads as enemy kills for merit, falsifies military intelligence, and exaggerates his battle results.","He secretly trades supplies with the enemy, exchanging weapons and armor for horses, medicinal herbs, and other goods.","And as one of the five major defending generals of the border army, the defense zone Murong Liang is stationed at is precisely the border between Great Yan, Nanzhao, and Nanyue.","So, Master, do you really think Murong Qian couldn't get his hands on some aphrodisiacs?]","\"Then did Hong Yueling return to the capital smoothly?\"","Everyone breathed a sigh of relief. The topic that these two ancestors had derailed was finally brought back on track.","However, Emperor Mingxi and his ministers didn't think the previous topic was off-track, because they heard crucial information from the words of those two ancestors.","Murong Qian was actually secretly trading with the enemy, and it was even important strategic materials like weapons and armor!","Hiss! Emperor Mingxi was so angry he almost pulled out a tuft of his own beard.","[Naturally, she did not. The Murong family was not completely ignorant of Murong Qian's condition, hence the issue of not being able to have children.","Although they had complaints, Murong Qian's backyard had several concubines and bedmates besides Hong Yueling, and not a single one could bear a child.","It was obvious at a glance who the problem lay with.","Therefore, the Murong family said they would invite renowned doctors from the capital to diagnose and treat them, so she didn't have to go through the arduous journey of traveling thousands of miles back.","After being rejected the first time, the resilient Hong Yueling still didn't give up. Just at this time, a letter from the Hong family arrived saying that Madam Fang was ill.","They asked Hong Yueling to help find a few precious medicinal herbs, because with the border mutual trade, herbs from Nanzhao and Nanyue were relatively easy to find.","Using this excuse, Hong Yueling continued to bring up her desire to return to the capital to visit her mother.]","\"Did she succeed?\"","This question also appeared in everyone's minds at the same time.","[No!]","Unfortunately, the Divine Artifact's answer disappointed them greatly once again.","\"Why is it this time? Isn't the Murong family being too overbearing? A daughter-in-law returning to her maiden home to visit her sick mother is very much in line with filial piety, isn't it?","What reason did they have to refuse?","Hong Yueling married into the Murong family; she wasn't sold to them.\"","[Master, because the Murong family naturally has its own intelligence channels in the upper capital city. As in-laws, they would naturally pay attention to the affairs of the Hong family.","At that time, Madam Fang was indeed ill, but she had merely caught a chill and it was nothing serious.","The Hong family used this as a pretext to ask Hong Yueling to collect good medicinal herbs, which were actually meant to be used to pull strings for Hong Feng's eldest illegitimate son, Hong Yulin.]","\"This Hong Feng is really something. Selling his daughter once for his son wasn't enough; now he's thinking of this daughter again for his future prospects.","Didn't Concubine Mu plot Hong Yueling's marriage in the first place just to get Hong Yulin a good teacher?","Why didn't that so-called great scholar of the Murong family accept him?\"","[He did accept him, but because Hong Yulin's aptitude was mediocre, he only took him in as an honorary disciple. However, he did accept Concubine Mu's nephew, Mu Cong, as a formal disciple.","Master, that so-called great scholar Murong Sheng is a fraud himself. He only has the title of a great scholar because the Murong family spent money to promote him.","Hong Yulin studied for a few years and was still just a provincial graduate. Concubine Mu then set her sights on Yuxi Academy, wanting to send her son to study under its headmaster.]","Hong Feng, who was kneeling on the ground and didn't dare to get up, felt like dying when he heard the Little Immortal Lord mention him again!","But in his heart, there was mostly incompetent rage and resentment—resentment towards the Mu clan and the Mu family.","Meanwhile, several officials beside Emperor Mingxi strongly agreed with the Divine Artifact's words.","In the eyes of these top-tier metropolitan graduates, Murong Sheng indeed had an unearned reputation; his profound knowledge might not even surpass theirs.","Not having experienced the baptism of the imperial examinations, not having crossed the single-log bridge with thousands of troops and horses, in their view, meant he was unworthy of the name.","All that talk about being indifferent to fame and fortune, focusing solely on scholarship, and disdaining an official career was just nonsense!","If you can't pass the exam, you can't pass it; spouting all that is useless.","After all, in their eyes, failing to pass the metropolitan exam and passing it but choosing not to be an official were two entirely different things.","\"So the Murong family, knowing the truth, rejected Hong Yueling's request?\"","[Yes. Master just said that Hong Yueling married into the Murong family and wasn't sold by the Hong family. Although the words sound harsh,","the actual situation is pretty much the same.","How could Hong Feng, a dignified and noble Hanlin academician, not know the consequences of not letting his own wife, Madam Fang, handle the Murong family's betrothal gifts and their daughter's dowry?","His own mother and concubine tampered with the dowry. To say he didn't know about it, not even a dog would believe it.","Since Hong Yueling got married, the family's living conditions improved, and they could casually buy curios they couldn't afford before. How could he not know?]","\"So this noble Hanlin Academy Reader-in-Waiting not only favored his concubine over his wife, but also sold his daughter for glory?\"","[Exactly! Hong Yueling later proposed returning to the capital to visit her family several times, but was rejected every time. This matter also aroused the suspicion of Murong Liang and his wife, who is Murong Qian's biological mother.","Later, it was her bedfellow Murong Qian who first discovered Hong Yueling's issue and found an excuse to place her under house arrest.","Later, Hong Yueling managed to escape and was just a hair's breadth away from getting away, but in the end, she was caught and brought back by Murong Qian's men.","However, before being caught, Hong Yueling deliberately exposed herself to lure away the pursuers, allowing her close maidservant Hongque to sneak back to the capital to deliver a message.","Unfortunately, Hongque told Hong Feng the message that Hong Yueling had exchanged her safety for, but Hong Feng did not report it to Emperor Mingxi, who was already bedridden with severe illness at the time.","This news wasn't just about Murong Qian nurturing the enemy to elevate his own status, secretly doing business with enemy nations, and keeping bandits to rob traveling merchants.","It was also about her husband Murong Qian being privately intimate with a Nanyue man. This Nanyue man was Ling Yuanhang, the Ghost Hand General who had already married Miss Jiang and would massacre Lan City in the future.]","Yue Fuguang made a bold guess, \"So, Ling Yuanhang attacking Lan City also had a contribution from the Murong family, or rather, Murong Qian?","Why did that Hong Feng cover up for the Murong family?\"","Bang!","Hong Feng, who was already scared silly and couldn't figure out even if he racked his brains why his future self wouldn't report such important news, was suddenly kicked flying by Emperor Mingxi's large foot, his body crashing into a flowerpot by the path.","With a loud bang!","Hong Feng collided with the flowerpot. The flowerpot shattered, and he felt like he was going to shatter too!","[Of course. Hong Feng initially had the thought of reporting it. The news his daughter traded her life for would only be a great merit for him. As for his in-law relationship with the Murong family, the Emperor certainly wouldn't punish him for it.","But this matter was found out by Hong Yulin. As a student of the great Murong scholar, even though he was only an honorary one, he still had a lot of face in literary circles.","Naturally, he didn't want his backer to fall, nor did he want his status as a disciple of Murong Wen to affect his future official career.","So, he persuaded Hong Feng by saying that the Emperor was plagued by severe illness and could pass away any day.]"]},{"number":289,"title":"Chapter 289: The Name of Hong Yueling Remembered by the World","paragraphs":["[He also said that the Emperor was gravely ill and the imperial court was in decline, so they definitely lacked the energy and strength to deal with the powerful Murong family. If his father reported it, it would only offend the Murong family and make life difficult for both siblings. With this, he successfully persuaded Hong Feng.]","Hong Feng is a dignified Hanlin scholar, yet he is so easily swayed! What happened to Hong Yueling after she was captured and taken back by Murong Qian?","[After being taken back, Hong Yueling would rather die than submit. In the end, Murong Qian broke her legs and placed her under strict house arrest.","She endured for nearly another year before finally dying of depression.","Before her death, she secretly left a final letter, which saw the light of day again a century later. Only then did the world learn of the rotten flesh hidden beneath the loyal and patriotic facade of the Murong family's founding ancestor Murong Liang and Emperor Shizu Murong Qian.","It could be said that Hong Yueling's final letter gave history its truth, tearing away the fig leaf the Murong family had hidden behind for a hundred years.","It also shattered the fragile outer shell of the Great Liang Dynasty, which supposedly governed the country with loyalty and filial piety.","Only then did the people of that time suddenly realize that the Murong family's frequent boasting about their past loyalty to their former master, Great Yan, was the biggest lie and joke of the Great Liang Dynasty.","Because of this, the name of Hong Yueling was remembered by the world.]","Hong Yueling and Chu Qiuyue were both extraordinary women; they used different methods to return the truth to the world.","So that means Emperor Shizong of Liang wasn't Hong Yueling's child. To think that the impotent Murong Qian could actually still have children!","Addicted to cutting off people's bloodlines, Yue Fuguang thought rather maliciously that it would have been great if Hong Yueling had a packet of sterilization poison called 'Not a Single Seed' on hand back then.","Just look at how the Pingyue Marquis's family had been turned upside down because of it.","That day, Xue Chao poisoned his three younger brothers with the sterilization drug overnight. Now, the Xue family had four infertile legitimate sons, and only two and a half grandsons. The old Marquis probably couldn't even enjoy his meals anymore.","[Murong Qian was heartbroken after Hong Yueling's death. After a period of decadence, he actually began to cultivate his moral character in a rare change of pace, no longer going out to visit brothels or getting close to women.","By the time war broke out everywhere and Great Yan perished, he was entirely focused on his career.]","Yue Fuguang was speechless for a moment. Is it really this melodramatic? Don't tell me Murong Qian only realized then that Hong Yueling was his true love!","This was an insult to Hong Yueling. Ultimately, Hong Yueling died because he imprisoned her. Yue Fuguang suddenly felt that Murong Qian was even more disgusting!","[Master, there's more. When Murong Qian later died of old age, he was buried together with Hong Yueling.]","Yue Fuguang ground her teeth. He shouldn't even dream of it in this lifetime. If that Hong Feng agrees to the marriage between the two families, Little Zhu, your master allows you to break Hong Feng's legs.","And confiscate Murong Qian's reproductive tools!","Everyone who heard this felt a chilling breeze run down their legs. Hong Feng was so scared that he curled up his body and shook his head repeatedly; he wouldn't dare do it again!","Curled up into a ball, Hong Feng didn't know if it was just his imagination, but his legs ached faintly.","Meanwhile, the eyes of the girls in the Hongwen Pavilion lit up. Yue Fuguang seemed to have accidentally opened the door to a whole new world for them.","[Rest assured, Master. Little Zhu promises to do it cleanly and efficiently, without leaving a trace.","Furthermore, as for this Murong Qian, those few years of cultivating his character really allowed him to nurse his body back to health. A year after the fall of Great Yan, his newly wedded wife gave birth to a son for him the following year.]","The Heavenly Dao really treats him well, actually letting him recover his health! Is this son the future Emperor Shizong of Liang, Murong Xi? So Murong Qian's so-called focus on his career was colluding with Nanyue to bring down Great Yan?","Yue Fuguang's questions cut straight to the bone, slicing into the hearts of the Great Yan monarch and his ministers, stabbing into Hong Feng, and sealing the doom of the Murong family.","[Master guessed correctly. Emperor Shizong of Liang is Murong Qian's only son, Murong Xi.","Murong Qian's so-called career building wasn't just as simple as colluding with Nanyue, being good brothers with Ling Yuanhang, and the two of them undermining Great Yan together.","He even persuaded his father to withdraw their troops early when Ling Yuanhang attacked Lancheng, calling it preserving their strength.","He also secretly joined Panshan, the mysterious organization that manipulated regime changes behind the scenes in various countries and provoked internal court disputes.","Panshan put in a lot of effort behind the scenes to help Murong Xi successfully replace the Southern Zhou established by the Tong family.]","Yue Fuguang instantly understood. A person's success, whether it was Ling Yuanhang or Murong Xi, always had various reasons behind it, or various people acting as driving forces.","And this Panshan organization was like a shadow enveloping this vast land; it wasn't just a threat to Great Yan.","Even the succession of heirs in those other countries faintly bore its traces.","Unfortunately, with the system's current capabilities, it was still unable to uproot this deeply entrenched organization, let alone lock onto the helmsman of Panshan.","All the two of them could do right now, when facing this invisible, shapeless behemoth, was to dismantle it node by node.","[Host, don't worry. Once my data recovers a bit more, I will definitely be able to find their bigger bosses.]","No rush, we'll take it slowly.","Now was the time to lay out their plans. They would first sort out Great Yan's internal problems. Only after enriching the country and strengthening the military would they begin to expand outward.","If the interior was unstable, doing more would only be working for the benefit of others.","To put it bluntly, her first step was simply to keep Great Yan from dying.","Then, she would cure its severe illnesses, nurse it back to health, arm it, and only then let it out to bite people!","The various officials in the imperial court didn't know what had suddenly provoked their Majesty, but ever since returning from the Hongwen Pavilion, he had angrily issued several edicts.","They covered both military and political matters, with their target pointing directly at the Southwest Border Army.","Minister of War Huo Ying had truly been having a hard time these past few days.","The new army of ten thousand men had actually been infiltrated. From the rear kitchens to the vanguard, if it hadn't been for the Junior Preceptor, they wouldn't have known how long it would take to discover it.","He and Wei Shouyi, along with others, investigated back and forth, but after several days, they had only found three people.","He hadn't even wrapped this matter up cleanly yet, and now the matter with Murong Liang had cropped up!","Huo Ying thought: My life is over!","Equally enveloped in gloom were Cai Xian, Wei Ping, and the others. It was already known that the Eastern Yi prince, Matsuyama, had secretly sneaked back into Shangjing City, and Feng Yang, the old pavilion master of the Wind and Rain Pavilion, had also come to Shangjing with an unknown purpose.","For these two people, they had dispatched extra manpower to search for about ten days, yet they hadn't found a single clue. This left the two of them feeling incredibly frustrated.","As if that wasn't enough, just as the two of them were leading their respective men on a city-wide search for Feng Yang and Matsuyama, the bait laid by their ruler and ministers was almost eaten by the fish due to a moment of inattention.","Of the Fourth Prince and the Ninth Prince, one was riding a horse outside the palace when it suddenly got spooked. If the guards beside him hadn't reacted quickly...","The Fourth Prince would certainly have been killed or injured then.","Meanwhile, the Ninth Prince, who still held the title of prince within the palace, accidentally slipped and fell into a lotus pond while playing in a secluded garden of the imperial palace.","If the weather hadn't been slowly warming up, he wouldn't have even lasted until the passing Eighth Prince discovered and rescued him; he would have inexplicably become yet another wrongfully dead ghost in the lotus pond.","The last person to die there seemed to be Zhuo Fei, his mother's cousin, who, in order to cover up their illicit affair, ruthlessly drowned a young palace maid who had witnessed their scandalous deed in that very lotus pond."]},{"number":290,"title":"Chapter 290: The Darkness Under the Lamp","paragraphs":["Therefore, ever since the Ninth Prince fell in, rumors spread through the palace that the little palace maid was seeking his life.","As soon as this happened, the emperor and his ministers all knew in their hearts that those people had started to cause trouble!","As for the rumors in the imperial palace, Emperor Mingxi did not order anyone to suppress them. Let them spread; if they didn't, how could he follow the vine to get the melon and uproot the hidden forces within the palace?","When the prince unexpectedly encountered danger, on the surface, the emperor merely ordered the palace servants to send some gifts to console the two of them before concluding the matter as an accident.","He appeared to be rather unconcerned about the two and the matters surrounding them.","Consequently, the helpless Ninth Prince could only swallow his anger.","However, the Fourth Prince, who still had some backing, refused to let it go.","From the grooms to the guards, he had them all arrested and thoroughly interrogated.","And his birth mother, Concubine Xin, who was usually as aloof from worldly strife as a Bodhisattva, smelled the scent of a conspiracy aimed solely at her son for the first time.","She could finally sit still no longer.","\"Master Yue, what should we do now? Little Four's startled horse incident this time was definitely premeditated!\"","Because she had eaten the fruits and vegetables bestowed by Emperor Mingxi, Concubine Xin had grown healthier day by day. Although Emperor Mingxi, upon learning the truth later, did not send much more, Concubine Xin's health had indeed greatly improved. Now, she was so anxious that she paced back and forth in her palace without feeling tired.","\"Your Highness, we are currently grounded and cannot go anywhere. Your anxiety will not help matters.\"","Yue Ying's face was pale at this moment. This cold had cost him half his life. For some unknown reason, no matter what medicine he took, he never seemed to get better; instead, his condition worsened day by day.","Because the Fourth Prince had offended Junior Preceptor Yue, everyone in their palace was implicated and grounded, and his illness had dragged on for over a month.","He had already missed the date to meet his junior martial brother Qi Ming. He only hoped that, without his help, his junior brother could successfully complete the mission assigned by the Emperor of Yue.","At this time, Yue Ying did not yet know that the good junior brother he was worrying about was currently locked up in the lowest level of the heavenly prison.","Just waiting for the day they would reunite.","\"But I feel that this time is different from the usual schemes and fights for favor in the harem. This incident was aimed directly at taking Little Four's life.","Moreover, the opponent's strength is unknown, and their origins and motives are unclear.\"","Over the past two days, Concubine Xin had even suspected Emperor Mingxi, the father himself.","She thought the emperor had discovered their plan and wanted to finish off Little Four, his own son, to break the Emperor of Yue's layout.","But all signs indicated that this matter was indeed not orchestrated by the emperor.","\"Your Highness, even if your guess is correct, our hands and feet are currently tied. So what you need to do now is figure out how to regain favor and have the emperor lift our grounding, cough... cough, cough...\"","Before he could finish two sentences, Yue Ying started coughing again. He felt like he was going to cough his lungs out, yet his throat still felt itchy and dry.","Seeing his face turn entirely red from coughing, as if he would stop breathing in the next second, Concubine Xin temporarily suppressed her worry for her son and turned to care about Yue Ying's health.","\"Master Yue, why is your illness not getting any better? Is the medicine not treating the symptoms?\"","Concubine Xin thought about it and concluded this was the only reason. After all, the medicine was from their own palace, and the prescription was written by themselves.","Surely no one would tamper with the medicine just to harm a senior palace maid by her side!","Emperor Mingxi would tell you that someone actually would!","If it weren't for the sake of keeping Gan Sheng steady, he wouldn't have to be so constrained and convoluted just to kill someone on his own turf!","Emperor Mingxi really wanted to swear, 'This is too damn frustrating!' Sooner or later, he would make Gan Sheng taste this feeling too!","Yue Ying leaned half against the pillow, waving his hand weakly, \"The prescription is fine. It is my own body that has a problem.\"","In his early years, when he studied under his master Du Zhongxian, he had tasted a hundred poisons, damaging the foundation of his body. Although he had slowly recuperated and recovered somewhat in the Great Yan imperial palace over the years.","But this cold came fiercely and immediately triggered the hidden ailments in his body.","There were even a few times when Yue Ying faintly felt that his end was approaching!","Both master and disciple could not help but frown, adding two more to the gloomy atmosphere.","Entering the end of April, the weather was just like the lingering haze in everyone's hearts, with continuous drizzling rain.","The over-forty-year-old Emperor Mingxi seemed to have hit his midlife crisis early. During today's morning assembly, he looked particularly displeased.","He had been single-handedly venting and roaring at the court for quite a while.","The reason was simply that the people he wanted to catch hadn't been caught, and those he wanted to kill still had to be dealt with slowly.","This had utterly frustrated the supreme emperor!","He had to secretly order the spies hidden in various countries to speed up their layout. Since they had fired the first shot, they shouldn't blame him for retaliating!","Yue Fuguang couldn't help but pick her ear and ask the system, \"Tongtong, have you found the whereabouts of Matsuyama and Feng Yang?\"","[Host, the points you spent were not wasted. The data of the Melon-Eating System has recovered a little bit more.","Isn't finding two people a piece of cake?]","The growth gap between the Melon-Eating System and the Merit System was gradually widening, and the system was becoming severely unbalanced.","Neither the person nor the system had realized the impropriety of this yet.","Because at this time, Yue Fuguang was more concerned about finding the two and eliminating them, so she could quickly earn back the spent points.","Therefore, she replied perfunctorily to the system, which felt it was capable again after just recovering a bit of data, \"I knew Tongtong, you are the most amazing system.","Hurry up and tell me, where are these two right now?\"","[Host, these two are really cunning. There is a saying in your hometown that a crafty rabbit has three burrows. These two have changed locations five times in ten days.","Tell me, isn't that outrageous!]","Yue Fuguang nodded in agreement, \"It really is outrageous! Don't tell me that right after you tell me their current spot,","they'll just move again!\"","The system thought about it and agreed, so it had a brainwave and said, [Master, I know where Matsuyama and Feng Yang are hiding.]","Yue Fuguang, who was still dozing with her eyes closed, only moved her eyeballs. Still maintaining a half-leaning posture, her lazy voice echoed in the grand hall.","\"Didn't you say yesterday that they just changed places? Where did they move to today?\"","[Hehe, the place they moved to today is very interesting. Moreover, the two rarely thought alike, both taking the route that the most dangerous place is the safest.","They pulled a 'darkness under the lamp' trick on Wei Ping and Cai Xian.]","Seeing Wei Ping and Cai Xian looking anxious like monkeys, the system stopped keeping them in suspense and readily started reporting the address.","[Matsuyama is currently hiding diagonally across from the Shangjing County Magistrate's Office, in the number one chain inn across multiple planes—Yuelai Inn.","This guy truly lives up to being royalty; he never wrongs himself no matter where he goes. He is now staying in the inn's best Heaven Number One room, letting his sister Yōko stay in a standard superior room.","The siblings are even pretending not to know each other.]","Yue Fuguang was a bit speechless and couldn't help but complain, \"This short melon, if you say he's cautious, he high-profilely stays next door to the county magistrate's office, and in the most eye-catching Heaven Number One room at that.","If you say he's not cautious, he knows not to put all his eggs in one basket.","Where are all his subordinates?\"","The Dongyi people's concept of hierarchy was even stronger than that of Great Yan. His subordinates would certainly not allow a prince and an imperial princess to stay in an inn alone."]},{"number":291,"title":"Chapter 291: To hide himself, he made quite a sacrifice","paragraphs":["[Some are staying in the servants' quarters, some are setting up stalls nearby, and a few others went out to gather information about the imperial estate. It's expected they will make a move on the imperial estate within these two days.]","\"Make a move on the imperial estate? Matsuyama secretly sneaked back into the capital just for the things inside the imperial estate?\"","As soon as Yue Fuguang's words came out, the Great Yan court instantly fell dead silent! All that remained was heavy breathing and the rustling sounds of clothes rubbing as people shifted uneasily.","Emperor Mingxi, who had just been performing a stand-up comedy routine of his own, suddenly looked like a goose caught by the neck. No matter how fierce or brave he was, he couldn't make a single sound for a moment.","A few people's faces instantly turned pale, cold sweat dripping down their temples. They all knew what the things inside meant for the current Great Yan and for its people three years from now.","If something went wrong with the things inside, they wouldn't just have to worry about how the emperor would deal with them; even the Junior Preceptor, who had slowly begun to change her opinion of them, would probably pack up and run away.","After all, she had explicitly said she didn't play with useless trash!","As the monarch and officials of Great Yan were terrified, everyone couldn't help but ask the same question in their hearts: How did the Dongyi people know that good things were planted in the imperial estate?","Although the private fields of emperors in various countries were planted with exotic flowers, rare herbs, and strange fruit trees not commonly seen by the outside world.","Because they were rare, they were destined to be enjoyed only by a few. Therefore, even if curious, no royalty would easily touch the things in another country's imperial estate.","Since Matsuyama wanted to touch the things in the imperial estate, he must be aiming for the high-yield premium seeds.","So the question was, who told him this news?","At this moment, Emperor Mingxi, who had recovered slightly, looked at everyone with suspicion.","Sitting upright on his high throne, his gloomy gaze slowly swept over the officials who had their heads bowed and eyes lowered.","The imperial majesty rushed forth, pressing down on the hundred or so people so hard they held their breath. The air grew so stagnant it felt as if water could be wrung from it.","The cold sweat seeping from the temples of Wang Shouchen, Huo Ying, Cai Xian, and the others was even worse than the continuous spring rain that had been falling outside the hall for three days.","The silence at this moment was more terrifying than thunder; it was the calm before the storm.","Yue Fuguang and the system ignored this tense, hostile atmosphere and continued their conversation. [It is indeed for the potatoes inside. These fools still don't know that besides potatoes, there are other good things of the same tier in there. However, with just a dozen or so lackeys under him, stealing potatoes from under Shen Jian and the others' strict guard is still a rather arduous task.]","\"Little Zhu, you are actually worrying for him!\"","[Oh, Master, isn't it because life has been too boring lately! When Matsuyama and his group of shorties go to steal from the imperial estate, I'll do a live broadcast for you, Master!]","Everyone felt helpless while also having a head full of question marks. The divine artifact was once again saying things they couldn't understand.","Not to mention they couldn't figure out what a live broadcast was.","Listening closely, these two ancestors had been talking for a long time, but neither of them remembered to give them a heads-up. Could it be that because of their incompetence, they had disappointed the little immortal once again!","\"Watching the Dongyi people steal vegetables? That sounds quite fun!\"","Ever since the system upgraded to level four, Yue Fuguang hadn't used the live broadcast function yet. This time, she could give it a try.","She just didn't know if Wei Ping and the others would arrest them right now, or cast a long line to catch a big fish.","Everyone: So live broadcast means to watch as a spectator? The Junior Preceptor wants to watch, so should they arrest the people now or not?","Wei Ping and Cai Xian carefully looked toward their emperor.","Their hearts instantly settled down by more than half, all because their emperor's complexion was much better now than before.","Emperor Mingxi saw their little movements and really wanted to snort coldly, but fearing Yue Fuguang might misunderstand, he forcefully held it back.","\"Little Zhu, now that we're done talking about Matsuyama, tell me where that Feng Yang is hiding right now?\"","[Master, this Feng Yang is even better at hiding. He is currently hiding in the Great Buddha Temple.]","The Great Buddha Temple? Wei Ping and Cai Xian exchanged a glance. They had led men to all the temples and Daoist shrines near the capital.","They hadn't found any suspicious persons in the Great Buddha Temple. Could it be that they had been careless and missed him again?","\"Are you talking about the temple that is as famous as the Baoye Temple, where my grandfather once stole golden lotus seeds?\"","Yu Chongshan: Great, a secret hidden for decades, now known by the entire court in a single day!","What a good granddaughter, truly honoring her grandfather to death!","Yu Chongshan couldn't help but blush. It had been a long time since he felt this embarrassed!","Yu Zhongchun and his two brothers couldn't help but twitch the corners of their mouths. Having accidentally learned their old man's secret today, wouldn't the old man fly into a rage out of humiliation and take it out on them!","After all, the old man couldn't bear to complain even a little bit about his precious golden nugget.","[That's the one. This time, his method of hiding is different from the last. Today's Feng Yang goes by the Buddhist name Liaofeng, and he is a legally certified wandering monk.","By staying temporarily at the Great Buddha Temple as a visiting monk, not only does he get free food and lodging, but it also helped him evade the imperial court's searches multiple times.]","\"Don't mortals value their hair very much? He made himself bald, and he can't be like us immortals, who can grow flowing long hair on a bald head with a single spell.","To hide himself, his sacrifice is quite big!\"","Immortals can grow hair with a single spell? The middle-aged and elderly officials, who had overworked their brains to the point where scratching their white heads makes their hair even thinner, barely able to hold a hairpin, were once again fiercely envious!","But even more people felt that it was just another day of the Junior Preceptor focusing on the wrong things.","[Feng Yang's public identity in Western Qiang was that of a monk, though he used body doubles back then.","He is only doing this now out of necessity for convenience. Hiding in the Great Buddha Temple not only provides an identity cover, but also because the temple keeper of the Great Buddha Temple is an undercover agent for the Wind and Rain Pavilion.","Master, the purpose of Feng Yang coming to the capital, apart from dealing with the aftermath of Luo Feng's capture and rebuilding the Great Yan headquarters of the Wind and Rain Pavilion, there is another purpose. Guess what it is?]","Yue Fuguang stroked her small chin, thinking of the chaos in the capital before the Crown Prince's wedding. \"Coming for me?\"","[Yes and no. Tonight, Feng Yang will order all the Wind and Rain Pavilion assassins in the capital to split into three groups. One group will set fire to the East Market to attract the city's attention and defense forces.","Another group will wait for an opportunity to sneak into the Yu Manor to abduct you. If they can't take you alive, dead is fine too.","Finally, he will personally lead people to sneak into the Xuanwei Manor to steal the potato seedlings.]","\"Quite a good calculation! It's just that his dog guts are too big, actually daring to covet my life. Then let him come but never return!","Little Zhu, keep an eye on tonight's operation. When all the people from the Wind and Rain Pavilion are out, if the Great Yan soldiers are incompetent and can't catch Feng Yang, remember to finish him off.\"","Yue Fuguang had opened her eyes by this time, just in time to see the sunlight spilling through the window lattices of the main hall, casting mottled halos of light and adding a touch of liveliness to the purple, crimson, blue, and green official robes.","\"The spring scenery is wonderful, perfect for sending him on his way.\"","Everyone heard a trace of murderous intent in the Junior Preceptor's plain words.","[Master, Little Zhu will open the live broadcast for you then!]","Wei Ping and Cai Xian exchanged a glance; Feng Yang could not be kept alive.","At this time, Emperor Mingxi's anger was also surging upwards. It was one thing for these people to covet his potatoes, but they actually greedily tried to abduct their Junior Preceptor time and time again."]},{"number":292,"title":"Chapter 292: One Person, One Hundred Taels","paragraphs":["It seemed that taking down the few strongholds of Youtan and Tianxing Pavilion a few days ago didn't hurt them enough!","Meanwhile, more intelligent people were thinking: since Western Qiang and Eastern Yi had already entered the fray for the potatoes, where were Southern Yue, Nanzhao, and Northern Li hiding at this moment?","And what sort of petty tricks would the mysterious Panshan and certain factions within the Great Yan pull?","After Yue Fuguang—one person and one system—\"shared\" the information they grasped, she simply waved her sleeves, leaving without taking a single worry with her.","Leaving behind only the emperor, whose face was as dark as still water, and his \"loyal\" officials who didn't dare speak a word.","In truth, the officials all had their hands raised like Erkang (reaching out desperately) toward Yue Fuguang's fading figure, with only one thought in mind: Please take us with you!","They didn't want to face the furious emperor alone!","According to later records in the Veritable Records of Great Yan, on the thirtieth day of the fourth month in the fifth year of Yuankang, the Emperor was enraged; the officials bowed their heads and dared not speak.","That night, shocking thunder fell from the sky, and riots broke out in multiple places across the capital. In this battle, several leaders of the Wind and Rain Pavilion, one of the three great assassin organizations of the martial world, were executed.","History called it the Bloody Late Spring!","At this time, Yue Fuguang was just woken up by the system: [Host, wake up quickly, the mice are out of their holes!]","Having only just met the Sandman for a short while, Yue Fuguang groggily opened her eyes, only to see a large screen with stereo sound and a VVIP-level high-definition live broadcast.","The long-lost cinematic big-screen live video instantly woke up Yue Fuguang, who hadn't watched a live stream in over three years.","Yue Fuguang glanced out the window and said, \"System, it's time to give this backward era a little bit of a shock!\"","Receiving the command, the system immediately lifted the restrictions. In an instant, a massive live broadcast screen appeared in the sky above Mingyue Pavilion.","In the footage, a man with his head and face covered, his specific appearance indistinguishable, quietly leaped out from the back wall of a temple.","By the time the man reached halfway up the mountain, over a dozen similarly masked people in black clothes had gathered behind him.","At this moment, some of the people hiding in various corners near the Yu Manor, who had been concealing themselves perfectly, were suddenly attracted by something in the sky.","They all craned their necks to look, their eyes and mouths wide open in extreme astonishment!","They let out suppressed, unintelligible gasping sounds.","It was fine for the companions beside them who could see the anomaly in the sky, but those who couldn't, seeing their comrades suddenly looking dumbfounded and then making expressions as if possessed, couldn't help but feel worried and afraid.","This expression clearly meant they had seen something terrifying and were frightened!","But no matter how wide they opened their eyes, they couldn't find anything amiss in the direction of the Yu Manor.","Could it be... could it be there was some evil spirit in the sky that they couldn't see!","While feeling afraid, they couldn't help but worry about what to do with their comrades who had suddenly been scared silly. After all, it didn't matter if they lived or died, but they absolutely couldn't delay the upcoming mission!","The comrades: Having you around is truly my blessing!","Just as some people were hesitating about whether to report to their superiors, these people suddenly returned to normal!","However, their occasional cautious glances up at the sky indicated that they were fine, but not completely fine.","How could those who couldn't see know just how huge of a psychological impact the sudden live broadcast in the sky had on them?","It was no exaggeration to say that their worldviews had been completely reshaped. If the environment hadn't forbidden it, they would have immediately burned incense, bowed, and knelt for a long time.","Especially the guards left behind at Mingyue Pavilion; after the initial shock, they simply marveled at the extraordinary and mighty power of their Lord.","They became even more aware that the golden thigh they were clinging to seemed much thicker than they had imagined.","With hearts full of infinite awe, everyone focused intently on the scenes and moving people in the broadcast from afar.","They still couldn't help but sigh in admiration, as it felt like it was truly happening right before their eyes.","Shen Chunying whispered to Liu Wei, \"Weiwei, look, is that the Giant Buddha Temple?\"","\"Sister Chunying, it is the Giant Buddha Temple. I even went there with my mother to offer incense last year.\"","Xu Xiaoman said in a low voice, \"Sister Chunying, is that person the old geezer Feng Yang?\"","Her eyes flashed with hatred. Her good friend's father, an upright man of the martial world, had died at the hands of the assassins of the Wind and Rain Pavilion.","Now, these people wanted to harm the Lord they had sworn to follow to the death. The newly sixteen-year-old Xu Xiaoman's hatred for Feng Yang's group was maxed out at this moment.","She wished she could go out right now and kill him with her own hands.","Shen Chunying nodded affirmatively, saying with a serious face, \"It's him! Tonight, even if we have to risk our lives, we must eliminate this hidden danger for the Lord!\"","Dai Yuxing, who had appeared behind them at some unknown time, interjected, \"With me and Zhang Fang here, it's not your turn to risk your lives.\"","Dai Yuxing raised the sword in his hand and said, \"It will properly greet those little thieves. You just need to protect the Lord so she isn't disturbed by these random cats and dogs outside.\"","He originally wanted to say not to disturb the Lord's sweet dreams, but the screen overhead made it impossible for him to say that the Lord was still sleeping.","This showed that Dai Yuxing was an honest person who hadn't yet developed superb acting skills, which was also one of the reasons he didn't dare to easily approach Yue Fuguang.","At this time, Feng Yang in the broadcast had already led his people to the foot of the mountain, where over ten more people emerged from the shadows.","The two sides simply made silent hand gestures upon meeting and merged into one group.","\"Little Zhu, didn't they say the imperial court had already wiped out the people of the Wind and Rain Pavilion in the capital?","Where did these thirty-plus people come from? If they slipped through the net, isn't the mesh of this net a bit too large?\"","Hearing the Junior Preceptor's complaint about the large mesh of the net, Wei Ping and Cai Xian, who were leading this matter, both looked embarrassed.","Shen Kang, who was responsible for the arrests, wasn't faring much better. Blushing slightly, he turned to look at his subordinates behind him and lowered his voice, \"Later, keep your eyes peeled. Do not let a single person slip away, or you will be dealt with under military law!\"","After a moment's thought, he added, \"For every person captured, I will personally reward an additional one hundred taels!\"","\"Yes, sir!\"","\"General, just watch us!\"","Hearing the heavy reward, the eyes of Shen Kang's subordinates gleamed with the light of money.","Everyone rubbed their fists and wiped their palms, ready for a fight at any moment.","[Master, Feng Yang brought fifteen people this time, and there are eighteen more left in the villages and towns near the capital. These eighteen are Feng Yang's own people.","Luo Feng, as the Young Pavilion Master, is unaware of this.]","\"Feng Yang doesn't even trust his own son-in-law and heir?\" As expected of an old veteran of the martial world, he had many schemes and always kept a card up his sleeve.","[Ultimately, Luo Feng is also a person of Great Yan, so Feng Yang naturally holds reservations about him. Originally, these people were the safeguard he left for his daughter and grandson.]","The crowd watched as Feng Yang led the thirty-something people along the way, unexpectedly meeting up with two more groups of people en route.","Although these two groups were also dressed in black and masked, observant people would notice that their clothing styles were different from Feng Yang's group. While all were in black, the styles of their night-walking suits were incredibly varied and not unified at all.","Yue Fuguang even spotted two people among them wearing dark blue night-walking suits.","Don't ask how she could see clearly in the dark night. If you must ask, it was because she had passively absorbed quite a bit of incense recently, and she had already transcended the realm of ordinary people with low-level tastes.","\"Little Zhu, are these two groups also Feng Yang's people?\""]},{"number":293,"title":"Chapter 293: Temporary Worker","paragraphs":["\"Master, you definitely wouldn't guess who these people are!\" Hearing the system speak like this, Yue Fuguang had already guessed a bit, but to keep the system working hard, she decided to play dumb and provide it with some emotional validation.","So she deliberately teased it, \"Master truly can't figure out the origins of these people. Why doesn't Little Zhu tell me, who are they all?\"","The system puffed out its little chest and replied, \"Master, both groups are assassins from the Wind and Rain Pavilion, hired at a high price by Feng Yang.","Didn't Little Zhu say before that a portion of the Wind and Rain Pavilion's assassins are 'temporary workers'? Well, these two groups are exactly that.\"","\"The leader of an assassin organization spends money to hire his own organization's external personnel? The Wind and Rain Pavilion really is a bizarre organization!","Hiring seventy or eighty people at once, this Feng Yang is certainly extravagant!\"","This clearly showed his determination to obtain the potato at all costs.","Wei Ping, Cai Xian, and the others, looking at these temporary assassins, secretly gritted their teeth. After capturing Luo Feng, they had heavily interrogated him on this very issue.","Luo Feng used these people as bargaining chips, trading their names for food, drink, and a transfer to a clean cell without rats.","He gave them ten names at a time.","The list they obtained included people from all walks of life, with the majority being from the martial world.","The most outrageous was that one of the assassins was a young woman without any strength to tie up a chicken. For that commission, she didn't hesitate to become a concubine to her target.","After laying plans for three months, she successfully killed the man, and remarkably, no one suspected his death had anything to do with this little concubine.","Indeed, the saying 'when wandering the martial world, do not provoke women, the elderly, or children' holds its weight, and its credibility only rose further after this incident.","They haggled with Luo Feng for over a month before getting a list of just over forty temporary assassins. Some were only known by nicknames, their real names completely unknown, and they had managed to capture barely over twenty people.","Today, seventy-eight arrived at once. Everyone's spirits were lifted; this net had caught far more fish than they had imagined.","\"Master, in the original historical timeline, Feng Yang was even wealthier. The Wind and Rain Pavilion also got a taste of the treasure left by successive ancestors of the Xie family.","For some reason, the treasure that should have fallen to the lineage of Prince Rong was unexpectedly obtained by the emperor.\"","\"What? The treasure of the Xie family's successive ancestors was obtained by Emperor Mingxi? Wasn't the key on Feng Suiyu?","Did she discover its secret?\"","Yue Fuguang felt her voice was thick with genuine confusion at that moment. In terms of vocal performance, giving it an 'excellent' rating wouldn't be an exaggeration, right?","\"It seems Prince Qi revealed this matter to the emperor to save his own life. The emperor questioned the two sisters and eventually found the key in Feng Suiyu's hairpin.","Even if Prince Qi hadn't spoken, Feng Suiyu, who had already become the Eastern Palace's Storehouse Officer, had already noticed something unusual about the hairpin.","It was only a matter of time before the treasure left by the Xie family's ancestors fell into the hands of the emperor and his son.\"","\"Little Zhu, the development of Dayan has completely deviated from the original historical timeline, becoming so distorted I hardly recognize it!","'Follow the circumstances and adapt to nature, progress along with the transformations!' We really should also jump out of the original historical timeline, comply with the trends, follow the current developments, and re-examine Dayan.\"","\"Master, the Divine Venerable once said, 'The Great Way is vast and overflowing; how can it be steered left or right?' The future path of Dayan now may hold infinite possibilities.","We, master and servant, need only quietly observe its cycles.\"","As the dialogue between the person and the system continued, Feng Yang had already led over a hundred people to a fork in the road.","He made a hand signal to several leaders, and the hundred-plus people quickly split into three groups, heading in different directions.","Feng Yang, as the Pavilion Master, led fifty men towards Xuanwei Prefecture.","\"Master, forty are coming from Chaoyu Prefecture. I wonder if Dai Yuxing and the others can hold them off.\"","Yue Fuguang didn't care whether they could hold them off or not; she would end up completely unscathed regardless. Her guards, with her backing them up, also wouldn't be in mortal danger.","She had just noticed something amusing and couldn't help asking, \"Little Zhu, was the place where Feng Yang and the others just stopped the Yue Lai Inn?","I think I saw Song Shan hiding by the window, secretly peeking outside.\"","Following Yue Fuguang's question, the camera view, which had shifted away, slowly panned back to the intersection where the assassins had split up.","Everyone could now clearly see a three-story inn standing on the left side of the road, its large signboard bearing the four powerful characters: Yue Lai Inn.","The view zoomed in. At a window on the third floor stood a person. Who else could it be but Song Shan!","\"Master, he pasted on a beard and changed his clothes, yet you still recognized him at a glance. So impressive!\"","Yue Fuguang fully accepted Little Zhu's flattery and casually added, \"Just average, only the third best in the world!\"","Little Zhu blurted out, \"I know the first is the Divine Venerable herself, and the second is the Eldest Senior Brother!\"","The onlookers: How did another Eldest Senior Brother appear? Who knows how many powerful immortals are in Little Immortal Lord's sect!","Little Immortal Lord dares to call herself the third best in the world, showing no regard for heaven and earth. That backing must be pretty solid!","Regardless of what everyone thought, the system continued, \"Master, look quickly! Song Shan is coming out with his men!\"","\"Judging by his direction, he's heading towards us.\"","Yue Fuguang felt helpless. She really was a popular target.","These heads delivered right to her doorstep... it would almost be impolite not to take them!","Carrying sharp weapons stirs the heart to kill! The amount of incense fire she had absorbed recently was a bit excessive, and her own growth was faster than anticipated.","After spending points to acquire the thunder technique from the system and later gathering the incantations for summoning wind, rain, and lightning, she always felt a bit of a restless itch.","If it weren't for the Merit System weighing on her, she might have forgotten, just like the system, that they were a Merit System, not a Gossip System, and couldn't kill indiscriminately.","Since she could absorb incense fire, the concept of karma was certainly not empty talk. Killing would inevitably stain her with karma and baleful energy.","This realization acted like a bridle on her, who was about to run wild.","\"System, do you think my urge to kill is too strong? Is it because I'm influenced by you?\"","Faced with the host's blame-shifting, the system sweated bullets. It vehemently refuted, \"Host, impossible! The system is a Merit System!","Merit Systems are all little cuties, compassionate at heart, only saving people!\"","By the end, its voice grew smaller and smaller, starting to sound a bit guilty.","It was a Merit System, that was true, but currently, the Merit System was being suppressed by the Gossip System.","If the Merit System weren't the main system, the Gossip System would have long since turned everything upside down!","The system wrung its fingers, secretly thinking that it hadn't dared to restore the Gossip System's data recently. The more it restored, the more it felt its own Gossip System seemed a bit different from other gossip systems?","The system didn't dare confess this to Yue Fuguang, but thinking about her words, it really might be its fault.","After all, when it chose a host, Yue Fuguang completely met the binding criteria for a Merit System. She was at least a good person, right?","At this moment, the system didn't consider that if its Gossip System was different from other systems, perhaps the Merit System was also somewhat special?","Yue Fuguang was far too clever. Based on her understanding of the system, she immediately detected the guilt and lack of confidence in its words.","However, she didn't expose it right away. Instead, she said, \"Should we play around and cast a few thunderbolts later?\""]},{"number":294,"title":"Chapter 294: This child knows how to hold back.","paragraphs":["Although it was a question, she opened her hands, and a pale purple lightning thread, a few shades deeper than before, lingered around her hands.","It changed into different shapes according to her will.","Yue Fuguang played with it for a while before the system suddenly called out, Master, the people have arrived!","Yue Fuguang looked up. It could be said that the current situation perfectly illustrated the idiom of the mantis stalking the cicada, unaware of the oriole behind.","The Yu Manor and she were the singing cicada. If the people sent by Feng Yang were the mantis, then Matsuyama, trailing behind with seven or eight people, clearly wanted to be the oriole.","Unfortunately, he did not know that behind the oriole, there was still a hunter holding a bow and arrow.","The eyes of the three groups led by Wei Ping, Cai Xian, and Shen Kang lit up. The surprises tonight came one after another.","The three men were smiling so hard their faces were about to split.","Among the three groups, their team would undoubtedly reap the greatest harvest.","They started fighting! Little Zhu, keep an eye out, do not let my guards die.","As the clashing sounds of weapons rang out from outside, Shen Chunying led Liu Wei, Xu Xiaoman, and a few other women with the best martial arts skills swiftly into the Mingyue Pavilion, standing guard outside Yue Fuguang's bedroom.","Hearing the rustling sounds inside, Cuizhu asked, Miss, were you woken up by the commotion outside?","She lifted the curtain and stepped into the inner chamber. Miss, do you need this servant to help you up?","Although Yue Fuguang had given Cuizhu an official rank of the secondary sixth grade, she was still accustomed to calling herself this servant instead of subordinate in her daily life.","Yue Fuguang nodded. What happened outside?","As Cuizhu helped her dress and get up, she said softly, A few petty thieves were found outside the manor. Lord Dai has already taken people over.","She adjusted Yue Fuguang's collar and added, Rest assured, Miss. They are just a few petty thieves. They will all be captured in a moment.","Little Zhu, quickly check the current situation. If they are all caught by Dai Yuxing and the others, who am I supposed to strike with my lightning?","The people inside and outside the bedroom could not help but twitch their mouths upon hearing Yue Fuguang's words.","Although they were not afraid, they still inevitably felt tense for the adult's safety.","Yet their adult treated this as a fun game. Was this the so-called boldness of the highly skilled?","Meanwhile, Dai Yuxing, Zhang Fang, and the others who were fighting outside heard Yue Fuguang's words.","Their movements paused for a moment. Then, when facing their opponents, they inevitably became a bit gentler, deliberately dragging out the fight.","Master, it is not over yet. Who do you want to strike?","Matsuyama! I find his shifty-eyed look very unpleasant. If he is caught later and uses his identity as an excuse, he might actually escape this ordeal.","So we cannot give him the chance to speak.","Master is right. The Emperor is a coward. He might actually be afraid of offending Dongyi and let Matsuyama go!","While the system flatteringly agreed with Yue Fuguang, it did not forget to step on Emperor Mingxi.","Poor Emperor Mingxi, waiting for the results far away in the imperial palace, only felt his nose itch, completely unaware that the Divine Artifact had handed him another scapegoat pot.","Hearing the Divine Artifact's complaints, his ministers and nephew subconsciously coughed lightly. To cover for the respected, they coughed so loudly just now that they heard absolutely nothing!","The people behind them lowered their heads or whispered among themselves. With the Junior Preceptor's guards controlling the scene, they decided not to go out just yet.","Right at this moment, the sky suddenly surged with wind and clouds, and the starry sky was covered by gauze-like mist and clouds.","Master, you just want to strike a few people, why make such a big scene?","Isn't this to make the thunder and lightning look more reasonable? It is a small scene, just a casual wave of the hand!","Everyone's eyelids twitched. Junior Preceptor, if you call summoning wind and clouds a small scene, then what is a big scene?","Before this thought could settle, they saw lightning flash and thunder roll above the Yu Manor, with golden electric arcs weaving through the clouds.","Rumble!","Rumble!","Everyone opened their mouths wide, watching helplessly as purple lightning roared down from the sky, accurately striking Matsuyama and his subordinates who were hiding in the corner of the Yu Manor's wall.","The crowd watched as wisps of green smoke slowly rose from Matsuyama and the others. Those standing close could even smell... the scent of roasted meat!","The few people standing frozen were not only smoking, but upon closer inspection, purple lightning threads occasionally flashed across them. Those nearby seemed to hear the crackling sound of exploding electric sparks.","Yet, such terrifying thunderbolts did not damage the walls of the Yu Manor in the slightest!","Gulp, gulp!","The crowd unanimously began to swallow their saliva. Wei Ping murmured to Cai Xian, who had just regrouped with him, Just now, I think I saw the Junior Preceptor in the sky!","Did you see it?","He stared blankly at the sky, doubting himself. Were my eyes playing tricks on me?","Cai Xian turned to him and said seriously, I saw it too! That was the Junior Preceptor's... dharma body formed by lightning!","Dharma body?","Shen Kang, who had stumbled over with somewhat messy footsteps, heard Cai Xian's words as soon as he arrived and could not help but ask out loud.","Wei Ping was jolted out of his own world by their words. He chewed them over repeatedly, and finally, with a look of pleasant surprise, said, \"Yes, the Minister is right, it is a dharma body! The Young Preceptor is a deity, so naturally, she has a dharma body!\"","Wei Ping firmly believed in this explanation.","He didn't understand Buddhism, Confucianism, or Taoism, but none of that mattered. Right now, they only believed in the Young Preceptor, their one true god!","Meanwhile, Dai Yuxing and the other guards, who had been fighting fiercely with their opponents, were suddenly brought to a halt by the two claps of thunder.","It was as if someone had pressed the pause button on the entire scene.","The lightning struck less than a hundred meters away from them, and two thunderbolts blasted seven or eight people.","Dai Yuxing, Zhang Fang, and the other guards were relatively fine. Although they were extremely shocked in their hearts, they had the spiritual rain as a foundation, so they accepted it quickly.","These people didn't yet know that the Cao residence being struck was also the doing of their Young Preceptor!","Anyway, they were very relieved. No matter how loud the thunder roared, it wouldn't fall on them.","But the people from the Wind and Rain Pavilion were different. First there was the incident at the Cao residence, and now this was happening right before their eyes.","Every time, it seemed to be because they targeted the Young Preceptor Yue, who had descended with a divine oracle...","Looking at the few people in the distance who had been struck unconscious, and after some wild imagination involving gods and ghosts, even those with \"faith\" couldn't hold on, no matter how good their mindset was!","Those with stronger willpower feigned an attack and staggered away, trying to run.","Those with weaker willpower simply chickened out.","They threw down their weapons with a clatter and began kowtowing toward the Yu residence, muttering to themselves.","They recounted every bad thing they had done since they wore open-crotch pants.","Yue Fuguang didn't care about these people's mutterings; the laws of Great Yan would naturally punish them.","She smugly said to the system, \"Little Zhu, did your master control the power well? Medium rare, seriously injured but not dead, and the courtyard wall wasn't damaged.\"","Regardless of how the Divine Artifact responded, Yu Chongshan and the rest of the Yu family silently nodded in their respective courtyards. Their Fuguang was naturally the most amazing!","In Old Madam Yu's words, \"This child has a good sense of proportion and knows how to be frugal. She saved the residence the money needed to repair the outer wall!\""]},{"number":295,"title":"Chapter 295: Overseas Expansion Plan","paragraphs":["[Master is the best in the whole wide world!] The system provided plenty of emotional support.","Chatting and laughing, the person and the system soon saw Yu Chongshan arriving at the Bright Moon Pavilion with Wei Ping, Cai Xian, and Shen Kang.","They had appeared in the Yu Manor with a hundred or so men, and the hiding spots of everyone were clearly displayed on the screen in the sky.","Now that the mop-up operation was over, they naturally had to come and give Yue Fuguang a reasonable explanation!","\"Lord Wei, are you saying that you found Feng Yang's hiding place a long time ago?\" Yue Fuguang invited everyone to sit down.","Wei Ping cupped his hands and said, \"The Junior Preceptor is correct. The reason we delayed making our move to arrest them was to bait everyone out today and capture them all in one fell swoop.\"","Cai Xian added, \"We received the news about their three main attack locations too late and couldn't inform the Junior Preceptor in time. Please forgive us!\"","Yue Fuguang waved her hand dismissively, \"Looking at the deployment of the guards in my courtyard and outside the manor, they must have received your message in time.\"","\"Fuguang, besides Feng Yang's men, the Dongyi prince Matsuyama and his subordinates also appeared outside our manor this time.","However, they were out of luck. The weather outside suddenly changed, and they were accidentally struck by falling lightning.\"","Yu Chongshan had a face full of joy when he mentioned this.","\"Matsuyama? Didn't he return to the Dongyi State? Why did he come back? How is he now? Is he badly injured?\"","Yue Fuguang wore all her doubts clearly on her face.","[Master, aren't you showing a bit too much doubt?]","Yue Fuguang felt a moment of embarrassment; her acting was indeed a bit over the top!","She forcefully tried to save face, 'Is it too much? Not at all!'","Yu Chongshan hid the smile in his eyes and said, \"He still has a breath left, so he won't die. As for his purpose in returning, we'll have to wait until Lord Wei and the others interrogate him to find out.\"","\"His Majesty wouldn't end up letting him go out of consideration for his status as a prince, right?\"","Yue Fuguang couldn't help but subtly slander Emperor Mingxi, giving him a long-distance warning.","Wei Ping, Cai Xian, and the others exchanged glances. Shen Kang, who had been silent all this time, spoke up, \"Rest assured, Junior Preceptor, His Majesty will absolutely not let him go this time.\"","The corners of his mouth curled up, revealing a sly smile. \"Besides, Matsuyama was struck beyond recognition by the lightning, and all the people we caught tonight are assassins from the Wind and Rain Pavilion.","We have never seen the Dongyi prince Matsuyama, who has already returned to his country!\"","[Master, there's actually a smart person hiding among a bunch of fools!]","Fool Cai and Fool Wei twitched the corners of their mouths. They just answered a step too late and were beaten to it by this kid Shen Kang.","How did they get grouped into the fool category by Lord Divine Artifact!","Shen Kang, who was praised as a smart person by Lord Divine Artifact, unconsciously puffed out his chest and sat even straighter.","Yue Fuguang covertly glanced behind him; if this guy had a tail, it would probably be wagging in the air by now!","Wei Ping and the others quickly nodded in agreement, \"Lord Shen is right. We indeed haven't seen any Dongyi prince today.\"","Speaking of Dongyi, Yue Fuguang remembered another matter, so she asked, \"Grandfather, how is the construction of the naval vessels at the shipyard going?\"","A few months have passed, there should be some progress by now!","At the mention of this, a smile appeared on Yu Chongshan's face. \"The blueprints for building the large ships that Fuguang provided are very detailed.","Several master craftsmen from the Ministry of Works are leading over a thousand artisans to simultaneously build two large ships at the Yining Shipyard according to the blueprints.","Everything is going smoothly so far. I imagine it won't take two years before our Great Yan can have several more large ships that fear no ocean storms.\"","By then, it will be time for them to venture east.","If Great Yan wants to sweep across the other five nations, the first one to destroy is the enemy at their back, Dongyi.","Well, of course, it's also because they have a mountain of gold and silver mines. Taking that place will provide an endless stream of financial support for Great Yan.","[Master, if they have the guts to deploy troops to Dongyi, will you tell them the locations of the gold and silver mines in the Dongyi archipelago?]","'If they have the courage to deploy troops, I will naturally consider it. Otherwise, let them find it themselves; who knows how long that will take!'","[Master, if they go a little further, there are not only gold and silver mines but also spices and timber that sell for astronomical prices in Great Yan.","Although we look down on them, it seems these mortals really like these things!]","The few people who were still looking down and drinking tea couldn't help but pause their movements. Shen Kang, after all, was only in his early twenties, young and unable to keep his composure.","The teacup in his hand trembled, and he didn't even notice a few drops of tea spilling onto his clothes.","Feeling that this wasn't stimulating enough, Yue Fuguang continued to raise the stakes, 'Little Zhu, didn't you say that there are various other mineral veins on the islands further away?'","[Yes, Master! Little Zhu remembers there are iron mines, copper mines, gold and silver mines, and some other precious mineral veins.","But with Great Yan's current technology, they wouldn't even recognize them.]","Every time the system mentioned one, it was like sticking a needle into everyone's hearts, providing a powerful jolt of excitement.","When the few of them finally took their leave, walking as if they were riding the wind, Yue Fuguang guessed that Emperor Mingxi wouldn't be getting any sleep tonight.","Yue Fuguang didn't care whether the emperor could sleep or not. Anyway, she had already asked her grandfather to request a leave of absence for her, so she wouldn't be attending the morning court tomorrow.","[Host, are you sure that the first place Great Yan will attack is Dongyi?]","\"I am not sure! That is why I kept raising the stakes tonight. With such massive profits dangling right in front of them, how could the donkey that is the Great Yan Dynasty not start running?\"","Developing maritime trade and training a naval force—if these things are not prepared in advance, are they supposed to wait until they actually have seafaring ships to even consider it?","\"I was just worried that the Emperor and his ministers of Great Yan might have a sudden rush of blood to the head and send their existing land army out to sea!\"","Great Yan did indeed have a water force along its coast, but its scale was small, and a portion of it was firmly in the hands of the Sima family.","If Emperor Mingxi did not start training a powerful navy of his own right now, even if he dealt with the Sima family before expanding eastward, there was no guarantee that the loyalties of those corrupted naval forces would not be compromised.","[Those shrewd foxes would not resort to such a foolish move, would they?]","The System, having read the history of Great Yan, said this out loud, but inwardly, it was not entirely confident either.","However, the person and the System soon received good news.","Because Yue Fuguang had not attended court today, she had to wait until Yu Chongshan finished his official duties to learn that the Emperor had proposed expanding the navy during the morning assembly.","\"Grandfather, His Majesty wants to expand the naval forces, but it probably will not go too smoothly, will it?\"","Setting aside the conservative faction, Sima Jing's people would never allow the emergence of another force outside their control to compete for power and profit with the navy currently held by the Sima family.","Yu Chongshan nodded. \"Fuguang, your guess is correct. There are indeed many opponents, but there are even more officials who support the expansion of the navy.\"","Yu Zhongchun chimed in, \"His Majesty is absolutely determined to build a new type of navy. How could those petty buffoons possibly stop him!\"","Yu Shuchun nodded in agreement. \"Big brother is right. The large ships are already under intense construction. If we do not expand the naval forces, we cannot exactly force our current landlubber soldiers onto those ships when the time comes!\"","[Master, from the looks of it, the Emperor and ministers of Great Yan have not lost their minds enough to use the land army as a navy.]","Land army? Navy?","The hearts of the father and sons stirred. Such terms were quite fitting. They faintly felt that, aside from these two military branches, there ought to be others as well.","Yet, given their current level of understanding, they had no idea what was missing!"]},{"number":296,"title":"Chapter 296: Are there still any spies among these people","paragraphs":["\"Every profession has its specialty. You can't expect a naval officer who commands ships to pilot an airplane, and likewise, an army soldier without proper training can't handle the sea.","Even without an enemy attack, the ocean's storms and waves alone can overwhelm them.\"","An airplane? After more than half a year, the Yu family father and son heard this word again, though they still didn't quite understand what it specifically referred to. Judging from the name, it must be something that flies in the sky?","\"But training a strong navy with sailors who know their way around water isn’t easy,\" he continued.","Most soldiers from the north are landlubbers. Even those who know how to swim aren’t necessarily fearless when facing the vast ocean.","Yue Fuguang didn’t understand these matters either but couldn’t help asking, \"Grandfather, why doesn’t the court recruit new soldiers from fishermen along the coast?","If the military pay is sufficient, wouldn’t it be easy to enlist good young men who are familiar with the water?\"","Currently, the treasury of Dayan, including the emperor’s private funds, is far from lacking silver.","Once the Sima family is dealt with, Emperor Mingxi will become even wealthier.","Yu Zhongchun’s eyes lit up with excitement, exclaiming, \"Yes, Father, Fuguang’s idea is excellent! I’ve heard that although the south is prosperous, wealth is concentrated among officials and merchants. Ordinary people living by the sea or lakes have it harder than those inland.","As for the northern fishermen, their lives are even tougher.\"","So, if the military pay is generous, it’s truly possible to recruit a group of hardy lads who spend their days working with water.","Yu Chongshan thought this made sense. Whether it would succeed or not, only trying would tell. He nodded and said, \"Alright, I’ll draft a memorial to submit later and see how His Majesty decides.\"","With this matter settled, Yue Fuguang brought up another point. She said, \"I’ve heard from my friend, a maritime merchant, that overseas wealth far exceeds our imagination.","Grandfather, Father, uncles—have you ever considered building a few ships of our own for the Yu family?\"","Once the big ships are built, Emperor Mingxi will surely promote maritime trade vigorously. Knowing that the outside world is so prosperous, there’s no reason to leave that wealth untapped.","This pie is too big; the royal family won’t and can’t eat it all alone without leaving some crumbs for others.","She believed many court officials would want a share, so the Yu family should prepare early. Most importantly, she wanted to go to sea herself—not just ride on someone else’s ship.","\"So, Fuguang means our family should follow the trend and develop maritime trade?\"","Yu Chongshan’s eyes brightened for a moment, but then hesitation crept in. \"Our family has never been involved in this kind of business before.","We don’t have the personnel for it. If we recruit now—\"","Yue Fuguang knew his concerns and smiled, \"Grandfather, you forgot I have a friend who’s a maritime merchant! Let him help us train a few skilled hands, and problem solved.\"","[Master, are you really going to train sailors for the Yu family? Be honest, is it because you want to go out to sea yourself?]","\"This isn’t difficult at all. When the time comes, we can just send over two puppet experts who know navigation, right? Just admit it—you want to go out and have some fun!\"","The system was caught perfectly by Yue Fuguang, answering without hesitation, [Little Zhu obviously wants to go out and play.","If we’re going to sail, we definitely need to properly train these people.","Not to mention everything else—routes, monsoons, tides, and preparing supplies for the voyage. Who knows these better than us?]","“So, remember to pick two people to be ready. Even if the Yu family doesn’t set sail, we’ll prepare ourselves just in case Dayan ends up following the old path!”","Father and son of the Yu family both smiled inwardly. It turned out the child just wanted to go out and play. The sea was perilous, and knowing they couldn’t persuade her otherwise, they could only do their best to ensure her safety.","With that, Yu Chongshan made the decision, “Alright. Since Floating Light has this plan, then your grandfather will send someone to the south to check things out. It’d be best if we could buy a ready-made sea vessel and modify it ourselves—that way it’ll be faster.”","[Master, I also have a large sea ship here. When it’s time to set sail, we’ll take our own ship.]","“But does it have the storm-warding formation carved on it?”","“Not only warding off storms, but fire as well. It’s a pity the spiritual energy here is insufficient. Otherwise, it could even fly into the sky—making it even faster!”","A ship flying into the sky? What a magnificent sight that would be!","The father and son exchanged a sigh of regret. Why was it that Dayan lacked that kind of spiritual energy?","Still, the storm-warding formation Floating Light mentioned sounded like a great asset. If Floating Light set sail on such a ship, they would feel much more at ease.","“It’s a pity my divine power hasn’t fully recovered yet, or I’d carve the same formation onto other ships as well.”","Yu family father and son exchanged a look and understood. They had to find a way to have His Majesty promote Floating Light’s reputation again. What they originally planned to do after the bountiful harvest of high-yield breeds had to be started ahead of schedule.","It wasn’t enough for Floating Light to become famous just within Dayan; their merchant fleet had to venture farther.","Whether it would be profitable or not was secondary—what mattered most was spreading Floating Light’s name.","While the Yu family was busy both assembling their merchant fleet and sending trusted managers south to buy ships, after several rounds of disputes, the proposal to expand the new navy finally ended with Emperor Mingxi’s victory.","Following that, the emperor issued an edict to recruit naval troops along the coastal regions, and even those from inland who knew how to handle water were welcome to sign up.","Surprisingly, many able-bodied men from the civilian population signed up. Well, who could blame them? The court was offering generous pay!","Good food, high military salary—what’s not to like about joining the army?","When Yue Floating Light visited the Right Martial Guard’s new camp again, she heard that the navy had already recruited over two thousand men.","“Young Master, here is the roster of soldiers for your review.”","Wei Shouyi handed a roster over to Yue Floating Light.","“Little Zhu, are there any spies among these people?”","The moment Yue Floating Light asked, the dozen or so civil and military officers standing behind her all felt a chill in their hearts.","Cai Xian, Wei Shouyi, and the others exchanged glances. After thorough screening, they had identified eight suspicious individuals.","At this moment, they were even more anxious to find out if any had slipped through the cracks.","[Master, there are still five more. Hu Wei on page two, Tang Xiaoshan on page eight, Lin Daqing on page eleven, Guan Tang on page twenty-five, and Li Pi on page forty-seven.","These people are all infiltrators from other factions.]","Hearing those names, Wei Shouyi’s grip tightened until his knuckles cracked.","Because both His Majesty and the Young Master valued this new army of ten thousand men, Wei Shouyi was especially attentive. While he couldn’t claim to know every soldier, his frequent inspections of the camp meant he was familiar with many.","And these five stood out in every way—he actually knew all of them.","Moreover, he had already accepted that these five were definitely among the Young Master’s quota of five thousand.","And now you tell him that the sand they had been searching for so long was nearly all given away in one fell swoop to the Young Master.","If those people cause trouble at the Three-Way Crossing, I, Wei Shouyi, will bear the blame with my life!","Yue Fuguang memorized the faces of these few and then turned to the assembled officials behind her. \"Gentlemen, how about accompanying me to the training grounds?\"","Originally, she had come just to select a few people and didn’t need such a large entourage, but since they heard that Wei Shouyi was throwing a pig slaughter feast today—both to celebrate and to apologize—they were all eager for a taste of the meat and found every excuse to tag along.","If Emperor Mingxi hadn’t been tied up with urgent matters and unable to attend, he would have surely come to join the festivities as well."]},{"number":297,"title":"Chapter 297: No Playing with Fools","paragraphs":["There was no other way. The livestock and poultry in the new military camp had not only eaten the grass in the Junior Preceptor's fields but also the grass in the imperial estate.","That smell...","Speaking of this, Wei Shouyi could brag about it for a year. That day, he had been caught in the rain following behind. After realizing the wondrous effects of the rainwater, he went to Emperor Mingxi and offered to help pull weeds at the imperial estate.","Emperor Mingxi agreed on the spot. He had to agree; the ten thousand acres of fertile land on the imperial estate could never be managed in time by the estate workers alone.","These ten thousand new recruits were considered reliable and easily controllable strong laborers.","As a result, the chickens, ducks, geese, pigs, sheep, and other small animals benefited greatly.","\"Junior Preceptor, please go first.\"","\"Let us go together, together.\"","The group listened to Wei Shouyi's highly professional explanation of animal husbandry and soon arrived at the drill ground.","Ten thousand men stood in a dense, orderly formation. Apart from the fluttering banners rustling in the wind, there was no other sound. Setting aside everything else, at the very least, their military discipline had been well-trained.","Yue Fuguang took the lead without hesitation, stepping up to the commanding platform that was much taller than her. The wind caught the hem of her skirt, making it bloom like a flower.","At this moment, her expression was calm. She looked up at the drill ground, her gaze sweeping over the dense army of ten thousand men below. She was not at all intimidated by the aura of the fully armed army, which felt like a drawn sword.","Instead, wherever her gaze, carrying an innate supreme coercion, fell, everyone bowed their heads.","It wasn't that Yue Fuguang had a protagonist's halo, nor did she possess a natural kingly aura. It was all because she had equipped the item 'Intimidation' that she had previously bought from the system shop.","She had stocked up on it long ago, just waiting for this day!","While she was observing the men below the platform, they were also subtly observing her.","The name Yue Fuguang had long spread throughout Great Yan along with the potatoes that yielded a thousand catties per acre. Leaving aside other places, in the prefectures near the capital, she was known to absolutely everyone.","The soldiers standing in the drill ground knew a bit more than the commoners. They knew that the brand-new, shiny armor they were currently wearing,","and the incredibly sharp swords they held in their hands, were among the best equipment in the Great Yan army. Their treatment also far exceeded that of other troops.","All of this, whether it was the craftsmanship used to forge their weapons and armor or their food, clothing, housing, and transportation, stemmed from the demands of the nine-year-old Junior Preceptor standing on the commanding platform.","She was the true person in the Great Yan Dynasty who was beneath only one person and above tens of millions!","The crowd looked at her exquisite and tender face, which was dignified without being angry, carrying a hint of divinity that they could not comprehend.","An inexplicable urge to kneel appeared in their minds.","Yue Fuguang, equipped with the Intimidation item, was completely unaware of her true power at this moment. Seeing the soldiers looking at her with faces full of reverence,","she thought it was entirely due to the item.","\"I am Yue Fuguang.\"","Her voice was faint, and she didn't even intentionally raise her volume when she spoke, but even those standing a hundred meters away could hear her clearly.","She continued, \"I have not come today on imperial orders to muster troops. Therefore, anyone who wishes to withdraw may step forward now.","I can guarantee that you will be pardoned of any crime, and it will not affect your future promotions.\"","Sancha Land did not seem like a good place to go right now, and it was hard to guarantee that some of them truly didn't want to go.","A forced melon is not sweet; she would absolutely never force others to do what they did not want to do.","She waved the roster in her hand but did not immediately open it. \"You have ten breaths of time to consider. If you miss this chance, I will begin calling names. Those who are selected will have no chance to back out, otherwise, they will be dealt with according to military law!\"","As Yue Fuguang's words fell, the formation of ten thousand men remained silent. It looked as calm as water, but some people, without moving their heads or bodies,","were darting their eyes left and right, wishing they could grow an eye on the back of their heads.","They couldn't help it. Choosing one out of two, they were terrified that the Junior Preceptor wouldn't favor them and they would be eliminated!","Therefore, they still hoped in their hearts that someone would voluntarily withdraw.","Most of these people were soldiers who were close to the dandies like Wei Yan, Cai Bing, and Huo Sui.","They had seen with their own eyes how hard the young masters had worked to curry favor with the Junior Preceptor's second brother.","Logically, these people had comparable statuses and shouldn't all have to suck up to one person. After asking around, they learned that they were all currying favor with the Second Young Master because they wanted to go to Sancha Land.","With their shallow knowledge, they naturally couldn't see what was so good about Sancha Land, which was thousands of miles away.","But foolish people also had their own ways of survival, which was to follow the smart people. It didn't matter if they didn't understand it themselves, as long as the path was right.","One day, they would know why they had chosen this way.","There are no walls in the world that don't leak wind. The dandies' little tricks, without being deliberately hidden, slowly spread throughout the military camp.","Some wanted to follow the smart people, and some were just following the crowd. Therefore, at this moment, more than half of these ten thousand men genuinely wanted to go or were not opposed to leaving their hometowns.","Because it was said that even if they went to Sancha Land, the food would not be any worse. So, for those who couldn't get enough to eat at home, their simplest thought was that eating rations anywhere was still eating rations.","\"System, sort by affection level.\"","Yue Fuguang still felt that she needed to let the data speak. She wasn't picking the strongest, only those who could be loyal to her in the future.","This affection data from the first meeting was very genuine.","Yue Fuguang looked at the flickering affection values going up and down on the system panel and curled the corners of her lips slightly. Leaving the others aside, the bottom five were completely motionless!","Ten breaths had passed. Yue Fuguang looked calmly at the crowd below the platform, her voice still carrying a faint sense of distance and an almost imperceptible pressure.","She didn't plan to take the approachable route to win people's hearts. Her people only needed to respect her, fear her, be loyal to her, and follow her!","It was still the same saying: she didn't make friends, she only gathered believers!","She said, \"Since no one has chosen to withdraw, I will begin calling names. Ren Erniu, Fang Daping, Ge Sanqi...\"","Yue Fuguang still did not open the roster. Instead, like she was taking a stroll, she walked around the commanding platform while calling out one name after another.","Calling names was also a physical task, let alone calling the names of five thousand people. For the sake of this damned sense of ceremony, and perhaps because this was the only time she would directly connect with these people, she gave it her all.","After all, having been personally selected from her mouth, emotionally, they would naturally feel different.","If it weren't for the fact that no one could replace her for this job, and if she hadn't taken a Body Strengthening Pill and a Throat Soothing Pill in advance, she might have actually held the thick roster and crossed out names.","And the people below the platform who were personally called by Yue Fuguang shouted loudly as they stepped forward half a pace, unable to hide the excitement and honor on their faces.","Yue Fuguang glanced over. Not bad, some people were grinning from ear to ear. It seemed that the overt and covert promotional efforts of her second brother and his dandy friends these past few days had been quite effective.","It was indeed true that Cai Bing, Wei Yan, and the others were currying favor with Yu Boming because they wanted to go to Sancha Land.","But if it weren't for those few deliberately leaking the information, how could those ordinary soldiers have found out the purpose behind the dandies' flattery?","Everything was an overt plot they had set up to recruit people for Yue Fuguang, without delaying their own affairs.","Whether to follow or not was entirely up to their own judgment.","They remembered the Junior Preceptor's words: she doesn't play with fools."]},{"number":298,"title":"Chapter 298: No Embezzling Soldiers' Pay, No Drawing Pay for Nonexistent Soldiers","paragraphs":["[Master, these ordinary soldiers all seem to really want to go to the Sancha region. Wei Yan, Cai Bing, and Huo Sui have put in a lot of effort. But the one who came up with the idea is that guy named Lin Huaijing.]","\"What did they do?\"","The few people whose names were mentioned by the great divine artifact unconsciously puffed out their chests. Their faces flushed red, and their palms sweated from nervousness.","Their ears perked up, waiting for the praise of the Junior Preceptor and the divine artifact!","And so, the system recounted everything they had done over the past month or so in detail.","Yue Fuguang asked knowingly, \"Little Zhu, are you saying the young masters also want to go to the Sancha region? Do their families agree? The conditions there are harsh. Having one Lin Huaijing is one thing, but why do they all want to go?\"","The system strongly disagreed with her words. It said, [Master, what is wrong with the Sancha region? Although it is sparsely populated and not as bustling as the capital, once they get there, they will be considered your people. Being protected by an Immortal Lord and a divine artifact like us, they certainly will not lose out! Besides, with our plans and the guarantees we provide, as long as they honestly follow instructions and do not cause trouble, their future paths will definitely surpass their ancestors and be completely smooth!]","The fathers of the young masters standing below the stage saw the smug little glances their brats were throwing their way.","They secretly ground their teeth. You little brats, you have not even surpassed your ancestors yet, and you are already showing off?","It is still hard to say whether the Junior Preceptor will even take you in the end!","The young masters obviously also understood their fathers' disdain and the looks that said, you haven't even boarded the ship yet, what are you showing off for?","Therefore, everyone cast eager glances toward Yue Fuguang, conveying only one meaning: We beg the Junior Preceptor to take us as your followers!","\"But look at them, all delicate and fair-skinned. Do they look like people who can endure hardship? Do not let them go there only to come crying back.\"","The young masters silently exchanged glances, seeing disdain in each other's eyes. After all, they had been training for nearly half a year. They had gotten a bit sturdier, but compared to the ordinary soldiers from farming families, they indeed looked a bit frail.","In Wei Shouyi's words, they were acting like a bunch of softies!","Wei Yan, Cai Bing, and the others looked down on each other, puffing out their chests even higher. They even looked at the others with haughty expressions. Anyway, they all felt that they were the most heroic among their brothers!","As for coming back crying, it would absolutely never be them!","[Is Master not planning to let them join in?]","The system's words stirred the hearts of all the young masters and parents present.","Although the parents despised their brats' showing off, if they could board the Junior Preceptor's ship, they could tolerate a little smugness. After all, if the brat succeeded, the whole family would rise with him!","Therefore, Wei Ping, Cai Xian, and the others subconsciously swallowed hard, secretly praying that the Junior Preceptor would look at their past friendship and take in their brats.","Among the young masters, except for Yu Boming and Lin Huaijing, everyone else's faces slowly turned pale, and the light in their eyes gradually faded.","Just as their hearts sank to the bottom, Yue Fuguang's voice rang in their ears like celestial music.","\"Forget it, for the sake of what they have done before and out of respect for the lords, since they want to go, there is no harm in bringing them along for now.","If they can really do well, it is not impossible to let them join in the future.\"","With just one sentence, Yue Fuguang reignited the dying light in the young masters' eyes.","Everyone smiled like the foolish sons of the neighboring landlord.","While the old fathers felt disdain, smiles that were not much smarter than their sons' bloomed on their faces.","\"However...\"","Yue Fuguang's however instantly made the hard-won relaxed atmosphere tense again.","\"However, forget about Bao Zihui. He is newly married, and it is not good to make the couple live apart for years.\"","One sentence decided Bao Zihui's fate.","In order to confuse the Sima family, Bao Qianjun, who had been idle at home after returning to the capital to report on his duties, had also come.","This was his second time seeing this famous Junior Preceptor, and he was extremely grateful to her for saving the lives of his whole family.","Hearing that his son could not go to the Sancha region, he felt sorry for him but also felt that the Junior Preceptor was right.","His son and daughter-in-law had a deep relationship, and it was indeed inappropriate for them to live apart.","Thinking of this, Bao Qianjun's mind suddenly became active. His son could not go, but he was currently without official duties, so could he...","Anyway, as long as they could board the Junior Preceptor's ship, what difference did it make whether it was his son or him?","Watching his brothers rejoice, Bao Zihui, who was still feeling lost alone, did not know that in just this short moment, while he was still placing high hopes on his father to play the emotional card with the Junior Preceptor to bring him along, he was about to face not only a breakup with his brothers but also a betrayal from his own father.","This was also Bao Zihui's first experience with betrayal. From his father's betrayal, he also thought of his original historical timeline, where he was framed by three classmates together. How painful and desperate he must have been then!","Finally nearing the end, Yue Fuguang slowly read out the names of the last five people: Hu Wei, Tang Xiaoshan, Lin Daqing, Guan Tang, and Li Pi.","Hearing the names of these five people, Wei Shouyi, Cai Xian, and the others looked at each other, not understanding why the Junior Preceptor would single out these problematic individuals.","Before they could figure out how to respond, they heard Yue Fuguang speak.","She said, \"Those whose names have been called will set off for the Sancha region in ten days. Before that, this official has a few words to say to everyone.\"","Yue Fuguang put her hands behind her back, standing there like a chilling javelin. Her gaze was calm, and her voice was powerful, \"This official will make a deal with you all. I will use the hundred miles of land in the Sancha region to exchange for an opportunity for all of you to soar to the heavens.\"","Her words immediately caused a commotion below the stage. The first to lose their composure were not the five thousand who were selected.","But those who were not chosen!","What did soaring to the heavens mean? Even the most foolish ordinary soldiers, who had learned a few words following the young masters, knew what it represented.","The empty promises painted by others might be false, but they dared not disbelieve the words spoken by the person in front of them, nor would they refuse to accept them.","Some sighed and wrung their wrists in regret, while others silently gritted their teeth. The Junior Preceptor had made a selection once, so there would be a second time. They had missed out this time, but they must grasp the opportunity next time.","They just did not know what the Junior Preceptor's criteria for selecting people were. Some smart ones had noticed early on that the Junior Preceptor had not looked at the roster.","Those who were selected were not all the ones with the best scores in various training subjects.","At least among the top ten, five were not chosen, including the second place, Fei Zhiyi.","Yue Fuguang paused, her calm gaze sweeping over the slightly restless crowd as an invisible pressure descended.","While scaring everyone and chilling their hearts, it inexplicably gave rise to a trace of admiration. Although Yue Fuguang did nothing, those who met her eyes could not help but feel that this was a truly strong person.","Seeing the crowd return to calm, she continued, \"The Ministry of Revenue has calculated that guarding the Sancha region will cost twelve taels of silver per person each year.","\"But those chosen by me today,\" she suddenly shook out several sheets of paper from her sleeve, \"will each receive a settlement allowance, disbursed directly from the Junior Preceptor's Estate. Should you fall in battle, your children will be granted entry to study at the Imperial Academy.","Should you be maimed or disabled, the Yu family's merchant guilds will give you priority in employment. This applies during times of peace!","In times of war, I guarantee that your military merits will never be stolen by another. Promotions within the army will be based entirely on merit, never on personal connections.","Your military pay will be distributed on time and in full. In my army, no one will siphon off your wages or claim the pay of phantom soldiers. Even if you are wounded, there will be dedicated physicians and abundant medicine to treat you.\"","As Yue Fuguang's words faded, the entire grounds fell into absolute silence!"]},{"number":299,"title":"Chapter 299: Your Merits Will Live Forever","paragraphs":["As she threw out her words one by one, those with shallow tear ducts had already begun to wipe their tears silently.","Of course, the ones crying the hardest were those who had not been selected.","Were the chosen ones not excited?","Naturally, they were excited. It was as if a massive pie had suddenly fallen from the sky and hit them; their brains had crashed, making their reactions a bit sluggish.","Instead, their faces were completely blank, leaving only a buzzing in their heads, as if hundreds of flies were buzzing around their ears.","They were gradually awakened by the quiet sobbing around them, and seeing the tears streaming down the faces of some of the people beside them, they finally felt a sense of reality.","The tears that had long welled up in their eyes also flowed out silently. Let alone everything, as long as even one of the aforementioned promises could be fulfilled, it would be enough for them to pledge their lives!","Yue Fuguang looked at the various reactions of the people below and continued, \"I know what you are thinking, but you only need to remember my words today, and then watch my future actions.","Whether my words are false or not, everyone present can judge for themselves.\"","Saying this, she walked to the edge of the commanding platform, seemingly getting closer to the crowd below. She said, \"Finally, I will give you all one last promise.","For all those who sacrifice their lives for the country, I will submit a memorial to the imperial court to erect a Monument of Heroes for them. With the heroes' names inscribed on the Monument of Heroes, even after thousands of years, people will still remember the soldiers who sacrificed themselves for the country.","Your names will be known to future generations, and your achievements will last forever!\"","Your names will be known to future generations, and your achievements will last forever!","With Yue Fuguang's words falling, a greater commotion instantly erupted after a few seconds of silence, in a much more intense manner than before.","For some, their silent tears and quiet sobbing were replaced by loud wailing.","Another portion of the people just mechanically patted each other's shoulders, exchanging pats and thumps.","They stumbled backward one by one, seemingly pounding each other as if they were foreign enemies.","Some even wanted to die right then and there; looking at their companions' expressions, it was as if they were saying, 'Brother, see you on the Monument of Heroes!'","Yue Fuguang was quite satisfied with their final performance. It showed that the ideological education and the cultivation of a sense of honor she had given them earlier were quite effective.","Otherwise, her last sentence could not have struck such a chord with these people.","Throughout history, how many people have left their names in the annals of history?","Being able to be inscribed on the Monument of Heroes was the closest these grassroots folks would ever get to being passed down to future generations. Once people have enough to eat, read some books, and learn some words, their need for personal achievement naturally rises infinitely.","Let alone these ordinary soldiers from commoner backgrounds, even high-ranking officials like Wei Ping, Cai Xian, and Huo Ying felt their blood boiling upon hearing this.","To have a place to return to after death and be worshipped by descendants was particularly tempting for the ancients, who treated death as they did life.","Yue Fuguang thought, this was probably similar to the temptation for modern people to have a dedicated page in their family genealogy!","The ten thousand soldiers watched as Yue Fuguang, surrounded by the officials, completely disappeared from the drill ground before the scene truly exploded into an uproar.","The suppressed emotions from earlier finally burst forth completely.","With red eyes and clenched fists, they very tacitly divided into two large groups in silence.","At this moment, even blood brothers born of the same mother stood clearly divided, one in the south and one in the north.","Those on the same side, even if they usually didn't get along well, just silently glanced at each other, thinking in their hearts that these were the comrades who would be on the Monument of Heroes with them in the future.","They all gave each other a stiff, awkward, and ugly smile.","Wei Shouyi finally turned around and glanced at the soldiers on the drill ground. If it were normal times, he would truly be afraid of a mutiny.","However, with the carrot dangled in front of them by the Junior Preceptor, and having told everyone in advance that if they weren't selected this time, there would be another chance in the second half of the year.","Therefore, no matter how envious and jealous the unselected ones were in their hearts, they didn't dare to act out.","Otherwise, if they really started a fight, they would not only face military punishment but also directly lose their eligibility for selection in the second half of the year.","So Wei Shouyi was certain that not a single one of these people dared to take the gamble; anyone who caused trouble would be instantly dealt with!","The facts were exactly as he thought. The two sides gathered in groups, led by the first and second place winners of the competition respectively, and at most, they just engaged in verbal battles and exchanged harsh words.","As for actually fighting, they didn't dare in the slightest!","After everyone had walked quite a distance away, Wei Shouyi leaned close to Yue Fuguang and whispered, \"Junior Preceptor, there are a few people among the five thousand soldiers you selected today who have some problems.\"","Yue Fuguang turned her head in confusion and asked, \"General Wei, what kind of problems do you mean? Who are they?\"","Wei Shouyi cupped his hands and said, \"Replying to the Junior Preceptor, the problems I mentioned are suspicions that these individuals are spies planted by other factions.","You might not know, but ever since that assassination incident, we have felt uneasy.","With your selection approaching, we were afraid of any mishaps, so we conducted a screening of all the soldiers in the army.","We actually found eight officers and soldiers who were confirmed as spies, but there are another five who are suspected, yet we have no substantial evidence against them.","Therefore, we haven't taken action against them yet. These five people are Hu Wei, Tang Xiaoshan, Lin Daqing, Guan Tang, and Li Pi.\"","\"I see!\" Yue Fuguang waved her hand indifferently and said, \"Since you have your suspicions, I will keep them, and you can just continue to track down clues.\"","She suddenly put on a serious face and said, \"General Wei, you must already know the importance of the new army. So even if you ultimately cannot find any problems with those five people.","As long as the suspicion remains, for the sake of safety, they should be transferred away as soon as possible.\"","Wei Shouyi bowed and said, \"I obey the Junior Preceptor's orders, I will handle this as soon as possible!\"","Saying this, Wei Shouyi led everyone towards the dining hall.","Yue Fuguang asked the system, 'Little Zhu, do you know the backgrounds of those five people? Who sent them?'","[Master, these five people belong to three factions.]","'Three factions? This new army camp is truly a piece of fat meat in the eyes of some!' Everyone wants to stick a foot in!","[Because the new army camp is related to you, Master, it naturally attracts the attention of those with hidden agendas.","Among these five, Hu Wei, Lin Daqing, Guan Tang, and one of the eight people caught by Wei Shouyi are all informants for those aristocratic families.","Tang Xiaoshan comes from the Tang family in Jiangnan. Master should be able to guess whose man he is, right?]","'Sima Jing's man? If the Emperor knew that this Tang Xiaoshan was sand mixed in by his good cousin, what kind of expression do you think he would have?'","[He might cry!]","Emperor Mingxi: My tears could never flow for a person with the wild ambition of a wolf!","Silently turning around to wipe away the 'drool' from the corner of his eyes, crying was absolutely impossible!","The people behind him tried hard to suppress their turned-up mouths. When they went back to report this matter, they didn't know if His Majesty would cry, but he would definitely stomp his feet in anger!","[As for the last person, Li Pi's parents were originally from Beili. They only came to Dayan because they were affected by the war for the throne twenty years ago.","This time, when Bei Ye came to Dayan to contact the Beili people exiled in Dayan, he reactivated the Li family. Hearing that Li Pi had entered the new recruit camp was an unexpected pleasant surprise for them.]","'I thought that after the scandal between Bei Ye and Wei Qingyi, he would settle down for a bit, but I didn't expect him to be so busy.","He hasn't been staying indoors behind closed doors at all, as the outside world thought!'"]},{"number":300,"title":"Chapter 300: I Hope to Join the Moon Army","paragraphs":["[Their scandals actually became his best cover. The ones hiding in the Northern Li relay station were always the body doubles of Bei Ye and Wei Qingyi.","In reality, the two of them disguised themselves as a married couple and had been wandering all over the capital city of Shangjing.]","The two disguised as a married couple? Everyone's expressions stiffened. Who could have imagined that a dignified prince and the eldest legitimate son of a powerful prime minister would make such a sacrifice for their goals!","\"By the way, Little Zhu, speaking of the noble families, Fourth Master Xie and Xie Xiaojiu first experienced a startled horse and a fall into the water.","Then, just a few days later, one ate poisonous mushrooms, and the other encountered a 'ghost' in the dead of night.","This was all the doing of the noble families, right?\"","Speaking of this, Yue Fuguang found it amusing. Poisoning a horse, pushing someone into the water, or even putting a few poisonous mushrooms in a chicken and mushroom soup were all understandable.","But she never expected that those people would actually think of dressing up as a ghost to scare the Ninth Prince, and the disguise was even of Zhou Yunxin bleeding from her seven orifices.","Screaming that she wanted to take him away, it was a miracle that the superstitious native Xie Xiaojiu wasn't scared out of his mind on the spot. He truly had a strong psyche!","The system also thought of this incident and said in a cheerful voice, [Master, it was indeed the noble families. Xie Xiaojiu got up in the middle of the night and secretly went to meet the hidden spy that Northern Li left in the Great Yan imperial palace.","As a result, he bumped into 'Zhou Yunxin'.","You have to admit, the Ninth Prince truly lives up to his reputation as a ruthless person who poisoned his own eldest brother and 'adoptive father'!","He was scared half to death, but he managed to run all the way back to his own palace before screaming for help!]","Everyone: Ancestor, you refer to His Majesty as an adoptive father, does His Majesty know?","Emperor Mingxi: The dried scab has started bleeding again! With Lord Divine Artifact constantly bringing up this scar, it can't heal at all!","\"If the Emperor still can't realize that these aren't accidents, his two sons are going to die at the hands of the noble families!\"","Wei Ping, Cai Xian, and the others' eyes flickered. Wasn't this exactly their Emperor's goal?","While letting the two take the blame for the Junior Preceptor, he could use the noble families to kill the two princes that he couldn't easily deal with himself.","This would not only wipe out the plans of Southern Yue and Northern Li but also serve as an opportunity to launch an attack against the noble families.","Before the imperial court expanded outward, these unstable factors had to be completely cleaned up.","If it weren't for their massive influence, the sovereign and his subjects wouldn't have had to endure so much.","[If they die, they die. These two have committed many evils, and the signs are already showing. Master, you aren't going to soften your heart just because they are still young, are you?","Southern Yue, behind the Fourth Prince, has been quite restless lately. Concubine Xin and the dying Yue Ying are even trying to contact the noble families.","They want to ally with them to turn their spearheads against the other princes and princesses.","And as for the Ninth Prince, don't think he's pitiful just because he lost his birth mother and the Emperor's favor.","Actually, when Zhou Yunxin fell out of favor, the mother and son had already contacted the Northern Li spies hidden in the palace.","The two of them might look like they are only in their teens, but their minds are already very mature. Even Xie Xiaojiu, this fake prince, has never given up on his ambition to seize the throne.","They even want to take advantage of the chaos while they are being targeted for assassination to fish in troubled waters and make a move against the Eastern Palace.]","Make a move against the Eastern Palace? Wei Ping and the others were so frightened that their legs went weak, almost tripping over flat ground.","The current Crown Prince held a much more important position in their hearts than before.","Especially knowing that the various countries would gradually fall into turmoil in the coming years, a mature, steady, and wise imperial heir who was favored by the Junior Preceptor was incredibly important.","If the Junior Preceptor was the stabilizing pillar of Great Yan from the fairy tales they had heard, then His Royal Highness the Crown Prince was undoubtedly the crucial cornerstone for Great Yan's future development.","Looking at the Emperor's many children, the only one capable and most suitable to inherit the throne was the Crown Prince.","If Great Yan lost Crown Prince Xie Zhiyan, then...","Everyone dared not imagine the consequences!","\"Concubine Xin and Yue Ying want to use someone else's hands to poison the Crown Prince again?\"","Are they still using the same old tricks? Don't they know how to change things up?","[They aren't using someone else's hands. After all, that kind of plotting takes too much time, and time is what they lack the most right now.","Moreover, the Emperor and Empress have strict control over the palace now, so few dare to act rashly at this time. Therefore, Concubine Xin and the others cannot hide behind the scenes this time.","Stepping to the front and doing it themselves is the best choice.","Not to mention that Yue Ying only has a few days left to live. Naturally, he wants to take a gamble before he dies and fight for a future for his child.]","Yue Fuguang was silent for a moment before saying, \"By the way, I remember the Eastern Palace sent a bunch of gifts the day before yesterday, and we haven't given a return gift yet.\"","[What does Master want to do?]","\"Since we said we would protect the Crown Prince, he cannot die. Tomorrow, send two detoxification pills to the Eastern Palace.\"","[Are you not going to tell them about the schemes of Northern Li and Southern Yue?]","\"As the Crown Prince, he should discover this himself. If we guide him at every turn, what will they do if we leave here one day?","Learning to walk on their own is better for them than us holding them up, isn't it?\"","Yue Fuguang spoke righteously, but deep down, she just wanted to be lazy and slack off. She felt that these people were good tools if they voluntarily helped complete her tasks.","But the people behind her didn't know she just wanted to be lazy!","They actually thought that this Junior Preceptor, who hadn't mentioned running away for a while, had truly settled down.","They never expected that the Junior Preceptor had never abandoned this idea!","Hearing this, everyone was terrified, infinitely more scared than when they learned the Southern Yue people were going to attack the Eastern Palace.","On the way to the dining hall, they were moving their legs purely on instinct. Wei Ping, Cai Xian, and the others only managed to avoid falling because they were supported by their sons.","Now that Great Yan was improving day by day, they felt even more inseparable from the Junior Preceptor's presence.","She was like the stabilizing pillar in the imperial court. The days she attended court and the days she didn't felt completely different to them.","They dared not even imagine an imperial court without the Junior Preceptor...","Yu Chongshan and his son exchanged a glance. Thinking of the ocean-going ships his granddaughter mentioned, Fuguang must have meant going out to sea, not truly leaving Great Yan or leaving this world.","Didn't they agree to stay until she was eighty? She couldn't possibly return early!","Little did they know, Yue Fuguang's plan was to finish her tasks before she turned eighteen. She still had nine years.","According to her plan, nine years was enough to build up Great Yan and pacify the five nations!","Everyone walked forward with different thoughts, their heads bowed and eyes lowered. Like defeated soldiers, they slouched and lost most of their spirit.","Wei Shouyi quickly picked up the previous topic and said, \"Junior Preceptor, since you don't plan to take those five people, should this humble general select another five to fill the spots for you?\"","Before Yue Fuguang could speak, Wei Ping and Cai Xian simultaneously pushed the sons supporting them and chimed in, \"Why would General Wei need to select more people? Aren't there a few ready-made ones right here?\"","Although the Junior Preceptor had said she would take their brats along, as long as it wasn't finalized, they couldn't be at ease.","Wei Yan, Cai Bing, Huo Sui, and a group of other playboys immediately stepped forward, bowed to Yue Fuguang, and said, \"Junior Preceptor, we hope to join the Yue Army and follow the soldiers to garrison the Three-Pronged Land.","We earnestly beseech Your Excellency to grant our request!\""]}]);
